{"parentUuid":"8aa2ab75-d936-439b-bdb4-791a939c31ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_0eb57267595624dc016a7a540e4d688191815660671fe88197","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":442,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":82432,"output_tokens":197,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_Cs68aKgrMn6nwk4KZLepLhrl","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts","offset":300,"limit":210}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"attributionSkill":"simplify","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3a91f24-ba36-4e0a-9f9c-f18eeb099984","timestamp":"2026-08-10T22:43:32.346Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"2306d4a5-fc17-4a0b-9a22-11aea896e181","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0a8de032-5fd3-4106-bcf4-797ed6a2efc2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_vISYhZM9YGTgpjSd8G9YYoX6","type":"tool_result","content":"760\t\t\t\torganizationId: options.organizationId,\n761\t\t\t\tversions: options.versions,\n762\t\t\t\tbridgeStartedMs,\n763\t\t\t\t// The real counter, from the only thing that advances it. A hardcoded 0\n764\t\t\t\t// would make every `TreeResponse.gseq` claim \"consistent with zero\n765\t\t\t\t// events\": the client latches 0 from the snapshot frame, the first live\n766\t\t\t\t// frame then looks like a sequence gap, §9.3.3 says refetch the tree, and\n767\t\t\t\t// the refetched tree reports 0 again — a refetch per event, forever, with\n768\t\t\t\t// `treeStale` (`lastEventGseq < 0`) unsatisfiable and therefore unable to\n769\t\t\t\t// catch it.\n770\t\t\t\tcurrentGseq: () => events.currentGseq(),\n771\t\t\t\t// (RECONCILE-RETRACT) `reconcile()` settles questions the hook never\n772\t\t\t\t// reported. That is exactly the moment an armed or delivered push must be\n773\t\t\t\t// withdrawn — on ARM64 a dead hook is a documented failure mode, and\n774\t\t\t\t// without this the phone keeps a notification standing for a question\n775\t\t\t\t// answered at the desk minutes ago.\n776\t\t\t\t//\n777\t\t\t\t// (TREE-FRESHNESS-GSEQ) It is also a change to the tree, so it mints an\n778\t\t\t\t// event. `gseq` is the ONLY freshness signal on the wire — `/v1/tree`\n779\t\t\t\t// stamps it and `/v1/heartbeat` compares against it for `treeStale` — and\n780\t\t\t\t// a settle that moved nothing would let the phone stamp a tree still\n781\t\t\t\t// showing this question as \"confirmed current\". `reconcile` yields ids\n782\t\t\t\t// rather than provenance, which is why the frame is built by reading each\n783\t\t\t\t// record back out of the store instead of from anything passed here.\n784\t\t\t\t// (SETTLE-CHOKE-POINT) No `push.cancelPending` here. `reconcile` settles\n785\t\t\t\t// these records through `settle()`, which retracts for every one of them\n786\t\t\t\t// — including the `stale` endings this list also carries. A second call\n787\t\t\t\t// here would be a second place to keep in step.\n788\t\t\t\tonQuestionsSettled: (questionIds) => {\n789\t\t\t\t\tfor (const questionId of questionIds) {\n790\t\t\t\t\t\tpublishSettledQuestion(questionId);\n791\t\t\t\t\t}\n792\t\t\t\t},\n793\t\t\t\t// (ANSWER-LEDGER) `hello` publishes the current epoch so a client's FIRST\n794\t\t\t\t// answer can be fenced; the read API never writes to the ledger.\n795\t\t\t\tledger,\n796\t\t\t});\n797\t\n798\t\t\tconst answerDeps = createAnswerDeps({\n799\t\t\t\tdb: options.db,\n800\t\t\t\thostDb,\n801\t\t\t\tliveness,\n802\t\t\t\tquestions,\n803\t\t\t\tleases,\n804\t\t\t\tlocks,\n805\t\t\t\tledger,\n806\t\t\t\tmessageAttempts,\n807\t\t\t\taudit,\n808\t\t\t\tagents: options.terminalAgentStore,\n809\t\t\t\tlogger,\n810\t\t\t\tbridgeStartedMs,\n811\t\t\t});\n812\t\t\t// Proves the acknowledged raw-writer marker HERE, at start, rather than on\n813\t\t\t// the first answer of the day. Without this call either the paste-framed or\n814\t\t\t// fire-and-forget writer could surface as a real answer failure long after\n815\t\t\t// every read path had been seen working.\n816\t\t\tassertAnswerDeps(answerDeps);\n817\t\t\tconst panic = createPanicHandler({ deviceStore, audit, events });\n818\t\n819\t\t\t// (CAPABILITY-WIRING-ASSERT) Boot-time proof that every capability the\n820\t\t\t// route table gates on is either granted or deliberately withheld. A token\n821\t\t\t// that is gated but ungranted 501s its route forever and the only symptom\n822\t\t\t// is a feature that never happens.\n823\t\t\tassertCapabilityWiring();\n824\t\n825\t\t\t// 3. Handlers. http.ts owns the route table, the pipeline and the\n826\t\t\t//    capability gate; this only binds each operation to its module.\n827\t\t\tconst handlers: SealedHandlers = {\n828\t\t\t\tping: readApi.handlePing,\n829\t\t\t\thello: readApi.handleHello,\n830\t\t\t\ttree: readApi.handleTree,\n831\t\t\t\ttranscript: readApi.handleTranscript,\n832\t\t\t\tquestion: readApi.handleQuestion,\n833\t\t\t\theartbeat: readApi.handleHeartbeat,\n834\t\t\t\tanswer: (ctx, body) => handleAnswer(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n835\t\t\t\tanswerStatus: (ctx, body) => handleAnswerStatus(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n836\t\t\t\tmessage: (ctx, body) => handleMessage(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n837\t\t\t\tregister: (ctx, body) =>\n838\t\t\t\t\thandleRegister(\n839\t\t\t\t\t\t{ devices: deviceStore, now: () => Date.now() },\n840\t\t\t\t\t\tctx,\n841\t\t\t\t\t\tbody,\n842\t\t\t\t\t),\n843\t\t\t\tpanic,\n844\t\t\t\teventsTicket: (ctx, body) => events.issueTicket(ctx, body),\n845\t\t\t};\n846\t\n847\t\t\t// 4. Listener. Binds 127.0.0.1:47610 exactly, or throws — never a fallback\n848\t\t\t//    port, because cloudflared's ingress rule is static and a\n849\t\t\t//    silently-moved bridge presents as \"phone says offline\".\n850\t\t\tconst http = createBridgeHttpServer({\n851\t\t\t\taccessValidator: createAccessValidator(),\n852\t\t\t\tdevices: deviceStore,\n853\t\t\t\tkeys: keyStore,\n854\t\t\t\tnonceCache,\n855\t\t\t\tsendNonce: sendNonces,\n856\t\t\t\thandlers,\n857\t\t\t\tevents,\n858\t\t\t\tfreeText: createClientClaimFreeTextPolicy(logger),\n859\t\t\t\tlogger,"}]},"uuid":"d923838c-a4f5-45ac-b1d6-00f6654d8f17","timestamp":"2026-08-10T22:43:32.992Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts","content":"\t\t\torganizationId: options.organizationId,\n\t\t\tversions: options.versions,\n\t\t\tbridgeStartedMs,\n\t\t\t// The real counter, from the only thing that advances it. A hardcoded 0\n\t\t\t// would make every `TreeResponse.gseq` claim \"consistent with zero\n\t\t\t// events\": the client latches 0 from the snapshot frame, the first live\n\t\t\t// frame then looks like a sequence gap, §9.3.3 says refetch the tree, and\n\t\t\t// the refetched tree reports 0 again — a refetch per event, forever, with\n\t\t\t// `treeStale` (`lastEventGseq < 0`) unsatisfiable and therefore unable to\n\t\t\t// catch it.\n\t\t\tcurrentGseq: () => events.currentGseq(),\n\t\t\t// (RECONCILE-RETRACT) `reconcile()` settles questions the hook never\n\t\t\t// reported. That is exactly the moment an armed or delivered push must be\n\t\t\t// withdrawn — on ARM64 a dead hook is a documented failure mode, and\n\t\t\t// without this the phone keeps a notification standing for a question\n\t\t\t// answered at the desk minutes ago.\n\t\t\t//\n\t\t\t// (TREE-FRESHNESS-GSEQ) It is also a change to the tree, so it mints an\n\t\t\t// event. `gseq` is the ONLY freshness signal on the wire — `/v1/tree`\n\t\t\t// stamps it and `/v1/heartbeat` compares against it for `treeStale` — and\n\t\t\t// a settle that moved nothing would let the phone stamp a tree still\n\t\t\t// showing this question as \"confirmed current\". `reconcile` yields ids\n\t\t\t// rather than provenance, which is why the frame is built by reading each\n\t\t\t// record back out of the store instead of from anything passed here.\n\t\t\t// (SETTLE-CHOKE-POINT) No `push.cancelPending` here. `reconcile` settles\n\t\t\t// these records through `settle()`, which retracts for every one of them\n\t\t\t// — including the `stale` endings this list also carries. A second call\n\t\t\t// here would be a second place to keep in step.\n\t\t\tonQuestionsSettled: (questionIds) => {\n\t\t\t\tfor (const questionId of questionIds) {\n\t\t\t\t\tpublishSettledQuestion(questionId);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t// (ANSWER-LEDGER) `hello` publishes the current epoch so a client's FIRST\n\t\t\t// answer can be fenced; the read API never writes to the ledger.\n\t\t\tledger,\n\t\t});\n\n\t\tconst answerDeps = createAnswerDeps({\n\t\t\tdb: options.db,\n\t\t\thostDb,\n\t\t\tliveness,\n\t\t\tquestions,\n\t\t\tleases,\n\t\t\tlocks,\n\t\t\tledger,\n\t\t\tmessageAttempts,\n\t\t\taudit,\n\t\t\tagents: options.terminalAgentStore,\n\t\t\tlogger,\n\t\t\tbridgeStartedMs,\n\t\t});\n\t\t// Proves the acknowledged raw-writer marker HERE, at start, rather than on\n\t\t// the first answer of the day. Without this call either the paste-framed or\n\t\t// fire-and-forget writer could surface as a real answer failure long after\n\t\t// every read path had been seen working.\n\t\tassertAnswerDeps(answerDeps);\n\t\tconst panic = createPanicHandler({ deviceStore, audit, events });\n\n\t\t// (CAPABILITY-WIRING-ASSERT) Boot-time proof that every capability the\n\t\t// route table gates on is either granted or deliberately withheld. A token\n\t\t// that is gated but ungranted 501s its route forever and the only symptom\n\t\t// is a feature that never happens.\n\t\tassertCapabilityWiring();\n\n\t\t// 3. Handlers. http.ts owns the route table, the pipeline and the\n\t\t//    capability gate; this only binds each operation to its module.\n\t\tconst handlers: SealedHandlers = {\n\t\t\tping: readApi.handlePing,\n\t\t\thello: readApi.handleHello,\n\t\t\ttree: readApi.handleTree,\n\t\t\ttranscript: readApi.handleTranscript,\n\t\t\tquestion: readApi.handleQuestion,\n\t\t\theartbeat: readApi.handleHeartbeat,\n\t\t\tanswer: (ctx, body) => handleAnswer(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n\t\t\tanswerStatus: (ctx, body) => handleAnswerStatus(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n\t\t\tmessage: (ctx, body) => handleMessage(answerDeps, ctx, body),\n\t\t\tregister: (ctx, body) =>\n\t\t\t\thandleRegister(\n\t\t\t\t\t{ devices: deviceStore, now: () => Date.now() },\n\t\t\t\t\tctx,\n\t\t\t\t\tbody,\n\t\t\t\t),\n\t\t\tpanic,\n\t\t\teventsTicket: (ctx, body) => events.issueTicket(ctx, body),\n\t\t};\n\n\t\t// 4. Listener. Binds 127.0.0.1:47610 exactly, or throws — never a fallback\n\t\t//    port, because cloudflared's ingress rule is static and a\n\t\t//    silently-moved bridge presents as \"phone says offline\".\n\t\tconst http = createBridgeHttpServer({\n\t\t\taccessValidator: createAccessValidator(),\n\t\t\tdevices: deviceStore,\n\t\t\tkeys: keyStore,\n\t\t\tnonceCache,\n\t\t\tsendNonce: sendNonces,\n\t\t\thandlers,\n\t\t\tevents,\n\t\t\tfreeText: createClientClaimFreeTextPolicy(logger),\n\t\t\tlogger,","numLines":100,"startLine":760,"totalLines":2653}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2306d4a5-fc17-4a0b-9a22-11aea896e181","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
