{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"d710da24-af25-4fcf-ab28-bdcd0488f7c2","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"manual","preTokens":202290,"postTokens":26893,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":4998451,"durationMs":307589,"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"154c444c-06b5-44e0-ae4d-f0013372057c","anchorUuid":"783f3da3-a2f5-43e1-85c4-d745f1ef1602","tailUuid":"d710da24-af25-4fcf-ab28-bdcd0488f7c2"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"783f3da3-a2f5-43e1-85c4-d745f1ef1602","uuids":["154c444c-06b5-44e0-ae4d-f0013372057c","208e8d89-db39-41ea-ad3a-5fbd879c2ec4","6d87d1a5-da5a-4116-9aec-3ae773c8187f","347a4313-62a2-4b47-8857-fa749e1dedc3","d710da24-af25-4fcf-ab28-bdcd0488f7c2"],"allUuids":["154c444c-06b5-44e0-ae4d-f0013372057c","6cae27ae-2e7b-431c-8c1b-2664cddc65b1","3fb82f47-d9db-4362-9950-54caff1e32d4","1be4460e-d479-4fa1-8b47-a8c8c897ab4c","208e8d89-db39-41ea-ad3a-5fbd879c2ec4","6d87d1a5-da5a-4116-9aec-3ae773c8187f","347a4313-62a2-4b47-8857-fa749e1dedc3","d710da24-af25-4fcf-ab28-bdcd0488f7c2"]}},"uuid":"abac061a-0b7d-43ad-9365-082f9a44f027","timestamp":"2026-08-12T01:48:19.905Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.226","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"abac061a-0b7d-43ad-9365-082f9a44f027","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c058ee1a-c275-4061-84af-fd980af01d80","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user’s governing companion-answer requirement is:\n\n   - Any captured, pending Claude question with a real terminal target must be answerable from a paired Android phone or Wear OS watch.\n   - It must still work when:\n     - the renderer is unavailable\n     - the display is off\n     - Windows is locked or at the login screen\n     - the transcript is missing, unreadable, rotated, or temporarily locked\n     - answer capability/session negotiation is absent or expired\n     - sidebar curation hides the thread\n     - mutable agent binding, permission axis, AskUser marker, screen state, or read-side liveness disagrees\n   - The production answer path must not refuse, veto, or downgrade an answer based on:\n     - transcript state or readability\n     - terminal screen/render state\n     - renderer availability\n     - Windows display/lock/login state\n     - mutable agent binding\n     - permission-axis state\n     - AskUser marker state\n     - read-side liveness\n     - negotiated companion answer capability/session state\n     - biometric/client claims\n     - post-write screen or transcript confirmation\n   - Pending questions must remain discoverable in:\n     - `/v1/tree`\n     - `/v1/question`\n     - heartbeat pending counts\n   - This discovery must survive missing capability negotiation and ordinary curation.\n   - Positive transcript settlement after a desk answer must remain.\n   - Protocol 0 must remain strictly read-only.\n\n   PTY honesty requirements:\n\n   - A write counts only after daemon-side `pty.write` acknowledgment.\n   - `confirmed` is returned only after:\n     1. every required acknowledged write succeeds\n     2. the durable ledger outcome is written\n     3. the durable ledger row is read back and matches\n   - If bytes may have landed but acknowledgment or durability is uncertain:\n     - return `unconfirmed`\n     - preserve the duplicate fence\n     - do not retry automatically\n   - Only a failure proving no bytes were written may be represented as zero-write/retryable.\n   - Detached protocol-v2 compatibility may queue the complete encoded answer in one legacy frame, but must never fabricate `confirmed`.\n\n   Boundaries that must remain:\n\n   - pairing and authenticated device identity\n   - Cloudflare Access validation\n   - sealed AES-GCM request and response transport\n   - nonce replay protection\n   - API schema validation\n   - semantic answer-shape validation\n   - exact current question ID and fingerprint check at the final synchronous point before writing\n   - answer-wide lease\n   - per-terminal lock\n   - durable request claim/idempotency/fencing\n   - real daemon and PTY failures\n   - honest zero-write and partial/unknown-write outcomes\n   - positive transcript settlement\n   - protocol-0 no-write invariant\n\n   Operational requirements:\n\n   - Work directly on `main`.\n   - Never force-push.\n   - Merge remote differences without losing functionality.\n   - Ship only through the full GitHub Windows ARM64 build/release workflow.\n   - Never hot-patch the installed application.\n   - Installation must happen only after explicit user authorization at that exact time because it closes Superset and the active session.\n   - Run `/simplify` fully before committing, pushing, or reporting completion.\n   - Run `/code-review low` on every committed change batch.\n   - Use `tmp/` for scratch files.\n   - No answer UX barrier may be introduced without explicit user approval.\n   - Security constraint, preserved verbatim:\n     - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - Never touch the production database unless explicitly requested and separately confirmed.\n\n   Most recent explicit direction:\n\n   - The user said: “use opus sub agents to continue”.\n   - Opus was then used to finish the cleanup and validation.\n   - The user explicitly selected:\n     - “Install now (Recommended)”\n   - The installer was downloaded, digest-verified, and launched detached.\n   - Installation completion and post-install E2E have not yet been verified.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   - Windows ARM64 Superset fork\n   - Bun/Turbo TypeScript monorepo\n   - Host-service companion bridge\n   - Android phone and Wear OS companion clients\n   - Cloudflare Tunnel and Cloudflare Access\n   - authenticated device pairing\n   - HKDF-derived directional keys\n   - AES-256-GCM sealed envelopes\n   - protocol/method/path/status/nonce AAD binding\n   - nonce replay protection\n   - semantic answer intents\n   - Claude picker byte encoding\n   - answer-wide leases\n   - per-terminal critical-section locks\n   - durable SQLite request claims\n   - idempotency and duplicate fencing\n   - host.db as source of truth\n   - PTY daemon protocol negotiation\n   - protocol-v3 correlated `input` / `input-ok`\n   - protocol-v2 detached daemon compatibility\n   - definite `not_written` versus ambiguous `unknown`\n   - detached PTY daemon adoption after host-service restart\n   - exact current-question/fingerprint arbitration\n   - durable result write/readback\n   - positive-only transcript reconciliation\n   - cache-first transcript stat identity\n   - pending-question curation escape\n   - tree/heartbeat parity\n   - scoped Biome validation\n   - TypeScript diagnostics\n   - `(REFERR-GATE)` cannot-find-name diagnostics\n   - full GitHub Windows ARM64 packaging/publish workflow\n   - NSIS installer\n   - Opus implementation subagents\n   - `/code-review low`\n   - Fable/Sol adversarial review history\n   - `/simplify` four-angle review:\n     - reuse\n     - simplification\n     - efficiency\n     - altitude\n\n   Proven Claude Code `2.1.226` byte contracts:\n\n   - Single-select:\n     - digit selects and submits in the proven shape.\n   - Free text in multi-question prompts:\n     - supported with proven per-question byte sequences.\n   - Multi-select within `N > 1`:\n     - toggle digits\n     - then `\\x1b[C`\n     - no `\\r` inside the multi-select group\n   - Multi-select free text:\n     - refused because live CLI proof showed the wrong option could be committed.\n   - Empty multi-select:\n     - refused because Claude silently omits the question from the result.\n   - Protocol-v2 fallback:\n     - sends the complete encoded sequence in one ordered frame\n     - returns durable `unconfirmed`\n     - preserves the fence\n     - never truncates after the first keystroke\n     - never reports false `confirmed`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   A. Central answer path\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts`\n\n   Importance:\n\n   - Owns `/v1/answer`, `/v1/answer/status`, and `/v1/message`.\n   - The answer route is now fully guardless.\n   - The message route still deliberately protects against typing a submit byte into an open picker.\n\n   Shipped answer sequence:\n\n   1. claim request durably\n   2. validate current pending question and fingerprint\n   3. semantically encode the answer\n   4. prepare/adopt PTY session outside lease and lock\n   5. acquire answer lease\n   6. acquire terminal lock\n   7. recheck exact current question/fingerprint\n   8. inject bytes\n   9. write durable outcome\n   10. read durable outcome back\n   11. return honest result\n\n   Final current-question wrapper:\n\n   ```ts\n   function requireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(\n     deps: AnswerDeps,\n     request: Pick<AnswerRequest, \"questionId\" | \"fingerprint\">,\n   ): PendingQuestion {\n     const question = requirePendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request);\n     if (\n       deps.questions.byHostTerminal(question.hostTerminalId)?.questionId !==\n       question.questionId\n     ) {\n       throw sealed(\n         410,\n         \"stale_question\",\n         \"the captured question changed before the terminal write; nothing was written\",\n       );\n     }\n     return question;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Critical placement:\n\n   ```ts\n   requireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request);\n   return injectSequence(deps, {\n     question,\n     host,\n     keystrokes,\n     leaseId: lease.leaseId,\n     acknowledgedInputSupported: prepared.acknowledgedInputSupported,\n     writer,\n   });\n   ```\n\n   Injection result:\n\n   ```ts\n   type InjectionResult =\n     | { kind: \"confirmed\" }\n     | {\n         kind: \"unconfirmed\";\n         reason: string;\n         abortedAt: number;\n         written: number;\n         writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n       };\n   ```\n\n   Simplified frame construction:\n\n   ```ts\n   const frames = acknowledgedInputSupported\n     ? keystrokes.map((keystroke, index) => ({\n         data: keystroke.data,\n         acknowledgedKeystrokes: 1,\n         abortAt: index,\n       }))\n     : keystrokes.length === 0\n       ? []\n       : [\n           {\n             data: keystrokes.map((keystroke) => keystroke.data).join(\"\"),\n             acknowledgedKeystrokes: keystrokes.length,\n             abortAt: keystrokes.length,\n           },\n         ];\n   ```\n\n   This lets protocol-v3 per-keystroke frames and protocol-v2 complete-sequence fallback share the same:\n\n   - deadline\n   - lease extension\n   - write call\n   - error logging\n   - abort handling\n\n   Durable outcome helper:\n\n   ```ts\n   async function recordOutcome(\n     deps: AnswerDeps,\n     record: AnswerAttemptRecord,\n   ): Promise<boolean> {\n     try {\n       if (record.status === \"in_flight\") return true;\n       deps.ledger.recordOutcome({\n         requestId: record.requestId,\n         status: record.status,\n         resolvedAtMs: record.resolvedAtMs,\n         failureCode: record.failureCode,\n         guardsPassed: record.guardsPassed,\n         leaseId: record.leaseId,\n       });\n       const durable = deps.ledger.get(record.requestId);\n       if (durable?.status !== record.status) {\n         throw new Error(\n           `ledger outcome verification read ${durable?.status ?? \"missing\"}, expected ${record.status}`,\n         );\n       }\n       return true;\n     } catch (error) {\n       deps.log({\n         event: \"companion.answer.attempt_persist_failed\",\n         requestId: record.requestId,\n         questionId: record.questionId,\n         status: record.status,\n         error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n       });\n       return false;\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Non-vetoing audit helper:\n\n   ```ts\n   async function appendAnswerAudit(\n     deps: AnswerDeps,\n     entry: AuditEntry,\n   ): Promise<void> {\n     try {\n       await deps.audit.append(entry);\n     } catch (error) {\n       deps.log({\n         event: \"companion.answer.audit_persist_failed\",\n         requestId: entry.requestId,\n         questionId: entry.questionId,\n         terminalId: entry.terminalId,\n         outcome: entry.outcome,\n         error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n       });\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n   `/simplify` cleanup in `7e0d25f3c`:\n\n   - Removed:\n     - `GUARD_CLASSES`\n     - `ABSTAINING_GUARDS`\n     - `LOAD_BEARING_GUARDS`\n     - `GUARD_EVALUATION_ORDER`\n     - `assertGuardClassification`\n     - `evaluateGuards`\n     - `mergeAttemptEvidence`\n     - answer-only guard source readers\n     - answer-only `matchPickerScreen`\n     - picker geometry/display-width machinery\n     - obsolete guard-specific comments and imports\n   - Preserved for `/v1/message`:\n     - `screenShowsPickerChrome`\n     - prompt-anchor matching\n     - `safeSnapshot`\n     - `awaitComposerEcho`\n     - `readPermissionAxis`\n     - `assertNoPickerOnScreen`\n     - mutable agent binding\n     - session liveness\n   - Persisted guard fields remain only for schema compatibility.\n   - Answer attempts use empty guard arrays and null evaluation.\n\n   Live minimal prompt matcher:\n\n   ```ts\n   type PromptMatchReason =\n     | \"match\"\n     | \"empty_screen\"\n     | \"anchor_absent\"\n     | \"anchor_too_weak\";\n\n   interface PromptScreenMatch {\n     ok: boolean;\n     reason: PromptMatchReason;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   B. Raw writer contract\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\keystrokes.ts`\n\n   Contract:\n\n   ```ts\n   export interface RawWriteTarget {\n     terminalId: string;\n     workspaceId: string;\n   }\n\n   export interface RawWriteInput extends RawWriteTarget {\n     data: string;\n   }\n\n   export type RawPrepareResult =\n     | { success: true; acknowledgedInputSupported: boolean }\n     | { error: string };\n\n   export type RawWriteResult =\n     | { success: true }\n     | {\n         error: string;\n         writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n       };\n   ```\n\n   Cleanup:\n\n   - Reused `AcknowledgedInputFailureKind` from the daemon client instead of repeating:\n     - `\"not_written\" | \"unknown\"`\n   - Retained branded raw-writer construction to prevent accidental use of:\n     - bracketed paste\n     - unvalidated fire-and-forget input\n\n   Deliberately skipped during `/simplify`:\n\n   - `Keystroke.expect` and `ScreenExpectation` are now write-only after guard removal, but removing them would ripple through encoding tests beyond the active cleanup.\n   - `provenMultiSelectFreeTextDetectLabels()` and related measured data are orphaned but retained because they are recorded CLI proof data guarded by feature markers.\n\n   C. Daemon client\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\DaemonClient\\DaemonClient.ts`\n\n   Core types:\n\n   ```ts\n   export type AcknowledgedInputFailureKind = \"not_written\" | \"unknown\";\n\n   export class AcknowledgedInputError extends Error {\n     readonly writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind;\n\n     constructor(\n       message: string,\n       writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind,\n     ) {\n       super(message);\n       this.name = \"AcknowledgedInputError\";\n       this.writeOutcome = writeOutcome;\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - Handshake advertises:\n     ```ts\n     protocols: [...SUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS]\n     ```\n   - Protocol v3:\n     - correlated request ID\n     - waits for `input-ok`\n     - correlated daemon error means `not_written`\n     - timeout/disconnect after queueing means `unknown`\n   - Protocol v2:\n     - queues supplied legacy frame\n     - returns/throws `unknown`\n     - answer injector supplies the entire encoded sequence in that frame\n\n   Risky `/simplify` finding deliberately skipped:\n\n   - `requestInput`, `requestSession`, and `requestNonSession` duplicate reply/timer/listener scaffolding.\n   - A generic helper was not introduced because that code owns timing-sensitive `not_written` versus `unknown` semantics.\n\n   D. Terminal preparation and writers\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts`\n\n   Preparation:\n\n   ```ts\n   export async function prepareAcknowledgedInputSession({\n     terminalId,\n     workspaceId,\n     db,\n   }): Promise<\n     | { success: true; acknowledgedInputSupported: boolean }\n     | { error: string }\n   >\n   ```\n\n   Acknowledged write:\n\n   ```ts\n   export async function writeAcknowledgedInputToSession({\n     terminalId,\n     workspaceId,\n     data,\n   }): Promise<\n     | { success: true }\n     | { error: string; writeOutcome: AcknowledgedInputFailureKind }\n   >\n   ```\n\n   Shared session precondition helper was added during `/simplify`.\n\n   Important Opus correction:\n\n   - Initial extraction changed the acknowledged-write missing-session error from:\n     - `\"Terminal session not prepared\"`\n   - to:\n     - `\"Terminal session not found\"`\n   - Opus restored the original externally visible distinction with an `absentError` parameter.\n   - It also removed a redundant map lookup after `getOrAdoptSession`, which already returns the checked session.\n\n   E. Composition root\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts`\n\n   Raw writer wiring:\n\n   ```ts\n   const writeInput = Object.assign(\n     (input: RawWriteInput) => writeAcknowledgedInputToSession(input),\n     {\n       writerKind: RAW_PTY_WRITER_KIND,\n       prepare: (input: RawWriteTarget) =>\n         prepareAcknowledgedInputSession({ ...input, db: deps.db }),\n     },\n   );\n   ```\n\n   Cleanup:\n\n   - Removed dead answer-only adapters:\n     - `toolResultExists`\n     - `askqMarkerExists`\n     - marker owner-key helper\n     - marker path validation helper\n     - associated filesystem imports\n   - Preserved message-path adapters:\n     - `agentBinding`\n     - `sessionActive`\n     - `permissionAxisLatched`\n     - `snapshotScreen`\n   - Updated comments to state these are `/v1/message` protections, not answer eligibility guards.\n\n   F. PTY daemon protocol\n\n   Full paths:\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\protocol\\version.ts`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\Server\\Server.ts`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\package.json`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\bun.lock`\n\n   Version contract:\n\n   ```ts\n   export const CURRENT_PROTOCOL_VERSION = 3 as const;\n   export const SUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS: readonly number[] = [3, 2];\n   ```\n\n   Package version:\n\n   ```json\n   \"version\": \"0.4.0\"\n   ```\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - v3 supports correlated daemon-side input acknowledgment.\n   - v2 stays available for ordinary terminal operations and controlled complete-sequence fallback.\n   - v2 rejects request-ID acknowledged input with `EPROTO`.\n\n   G. Daemon supervisor\n\n   Full paths:\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\daemon\\DaemonSupervisor.ts`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\daemon\\DaemonSupervisor.test.ts`\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - probes `[3, 2]`\n   - can identify protocol-v2 daemon package version\n   - marks old daemon `updatePending`\n   - proves v2 is still adoptable\n   - proves v2 companion input is queued but returns `unknown`\n\n   H. Question reconciliation\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts`\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - Positive transcript `tool_result` settles a desk answer.\n   - `unreadable` is never cached as a terminal verdict.\n   - Reconciliation settles through the store after async reads, preserving current provenance and preventing resurrection.\n\n   Relevant call:\n\n   ```ts\n   store.resolve(\n     question.questionId,\n     { deviceLabel: null, surface: \"desktop\" },\n     nowMs,\n   );\n   ```\n\n   Cleanup:\n\n   - Removed stale commentary tying `agentId` to retired AskUser marker guard.\n   - Clarified that `agentId` is still validated at capture but is currently unread by production answer logic.\n\n   Risky `/simplify` findings deliberately skipped:\n\n   - incremental transcript scanning\n   - parallel per-question transcript reads\n   - changing tail-window/rotation/partial-line semantics\n   - multiplying concurrent 8 MiB allocations\n\n   I. Discovery and curation\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\read-api.ts`\n\n   Shared predicate:\n\n   ```ts\n   function terminalPiercesCuration(\n     visibleWorkspaces: ReadonlyMap<string, HostWorkspaceRow>,\n     workspaceId: string,\n     pending: PendingQuestion | null,\n   ): boolean {\n     return visibleWorkspaces.has(workspaceId) || pending !== null;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - A pending question pierces normal workspace/project curation.\n   - Tree and heartbeat use the same predicate.\n   - Pending question detail does not require answer capability negotiation.\n   - A redundant workspace-empty guard was removed.\n\n   Opus fixed a partial-cleanup type error:\n\n   - The helper had initially been typed as `ReadonlySet<string>`.\n   - The real source is a `Map<string, HostWorkspaceRow>`.\n   - It was corrected to `ReadonlyMap<string, HostWorkspaceRow>`.\n\n   Altitude redesign deliberately skipped:\n\n   - Folding pending admission into the original visible-workspace source could change curation provenance and hidden-count semantics.\n\n   J. Protocol boundary\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\http.ts`\n\n   Behavior:\n\n   - `/v1/answer`, `/v1/answer/status`, `/v1/question`, `/v1/tree`, heartbeat, hello, and panic are not capability-gated at route policy.\n   - Protocol path is validated against the opened request protocol:\n     ```ts\n     requireProtocolPath(path, opened.protocolVersion);\n     ```\n   - Protocol 0 permits only hello/tree/heartbeat.\n   - Protocol 0 still blocks answer and panic writes.\n   - `confirmedBiometric` is optional and ignored, but malformed supplied values remain invalid.\n\n   K. Wire and persistence types\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\types.ts`\n\n   Cleanup:\n\n   - Preserved runtime guard-name values needed for persisted ledger compatibility and live `/v1/message` `GuardFailedDetail`.\n   - Corrected comments that had incorrectly described all guard names as legacy-read-only.\n   - Made `guardsPassed`, `guardsAbstained`, and audit documentation honest now that answer evaluation no longer occurs.\n\n   Deliberately skipped:\n\n   - Unifying all `guardsAbstained` output sites from mixed `null`/`[]` because that would change persisted audit content.\n\n   L. Tests\n\n   Full paths:\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\picker-chrome.test.ts`\n   - deleted:\n     - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\guard-abstain.test.ts`\n     - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\picker-screen.test.ts`\n   - scratch:\n     - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\answer-guardless-probe.test.ts`\n\n   `answer-guardless.test.ts` proves:\n\n   - valid answer without obsolete biometric claim\n   - malformed supplied biometric still rejected by schema\n   - direct confirmed writes without transcript/screen/session/binding/permission/marker consultation\n   - whole-sequence protocol-v2 fallback\n   - thrown write becomes `unknown`\n   - definite zero-write `not_written`\n   - partial write outcome\n   - replay contract coverage restored from deleted historical test\n\n   `picker-chrome.test.ts` was newly created because `screenShowsPickerChrome` remained live and previously had no focused coverage. Its 14 tests cover:\n\n   - live picker detection\n   - unbounded gaps\n   - digit-decoy continuation lines\n   - box-drawing prefixes\n   - descending rows\n   - mid-line numbers\n   - multi-digit markers\n   - single-row non-picker cases\n\n   `guard-abstain.test.ts` was deleted because the answer guard evaluator no longer exists. Its still-live replay tests were moved into `answer-guardless.test.ts`.\n\n   `picker-screen.test.ts` was deleted because it tested only removed `matchPickerScreen`; it never exercised live `/v1/message` behavior.\n\n   Scratch fault probe covers:\n\n   - confirmed\n   - duplicate replay fencing\n   - definite zero-write retry\n   - ambiguous first write\n   - partial write\n   - supersede under lock\n   - confirmed ledger failure\n   - both outcome writes failing\n   - audit failure\n   - preparation failure and fresh retry\n   - supersede during preparation\n\n   M. Feature manifest\n\n   Full path:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\FEATURES.md`\n\n   `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS)` records:\n\n   - answer discovery without capability/session\n   - curation escape\n   - no transcript/screen/renderer/login/session/binding/permission/marker/liveness/capability veto\n   - display-off and locked-screen intent\n   - daemon acknowledgment\n   - durable outcome semantics\n   - protocol-v2 whole-sequence unconfirmed fencing\n\n   Feature marker validation reported:\n\n   - `147/147`\n\n   N. Persistent memory\n\n   Full paths:\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md`\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\MEMORY.md`\n\n   Updated to record:\n\n   - final guardless contract\n   - commits `ec83cf8e4` and `7e0d25f3c`\n   - build `31443284669`\n   - installer still awaiting verification\n   - post-install E2E list\n   - sensitive logging prohibition\n\n   O. Published installer\n\n   Download location:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\guardless-install\\Superset-1.20.0-arm64.exe`\n\n   GitHub release:\n\n   - tag: `desktop-v1.20.0`\n   - asset: `Superset-1.20.0-arm64.exe`\n   - size: `484127502`\n   - release URL:\n     `https://github.com/khairm/superset-windows-arm64/releases/tag/desktop-v1.20.0`\n\n   Verified digest:\n\n   ```text\n   sha256:a42f6715ee58849fbb018f262a6a8a7d14b3906ca451c9b910d7d7af792a96e3\n   ```\n\n   Detached launch output:\n\n   ```text\n   verified sha256 a42f6715ee58849fbb018f262a6a8a7d14b3906ca451c9b910d7d7af792a96e3\n   installer launched pid 1704515\n   ```\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - Original user-visible refusal:\n     - “The desktop refused: the question wasn’t safely on screen”\n     - Root cause was production answer guard evaluation.\n     - Fixed by removing every production answer guard.\n\n   - Fire-and-forget PTY enqueue was treated as success:\n     - Fixed with protocol-v3 correlated `input-ok` after daemon-side `pty.write`.\n\n   - `confirmed` could be returned before durable verification:\n     - Fixed with ledger write followed by ledger readback.\n\n   - Audit failure could veto or replace a real write outcome:\n     - Fixed with non-vetoing `appendAnswerAudit`.\n\n   - Transient transcript unreadability was cached:\n     - Fixed by never caching `unreadable`.\n\n   - `/v1/question` and pending discovery could be hidden by capability or curation:\n     - Fixed by capability-null question detail and curation escape.\n\n   - Heartbeat and tree counts disagreed:\n     - Fixed with shared pending-question curation predicate.\n\n   - Protocol-0 sessionless path bypass:\n     - Fixed by validating against `opened.protocolVersion`.\n\n   - Ignored biometric claim remained schema-required:\n     - Made optional, while malformed supplied values remain invalid.\n\n   - First-write timeout/disconnect was misreported as definite zero-write:\n     - Added `not_written | unknown`.\n     - Ambiguous first write now yields durable fenced `unconfirmed`.\n\n   - Detached