{"parentUuid":"304b2bd9-40d1-4904-818b-53ffc0abd50d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_0fa07188e851bb5c016a7c55d729b0819193d1a7a0b4e39f8b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":120320,"output_tokens":57,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_sUGQQtxlK6Kk36uCz9fXvRWh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts","offset":1000,"limit":260}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"attributionSkill":"windows-computer-use","type":"assistant","uuid":"aed68a9b-e38b-4537-92bd-6cd071cb2a8a","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:15:38.212Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"aed68a9b-e38b-4537-92bd-6cd071cb2a8a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44611460-2829-462e-b2e9-af8e653be0db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_sUGQQtxlK6Kk36uCz9fXvRWh","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1001\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1002\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1003\t\t\t\tpayloadHash,\n1004\t\t\t\t// (ANSWER-GUARDLESS) No guard stack runs, so no audit line can claim a\n1005\t\t\t\t// guard evaluation. The default is `null` — \"never asked\" — and the sites\n1006\t\t\t\t// that write `[]` do so because the record type they feed cannot express\n1007\t\t\t\t// the difference. `[]` is never a claim that a guard abstained.\n1008\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: null as AnswerGuardName[] | null,\n1009\t\t\t};\n1010\t\n1011\t\t\t/**\n1012\t\t\t * The identity every attempt record for this request carries, spread into the\n1013\t\t\t * six outcome records below exactly as `baseAudit` is spread into the audit\n1014\t\t\t * lines.\n1015\t\t\t *\n1016\t\t\t * ONLY the identity. `status`, `resolvedAtMs`, `failureCode` and\n1017\t\t\t * `guardsPassed` stay written out at each site on purpose: the difference\n1018\t\t\t * between `confirmed`, `failed`, `unconfirmed` and `in_flight` is the whole\n1019\t\t\t * point of §11.5, and a default for any of them here would let a new outcome\n1020\t\t\t * inherit another outcome's honesty by omission.\n1021\t\t\t */\n1022\t\t\tconst baseAttempt = {\n1023\t\t\t\trequestId: request.requestId,\n1024\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1025\t\t\t\tdeviceId: ctx.device.deviceId,\n1026\t\t\t\tsurface: request.surface,\n1027\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1028\t\t\t\tstartedAtMs,\n1029\t\t\t};\n1030\t\n1031\t\t\t// 11. Audit BEFORE execution (§14). Inside the try, so a failure to write the\n1032\t\t\t//     audit line still releases the lease — and still refuses the answer,\n1033\t\t\t//     because an unauditable write is not one we are willing to perform.\n1034\t\t\ttry {\n1035\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1036\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1037\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: startedAtMs,\n1038\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1039\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: null,\n1040\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"attempted\",\n1041\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1042\t\t\t\t});\n1043\t\n1044\t\t\t\t// (ANSWER-LEDGER) There is no `in_flight` write here any more, and its absence\n1045\t\t\t\t// is the fix rather than an omission.\n1046\t\t\t\t//\n1047\t\t\t\t// This block used to build an `in_flight` record and durably write it just\n1048\t\t\t\t// before taking the lock, with a long comment explaining that the ~15 s of\n1049\t\t\t\t// lock-wait-plus-sequence was a window in which the client's recovery read\n1050\t\t\t\t// answered \"the desktop never saw this request\". Writing it HERE only narrowed\n1051\t\t\t\t// that window; it could not close it, because everything above this line —\n1052\t\t\t\t// preflight, the agent-kind check, the writer probe, the lease — still ran\n1053\t\t\t\t// before the record existed.\n1054\t\t\t\t//\n1055\t\t\t\t// The claim now happens at the very top of `handleAnswer`, as an atomic\n1056\t\t\t\t// compare-and-set, so by the time control reaches here the requestId has been\n1057\t\t\t\t// occupied for the whole of that work and a status read can only ever report\n1058\t\t\t\t// `in_flight`. The unwritable-store branch is gone with it: a claim that cannot\n1059\t\t\t\t// be persisted throws out of `claimForAnswer` before any of this runs, which is\n1060\t\t\t\t// the same refusal one step earlier and without a record to take back out.\n1061\t\n1062\t\t\t\tconst result = await deps.locks.runExclusive(\n1063\t\t\t\t\tquestion.terminalId,\n1064\t\t\t\t\tLOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS,\n1065\t\t\t\t\t() => {\n1066\t\t\t\t\t\t// The preflight happened before audit I/O and lock acquisition. Re-check\n1067\t\t\t\t\t\t// the store at the last synchronous point before the first PTY write so a\n1068\t\t\t\t\t\t// desk answer or superseding capture cannot turn this answer into composer\n1069\t\t\t\t\t\t// text or an answer to the replacement picker. This is question identity,\n1070\t\t\t\t\t\t// not screen/transcript/session evidence.\n1071\t\t\t\t\t\trequireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request);\n1072\t\t\t\t\t\treturn injectSequence(deps, {\n1073\t\t\t\t\t\t\tquestion,\n1074\t\t\t\t\t\t\thost,\n1075\t\t\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokes,\n1076\t\t\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1077\t\t\t\t\t\t\tacknowledgedInputSupported: prepared.acknowledgedInputSupported,\n1078\t\t\t\t\t\t\twriter,\n1079\t\t\t\t\t\t});\n1080\t\t\t\t\t},\n1081\t\t\t\t);\n1082\t\n1083\t\t\t\tif (result.kind === \"confirmed\") {\n1084\t\t\t\t\tconst resolvedAtMs = deps.now();\n1085\t\t\t\t\tconst recorded = deps.questions.resolve(\n1086\t\t\t\t\t\trequest.questionId,\n1087\t\t\t\t\t\t{ deviceLabel: ctx.device.label, surface: request.surface },\n1088\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs,\n1089\t\t\t\t\t);\n1090\t\t\t\t\tif (!recorded) {\n1091\t\t\t\t\t\t// The record left `pending` while the sequence ran — the hook\n1092\t\t\t\t\t\t// superseded or settled it. The keystrokes still landed and the audit\n1093\t\t\t\t\t\t// entry below still carries the true provenance; what we must NOT do\n1094\t\t\t\t\t\t// is stamp this device onto a record it did not resolve.\n1095\t\t\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1096\t\t\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.resolve_skipped\",\n1097\t\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1098\t\t\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1099\t\t\t\t\t\t\tstate: question.state,\n1100\t\t\t\t\t\t});\n1101\t\t\t\t\t}\n1102\t\t\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n1103\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n1104\t\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"confirmed\",\n1105\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs,\n1106\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1107\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n1108\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1109\t\t\t\t\t};\n1110\t\t\t\t\tif (!(await recordOutcome(deps, record))) {\n1111\t\t\t\t\t\tconst unconfirmed: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n1112\t\t\t\t\t\t\t...record,\n1113\t\t\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"unconfirmed\",\n1114\t\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n1115\t\t\t\t\t\t};\n1116\t\t\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1117\t\t\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.confirmed_downgraded_not_durable\",\n1118\t\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1119\t\t\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1120\t\t\t\t\t\t\trequestId: request.requestId,\n1121\t\t\t\t\t\t});\n1122\t\t\t\t\t\t// A transient first failure may still allow this downgrade to commit. If\n1123\t\t\t\t\t\t// it does not, the original durable in-flight claim remains the fence.\n1124\t\t\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, unconfirmed);\n1125\t\t\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1126\t\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1127\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: resolvedAtMs,\n1128\t\t\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1129\t\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1130\t\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"unconfirmed\",\n1131\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1132\t\t\t\t\t\t});\n1133\t\t\t\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(unconfirmed);\n1134\t\t\t\t\t}\n1135\t\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1136\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1137\t\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: resolvedAtMs,\n1138\t\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1139\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1140\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"confirmed\",\n1141\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1142\t\t\t\t\t});\n1143\t\t\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(record);\n1144\t\t\t\t}\n1145\t\n1146\t\t\t\tif (result.written === 0 && result.writeOutcome === \"not_written\") {\n1147\t\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1148\t\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.write_failed_before_input\",\n1149\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1150\t\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1151\t\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1152\t\t\t\t\t\treason: result.reason,\n1153\t\t\t\t\t});\n1154\t\t\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n1155\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n1156\t\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"failed\",\n1157\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n1158\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n1159\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n1160\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1161\t\t\t\t\t};\n1162\t\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, record);\n1163\t\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1164\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1165\t\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: deps.now(),\n1166\t\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1167\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1168\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"failed\",\n1169\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n1170\t\t\t\t\t});\n1171\t\t\t\t\tthrow sealed(\n1172\t\t\t\t\t\t503,\n1173\t\t\t\t\t\t\"internal\",\n1174\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the terminal accepted no answer input; nothing was written — submit a new request to retry\",\n1175\t\t\t\t\t);\n1176\t\t\t\t}\n1177\t\n1178\t\t\t\tdeps.questions.markStale(\n1179\t\t\t\t\trequest.questionId,\n1180\t\t\t\t\tresult.writeOutcome === \"unknown\"\n1181\t\t\t\t\t\t? `write outcome unknown after ${result.written}/${keystrokes.length} acknowledged keystrokes: ${result.reason}`\n1182\t\t\t\t\t\t: `partial write: ${result.written}/${keystrokes.length} keystrokes landed, then ${result.reason}`,\n1183\t\t\t\t);\n1184\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1185\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.unconfirmed\",\n1186\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1187\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1188\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1189\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokesWritten: result.written,\n1190\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokesTotal: keystrokes.length,\n1191\t\t\t\t\tabortedAt: result.abortedAt,\n1192\t\t\t\t\twriteOutcome: result.writeOutcome,\n1193\t\t\t\t\treason: result.reason,\n1194\t\t\t\t});\n1195\t\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n1196\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n1197\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"unconfirmed\",\n1198\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n1199\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1200\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n1201\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1202\t\t\t\t};\n1203\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, record);\n1204\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1205\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1206\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: deps.now(),\n1207\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1208\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1209\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"unconfirmed\",\n1210\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n1211\t\t\t\t});\n1212\t\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(record);\n1213\t\t\t} catch (error) {\n1214\t\t\t\tif (error instanceof SealedError) throw error;\n1215\t\n1216\t\t\t\t// The lock was never taken, so the critical section never ran and nothing\n1217\t\t\t\t// was written. Reported honestly; the client MUST NOT retry a write.\n1218\t\t\t\tif (error instanceof TerminalLockTimeoutError) {\n1219\t\t\t\t\t// LEDGER FIRST, AUDIT SECOND, and the order is load-bearing rather than\n1220\t\t\t\t\t// stylistic. `audit.append` does I/O and can throw; when it went first, a\n1221\t\t\t\t\t// failed audit write skipped the ledger advance entirely and left the\n1222\t\t\t\t\t// claim `in_flight` — \"keystrokes are landing right now\" for a request\n1223\t\t\t\t\t// whose lock was never even taken. `recordOutcome` swallows its own\n1224\t\t\t\t\t// failures, so putting it first cannot cost the audit entry, while the\n1225\t\t\t\t\t// reverse order costs the ledger. The branch below already had this order;\n1226\t\t\t\t\t// this one did not.\n1227\t\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, {\n1228\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n1229\t\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"failed\",\n1230\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n1231\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n1232\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n1233\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n1234\t\t\t\t\t});\n1235\t\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n1236\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n1237\t\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: deps.now(),\n1238\t\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n1239\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: null,\n1240\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"failed\",\n1241\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n1242\t\t\t\t\t});\n1243\t\t\t\t\tthrow sealed(\n1244\t\t\t\t\t\t503,\n1245\t\t\t\t\t\t\"internal\",\n1246\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the terminal was busy; nothing was written\",\n1247\t\t\t\t\t);\n1248\t\t\t\t}\n1249\t\t\t\t// (ANSWER-INFLIGHT) An unexpected throw from inside the critical section.\n1250\t\t\t\t// The `in_flight` record MUST NOT be left behind — the client would poll it\n1251\t\t\t\t// forever — and it must not be downgraded to \"never sent\" either, because\n1252\t\t\t\t// bytes may already have landed. Unknown outcome, stated as such.\n1253\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n1254\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.internal_error\",\n1255\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n1256\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n1257\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n1258\t\t\t\t\terror: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n1259\t\t\t\t});"}]},"uuid":"849e039f-0e63-4575-b1b0-8a9a098517f7","timestamp":"2026-08-12T11:15:38.600Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts","content":"\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n\t\t\tpayloadHash,\n\t\t\t// (ANSWER-GUARDLESS) No guard stack runs, so no audit line can claim a\n\t\t\t// guard evaluation. The default is `null` — \"never asked\" — and the sites\n\t\t\t// that write `[]` do so because the record type they feed cannot express\n\t\t\t// the difference. `[]` is never a claim that a guard abstained.\n\t\t\tguardsAbstained: null as AnswerGuardName[] | null,\n\t\t};\n\n\t\t/**\n\t\t * The identity every attempt record for this request carries, spread into the\n\t\t * six outcome records below exactly as `baseAudit` is spread into the audit\n\t\t * lines.\n\t\t *\n\t\t * ONLY the identity. `status`, `resolvedAtMs`, `failureCode` and\n\t\t * `guardsPassed` stay written out at each site on purpose: the difference\n\t\t * between `confirmed`, `failed`, `unconfirmed` and `in_flight` is the whole\n\t\t * point of §11.5, and a default for any of them here would let a new outcome\n\t\t * inherit another outcome's honesty by omission.\n\t\t */\n\t\tconst baseAttempt = {\n\t\t\trequestId: request.requestId,\n\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\tdeviceId: ctx.device.deviceId,\n\t\t\tsurface: request.surface,\n\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n\t\t\tstartedAtMs,\n\t\t};\n\n\t\t// 11. Audit BEFORE execution (§14). Inside the try, so a failure to write the\n\t\t//     audit line still releases the lease — and still refuses the answer,\n\t\t//     because an unauditable write is not one we are willing to perform.\n\t\ttry {\n\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n\t\t\t\ttsMs: startedAtMs,\n\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: null,\n\t\t\t\toutcome: \"attempted\",\n\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t});\n\n\t\t\t// (ANSWER-LEDGER) There is no `in_flight` write here any more, and its absence\n\t\t\t// is the fix rather than an omission.\n\t\t\t//\n\t\t\t// This block used to build an `in_flight` record and durably write it just\n\t\t\t// before taking the lock, with a long comment explaining that the ~15 s of\n\t\t\t// lock-wait-plus-sequence was a window in which the client's recovery read\n\t\t\t// answered \"the desktop never saw this request\". Writing it HERE only narrowed\n\t\t\t// that window; it could not close it, because everything above this line —\n\t\t\t// preflight, the agent-kind check, the writer probe, the lease — still ran\n\t\t\t// before the record existed.\n\t\t\t//\n\t\t\t// The claim now happens at the very top of `handleAnswer`, as an atomic\n\t\t\t// compare-and-set, so by the time control reaches here the requestId has been\n\t\t\t// occupied for the whole of that work and a status read can only ever report\n\t\t\t// `in_flight`. The unwritable-store branch is gone with it: a claim that cannot\n\t\t\t// be persisted throws out of `claimForAnswer` before any of this runs, which is\n\t\t\t// the same refusal one step earlier and without a record to take back out.\n\n\t\t\tconst result = await deps.locks.runExclusive(\n\t\t\t\tquestion.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\tLOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS,\n\t\t\t\t() => {\n\t\t\t\t\t// The preflight happened before audit I/O and lock acquisition. Re-check\n\t\t\t\t\t// the store at the last synchronous point before the first PTY write so a\n\t\t\t\t\t// desk answer or superseding capture cannot turn this answer into composer\n\t\t\t\t\t// text or an answer to the replacement picker. This is question identity,\n\t\t\t\t\t// not screen/transcript/session evidence.\n\t\t\t\t\trequireCurrentPendingAnswerQuestion(deps, request);\n\t\t\t\t\treturn injectSequence(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tquestion,\n\t\t\t\t\t\thost,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tkeystrokes,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tacknowledgedInputSupported: prepared.acknowledgedInputSupported,\n\t\t\t\t\t\twriter,\n\t\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t);\n\n\t\t\tif (result.kind === \"confirmed\") {\n\t\t\t\tconst resolvedAtMs = deps.now();\n\t\t\t\tconst recorded = deps.questions.resolve(\n\t\t\t\t\trequest.questionId,\n\t\t\t\t\t{ deviceLabel: ctx.device.label, surface: request.surface },\n\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs,\n\t\t\t\t);\n\t\t\t\tif (!recorded) {\n\t\t\t\t\t// The record left `pending` while the sequence ran — the hook\n\t\t\t\t\t// superseded or settled it. The keystrokes still landed and the audit\n\t\t\t\t\t// entry below still carries the true provenance; what we must NOT do\n\t\t\t\t\t// is stamp this device onto a record it did not resolve.\n\t\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n\t\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.resolve_skipped\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstate: question.state,\n\t\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"confirmed\",\n\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs,\n\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\t};\n\t\t\t\tif (!(await recordOutcome(deps, record))) {\n\t\t\t\t\tconst unconfirmed: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t...record,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n\t\t\t\t\t};\n\t\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n\t\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.confirmed_downgraded_not_durable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\t\t\trequestId: request.requestId,\n\t\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\t\t// A transient first failure may still allow this downgrade to commit. If\n\t\t\t\t\t// it does not, the original durable in-flight claim remains the fence.\n\t\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, unconfirmed);\n\t\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n\t\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: resolvedAtMs,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(unconfirmed);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: resolvedAtMs,\n\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"confirmed\",\n\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(record);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif (result.written === 0 && result.writeOutcome === \"not_written\") {\n\t\t\t\tdeps.log({\n\t\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.write_failed_before_input\",\n\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n\t\t\t\t\treason: result.reason,\n\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n\t\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n\t\t\t\t\tstatus: \"failed\",\n\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\t};\n\t\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, record);\n\t\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n\t\t\t\t\ttsMs: deps.now(),\n\t\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n\t\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"failed\",\n\t\t\t\t\tfailureCode: \"internal\",\n\t\t\t\t});\n\t\t\t\tthrow sealed(\n\t\t\t\t\t503,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"internal\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"the terminal accepted no answer input; nothing was written — submit a new request to retry\",\n\t\t\t\t);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tdeps.questions.markStale(\n\t\t\t\trequest.questionId,\n\t\t\t\tresult.writeOutcome === \"unknown\"\n\t\t\t\t\t? `write outcome unknown after ${result.written}/${keystrokes.length} acknowledged keystrokes: ${result.reason}`\n\t\t\t\t\t: `partial write: ${result.written}/${keystrokes.length} keystrokes landed, then ${result.reason}`,\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t\tdeps.log({\n\t\t\t\tevent: \"companion.answer.unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\tquestionId: request.questionId,\n\t\t\t\tterminalId: question.terminalId,\n\t\t\t\tleaseId: lease.leaseId,\n\t\t\t\tkeystrokesWritten: result.written,\n\t\t\t\tkeystrokesTotal: keystrokes.length,\n\t\t\t\tabortedAt: result.abortedAt,\n\t\t\t\twriteOutcome: result.writeOutcome,\n\t\t\t\treason: result.reason,\n\t\t\t});\n\t\t\tconst record: AnswerAttemptRecord = {\n\t\t\t\t...baseAttempt,\n\t\t\t\tstatus: \"unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs: null,\n\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t\tguardsPassed: [],\n\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t\tawait recordOutcome(deps, record);\n\t\t\tawait appendAnswerAudit(deps, {\n\t\t\t\t...baseAudit,\n\t\t\t\ttsMs: deps.now(),\n\t\t\t\tguards: null,\n\t\t\t\tguardsAbstained: [],\n\t\t\t\toutcome: \"unconfirmed\",\n\t\t\t\tfailureCode: null,\n\t\t\t});\n\t\t\treturn recordToResponse(record);\n\t\t} catch (error) {\n\t\t\tif (error instanceof SealedError) throw error;\n\n\t\t\t// The lock was never taken, so the critical section never ran and nothing\n\t\t\t// was written. Reported honestly; the client MUST NOT retry a write.\n\t\t\tif (error instanceof TerminalLockTimeoutError) {\n\t\t\t\t// LEDGER FIRST, AUDIT SECOND, and the order is load-bearing rather than\n\t\t\t\t// stylistic. `audit.append` does I/O and can throw; when it went first, a\n\t\t\t\t// failed audit write skipped the ledger advance entirely and left the\n\t\t\t\t// claim `in_flight` — \"keystrokes are landing right now\" for a request\n\t\t\t\t// whose lock was never even taken. `recordOutcome` swallo