{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T12:49:04.246Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af863f56092c9b4f1</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\af863f56092c9b4f1.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review simplification opportunities\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Simplification review of the current companion settlement/repaint diff:\n\n1. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/question-store.ts:562` — combine paired remote-answer fields**\n   - **Summary:** `remoteAnswerBy` and `remoteAnsweredAtMs` are one logical fact represented as two independently mutable nullable fields.\n   - **Cost:** Every capture, resolve, race handler, and test must update/check both fields, while invalid half-populated states remain representable.\n   - **Simpler form:** Replace both with:\n     ```ts\n     remoteAnswer: {\n       resolvedBy: ResolvedBy;\n       deliveredAtMs: number;\n     } | null;\n     ```\n     Then `resolve()` reads one value atomically.\n\n2. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/attempt-ledger.ts:744` — avoid array-plus-loop for one fence**\n   - **Summary:** `findQuestionFence()` calls `.all()`, loops, and returns on the first iteration.\n   - **Cost:** The implementation suggests multiple rows are meaningfully processed when only one validated fence is needed.\n   - **Simpler form:** Apply `limit(1)`/single-row retrieval, validate that row, and return it directly.\n\n3. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/answer-guardless.test.ts:130` — oversized hand-built store stub**\n   - **Summary:** `answerHarness()` manually reimplements `QuestionStore` settlement/provenance behavior.\n   - **Cost:** The test harness duplicates production mutation logic and must stay synchronized with `createQuestionStore`; the new race test can pass while the real store differs.\n   - **Simpler form:** Construct the real `createQuestionStore()` with deterministic dependencies, or extract a shared focused test fixture, leaving only writer/ledger/repaint adapters mocked.\n\n4. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/answer-guardless.test.ts:305` — redundant race flag**\n   - **Summary:** `settled` duplicates the observable `question.state = \"resolved\"` mutation.\n   - **Cost:** Extra state and assertion add noise without proving anything beyond the final question-state/provenance assertions.\n   - **Simpler form:** Remove `settled` and `expect(settled).toBe(true)`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>179002</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
