{"parentUuid":"d811fafd-3cbd-4a2a-8203-e58e05b8fa58","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44611460-2829-462e-b2e9-af8e653be0db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_pZjfk2UoBVekbcFM8S4oUA5l","type":"tool_result","content":"  1440\t * malformed capture and that throw propagates to the hook route, which is a\n  1441\t * loud 500 in the notify hook's log. The dot work already happened by then, so\n  1442\t * the agent-status broadcast is unaffected.\n  1443\t */\n  1444\tfunction createNotifyingCaptureSink(\n  1445\t\tdeps: NotifyingSinkDeps,\n  1446\t): QuestionCaptureSink {\n  1447\t\treturn {\n  1448\t\t\tcapture(input) {\n  1449\t\t\t\tdeps.inner.capture(input);\n  1450\t\t\t\tconst question = deps.questions.byHostTerminal(input.hostTerminalId);\n  1451\t\t\t\tif (question === null) {\n  1452\t\t\t\t\t// Captured and immediately superseded inside the same tick. Nothing to\n  1453\t\t\t\t\t// arm — but say so, because a silent miss here is a question that\n  1454\t\t\t\t\t// never buzzes.\n  1455\t\t\t\t\tdeps.logger.warn(\n  1456\t\t\t\t\t\t\"captured question was not pending immediately after capture; push not armed\",\n  1457\t\t\t\t\t\t{ hostTerminalId: input.hostTerminalId },\n  1458\t\t\t\t\t);\n  1459\t\t\t\t\treturn;\n  1460\t\t\t\t}\n  1461\t\t\t\tarmPush(deps, question);\n  1462\t\t\t\tpublishPendingQuestion(deps, question);\n  1463\t\t\t},\n  1464\t\n  1465\t\t\tresolve(input) {\n  1466\t\t\t\tconst before = deps.questions.byHostTerminal(input.hostTerminalId);\n  1467\t\t\t\tdeps.inner.resolve(input);\n  1468\t\t\t\tif (before === null || before.toolUseId !== input.toolUseId) return;\n  1469\t\t\t\tif (before.state !== \"resolved\") return;\n  1470\t\n  1471\t\t\t\t// `QuestionStore.resolve` writes both fields BEFORE it settles the\n  1472\t\t\t\t// record, so `state === \"resolved\"` means both are set. The type system\n  1473\t\t\t\t// cannot see that, and the old `??` fallbacks papered over it — they read\n  1474\t\t\t\t// as a reachable \"resolved but we do not know by whom\" case, which does\n  1475\t\t\t\t// not exist. Assert the invariant instead of inventing a provenance.\n  1476\t\t\t\tconst { resolvedAtMs, resolvedBy } = before;\n  1477\t\t\t\tif (resolvedAtMs === null || resolvedBy === null) {\n  1478\t\t\t\t\tthrow new Error(\n  1479\t\t\t\t\t\t`${LOG_PREFIX} question ${before.questionId} is resolved but carries no resolvedAtMs/resolvedBy — refusing to publish a question.resolved frame with a fabricated provenance`,\n  1480\t\t\t\t\t);\n  1481\t\t\t\t}\n  1482\t\n  1483\t\t\t\t// §13.3 is handled by `(SETTLE-CHOKE-POINT)`: `inner.resolve` above\n  1484\t\t\t\t// settled this record, and `settle()` retracted the notification on the\n  1485\t\t\t\t// way out. This wrapper is left with the one effect that genuinely\n  1486\t\t\t\t// belongs to the DESK route — the frame naming who answered.\n  1487\t\t\t\tdeps.events.publish({\n  1488\t\t\t\t\tt: \"question.resolved\",\n  1489\t\t\t\t\td: {\n  1490\t\t\t\t\t\tquestionId: before.questionId,\n  1491\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedAtMs,\n  1492\t\t\t\t\t\tresolvedBy,\n  1493\t\t\t\t\t\toutcome: \"answered\",\n  1494\t\t\t\t\t},\n  1495\t\t\t\t});\n  1496\t\t\t},\n  1497\t\t};\n  1498\t}\n  1499\t\n  1500\t/**\n  1501\t * (PUSH-CURATION-GATE) Is this question's thread one the user has taken OFF\n  1502\t * their sidebar?\n  1503\t *\n  1504\t * `/v1/tree` has consumed the sidebar mirror since `(BRIDGE-SIDEBAR-FILTER)`\n  1505\t * shipped, but the push path never did, because arming does not go through the\n  1506\t * read API — it hangs off the capture sink. The result was the loudest possible\n  1507\t * disagreement between two surfaces of the same feature: a binned, archived,\n  1508\t * completed or snoozed thread would buzz the user's WATCH, and tapping the\n  1509\t * notification would open a tree that does not contain it. Snooze is the worst\n  1510\t * of the four, because \"not now\" is precisely a statement about being\n  1940\t\t\t\t\t}\n  1941\t\t\t\t}\n  1942\t\t\t\tout.sort((a, b) => a.askedAtMs - b.askedAtMs);\n  1943\t\t\t\treturn out;\n  1944\t\t\t},\n  1945\t\n  1946\t\t\tresolve(questionId, resolvedBy, atMs) {\n  1947\t\t\t\tconst question = byId.get(questionId);\n  1948\t\t\t\tif (question === undefined) {\n  1949\t\t\t\t\tthrow new Error(`companion: resolve on unknown question ${questionId}`);\n  1950\t\t\t\t}\n  1951\t\t\t\tif (question.state === \"resolved\") return false;\n  1952\t\t\t\t// `markStale` already refuses to move a non-pending record; `resolve` has\n  1953\t\t\t\t// to match, or the two disagree about whether `stale` is terminal. It is:\n  1954\t\t\t\t// `settle()` has already removed a stale record from\n  1955\t\t\t\t// `pendingByHostTerminal`, and re-labelling it `resolved` with a device's\n  1956\t\t\t\t// provenance records an answer that device never gave.\n  1957\t\t\t\tif (question.state !== \"pending\") return false;\n  1958\t\t\t\tquestion.resolvedAtMs = question.remoteAnswer?.deliveredAtMs ?? atMs;\n  1959\t\t\t\tquestion.resolvedBy = question.remoteAnswer?.resolvedBy ?? resolvedBy;\n  1960\t\t\t\tsettle(question, \"resolved\");\n  1961\t\t\t\treturn true;\n  1962\t\t\t},\n  1963\t\n  1964\t\t\tmarkRemoteAnswered(questionId, resolvedBy, deliveredAtMs) {\n  1965\t\t\t\tconst question = byId.get(questionId);\n  1966\t\t\t\tif (question === undefined) return false;\n  1967\t\t\t\tif (question.state === \"stale\") return false;\n  1968\t\t\t\tquestion.remoteAnswer = { resolvedBy, deliveredAtMs };\n  1969\t\t\t\tif (question.state === \"resolved\") {\n  1970\t\t\t\t\tquestion.resolvedBy = resolvedBy;\n  1971\t\t\t\t\tquestion.resolvedAtMs = deliveredAtMs;\n  1972\t\t\t\t}\n  1973\t\t\t\treturn true;\n  1974\t\t\t},\n  1975\t\n  1976\t\t\tmarkStale(questionId, reason) {\n  1977\t\t\t\tconst question = byId.get(questionId);\n  1978\t\t\t\tif (question === undefined) {\n  1979\t\t\t\t\tthrow new Error(\n  1980\t\t\t\t\t\t`companion: markStale on unknown question ${questionId}`,\n  1981\t\t\t\t\t);\n  1982\t\t\t\t}\n  1983\t\t\t\tif (question.state !== \"pending\") return;\n  1984\t\t\t\t// LOGGED, not stored. The reason was a write-only field on the record;\n  1985\t\t\t\t// the caller's diagnostic is worth keeping, the dead field is not.\n  1986\t\t\t\tconsole.info(\"[companion-bridge] question marked stale\", {\n  1987\t\t\t\t\tquestionId,\n  1988\t\t\t\t\treason,\n  1989\t\t\t\t});\n  1990\t\t\t\tsettle(question, \"stale\");","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"213d70c8-e3f1-4cc8-af82-339e2823f2b1","timestamp":"2026-08-12T13:24:48.704Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  1440\t * malformed capture and that throw propagates to the hook route, which is a\n  1441\t * loud 500 in the notify hook's log. The dot work already happened by then, so\n  1442\t * the agent-status broadcast is unaffected.\n  1443\t */\n  1444\tfunction createNotifyingCaptureSink(\n  1445\t\tdeps: NotifyingSinkDeps,\n  1446\t): QuestionCaptureSink {\n  1447\t\treturn {\n  1448\t\t\tcapture(input) {\n  1449\t\t\t\tdeps.inner.capture(input);\n  1450\t\t\t\tconst question = deps.questions.byHostTerminal(input.hostTerminalId);\n  1451\t\t\t\tif (question === null) {\n  1452\t\t\t\t\t// Captured and immediately superseded inside the same tick. Nothing to\n  1453\t\t\t\t\t// arm — but say so, because a silent miss here is a question that\n  1454\t\t\t\t\t// never buzzes.\n  1455\t\t\t\t\tdeps.logger.warn(\n  1456\t\t\t\t\t\t\"captured question was not pending immediately after capture; push not armed\",\n  1457\t\t\t\t\t\t{ hostTerminalId: input.hostTerminalId },\n  1458\t\t\t\t\t);\n  1459\t\t\t\t\treturn;\n  1460\t\t\t\t}\n  1461\t\t\t\tarmPush(deps, question);\n  1462\t\t\t\tpublishPendingQuestion(deps, question);\n  1463\t\t\t},\n  1464\t\n  1465\t\t\tresolve(input) {\n  1466\t\t\t\tconst before = deps.questions.byHostTerminal(input.hostTerminalId);\n  1467\t\t\t\tdeps.inner.resolve(input);\n  1468\t\t\t\tif (before === null || before.toolUseId !== input.toolUseId) retu