uestion.resolved\", d:{questionId, resolvedAtMs, resolvedBy, outcome}})`, differing only in provenance source and outcome.\nCost: ~27 lines where ~12 would do; any frame-shape change is a 3-site edit. Fix = `publishQuestionResolved(events, {questionId, resolvedAtMs, resolvedBy, outcome})`.\n\n**3. Publish-containment pattern not reused → 11 lines of try/catch pushed to the caller**\n`answer.ts:1177-1193` vs `index.ts:716-746`.\n`publishSettledQuestion` already establishes the house rule (\"Never throws into the caller: a frame nobody can currently receive must not break…\") by wrapping publish in try/catch + log. `markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish` does not, so `answer.ts` had to hand-roll its own try/catch + `companion.answer.remote_provenance_failed` log around the dep call.\nCost: 11 added lines in the hot answer path, and containment placed at the call site so any future caller must remember it. Fix = contain inside `markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish` (semantics identical — the answer.ts catch already swallows everything).\n\n**4. Dep name collides with a still-reachable store method**\n`answer.ts:240` (`questions: QuestionStore`) + `answer.ts:246` (new `markRemoteAnswered(...)`).\n`deps.questions.markRemoteAnswered(...)` still exists on the same deps object with the same name and near-identical signature, but skips the publish. `answer-guardless.test.ts:262` already wires the raw store method into the new slot, so that suite never exercises publishing.\nCost: two same-named APIs one property apart, one silently skipping the corrective frame. Fix = name the dep `markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish`, matching the impl (2 call sites, no behaviour change).\n\n**5. Duplicate `LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES` membership test, both via unchecked casts**\n`attempt-ledger.ts:134-138` (new) and `attempt-ledger.ts:549-551` (read boundary).\n`(LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES as readonly SealedErrorCode[]).includes(code)` vs `(LEDGER_FAILURE_CODES as readonly string[]).includes(row.failureCode)` — same test, two