obvious win.\n\n**2. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts:398` — throwaway registry allocated to restore a method.**\n`harness.deps.locks.runExclusive = createTerminalLockRegistry().runExclusive;` builds a whole second registry (Map + closures) and discards everything but one method. Cheaper: capture `const realRunExclusive = locks.runExclusive;` at `answer-guardless.test.ts:253` before the override and expose it on the harness. Also removes the oddity that the retry then serializes on a *different* queue than the harness's registry.\n\n## Checked, not findings\n- `index.ts:1451` `questions.get` followed by `markRemoteAnswered`'s internal `byId.get` — two `Map.get`s, negligible.\n- `isLedgerFailureCode` linear `.includes` over 8 codes — dwarfed by the SQLite query it accompanies.\n- `index.ts:2028` closure capturing `deps` — one per bridge, already-live object, no retention added.\n- `await recordOutcome` → `await appendAnswerAudit` sequencing: `recordOutcome` has no internal awaits and resolves synchronously, so parallelising buys nothing.\n- New `answer-settlement-events.test.ts`: one store/sink per test, no repeated I/O.\n\n## Aside (outside my angle, flagging as free)\nInterface at `answer.ts:246` declares `markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish` and call site `answer.ts:1177` uses it, but `index.ts:2028` supplies the key as `markRemoteAnswered:`, and `answer-guardless.test.ts:262` also uses `markRemoteAnswered`. Type mismatch / runtime `undefined is not a function` unless a concurrent agent is mid-edit.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>77736</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>18</tool_uses><duration_ms>174420</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
