{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T13:59:02.767Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a808bc36142fe0c64</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a808bc36142fe0c64.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Race fix efficiency review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Efficiency review only.\n\n1. `packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:1518` — remote provenance correction performs two question-store lookups.\n   - **Summary:** `markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish()` calls `questions.get(questionId)` to capture `wasResolved`, then `questions.markRemoteAnswered(...)`, which performs another `byId.get(questionId)`.\n   - **Cost:** Every confirmed remote answer performs duplicate map lookup/state inspection, and the publication decision is split across two reads.\n   - **Cheaper form:** Have `markRemoteAnswered()` return a discriminated result such as `{ updated: boolean; wasResolved: boolean }`, allowing one lookup/mutation to determine whether the corrective frame is needed.\n\nNo other efficiency findings.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>59591</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T13:59:43.104Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3b2b4b39949a71bb</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_e1hzWAIC7F4YpSh5CABOrLvl</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a3b2b4b39949a71bb.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Race fix simplification review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Simplification review of `tmp/race-simplify-working.diff`:\n\n1. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts:markRemoteAnsweredAndPublish` — avoid duplicated state lookup**\n   - **Summary:** The helper reads the question with `get()`, then immediately looks it up again through `markRemoteAnswered()`.\n   - **Cost:** Two map lookups and split reasoning about one state transition make the settlement race harder to maintain.\n   - **Simpler form:** Have `QuestionStore.markRemoteAnswered()` return a discriminated result such as `{ updated: boolean; wasResolved: boolean }`, then publish based on that single operation.  \n   - **Recommendation:** Skip in this batch because changing the store contract ripples beyond the race-fix diff and could alter settlement behavior.\n\n2. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/answer-guardless.test.ts:190-260` — lock override adds mutable fixture plumbing**\n   - **Summary:** The harness creates a real lock registry and then replaces `runExclusive`; the test later replaces it again to retry.\n   - **Cost:** Mutable method swapping obscures fixture state and makes future lock-registry refactors harder.\n   - **Simpler form:** Accept a complete `locks` dependency in the harness options, defaulting to `createTerminalLockRegistry()`, and construct a fresh production registry for the retry.\n   - **Recommendation:** Safe cleanup, but minor.\n\nNo other simplification findings. The resolved-event helper and durable failure-code mapper appropriately centralize duplicated behavior.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>55170</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
