{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-12T14:00:35.517Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a23c7e13ac6cfd007</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_MePFmoNZQnwuLSws1SoXoTCV</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\a23c7e13ac6cfd007.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Race fix altitude review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Reviewed the race-fix diff for implementation altitude only.\n\nNo findings. The changes are placed at the appropriate mechanisms:\n\n- Zero-write classification derives from the durable ledger state, rather than adding another answer-path heuristic.\n- Failure-code normalization sits at the ledger persistence boundary.\n- Resolution-frame publication is centralized, with late remote provenance handled through the same event primitive.\n- Repaint and settlement remain non-vetoing and separate from write eligibility.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>3</tool_uses><duration_ms>80289</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
