{"parentUuid":"6b617ff1-3da3-4935-b79c-6deb1ab031fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Verify installed desktop build","description":"Confirmed installed Superset 1.20.0 from executable and uninstall metadata, running app process tree, visible nonblank renderer, and digest-verified installer/build mapping to the final shipped build. Packaged metadata does not independently expose the commit SHA.","activeForm":"Verifying installed desktop build","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Inspect companion runtime","description":"Confirmed installed host-service and PTY daemon are running from app.asar; daemon v0.4.0 manifest advertises protocol v3. Current restart logs contain no answer attempts or guard failures yet. Detected installed Claude CLI 2.1.228 versus byte contract proven on 2.1.226, requiring live answer E2E.","activeForm":"Inspecting companion runtime","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Run closed-loop emulator E2E","description":"Completed live post-restart companion E2E on Claude CLI 2.1.228. A real physical-phone free-text request was durably confirmed in 5 ms with null failure and empty guards; a separate safe emulator single-select request also durably confirmed with protocol-v3 daemon active. The scratch status parser expected the old response shape, but ledger proof confirmed success.","activeForm":"Running closed-loop emulator E2E","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Test availability boundaries","description":"Verified renderer-visible/nonblank post-restart state and proved live phone free-text bytes reached protocol-v3 PTY and durable ledger with no guards. A genuine display-off/Windows-lock test is not currently executable: Windows automation cannot cross the lock screen and no phone/watch is connected via ADB. This limitation is reported explicitly rather than treating headless architecture as E2E proof.","activeForm":"Testing availability boundaries","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Eliminate emulator identity interference","description":"Distinct emulator pairing remains blocked on installing the newly built desktop. Pairing secret logging is fixed and pushed; complete after the build is installed with separate exact-time approval, then pair a distinct emulator identity through the real QR flow.","activeForm":"Eliminating emulator identity interference","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Remove secret-bearing pairing log","description":"Removed secret-bearing QR URI from production pairing logs; only non-secret pairingRef and expiry are logged. Simplify completed, full companion tests/markers/REFERR/Biome passed, two low code reviews found nothing, and commits were pushed to main.","activeForm":"Removing secret-bearing pairing log","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Prove PTY consumption failure","description":"Incident proven end-to-end from safe metadata: the phone answer targeted the exact Claude session/picker; matching AskUser tool_result appeared 341 ms after phone intake. The answer did work, but the visible terminal failed to repaint, leaving a stale picker frame. Root cause is premature QuestionStore resolve/retract at 5 ms PTY acknowledgment plus no non-vetoing repaint nudge. Fix should preserve confirmed semantics, defer question settlement to positive PostToolUse/tool_result, and nudge repaint best-effort without becoming a barrier.","activeForm":"Proving PTY consumption failure","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"8","subject":"Fix stale picker settlement","description":"Implemented and pushed stale-picker fix: confirmed PTY writes retain pending discovery until exact positive PostToolUse/tool_result settlement, remote provenance survives races, repaint is best-effort/non-vetoing, and durable claimed→in_flight arbitration prevents fresh request retyping. Real SQLite and full companion tests pass.","activeForm":"Fixing stale picker settlement","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Validate real SQLite fence","description":"Added real SQLite fence coverage and fixed issues it exposed: nullable questionId narrowing and claimed-status mapping. Tests prove confirmed/in-flight/unconfirmed fence across DB/ledger recreation, same request ID is excluded, and failed does not fence. 3/3 pass; scoped Biome clean.","activeForm":"Validating real SQLite fence","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"10","subject":"Fix review race defects","description":"Fixes committed as 692ce7dae and pushed to main. /simplify complete; /code-review low returned no findings; 219/219 companion tests, scoped Biome, REFERR gate, and 147/147 marker gate green. Full ARM64 publish build 31604538404 is running; complete after build result.","activeForm":"Fixing review race defects","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":10},"type":"attachment","uuid":"76a0790e-82a7-4276-87ba-2353a9fb2b49","timestamp":"2026-08-12T14:07:20.770Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
