{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:30:11.749Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"pacing-proof\">\nCurrent trial set complete; no more added. Root cause proven on real Claude Code 2.1.228: protocol-v3 daemon ACK is only synchronous pty.write acceptance, not picker-state consumption. Exact N=4 frames [digit,digit,digit,digit,CR] burst failed 2/2 (all writes returned ~1ms; picker remained incomplete; no tool_result). Fixed gaps 100/250/500/1000ms each passed their current single runs with exact AskUserQuestion tool_result containing all 4 intended answers; 100ms is edge and screen snapshots show frames sometimes sent before previous transition visibly rendered, so it is not a conservative shipping value. Transition-observed pacing passed 2/2 with observed ~750–820ms gaps. Recommend deterministic 500ms between every daemon-acknowledged v3 frame (not screen/transcript/renderer gated), preserving v2 whole-sequence unconfirmed fallback. T3 Code has no applicable pacing: it answers AskUserQuestion atomically through Claude Agent SDK Deferred/updatedInput rather than PTY; its PTY writes are fire-and-forget and unserialized. No production files changed; repo remains clean.\n</agent-message>"}
