{"parentUuid":"d2171f7b-501f-4105-91bd-e543cbfb6daf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5548f27b-2b1d-4e0e-84da-bd27822c3dc9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user’s governing companion-answer requirement remains:\n\n   - Any captured pending Claude question with a real terminal target must be answerable from the paired Android phone or Wear OS watch.\n   - It must work when:\n     - the renderer is unavailable\n     - the display is off\n     - Windows is locked or at the login screen\n     - the transcript is missing, unreadable, rotated, or locked\n     - answer capability/session negotiation is missing or stale\n     - normal sidebar curation hides the thread\n     - mutable binding, permission, AskUser marker, screen state, or read-side liveness disagrees\n   - The production answer path must not refuse or veto an answer based on those conditions.\n   - Pending questions must stay discoverable through `/v1/tree`, `/v1/question`, and heartbeat counts.\n   - Protocol 0 remains strictly read-only.\n   - Pairing, authenticated identity, Cloudflare Access, AES-GCM sealed transport, nonce replay protection, schema validation, semantic answer-shape validation, exact question/fingerprint arbitration, leases, terminal locks, durable request fencing, and real PTY failures remain enforced.\n\n   PTY honesty requirements remain:\n\n   - A write counts only after daemon-side `pty.write` acknowledgment.\n   - `confirmed` requires every required acknowledged write plus durable outcome write/readback.\n   - Ambiguous writes remain `unconfirmed`, fenced, and are never automatically retried.\n   - Definite zero-write failures remain retryable.\n   - Protocol-v2 may queue the complete sequence in one legacy frame but must never fabricate `confirmed`.\n\n   Operational requirements:\n\n   - Work directly on `main`.\n   - Never force-push.\n   - Merge current `origin/main` first.\n   - Ship only through the full Windows ARM64 GitHub workflow.\n   - Never hot-patch the installed app.\n   - Run `/simplify` fully before committing, pushing, or reporting production work complete.\n   - Run `/code-review low` for each committed batch.\n   - Installation requires explicit authorization at the exact time because it closes Superset and the active session.\n   - Use `tmp/` for scratch files.\n   - Do not introduce answer UX barriers without explicit approval.\n   - Security constraint, verbatim:\n     - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - Never touch the production database unless explicitly requested and separately confirmed.\n\n   Newest explicit investigation request:\n\n   - The user reported an untouched four-question picker where all four answers were submitted on the phone but only the first answer visibly reached Claude.\n   - The user supplied a screenshot showing the picker advanced to question 2 while questions 2–4 remained unanswered.\n   - The user requested the root cause from the live state and logs.\n   - The user also requested:\n     - “Send an opus agent to explore the t3 code public repository to see how they interact with terminals, etc. I don't know if there's anything useful there.”\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   - Windows ARM64 Electron/Superset fork\n   - Bun/Turbo TypeScript monorepo\n   - Host-service companion bridge\n   - Android and Wear OS companion clients\n   - Cloudflare Tunnel and Cloudflare Access\n   - AES-256-GCM sealed request/response envelopes\n   - HKDF directional keys\n   - nonce replay protection\n   - semantic answer intents\n   - Claude AskUserQuestion picker byte encoding\n   - multi-question picker state transitions\n   - PTY daemon protocol v3 `input` / `input-ok`\n   - protocol-v2 whole-sequence compatibility\n   - difference between OS/PTY acceptance and application/TUI consumption\n   - durable SQLite answer ledger\n   - `claimed → in_flight → confirmed|failed|unconfirmed`\n   - answer-wide leases\n   - per-terminal locks\n   - durable duplicate fences\n   - positive PostToolUse and transcript `tool_result` settlement\n   - remote answer provenance races\n   - renderer repaint via temporary PTY resize\n   - pairing QR single-use secret handling\n   - deterministic inter-frame pacing\n   - real Claude Code 2.1.228 PTY canaries\n   - FCM capability/session negotiation\n   - isolated emulator identities\n   - Drizzle ORM with SQLite\n   - scoped Biome, feature-marker gate, and REFERR gate\n   - full GitHub Windows ARM64 publish workflow\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   A. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts`\n\n   Importance:\n\n   - Owns the production `/v1/answer` flow.\n   - Performs durable request claim, question arbitration, lease/lock acquisition, PTY injection, durable outcome recording, provenance marking, and repaint nudge.\n   - The current multi-frame race is in `injectSequence`.\n\n   Existing guardless frame construction:\n\n   ```ts\n   const frames = acknowledgedInputSupported\n     ? keystrokes.map((keystroke, index) => ({\n         data: keystroke.data,\n         acknowledgedKeystrokes: 1,\n         abortAt: index,\n       }))\n     : keystrokes.length === 0\n       ? []\n       : [\n           {\n             data: keystrokes.map((keystroke) => keystroke.data).join(\"\"),\n             acknowledgedKeystrokes: keystrokes.length,\n             abortAt: keystrokes.length,\n           },\n         ];\n   ```\n\n   Existing protocol-v3 write loop:\n\n   ```ts\n   for (let frameIndex = 0; frameIndex < frames.length; frameIndex += 1) {\n     const frame = frames[frameIndex];\n     // deadline and lease checks\n     const result = await writer.write({\n       terminalId: host.hostTerminalId,\n       workspaceId: host.hostWorkspaceId,\n       data: frame.data,\n     });\n     // error handling\n     written += frame.acknowledgedKeystrokes;\n   }\n\n   return { kind: \"confirmed\" };\n   ```\n\n   Critical defect:\n\n   - There is no delay or application-consumption barrier after `input-ok`.\n   - `input-ok` proves only synchronous `pty.write()` acceptance.\n   - For a four-question sequence, all frames can be queued before Claude’s Ink/React TUI advances from one question to the next.\n\n   Latest proven incident:\n\n   - Phone supplied four valid `select` answers.\n   - Encoder produced five correct frames:\n     1. question 1 selection digit\n     2. question 2 selection digit\n     3. question 3 selection digit\n     4. question 4 selection digit\n     5. review-screen carriage return\n   - All five were acknowledged and durably marked confirmed in 82 ms.\n   - The untouched picker advanced only from question 1 to question 2.\n   - No matching AskUser `tool_result` followed.\n\n   Required next production change:\n\n   - Insert a deterministic 500 ms delay between acknowledged protocol-v3 frames, excluding after the final frame.\n   - The delay must:\n     - remain inside the terminal lock\n     - preserve sequence deadline checks\n     - preserve lease extension\n     - not read screen, transcript, renderer, lock state, or liveness\n     - never become a veto or guard\n     - leave protocol-v2 whole-sequence `unconfirmed` behavior unchanged\n\n   B. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\handlers\\handlers.ts`\n\n   Relevant behavior:\n\n   - Protocol-v3 handler calls `session.pty.write(...)`.\n   - It emits `input-ok` immediately after that synchronous call returns.\n   - This proves the bytes entered the PTY but not that Claude processed them or changed picker state.\n   - This distinction is the root of the latest N=4 failure.\n\n   C. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\keystrokes.ts`\n\n   Important encoding contracts:\n\n   - Single question select:\n     - `[digit]`\n   - N-question all-select:\n     - `[digit × N, \"\\r\"]`\n   - One-question free text:\n     - `[digit N+1, body, \"\\r\"]`\n   - N-question free text:\n     - per-question digit or `[digit N+1, body, \"\\r\"]`, then final review return\n   - N-question multi-select:\n     - toggles then right-arrow per group, final review return\n   - Empty multi-select remains refused because Claude drops the question from the result.\n   - Multi-select free text remains refused because live proof showed wrong-answer behavior.\n\n   Version constants:\n\n   ```ts\n   export const PROVEN_AGAINST = \"claude-code@2.1.226\";\n   export const RENDER_OBSERVED_AGAINST = \"claude-code@2.1.226\";\n   ```\n\n   Installed CLI during testing:\n\n   - `@anthropic-ai/claude-code` version `2.1.228`\n\n   D. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.ts`\n\n   Shipped/published changes:\n\n   - Added pre-write `claimed` status.\n   - Added transactional `beginWrite()` that:\n     - reads and validates the claimed row\n     - checks for another request fencing the same question\n     - atomically promotes `claimed → in_flight`\n   - Restart handling:\n     - abandoned `claimed → failed` because zero bytes could have moved\n     - abandoned `in_flight → unconfirmed`\n   - Fencing statuses:\n     - `in_flight`\n     - `confirmed`\n     - `unconfirmed`\n   - `failed` does not fence a fresh request.\n   - Real SQLite tests verify behavior across database recreation.\n\n   Core contract:\n\n   ```ts\n   beginWrite(requestId: RequestId, leaseId: string): LedgerRecord | null;\n   ```\n\n   A later race fix corrected failure classification:\n\n   - durable status `claimed` on unexpected failure → `failed`\n   - durable status `in_flight` on unexpected failure → `unconfirmed`\n\n   This prevents a pre-write SQLite/lock failure from permanently fencing an unanswered question.\n\n   E. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\attempt-ledger.test.ts`\n\n   Added real migrated SQLite coverage:\n\n   - confirmed rows fence a fresh request after DB/ledger reopen\n   - original request ID is excluded from its own fence\n   - failed rows do not fence\n   - in-flight and unconfirmed rows fence\n   - real Drizzle/better-sqlite3 query behavior is exercised, not only a memory stub\n\n   F. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-store.ts`\n\n   Published settlement behavior:\n\n   - PTY acknowledgment no longer immediately resolves/removes the question.\n   - `markRemoteAnswered()` attaches phone/watch provenance while leaving the question pending.\n   - Exact positive PostToolUse or transcript `tool_result` settles the question.\n   - Remote provenance is inherited when positive settlement occurs.\n\n   Current relevant logic:\n\n   ```ts\n   resolve(questionId, resolvedBy, atMs) {\n     const question = byId.get(questionId);\n     if (question === undefined) {\n       throw new Error(`companion: resolve on unknown question ${questionId}`);\n     }\n     if (question.state === \"resolved\") return false;\n     if (question.state !== \"pending\") return false;\n     question.resolvedAtMs = question.remoteAnswer?.deliveredAtMs ?? atMs;\n     question.resolvedBy = question.remoteAnswer?.resolvedBy ?? resolvedBy;\n     settle(question, \"resolved\");\n     return true;\n   }\n\n   markRemoteAnswered(questionId, resolvedBy, deliveredAtMs) {\n     const question = byId.get(questionId);\n     if (question === undefined) return false;\n     if (question.state === \"stale\") return false;\n     question.remoteAnswer = { resolvedBy, deliveredAtMs };\n     if (question.state === \"resolved\") {\n       question.resolvedBy = resolvedBy;\n       question.resolvedAtMs = deliveredAtMs;\n     }\n     return true;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   G. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\index.ts`\n\n   Published changes:\n\n   - Pairing logs no longer contain the secret QR URI.\n   - The log now carries only:\n\n   ```ts\n   logger.warn(\"pairing window OPEN for 120s\", {\n     pairingRef: handle.pairingRef,\n     expiresAtMs: handle.expiresAtMs,\n   });\n   ```\n\n   - Added answer repaint wiring through `nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint`.\n   - Added corrective resolution-event publication when PostToolUse wins the race before remote provenance is attached.\n   - The corrective event ensures connected clients ultimately receive phone/watch provenance rather than retaining a false desktop provenance frame.\n\n   H. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\terminal\\terminal.ts`\n\n   Added best-effort repaint support:\n\n   ```ts\n   export function nudgeTerminalSessionRepaint({\n     terminalId,\n     workspaceId,\n   }: {\n     terminalId: string;\n     workspaceId: string;\n   }): { success: true } | { error: string }\n   ```\n\n   Mechanism:\n\n   - Temporarily resize the PTY by one row.\n   - Restore dimensions after a short timeout.\n   - Catch resize errors.\n   - Failure only logs; it never changes the answer outcome.\n\n   This addressed stale visible frames after a successfully consumed answer, but does not solve the newer multi-question sequencing race.\n\n   I. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-guardless.test.ts`\n\n   Expanded coverage includes:\n\n   - confirmed write remains pending until positive settlement\n   - repaint invoked after confirmed write\n   - repaint failure is non-vetoing\n   - fresh request cannot retype a delivered/maybe-delivered answer\n   - lock and begin-write zero-write failures remain retryable\n   - claimed versus in-flight failure classification\n   - simplified lock dependency injection instead of monkey-patching `runExclusive`\n\n   J. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer-settlement-events.test.ts`\n\n   Added during race repair:\n\n   - Tests the actual notifying sink/event publisher path.\n   - Covers PostToolUse-before-remote-provenance race.\n   - Verifies corrective phone/watch provenance publication.\n\n   K. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\question-lifecycle.test.ts`\n\n   Covers:\n\n   - positive settlement\n   - remote provenance inheritance\n   - settlement ordering/races\n   - pending/discoverability behavior\n\n   L. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\types.ts`\n\n   Important correction:\n\n   - `claimed` remains internal.\n   - Wire `AnswerStatusOutcome.known.status` remains only:\n     - `in_flight`\n     - `confirmed`\n     - `failed`\n     - `unconfirmed`\n   - `toWireOutcome()` maps internal `claimed` to wire `in_flight`.\n\n   M. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\db\\schema.ts`\n\n   Added internal ledger status:\n\n   ```ts\n   export const answerAttemptStatuses = [\n     \"claimed\",\n     \"in_flight\",\n     \"confirmed\",\n     \"failed\",\n     \"unconfirmed\",\n     \"closed_not_received\",\n   ] as const;\n   ```\n\n   No generated Drizzle migration was manually edited for this text-status widening.\n\n   N. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\trpc\\router\\notifications\\notifications.ts`\n\n   Updated stale comments that still claimed retired transcript/screen guards secured the unauthenticated localhost capture route.\n\n   O. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\FEATURES.md`\n\n   `(ANSWER-GUARDLESS)` was updated to document:\n\n   - confirmed writes do not prematurely remove pending discovery\n   - settlement waits for positive completion evidence\n   - repaint is non-vetoing\n   - durable fresh-request fencing\n   - pairing logs do not persist secret QR material\n\n   Feature marker gate remained `147/147`.\n\n   P. Scratch proof files\n\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pty-proof-228\\proof-freetext.mjs`\n     - proved one-question free text works in both burst and paced modes on Claude 2.1.228\n   - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pty-proof-4q\\...`\n     - isolated four-question pacing proof\n     - persisted only safe metadata, not question/answer content\n   - `tmp\\phone-emu\\safe-e2e.ts`\n   - `tmp\\phone-emu\\safe-freetext-e2e.ts`\n     - scratch sealed-protocol harnesses\n     - must not be run again with the physical phone identity\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - Initial post-install conclusion was too optimistic:\n     - PTY acknowledgment was treated as equivalent to visible/question completion.\n     - The user corrected this:\n       - “It wasn't phone side UI, because the question remained on screen - the answer you saw was me typing it on desktop after phone failed”\n     - Subsequent exact trace showed one earlier free-text answer did produce a matching tool result 341 ms later, but the visible frame remained stale.\n     - This led to deferred positive settlement and repaint changes.\n\n   - Latest four-question failure exposed a second, distinct defect:\n     - Phone supplied all four answers.\n     - Five frames were sent and acknowledged in 82 ms.\n     - Only the first picker transition occurred.\n     - Root cause: protocol-v3 `input-ok` acknowledges PTY acceptance, not Claude TUI consumption.\n     - Published `4a9978200` does not yet fix this.\n\n   - Controlled one-question proof initially weakened the pacing theory:\n     - Burst free text worked.\n     - This was not representative of N=4 question-to-question transitions.\n     - A dedicated N=4 proof later showed burst failure 2/2.\n\n   - N=4 pacing proof:\n     - burst: failed 2/2\n     - 100 ms: passed current single run but is considered edge\n     - 250 ms: passed current single run\n     - 500 ms: passed current single run\n     - 1000 ms: passed current single run\n     - transition-observed mode: passed 2/2 with approximately 750–820 ms observed gaps\n     - recommended shipping value: deterministic 500 ms\n\n   - Emulator identity interference:\n     - Scratch emulator reused the physical phone’s paired identity.\n     - Its reduced-capability hello temporarily caused the phone’s FCM registration to receive `capability_unsupported`.\n     - The physical phone later restored capabilities with a full re-hello.\n     - Further emulator work must use a separate paired identity.\n\n   - Pairing flow could not safely create that identity:\n     - `openPairing()` logged the complete secret-bearing QR URI.\n     - This violated:\n       - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n     - Fixed to log only `pairingRef` and expiry.\n\n   - Safe emulator status parser used the old response shape:\n     - It looked for a flat `outcome`.\n     - Current `/v1/answer/status` uses a discriminated outcome object.\n     - The scratch script failed despite a confirmed durable row.\n     - Ledger inspection proved the answer itself succeeded.\n\n   - First safe emulator watched only `SUPERSET_TERMINAL_ID` from the current shell:\n     - The created AskUser question could belong to a different terminal.\n     - It timed out.\n     - Scratch discovery was revised to search pending questions across terminals.\n\n   - Initial full validation commands ran from a persisted temporary working directory:\n     - Bun tests, scripts, and Biome could not find repository paths.\n     - Fixed by explicitly running from:\n       - `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64`\n\n   - Build workflow dispatch incorrectly used `-f ref=main`:\n     - `workflow_dispatch` does not define a `ref` input.\n     - Fixed with:\n       - `--ref main -f publish=true`\n\n   - Several builds were intentionally cancelled:\n     - `31601012858` cancelled after late review found two race defects.\n     - `31604538404` cancelled after `/simplify` produced a final test-only commit.\n     - Final successful build:\n       - `31605016224`\n       - SHA `4a997820034d96ef0df479069dab4237056ebbcc`\n\n   - Installer launch sequence:\n     - First download command failed because `jq` was unavailable.\n     - Replaced with `gh ... --jq`.\n     - Digest verified:\n       - `sha256:14a78e27847e7ca33e35e98ac946204ecd1ca9ab936dca946bfd39fb42cb6c29`\n     - First `Start-Process` invocation used a bad path expansion and failed.\n     - A direct PowerShell path check then launched PID `21928`.\n     - However, the user later explicitly said:\n       - “I haven't installed the new version yet”\n     - Therefore the new version must be treated as not installed despite installer launch.\n\n   - Late review findings:\n     - Pre-write `claimed` exceptions were incorrectly becoming `unconfirmed` and permanently fencing a zero-write request.\n       - Fixed: `claimed → failed`; only `in_flight → unconfirmed`.\n     - PostToolUse-first settlement could emit false desktop provenance before remote provenance arrived.\n       - Fixed with corrective resolution-event publication and production-wrapper tests.\n     - `claimed` was accidentally exposed in the wire union.\n       - Fixed by keeping it internal and mapping it to wire `in_flight`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   Completed and pushed:\n\n   - Guardless answer path with protocol-v3 acknowledgments and durable readback.\n   - Deferred QuestionStore settlement until exact positive PostToolUse/tool-result evidence.\n   - Best-effort non-vetoing PTY repaint.\n   - Durable `claimed → in_flight` question-level arbitration.\n   - Restart-safe duplicate fencing.\n   - Correct zero-write versus ambiguous-write classification.\n   - Correct phone/watch provenance across settlement races.\n   - Secret QR URI removed from logs.\n   - Real SQLite fence tests.\n   - Updated comments, feature markers, and focused tests.\n   - Full validation and review for those batches.\n\n   Pushed commits:\n\n   ```text\n   408ecc9c5 fix(host-service): settle companion answers after Claude consumes them\n   5bc2dd144 fix(host-service): keep claimed status internal\n   692ce7dae fix(host-service): preserve answer race outcomes\n   4a9978200 test(host-service): simplify answer lock fixtures\n   ```\n\n   Validation for the published settlement batch:\n\n   - Full companion suite: 219 passed, 0 failed\n   - Focused race tests: 45 passed, 0 failed\n   - Feature markers: 147/147\n   - REFERR gate: clean\n   - Scoped Biome: clean\n   - `/simplify`: completed\n   - `/code-review low`: no findings\n   - Build `31605016224`: success on exact SHA `4a9978200`\n\n   New ongoing issue:\n\n   - Multi-question PTY frames are sent too quickly.\n   - The phone, schema validation, encoder, targeting, lock screen, and daemon were not at fault.\n   - The bridge needs deterministic inter-frame pacing.\n   - The fix must be included in a new build before installation/final E2E.\n\n   T3 Code exploration:\n\n   - An Opus architect agent was dispatched to inspect the public T3 Code repository.\n   - Preliminary conclusion from the pacing investigator:\n     - T3 does not offer a directly reusable PTY pacing precedent.\n     - It handles AskUserQuestion atomically through the Claude Agent SDK using a deferred/updated-input style flow.\n     - Its ordinary PTY writes are fire-and-forget and not serialized against TUI state.\n   - The precise Opus repository/file report had not yet been returned in this context.\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n   Earlier genuine user messages preserved from prior context:\n\n   - `/compact`\n   - “This desktop is too old to answer this kind of question from here. i didn't answer the existing adams email thread still open for an hour and it gave me this. I didn't approve this barrier. remove all barriers, if I can answer in the terminal I want the phone to be able to handle it. end of story, stop building stupid safety mechanisms for this 1 person app”\n   - “i typed in an askuser and gpt yhis Unconfirmed - the desktop accepted the write but did not confirm the outcome”\n   - “This may or may not have gone through. Nothing will be sent again - checking reads the outcome from the desktop... this is bullshit how far can it be to type in a box... why are we getting these errors.. the question remained unanswered still I'm gonna do it on desktop now... make sure everything has heavy logging so you can tackle everything 1st shot”\n   - “I couldn't even respond on my watch it said desktop bridge wouldn't allow - wtf is this man... I need to kill all barriers to my perfect ux - follow simple rule if there is a question in terminal I need to be able to answer phone or watch - no blockers without my explciti approval per blocker (currently I want none and we add over time)”\n   - “all installed now - do you need to do e2e testing on your emulated versions etc?”\n   - `/compact`\n   - “Continue from where you left off.”\n   - “dude what is this? I thought you I told you to get rid of all the guards. it's killing the ux. I need to be able to respond. In every scenario no matter what. that chat is still open so you can emulate right now. I wanted to choose option one if you need to test.”\n   - “it needs to work even if the screen is off and I need to enter my password to open it again”\n   - “get sol and fable to thoroughly review the approach - use emulators to test where possible”\n   - “please confirm that this issue will be resolved as well. by this, you better make sure from logs that you're really tackling the root cause ux comes first. these guards need to be killed off... generally make sweeping changes to kill the odds of my messages not being able to get through”\n   - “if you need to test that question is still open, I'd like to choose the option that gives us a one-off script in the CWD”\n   - “Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content.”\n   - “use opus sub agents to continue”\n   - “Install now (Recommended)”\n\n   Genuine user messages in this continuation:\n\n   - “Continue from where you left off.”\n   - “ok installed and PC restarted do whatever e2e testing you need to do”\n   - “1.”\n   - “I haven't installed the new version yet, but I just answered some questions in another chat. Only the first of four questions got answered. I did all four on my phone, but only one of four worked on here. What is the root cause of this? I've left you the message image of the chat that's open. I still haven't touched it since I did the submissions on the phone. You can see the current state of that chat and look at the logs to see what I did on my phone and see the mismatch.”\n   - “Send an opus agent to explore the t3 code public repository to see how they interact with terminals, etc. I don't know if there's anything useful there.”\n   - The current request asking for this text-only detailed compaction summary.\n\n   Important human feedback received through interactive answer UI during this continuation:\n\n   - “what - you decide just make sure the app works as expected”\n   - “i have no idea what you're talking about just test the latest changes with with emulated app if you need to. I can tell you already I just tried to freetype this response from my phone and it didn't work... this has to work even if the pc screen turns off”\n   - “It wasn't phone side UI, because the question remained on screen - the answer you saw was me typing it on desktop after phone failed”\n   - “Yeah, okay. Do whatever needs doing.”\n   - “Install now (Recommended)”\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n   - Task #13: Implement deterministic non-vetoing inter-frame pacing.\n     - Add 500 ms between protocol-v3 acknowledged frames.\n     - Do not delay after the final frame.\n     - Keep the terminal lock held.\n     - Preserve deadline and lease checks.\n     - Do not consult screen, transcript, renderer, Windows lock/display, binding, liveness, or capability state.\n     - Preserve protocol-v2 whole-sequence unconfirmed fallback.\n\n   - Task #15: Simplify and review the pacing fix.\n     - Run `/simplify` fully.\n     - Run focused and full companion tests.\n     - Run real Claude N=4 PTY proof after implementation.\n     - Run scoped Biome, feature markers, and REFERR gate.\n     - Commit and run `/code-review low`.\n\n   - Task #16: Publish the ARM64 pacing fix.\n     - Push final commit to `main`.\n     - Dispatch a new full Windows ARM64 publish build.\n     - Do not use already-published `4a9978200` as the final build because it lacks pacing.\n\n   - Task #5 remains operationally open:\n     - Create a distinct paired emulator identity after the final pacing build is installed.\n     - Never reuse the physical phone identity.\n     - Run final emulator, physical phone, physical watch, display-off, and locked/login-screen E2E.\n     - Verify actual AskUser completion, not only PTY acknowledgment or ledger status.\n\n   - Obtain the precise Opus T3 repository report if it has not yet arrived.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before this summary request, the investigation had conclusively established the four-question root cause.\n\n   Live incident evidence:\n\n   - The user left the picker untouched.\n   - Phone request contained four valid selections.\n   - Production encoded five frames:\n     - four answer digits\n     - one final carriage return\n   - Protocol-v3 acknowledged all frames in 82 ms.\n   - The picker visibly advanced only to question 2.\n   - No completed AskUser tool result followed.\n   - Therefore frames 2–5 arrived before Claude’s TUI had transitioned to the states where those keys had the intended meaning.\n\n   Isolated proof:\n\n   - Real Claude Code 2.1.228.\n   - Exact N=4 production sequence.\n   - Burst mode failed 2/2.\n   - Fixed-gap trials at 100, 250, 500, and 1000 ms passed current runs.\n   - Transition-observed pacing passed 2/2 with approximately 750–820 ms observed delays.\n   - Recommended production delay: 500 ms.\n   - This delay is deterministic and independent of renderer/screen/transcript/lock state.\n\n   Published versus installed state:\n\n   - Final successful published settlement build:\n     - run `31605016224`\n     - SHA `4a997820034d96ef0df479069dab4237056ebbcc`\n     - desktop release `1.20.2`\n   - Verified installer digest:\n     - `sha256:14a78e27847e7ca33e35e98ac946204ecd1ca9ab936dca946bfd39fb42cb6c29`\n   - Despite an installer process being launched, the user explicitly stated the new version was not installed.\n   - Treat the running installation as the older `1.20.0` / `7e0d25f3c` guardless build.\n   - Do not ask the user to install `4a9978200` as the final answer; it does not contain the multi-frame pacing fix.\n\n   The repository was clean after the isolated pacing proof. No production pacing edit had yet been made by the proof agent.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Implement the proven pacing fix in:\n\n   `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\answer.ts`\n\n   Specifically:\n\n   - after each successful protocol-v3 `writer.write(...)`\n   - if another frame remains\n   - wait 500 ms\n   - then re-check deadline and renew the lease before the next frame\n   - do not apply this wait to the protocol-v2 single whole-sequence fallback frame\n   - do not read or wait on renderer, screen, transcript, or lock state\n\n   Then repeat the isolated N=4 proof and full validation before publishing a replacement installer.\n\n   Direct quotes anchoring the active task:\n\n   - User:\n     - “Only the first of four questions got answered. I did all four on my phone, but only one of four worked on here. What is the root cause of this?”\n   - Proven result:\n     - “Burst input failed 2/2 on real Claude Code 2.1.228.”\n     - “500 ms is the recommended conservative deterministic inter-frame delay.”\n   - User’s architecture requirement:\n     - “this has to work even if the pc screen turns off”\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"3b039058-bf2e-4b66-b9c6-fd0bfd234fb4","timestamp":"2026-08-12T17:35:34.160Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
