{"parentUuid":"07c72a03-7716-4b17-a6c7-da4870be1923","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5548f27b-2b1d-4e0e-84da-bd27822c3dc9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1T5gXwwPxVjSinr6b1BMLjrM","type":"tool_result","content":"<retrieval_status>timeout</retrieval_status>\n\n<task_id>ab9207100517be12f</task_id>\n\n<task_type>local_agent</task_type>\n\n<status>running</status>\n\n<output>\n[Truncated. Full output: C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\083b7de7-951b-4059-a4aa-3dd81cb5a6cf\\tasks\\ab9207100517be12f.output]\n\nte can't false-abort | `(REFERR-GATE)` |\\n | Nightly dependency-consistency + lock regen | the nightly merge can introduce dependency-state drift that only the build discovers (after a windows-arm64 runner spins up): a stale fork root `overrides` entry that pins a package to a version different from the merged workspace pin (electron-builder \\\"production dependency not found …\\\"), or a `bun.lock` left stale by an upstream package.json bump (frozen-install fails). The merge now runs an override-consistency gate (fails loud on any exact override↔pin mismatch) + regenerates `bun.lock` to match the merged manifests with the build's exact bun version (which also fails loud, in the cheap merge job, if the merged manifests don't resolve or a pin is age-blocked) — so this class of build failure is caught/fixed before the windows-arm64 build spins up, baseline untouched on failure (recovery loop). No full `--frozen-lockfile` install runs here: the merge runner is linux, so a platform-specific install quirk would be a false abort, and the regenerated lock is consistent with the manifests by construction. The fork carries NO mastra `overrides` and pins `@mastra/core`/`mastracode` to upstream's exact versions in all three workspaces (upstream keeps mastra consistent via identical exact pins; the seed commit's redundant override + a recovery merge that resolved the pins DOWN to 0.18.0 were the recurring breakage, both corrected) | `(LOCK-REGEN)` |\\n | Fork-owned workflow dir | `.github/workflows/` carries ONLY the fork's own workflows — upstream CI files were dropped at fork creation (they target upstream's infra/secrets) and the Actions `GITHUB_TOKEN` can NEVER push a workflow-file change anyway (no `workflows` scope exists for it: \\\"refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow\\\"). Upstream desktop-v1.14.3 added `deploy-relay.yml`, which merged CLEANLY and then killed the candidate push after every gate had already passed. The nightly now deterministically restores the fork's exact workflow set mid-merge (`git checkout --no-overlay HEAD -- .github/workflows`) BEFORE conflict detection, so upstream workflow additions/edits never enter the fork, never reach the AI resolver, and never hit the push restriction — and the dropped upstream CI delta is SURFACED, not silently erased (job summary + log + handed to the semantic review, which appends advisory `CI-NOTE:` lines when upstream moves build-relevant logic into its CI), with a pre-commit postcondition proving the committed tree carries zero workflow-dir changes. Wanting an upstream workflow = deliberate local commit with a user token | `(WORKFLOW-FORK-OWNED)` |\\n | Nightly pipeline integrity | three cheap deterministic guards on the merge→build→advance hand-offs: a fatal (non-conflict) `git merge` failure is caught via missing MERGE_HEAD instead of masquerading as a clean merge (the `set +e` wrapper accepts every nonzero exit); the build + advance jobs consume the merge commit's immutable SHA — not the mutable `nightly/*` branch name — under a workflow-level `concurrency` group (queue, never cancel), and advance refuses to fast-forward main if the candidate ref moved; `gh release create` tags the exact built commit via `--target` + a post-publish remote-tag assert (without `--target` gh tags the DEFAULT branch tip, which during a nightly is pre-advance main — every nightly-published release tag pointed one commit behind the installer's true source until 2026-07-11) | `(NIGHTLY-INTEGRITY)` |\\n | Companion keep-awake | the phone/watch companion is worthless if the desktop sleeps mid-question: the answer path lives in host-service, which dies with the machine. The main process ho\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"persistedOutputPath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\.claude\\\\projects\\\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\\\41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91\\\\tool-results\\\\b7hcd3cgw.txt\",\"persistedOutputSize\":121809},\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"91aa5f11-7bb0-4b97-a060-25c5e4cc22f8\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\",\"sessionId\":\"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91\",\"version\":\"2.1.228\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"slug\":\"jolly-singing-lemur\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"ff2139b5-42ae-4171-b94e-39ebba9585f3\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"ab9207100517be12f\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"resp_021fd8ae7d031758016a7cb315571881919ec98aa2fae473b2\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"codex-gpt-5-6-sol\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1349,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":97792,\"output_tokens\":117,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_a9TxlP0ILq3imwLVVr2A3mEc\",\"name\":\"Agent\",\"input\":{\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"description\":\"Review pacing reuse\",\"prompt\":\"Act as /simplify Phase 1 Reuse reviewer. Review ONLY uncommitted diff in FEATURES.md, packages/host-service/src/companion/ans