ript prompt failed on that one entry forever -> the lead\n451-        # terminal's dot latched yellow with zero agents running. Strict\n452-        # decode first (payloads are harness-emitted JSON, always valid\n453-        # UTF-8); on the never-expected failure, log loud and fall back to\n454-        # replacement decoding so the hook still POSTs the lifecycle event.\n455-        data = sys.stdin.buffer.read()\n456-        try:\n457-            raw = data.decode(\"utf-8\")\n458-        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n459-            try:\n460-                _log({\n461-                    \"action\": \"payload-decode-error\",\n--\n545-    # long-lived teammate, or one that died without a clean SubagentStop, to a\n546-    # finished status). Refreshed ONLY on genuine forward activity (never on the\n547-    # hold itself, which would keep it perpetually fresh); the JSONL watcher\n548-    # re-asserts yellow within its poll if a reaped set turns out to still write.\n549-    return (\n550-        pathlib.Path.home()\n551-        / \".superset\"\n552-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n553-        / (terminal_id + \".bgactive\")\n554-    )\n555-\n556-\n557:def _teamstate_path(terminal_id):\n558-    # (TEAMMATE-IDLE) incremental parse cache for the lead transcript's\n559-    # teammate ledger plus named-fork tool-use mapping. Versioned so a schema\n560-    # change forces a full reparse and heals entries written by older code.\n561-    # Keyed by transcript path, so a /resume (new transcript file) or terminalId\n562-    # reuse also self-invalidates. Corruption tolerated: any read failure falls\n563-    # back to offset 0 — self-healing, never trusted blindly.\n564-    return (\n565-        pathlib.Path.home()\n566-        / \".superset\"\n567-        / \"agent-subagent-running\"\n568:        / (terminal_id + \".teamstate.json\")\n569-    )\n570-\n571-\n572-def _askq_dir(terminal_id):\n573-    # (UNTAGGED-BG-RED) a DIRECTORY of per-owner \"an AskUserQuestion is pending\"\n574-    # markers for this terminal — one file per owner (the raising agent). An\n575-    # AskUserQuestion red's ONLY valid clear is its own answer\n576-    # (PostToolUse:AskUserQuestion) or that owner's turn boundary — NEVER a\n577-    # generic main-loop tool completion. While ANY marker exists an untagged\n578-    # ordinary PostToolUse asserts working WITHOUT clearing the red, so a\n579-    # teammate/fork's parent-attributed (agent_id-less) tool cannot stomp a\n580-    # still-open question. Keyed PER OWNER (not one terminal-wide flag) so two\n--\n935-            has_shell = True\n936-        else:\n937-            has_agent = True\n938-    return (has_any, has_agent, has_shell)\n939-\n940-\n941-# (TEAMMATE-IDLE) Claude Code NEVER flips an idle teammate's background_tasks[]\n942-# entry off \"running\" (captured live 2026-07-10: 33 teammate entries, all\n943-# status \"running\", for a session whose 44 teammates had ALL finished hours\n944-# earlier), so the payload alone cannot green a lead whose teammates are done —\n945-# once no further hook event arrived, the dot stayed yellow forever. The lead\n946-# TRANSCRIPT has the missing truth: every teammate that finishes delivers an\n947:# idle_notification teammate-message into it, and every (re)activation is\n948-# visible too (an Agent spawn tool_use, a SendMessage tool_use to it, a\n949-# non-idle teammate-message/agent-message from it).\n950-#\n951:# (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) The original all-idle predicate (drop teammate entries\n952-# only when EVERY tracked name is idle) proved unsatisfiable in real sessions\n953-# (captured live 2026-07-22: 55 permanently-\"active\" names — named non-fork\n954-# Agent spawns like sol/general-purpose review agents that finish via\n955-# task-notification and never idle-notify, forks re-marked active by a later\n956-# SendMessage, and \"name [hash]\" duplicate-suffix splits — held 25 finished\n957-# wrangler teammates yellow all day). The decision is now PER ENTRY: a\n958-# running teammate entry's payload \"description\" is the spawn prompt's head\n959-# (observed live: first 50 chars + \"...\"), so match it against the prompt\n960-# prefix recorded at each named Agent spawn; an entry may be dropped only\n961-# when it matches at least one recorded spawn AND every matching name's last\n962:# ledger event is an idle_notification. Unmatched, ambiguous-with-active, or\n963-# unparseable -> keep that entry (the safe yellow direction). Poisoned\n964-# \"active\" names can no longer block OTHER teammates' drops. A teammate that\n965-# dies WITHOUT ever reporting stays \"active\" and keeps its own hold: from\n966-# the logs that case is indistinguishable from a long think, so it is\n967-# deliberately left to (BG-STALE).\n968-\n969-\n970-def _team_norm(text):\n971-    # Collapse whitespace runs to single spaces so a spawn prompt and the\n972-    # payload description derived from it compare equal even if truncation\n973-    # or the harness normalized newlines. String ops only (NO regex: this\n974-    # file is a TS template literal and single backslashes in regex escapes\n975-    # would be silently swallowed).\n976-    return \" \".join(str(text or \"\").split())\n977-\n978-\n979-def _team_scan_text(state, text):\n980-    # Update the name -> \"active\"|\"idle\" ledger from one transcript text blob.\n981-    # String scanning only (NO regex): this file is a TS template literal, and\n982-    # single backslashes in regex escapes would be silently swallowed.\n983:    # (TEAM-ENTRY-MATCH) A duplicate teammate name is delivered with a\n984-    # \" [hash]\" suffix in its messages while the spawn recorded the base name;\n985-    # mirror every suffixed update onto the base key so the base key tracks\n986-    # the LATEST same-named instance instead of latching a stale idle.\n987-    # Accepted narrow risk (review 2026-07-22): same name + identical prompt\n988-    # head + the OLD instance silently working when the new one idles can\n989- 