unknown event; an\n318-unmapped event is a silent no-op, exactly like notify.sh):\n319-  UserPromptSubmit            -> Start            (working / yellow)\n320-  Stop                        -> Stop             (review/green) UNLESS a\n321-                                 subagent is still running (then suppressed —\n322-                                 stay yellow; greens on the last SubagentStop).\n323-                                 With background_tasks[] still running, the\n324:                                 entry TYPES decide: any agent-type entry\n325-                                 (subagent/teammate/workflow) -> SubagentActive\n326-                                 (yellow; red-respecting in the renderer);\n327-                                 shell-only -> BackgroundRunning (blue)\n328-  SessionEnd                  -> Stop             (review / green; clears state)\n329-  StopFailure(main loop)      -> Stop + clears state, UNLESS a codex-companion\n330-                                 job for this session is still alive ->\n331-                                 SubagentActive (BF: codex runs on its OWN API;\n332-                                 a Claude rate-limit abort does not stop it)\n333-  StopFailure(in a subagent)  -> (STOPFAIL-SUBAGENT) self-scoped: drops only that\n334-                                 fork's markers, never the shared session state /\n335-                                 the main question guard; the central red guard\n336-                                 keeps a still-pending AskUserQuestion red\n337-  Notification                -> PermissionRequest (permission / red)\n338-  PreToolUse(AskUserQuestion) -> PermissionRequest (red)   else no-op\n--\n350-                                 — superset-notify.py owns it; notify.sh no longer does)\n351-  SubagentStart               -> SubagentActive   (working, red-respecting — a\n352-                                 workflow/teammate spawning an agent while a red\n353-                                 is pending must not stomp it; the subagent\n354-                                 marker still holds yellow through the main Stop)\n355-  SubagentStop                -> Stop iff it was the LAST subagent AND main had\n356-                                 already stopped, else no-op (see _decide_event_type)\n357-  PreCompact                  -> Start            (working — context compaction is\n358-                                 a minutes-long LLM call during which no other\n359-                                 hook fires; manual /compact does not even fire\n360-                                 UserPromptSubmit, verified live)\n361-  SessionStart(source=compact)-> Stop after a MANUAL compact (same decision as\n362-                                 Stop, so the subagent yellow-hold is respected\n363-                                 and the persisted turn-end snapshot markers\n364:                                 restore yellow for agent-type background work\n365-                                 or BLUE for a still-running background shell);\n366-                                 re-asserts Start after an AUTO compact (the turn\n367-                                 is still live); no-op when we never marked a\n368-                                 compact as running\n369-\n370-Server maps Start->working, Stop->review, PermissionRequest->permission and\n371-returns {\"result\":{\"data\":{\"json\":{\"success\":true,...}}}}. Uses only stdlib\n372-urllib so it has no third-party dependency. Silent on every failure path — a\n373-broken hook must NEVER raise or abort the agent.\n374-\n375-(COMPANION-CAPTURE) The POST body additionally carries the whole\n376-AskUserQuestion payload — companionQuestion on PreToolUse, and\n377-companionQuestionResolved on the matching PostToolUse — so the companion\n378-bridge can render a question on a phone/watch and retract the notification\n--\n496-\n497-def _compact_marker_path(terminal_id):\n498-    # (COMPACT-YELLOW) records \