{"parentUuid":"6663b8d6-3f54-458a-a87a-88ec2fbcd358","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdyY6LCo1nTVeY4Te3zdV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HqmXzLmgvparrjPv1UDmv7","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\memory\\project_companion_guard5_answer_path_fix.md","old_string":"Related: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]].","new_string":"**2026-08-12 ANSWER-FRAME-PACING (commit `7b56fc6fa`, build 31627045823, desktop-v1.20.2 INSTALLED + post-install E2E PASSED):** live incident: untouched 4-question picker, phone sent 4 valid selects, all 5 frames daemon-acked in 82ms, only Q1 advanced, no tool_result — root cause: protocol-v3 `input-ok` proves `pty.write()` acceptance, NOT Claude TUI consumption; burst frames land during the picker's question-transition unmount window and are dropped. Worse failure mode PROVEN: a 250ms-gap run produced a tool_result with EVERY answer silently misattributed one question over (committed, no error) — small pacing constants are actively dangerous, lost answers are the good case. N=4 sweep on real 2.1.228 (tmp/pty-proof-4q/proof-4q.mjs): burst 0/2, 100ms 1/3, 250ms 2/3 (1 silent-wrong), 500ms 3/3, 1000ms 3/3. Fix in answer.ts `injectSequence`: `ANSWER_INTER_FRAME_DELAY_MS = 500` state-blind sleep after every acked non-final v3 frame (never after final, never on the v2 single legacy frame); injected `delay` dep (production wires crypto `sleep`, assertAnswerDeps fails loud unwired); a REJECTING timer propagates fail-loud (never bursts the remainder — outer handler classifies claimed→failed / in_flight→unconfirmed); dynamic deadline = 10s + (frames-1)×500ms derived from actual frame count (do NOT duplicate encoder limits in the injector — /simplify altitude finding removed the 321-frame mirror); deadline checked and lease renewed after each sleep immediately before next write; terminal lock held across sleeps (documented on LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS). Review trap: FEATURES.md said 1000ms while code said 500ms — reviewers flagged manifest-vs-code drift on the one safety number; keep them lockstep. T3 Code explored (pingdotgg/t3code): answers AskUserQuestion atomically via Agent SDK canUseTool, no PTY answer path, nothing to port. POST-INSTALL E2E on installed 1.20.2: fresh emulator identity paired (never reuse phone identity), 4-question canary through the real bridge → confirmed in 2025ms (=4×500ms gaps), tool_result 4/4 correctly attributed, resolved with phone provenance after tool_result. Residue: 2 dead emulator device records in device store (keys unrecoverable, inert; no per-device revoke exists — only revokeAllDevices which would nuke the phone); PROVEN_AGAINST still 2.1.226 vs installed 2.1.228 (drift warning only, answers work). Physical phone/watch/screen-off/lock-screen spot-check is user-side.\n\nRelated: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6440,"cache_read_input_tokens":422123,"output_tokens":1282,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6440,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":422123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6440},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"30a5a077-8145-45ea-a856-db4d3f14f3b3","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:07:51.308Z","effor