k assumed option rows are adjacent lines, but real pickers render wrapped descriptions between rows (4 rows span 9-11 lines). Second barrier: 8-char label floor refused short labels (\"Skip\") upstream documents as the normal shape. Third: free-text row label drifted \"Other\"→\"Type something.\" (2.1.220→2.1.226). Lifetime answer_attempts before fix: 0 confirmed."]},{"oldStart":32,"oldLines":4,"newStart":32,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **2026-08-10/11 ANSWER-GUARDLESS FINAL SHIP:** user locked the whole-UX contract: any captured pending Claude question with a real terminal target must remain discoverable and answerable from phone/watch regardless of transcript readability/state, live screen/render state, renderer availability, Windows display/lock/login state, mutable agent binding, permission axis, AskUser marker, read-side liveness, or negotiated answer capability/session state. Security/API boundaries retained: pairing/authenticated device, Cloudflare Access, sealed AES-GCM transport, nonce replay protection, schemas/semantic shape validation, exact current question+fingerprint at the last synchronous pre-write point, answer-wide lease, terminal lock, durable request claim/fence, actual PTY failures, and protocol-0 read-only. Commit `ec83cf8e4` removed every production answer guard, made pending questions pierce curation and capability hiding, added protocol-v3 correlated daemon-side `pty.write` acknowledgments, v2 whole-sequence legacy fallback with durable `unconfirmed` fencing, detached-session adoption before lease/lock, durable outcome write+readback, honest `not_written` vs `unknown`, audit-failure containment, and positive-only transcript settlement. Cleanup commit `7e0d25f3c` removed the retired ~4.6k-line guard/matcher/test stack while preserving `/v1/message` picker protections; Opus validation: REFERR clean, 200 companion tests + 11 fault probes passed, only accepted TS2554 debt; `/code-review low` found nothing. Both pushed to main. Full Windows ARM64 publish build `31443284669` succeeded on sha `7e0d25f3c0ecec91324b5302b265674269800cac`; prior build `31437447650` also succeeded on `ec83cf8e4`. Installer NOT installed yet—must wait for the user's explicit exact-time authorization because it closes Superset/session. Post-install verification still required: real phone/watch answer, renderer hidden/display off/Windows locked-login boundary, detached v2→v3 migration, acknowledgment+ledger logs, and no `guard_failed` answer outcome. Never log free-text bodies, keys, tokens, or transcript content."," ","+**2026-08-12 ANSWER-FRAME-PACING (commit `7b56fc6fa`, build 31627045823, desktop-v1.20.2 INSTALLED + post-install E2E PASSED):** live incident: untouched 4-question picker, phone sent 4 valid selects, all 5 frames daemon-acked in 82ms, only Q1 advanced, no tool_result — root cause: protocol-v3 `input-ok` proves `pty.write()` acceptance, NOT Claude TUI consumption; burst frames land during the picker's question-transition unmount window and are dropped. Worse failure mode PROVEN: a 250ms-gap run produced a tool_result with EVERY answer silently misattributed one question over (committed, no error) — small pacing constants are actively dangerous, lost answers are the good case. N=4 sweep on real 2.1.228 (tmp/pty-proof-4q/proof-4q.mjs): burst 0/2, 100ms 1/3, 250ms 2/3 (1 silent-wrong), 500ms 3/3, 1000ms 3/3. Fix in answer.ts `injectSequence`: `ANSWER_INTER_FRAME_DELAY_MS = 500` state-blind sleep after every acked non-final v3 frame (never after final, never on the v2 single legacy frame); injected `delay` dep (production wires crypto `sleep`, assertAnswerDeps fails loud unwired); a REJECTING timer propagates fail-loud (never bursts the remainder — outer handler classifies claimed→failed / in_flight→unconfirmed); dynamic deadline = 10s + (frames-1)×500ms derived from actual frame count (do NOT duplicate encoder limits in the injector — /simplify altitude finding removed the 321-frame mirror); deadline checked and lease renewed after each sleep immediately before next write; terminal lock held across sleeps (documented on LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS). Review trap: FEATURES.md said 1000ms while code said 500ms — reviewers flagged manifest-vs-code drift on the one safety number; keep them lockstep. T3 Code explored (pingdotgg/t3code): answers AskUserQuestion atomically via Agent SDK canUseTool, no PTY answer path, nothing to port. POST-INSTALL E2E on installed 1.20.2: fresh emulator identity paired (never reuse phone identity), 4-question canary through the real bridge → confirmed in 2025ms (=4×500ms gaps), tool_result 4/4 correctly attributed, resolved with phone provenance after tool_result. Residue: 2 dead emulator device records in device store (keys unrecoverable, inert; no per-device revoke exists — only revokeAllDevices which would nuke the phone); PROVEN_AGAINST still 2.1.226 vs installed 2.1.228 (drift warning only, answers work). Physical phone/watch/screen-off/lock-screen spot-check is user-side.","+"," Related: [[superset-companion-planning]], [[companion-durability-moved-to-hostdb]], [[companion-verification-recipes-and-traps]]."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30a5a077-8145-45ea-a856-db4d3f14f3b3","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
