{"parentUuid":"2ea8ecb2-2413-49b6-a5ba-0ba2da962656","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"52cce213-cad2-4029-85c1-39d16bf458df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"The companion app now tells me when a chat has finished, but it doesn't tell me which chat. It should tell me the name on the left, for example:\n- the name of the project (e.g. PX V1 apps)\n- the name of the worktree/space (eg super simplify)\n- the tab name (if there are multiple tabs) (eg Claude Resume)\nThese should be in the notification, and if I open that up I can see them there too. Make sense? asksuer tool always to perfect the ux"},"uuid":"7c33a9d4-052a-4151-a393-a955d032109e","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:40:42.819Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"7c33a9d4-052a-4151-a393-a955d032109e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"agent_listing_delta","addedTypes":["architect-fable","architect-opus","architect-sol","claude","code-reviewer-fable","code-reviewer-opus","code-reviewer-sol","codex:codex-rescue","entire-search","Explore","feature-dev:code-architect","feature-dev:code-explorer","feature-dev:code-reviewer","general-purpose","project-structure-validator","sol","statusline-setup","understand-anything:architecture-analyzer","understand-anything:article-analyzer","understand-anything:assemble-reviewer","understand-anything:domain-analyzer","understand-anything:file-analyzer","understand-anything:graph-reviewer","understand-anything:knowledge-graph-guide","understand-anything:project-scanner","understand-anything:tour-builder"],"addedLines":["- architect-fable: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- architect-opus: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- architect-sol: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)","- code-reviewer-fable: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- code-reviewer-opus: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- code-reviewer-sol: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- codex:codex-rescue: Proactively use when Claude Code is stuck, wants a second implementation or diagnosis pass, needs a deeper root-cause investigation, or should hand a substantial coding task to Codex through the shared runtime (Tools: Bash)","- entire-search: Search Entire checkpoint history and transcripts with `entire search --json`. Use proactively when the user asks about previous work, commits, sessions, prompts, or historical context in this repository. (Tools: Bash)","- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: \"medium\" for moderate exploration, \"very thorough\" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- feature-dev:code-architect: Designs feature architectures by analyzing existing codebase patterns and conventions, then providing comprehensive implementation blueprints with specific files to create/modify, component designs, data flows, and build sequences (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- feature-dev:code-explorer: Deeply analyzes existing codebase features by tracing execution paths, mapping architecture layers, understanding patterns and abstractions, and documenting dependencies to inform new development (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- feature-dev:code-reviewer: Reviews code for bugs, logic errors, security vulnerabilities, code quality issues, and adherence to project conventions, using confidence-based filtering to report only high-priority issues that truly matter (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)","- project-structure-validator: Validates project structure against co-location and architecture patterns defined in AGENTS.md (Tools: All tools)","- sol: General-purpose subagent running on Codex GPT-5.6 Sol via the claude-all gateway. Use for heavy implementation, deep debugging, second-opinion reviews, or any Task the orchestrator wants executed by GPT-5.6 Sol instead of a Claude model. Accepts any prompt a general-purpose agent would. (Tools: All tools)","- statusline-setup: Use this agent to configure the user's Claude Code status line setting. (Tools: Read, Edit)","- understand-anything:architecture-analyzer: Analyzes a codebase's file structure, summaries, and import relationships to identify\nlogical architectural layers and assign every file to exactly one layer. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:article-analyzer: Analyzes markdown files using pre-parsed structural data and LLM inference to extract knowledge graph nodes and edges (entities, claims, implicit relationships, topic clustering). (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:assemble-reviewer: Reviews the output of merge-batch-graphs.py for semantic issues the script\ncannot catch. Recovers dropped nodes/edges and fills cross-batch gaps. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:domain-analyzer: Analyzes codebases to extract business domain knowledge — domains, business flows, and process steps. Produces a domain-graph.json that maps how business logic flows through the code. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:file-analyzer: Analyzes batches of source files to produce knowledge graph nodes and edges.\nExtracts file structure, functions, classes, and relationships using a two-phase\napproach: structural extraction script followed by LLM semantic analysis. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:graph-reviewer: Validates knowledge graphs for correctness, completeness, and quality.\nRuns systematic checks and renders approval or rejection decisions. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:knowledge-graph-guide: Use this agent when users need help understanding, querying, or working\nwith an Understand-Anything knowledge graph. Guides users through graph\nstructure, node/edge relationships, layer architecture, tours, and\ndashboard usage. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:project-scanner: Scans a codebase directory to produce a structured inventory of all project files,\ndetected languages, frameworks, import maps, and estimated complexity. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:tour-builder: Designs guided learning tours through codebases, creating 5-15 pedagogical steps\nthat teach project architecture and key concepts in logical order. (Tools: All tools)"],"removedTypes":[],"isInitial":true,"showConcurrencyNote":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a30c59fb-971f-4853-874c-337b19aba3ef","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:40:42.819Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
