{"parentUuid":"5b4321f6-d539-4316-b24f-4c1c15d2ffe8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5aPiBs4pcNbQjjsBXpW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019gTWh4mEvhL9LDnDsZhPJP","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Map companion alert composition","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (Superset fork, Bun monorepo).\n\nTask: Map how companion phone/watch lifecycle alerts (\"chat finished\" / ready-for-review / blocked-question / agent-failure notifications) are composed and delivered, and what naming/context data is available at that point. Search breadth: very thorough.\n\nRecent commits: \"feat(companion): add lifecycle alerts and Kanban completion\", \"fix(companion): preserve repeated lifecycle alerts\", \"feat(desktop): add session lifecycle and companion parity\". Relevant areas likely: packages/host-service/src/companion/ (bridge, alerts, tree endpoint), apps/desktop/src/main/ (agent status dots, pane-map-hook, lifecycle), and whatever pushes to the phone (FCM or similar).\n\nAnswer these:\n1. Where is the alert payload built (file:line) for \"ready for review\" / finished-chat alerts? What fields does it currently carry (title, body, terminal id, etc.)? What exact text does the user currently see?\n2. What identifiers exist at that point in code: project name, workspace/worktree name, tab/pane title? Where does /v1/tree get its node names from — does it already expose project/workspace/tab names, and what are the field names?\n3. How does the alert get from host-service to the phone/watch — push via FCM, via the companion poll, sealed payload? Where's the Android companion app repo/code (in this repo or external)?\n4. Is there an existing mapping from terminal/session id → (project, workspace, tab) names in host-service or desktop main? File:line.\n5. Any constraints: payload size limits, fields deliberately excluded for privacy (\"never log free-text bodies\"), sealed AES-GCM envelope schema versioning, capability negotiation for alert schema.\n\nReturn: concise findings with file:line references, current alert schema (field names), available name sources, and where the change would need to happen (host-service only vs desktop + host-service vs companion app too)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59623,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1253,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":438},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1253,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59623},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3e964f66-917b-4f72-8207-7206b11e8837","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:41:33.535Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
