{"parentUuid":"488ef68a-2c07-4bbd-88e1-b246d9a93268","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5bLL3PAftjELrQJdQFJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VWqRP7wiFp9nJr6zn3S3DY","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md","old_string":"### 2. Sealed names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus `t` (opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`) and `n` = base64url AES-256-GCM ciphertext, sealed **per device key** (per-device send, no shared blob).\n- Plaintext = JSON `{ p: projectName, w: workspaceName, t?: tabTitle, c: tabCount }`, name fields length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis), **padded to one fixed size** before sealing so ciphertext length leaks nothing.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `n` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but must be base64url of the exact fixed sealed length; all other keys unchanged rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (user-approved): plaintext content never; fixed-length per-device sealed ciphertext allowed.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that field; nothing resolvable → omit `n` entirely (phone falls back to generic). Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same `n` (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.","new_string":"### 2. Plaintext names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus:\n  - `t` — opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`\n  - `pn` — project name (plaintext)\n  - `wn` — workspace name (plaintext)\n  - `tn` — tab title (plaintext, optional)\n  - `tc` — workspace tab count (digits)\n- Name values: UTF-8, length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis, e.g. ≤64 chars each), no control chars/newlines.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `pn/wn/tn` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but bounded length and control-char-free; all other keys keep existing rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (explicit owner decision, 2026-08-16): project/workspace/tab names may ride pushes in plaintext; question text, option text, file paths, and all other free text remain banned. The assertion still throws on any other free-text key.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that key; phone falls back per-field. Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same name keys (and `t` if absent) under the same rules."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":79882,"output_tokens":1182,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1182,"cache_read_input_tokens":79882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c85ff3ea-a873-40ee-93ac-bfb04e443372","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:53:45.356Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"c85ff3ea-a873-40ee-93ac-bfb04e443372","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"52cce213-cad2-4029-85c1-39d16bf458df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWqRP7wiFp9nJr6zn3S3DY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e4747f50-9b81-4d86-8a55-66ba3c3b6c70","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:53:46.005Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md","oldString":"### 2. Sealed names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus `t` (opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`) and `n` = base64url AES-256-GCM ciphertext, sealed **per device key** (per-device send, no shared blob).\n- Plaintext = JSON `{ p: projectName, w: workspaceName, t?: tabTitle, c: tabCount }`, name fields length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis), **padded to one fixed size** before sealing so ciphertext length leaks nothing.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `n` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but must be base64url of the exact fixed sealed length; all other keys unchanged rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (user-approved): plaintext content never; fixed-length per-device sealed ciphertext allowed.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that field; nothing resolvable → omit `n` entirely (phone falls back to generic). Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same `n` (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.","newString":"### 2. Plaintext names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus:\n  - `t` — opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`\n  - `pn` — project name (plaintext)\n  - `wn` — workspace name (plaintext)\n  - `tn` — tab title (plaintext, optional)\n  - `tc` — workspace tab count (digits)\n- Name values: UTF-8, length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis, e.g. ≤64 chars each), no control chars/newlines.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `pn/wn/tn` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but bounded length and control-char-free; all other keys keep existing rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (explicit owner decision, 2026-08-16): project/workspace/tab names may ride pushes in plaintext; question text, option text, file paths, and all other free text remain banned. The assertion still throws on any other free-text key.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that key; phone falls back per-field. Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same name keys (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.","originalFile":"# (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) — companion alerts name their chat\n\n## Goal / approved UX (user-decided, do not re-litigate)\n\nEvery companion phone/watch alert — ready-for-review (`g`), agent-error (`e`), and blocked-question — identifies its chat:\n\n- **Title:** `<Project name> · <Workspace name>` (e.g. `PX V1 apps · super simplify`)\n- **Body:** `<Tab name> — <event text>` (e.g. `Claude Resume — finished, ready for review`)\n- Tab name **omitted when the workspace has only one tab** (body then just event text).\n- **Watch shows the same text as the phone.**\n- Expanded notification shows the same names (automatic with title/body).\n- **Names travel as PLAINTEXT keys inside the FCM push** — user explicitly waived the Google-visibility concern for these three names (\"i dont care if google sees it\", confirmed via AskUser 2026-08-16). Notification is self-contained — full names even if the PC is asleep/unreachable when it lands. Question text and all other free text remain banned from pushes; only project/workspace/tab names are waived.\n- Fallback: name keys absent/malformed → today's exact generic strings. Never drop or delay the alert.\n\n## Current state (verified by exploration)\n\n- Push is opaque 5-key `PushDataV2` (`packages/host-service/src/companion/types.ts:1356`): `v,k,i,w,x`. No terminal handle, no names. Text composed on-device from `k` alone (`superset-companion/app-phone/.../CompanionNotifications.kt:221`, `app-watch/.../LifecycleAlertPresentation.kt:50`).\n- Hard privacy rule `push.ts:5-8`: no free text ever in FCM; enforced by throwing `assertPushDataSafe` (`push.ts:345`), value pattern `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,43}$` (`config.ts:288`), 160-byte cap (`config.ts:286`), closed per-version key set (`push.ts:298`).\n- Host-service CAN resolve project+workspace names from `hostWorkspaceId` at mint time: `HostDbReader.findWorkspace` (`read-api.ts:191`), `listProjects` (`read-api.ts:182`); lifecycle manager already holds a `HostDbReader` (`companion/index.ts:702`).\n- Real tab titles exist ONLY in desktop main renderer state (`apps/desktop/src/main/lib/notifications/utils.ts:73`, priority `tab.userTitle > tab.name > pane.name`); `host.db` has no terminal title (`read-api.ts:694`).\n- Alert mint/send: `lifecycle-alerts.ts:448` / `:388`; retry backoff 30s→15min; broadcast per registered device (`push.ts:1600`).\n- Companion app is sibling repo `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion` (Kotlin: `app-phone`, `app-watch`, `core`, normative `PROTOCOL.md`). Phone relays to watch over Wear Data Layer `/companion/v1/lifecycle` (`WearProtocol.kt:77`), 60 KiB cap.\n\n## Changes — repo 1: fork-superset-windows-arm64\n\n### 1. Desktop → host-service tab-title plumbing\nDesktop main pushes per-terminal display context to host-service so it is available at alert send time:\n`{ hostTerminalId → { tabTitle: string, workspaceTabCount: number } }`\n- Source: renderer `tabsState` already mirrored into desktop main (`main.ts:360`); title priority per `notifications/utils.ts:73`.\n- Transport: extend the existing desktop→host-service companion-lifecycle sink path (`packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/notifications/companion-lifecycle-sink.ts`) or a sibling endpoint; keep host-side store in memory keyed by terminal id (staleness acceptable: names are a snapshot).\n- The omit-tab decision belongs to the client: send `tabTitle` + `workspaceTabCount`; phone omits tab when count < 2.\n\n### 2. Sealed names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus `t` (opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`) and `n` = base64url AES-256-GCM ciphertext, sealed **per device key** (per-device send, no shared blob).\n- Plaintext = JSON `{ p: projectName, w: workspaceName, t?: tabTitle, c: tabCount }`, name fields length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis), **padded to one fixed size** before sealing so ciphertext length leaks nothing.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `n` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but must be base64url of the exact fixed sealed length; all other keys unchanged rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (user-approved): plaintext content never; fixed-length per-device sealed ciphertext allowed.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that field; nothing resolvable → omit `n` entirely (phone falls back to generic). Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same `n` (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.\n\n### 3. Rollout ordering (hard requirement)\nOld phone app silently ignores unknown `v` → shipping host v3 first kills all alerts. **Phone/watch app must be updated and installed BEFORE the desktop/host build.** Phone app v-next accepts both v2 and v3. No dual-send.\n\n### 4. Gates / hygiene\n- `FEATURES.md`: add `(ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES)` marker + companion-bridge row update; marker gate must stay green.\n- Tests (host-service): v3 schema assertions incl. `n` shape + fixed length; seal/pad round-trip; padding uniformity across name lengths; name-resolution fallback tiers; question-push parity; tab-title store update/eviction.\n- Never log names/plaintext blobs in host-service or repair logs.\n- `/simplify` before commit; `/code-review` low; commit conventional; push main; full Windows ARM64 GH build; install only on explicit user authorization.\n\n## Changes — repo 2: superset-companion\n\n### 5. Phone\n- `LifecyclePush.kt`: accept `v:\"2\"` AND `v:\"3\"`; parse `t`, `n`; decrypt `n` with device key; strict JSON parse; on ANY failure → generic path (never crash, never drop).\n- `CompanionNotifications.kt` compose:\n  - ready: title `P · W`, body `T — finished, ready for review` (no tab: `Finished — ready for review`)\n  - error: title `P · W`, body `T — stopped on an error` (no tab: `Stopped on an error`); keep channels/vibration semantics\n  - question: same title pattern; body prefixes tab before the existing question presentation\n  - fallback: byte-for-byte today's strings.\n- Question-alert path gets the same treatment wherever its notification is composed.\n\n### 6. Watch\n- Extend `WatchLifecycleAlert` (`WearProtocol.kt:360`) with decrypted plaintext names (phone↔watch Data Layer is inside the trust boundary; 60 KiB cap trivially satisfied). Watch renders identical text; missing fields → current generic strings. Old watch ignores unknown fields.\n\n### 7. Protocol\n- `PROTOCOL.md`: normative v3 section — key set, sealing (key, nonce rules, padding size), fallback ladder, v2 coexistence, rollout note.\n\n## Verification\n- Unit tests both repos (incl. Kotlin parse/decrypt/fallback).\n- E2E on installed build with a FRESH emulator identity (never the physical phone's identity): trigger a real ready alert → notification title/body carry correct names; kill host-service before delivery → names still complete (sealed in push); v2-only simulated push → generic fallback; single-tab workspace → tab omitted; watch relay carries names.\n- Existing invariants untouched: pairing/auth, nonce replay, protocol 0 read-only, question path, (ANSWER-FRAME-PACING).\n\n## Open items for architects\n- Best transport for tab-title plumbing (reuse lifecycle sink vs new tRPC route) and eviction/staleness policy.\n- Exact padded plaintext size budget (names are UTF-8; emoji in tab titles).\n- Whether question pushes share `buildLifecyclePushData` or have a separate builder needing parallel edits.\n- Nonce/AAD scheme for the sealed blob consistent with existing sealed-transport code (reuse `crypto.ts` seal primitives).\n- Phone app build/install flow for the user (how is superset-companion currently built/installed?).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":13,"newStart":30,"newLines":18,"lines":[" - Transport: extend the existing desktop→host-service companion-lifecycle sink path (`packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/notifications/companion-lifecycle-sink.ts`) or a sibling endpoint; keep host-side store in memory keyed by terminal id (staleness acceptable: names are a snapshot)."," - The omit-tab decision belongs to the client: send `tabTitle` + `workspaceTabCount`; phone omits tab when count < 2."," ","-### 2. Sealed names in push (`PushDataV3`)","-- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus `t` (opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`) and `n` = base64url AES-256-GCM ciphertext, sealed **per device key** (per-device send, no shared blob).","-- Plaintext = JSON `{ p: projectName, w: workspaceName, t?: tabTitle, c: tabCount }`, name fields length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis), **padded to one fixed size** before sealing so ciphertext length leaks nothing.","-- `assertPushDataSafe`: `n` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but must be base64url of the exact fixed sealed length; all other keys unchanged rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).","-- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (user-approved): plaintext content never; fixed-length per-device sealed ciphertext allowed.","-- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that field; nothing resolvable → omit `n` entirely (phone falls back to generic). Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.","-- Blocked-question pushes gain the same `n` (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.","+### 2. Plaintext names in push (`PushDataV3`)","+- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus:","+  - `t` — opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`","+  - `pn` — project name (plaintext)","+  - `wn` — workspace name (plaintext)","+  - `tn` — tab title (plaintext, optional)","+  - `tc` — workspace tab count (digits)","+- Name values: UTF-8, length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis, e.g. ≤64 chars each), no control chars/newlines.","+- `assertPushDataSafe`: `pn/wn/tn` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but bounded length and control-char-free; all other keys keep existing rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).","+- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (explicit owner decision, 2026-08-16): project/workspace/tab names may ride pushes in plaintext; question text, option text, file paths, and all other free text remain banned. The assertion still throws on any other free-text key.","+- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that key; phone falls back per-field. Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.","+- Blocked-question pushes gain the same name keys (and `t` if absent) under the same rules."," "," ### 3. Rollout ordering (hard requirement)"," Old phone app silently ignores unknown `v` → shipping host v3 first kills all alerts. **Phone/watch app must be updated and installed BEFORE the desktop/host build.** Phone app v-next accepts both v2 and v3. No dual-send."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c85ff3ea-a873-40ee-93ac-bfb04e443372","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
