{"parentUuid":"6976aec3-e3ec-4d62-9bd6-1c95215b7159","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5bd4XCxN75aw9WTFWVg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015DWjVjkVjaULXP4wCX2uKv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Map alert retraction machinery","prompt":"Two repos:\n1. C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 — host-service companion code in packages/host-service/src/companion/ (push.ts, lifecycle-alerts.ts, types.ts, question-store.ts, read-api.ts, config.ts, index.ts), desktop lifecycle events in apps/desktop/src/main/lib/agent-jsonl-watcher/pane-map-hook.ts and packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/notifications/.\n2. C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion — Kotlin phone/watch companion (app-phone, app-watch, core, PROTOCOL.md).\n\nQuestion: what NOTIFICATION RETRACTION machinery exists today, end to end? Search breadth: very thorough. Specifically:\n\n1. Question alerts: when a pending Claude question is answered or cleared on desktop, is there any push/signal that makes the PHONE cancel its posted notification? And the WATCH? Find the push kind/key, phone-side NotificationManager.cancel call sites, and watch relay path (Wear Data Layer messages) if any. File:line.\n2. Lifecycle alerts (`g` ready / `e` error): the held-alert struct in lifecycle-alerts.ts has a `superseded` field — what sets it, and does supersession ever reach the phone/watch to retract an already-delivered notification? Or is it purely host-side send suppression?\n3. What desktop-side event exists for \"user read the chat / green dot cleared\" — does pane-map-hook.ts (or the renderer→main state flow) emit anything when the ready-for-review state clears (user focused/opened the chat)? The green \"ready\" axis reportedly lives in renderer storage the bridge can't reach — find where green-dot CLEAR happens and whether it's already forwarded anywhere (e.g. companion-lifecycle-sink).\n4. Phone/watch notification identity: how are posted notifications keyed (notification id / tag) — could a later push target and cancel a specific earlier one? Watch: how would the phone tell the watch to dismiss (existing message paths in WearProtocol.kt)?\n5. FCM: any existing use of collapse keys / data-message cancellation patterns in push.ts?\n\nReturn concise findings with file:line, and a verdict per surface: question-phone, question-watch, lifecycle-phone, lifecycle-watch — retraction EXISTS / PARTIAL / ABSENT, and if absent what the minimal-fit addition would be given existing patterns.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":87305,"output_tokens":1926,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":904},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1926,"cache_read_input_tokens":87305,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"52cd6879-7b2a-4be5-8dbf-73e3747f9e16","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:57:52.835Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
