rvice.kt:151-170`.\n- `CompanionNotifications.retract(questionId)` → `manager.cancel(questionId, ID_QUESTION)` — `CompanionNotifications.kt:281-283`.\n- Foreground sweep (best-effort backstop, PROTOCOL §13.3) — `CompanionNotifications.kt:293-303`; driven by `SessionViewModel.sweepNotifications()` — `SessionViewModel.kt:219-231`, called on foreground/refresh (`:181`, `:214`).\n\n**Watch relay path**:\n- Phone → watch `WearPaths.QUESTION_RESOLVED = \"/companion/v1/question/resolved\"` — `WearProtocol.kt:49`; payload `WatchQuestionResolved` — `WearProtocol.kt:331`.\n- Send: `WatchLink.sendResolved` — `WatchLink.kt:63-64`; `WatchBridge.pushResolved` — `WatchBridge.kt:184`, `:445`.\n- Watch receive → `onResolved` → `QuestionNotifier.cancel(this, info.questionId)` — `CompanionWearListenerService.kt:51, 71-76`.\n- Also cancels on confirmed answer (`:78-83`), on notification tap (`MainActivity.kt:87`), on dismiss (`MainActivity.kt:234`).\n- Sweep results are relayed to the watch too — `SessionViewModel.kt:227-231`.\n\n## 2. Lifecycle `superseded` — host-side send suppression ONLY\n\n- Field decl + doc — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:62-68` (\"A `sending` alert cannot be un-sent, but it must not be RE-held on failure\").\n- Set by `supersede(hostTerminalId, reason)` — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:429-446`. `held` → deleted outright; `sending` → flagged `superseded: true`.\n- Called from exactly one place: `record()` when `outcome === \"progress\" || \"session-end\"` — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:532-534`.\n- Consumed only in `holdAfterFailure` — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:353-360`: drops a *failed* delivery instead of re-holding it.\n- Initialized `false` at `mint` — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:470`.\n\n**Verdict**: purely host-side. It suppresses an unsent/retryable alert. Once `sendLifecycleAlert` succeeds, nothing reaches phone or watch. Explicitly by design:\n- `push.ts:500-511` — \"THERE IS NO RETRACTION FOR THESE AND THAT IS DELIBERATE… 'this turn ended' … do not stop being true because the user later opened the app.\"\n- PROTOCOL.md ~2183 — \"Lifecycle alerts are not retracted (§13.3)… the alert simply expires or is dismissed.\"\n- PROTOCOL.md ~2124 — \"the wrist keeps its own notification and the phone cannot retract it\".\n- Push-kind sets are closed per version: v1 `[\"q\",\"r\"]`, v2 `[\"g\",\"e\"]` — `push.ts:303-306`. No v2 retract kind exists; adding one requires widening `PUSH_KINDS_BY_VERSION` (v2 key set has no `n`, so a v2 retract fits the existing `[\"v\",\"k\",\"i\",\"w\",\"x\"]` shape unchanged).\n- `ALERT_TTL_MS = 6h` — `lifecycle-alerts.ts:11`. That is the only thing that ends a delivered alert host-side.\n\n## 3. Green-dot CLEAR — exists, renderer-only, forwarded NOWHERE\n\n- `pane-map-hook.ts` derives `lifecycle_outcome` from hook events only — `pane-map-hook.ts:2388-2405`. Mapping: `SessionEnd`→`session-end`, `StopFailure`→`hold`/`failed`, `Failed`→`failed`, `Start`→`progress`, `Stop`/`SubagentStop`→`ready`. Fields attached at `:2417-2419`.\n- Explicit comment at `pane-map-hook.ts:2380-2381`: **\"Only hook-originated events carry it; administrative status clears never pass through this producer.\"**\n- Host route: `notifications.ts:298-306` → `forwardCompanionLifecycle` → `companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:57-87` → `sink.record`. Only the 5 hook outcomes exist (`companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:9, 27`).\n- Green CLEAR actually lives in renderer zustand:\n  - `useClearActivePaneAttention` — `useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:35-46`. Fires when the user focuses a pane whose status is `review` → `markTerminalSeen(terminalId, binding.lastEventAt)`.\n  - `markTerminalSeen` impl — `stores/v2-notifications/store.ts:250-276`. Bumps `terminalSeenAt` (monotonic) and drops the source's `review` entry.\n  - Other callers: `useMarkWorkspaceTerminalsSeen` (sidebar \"mark read\") — `useV2NotificationStatus.ts:94-105`; resync — `resyncAgentStatus.ts:361`.\n- Confirms `types.ts:524-529`: *\"There is no `green` / 'ready for review' and there never will be: the review axis lives in renderer storage the bridge cannot reach.\"*\n\n**No IPC/tRPC forwarding of the clear exists.** `markTerminalSeen` has zero call sites outside `src/renderer`. Nothing reaches `companion-lifecycle-sink`.\n\n## 4. Notification identity — both surfaces are addressable\n\n| Surface | Question | Lifecycle |\n|---|---|---|\n| Phone | tag = `questionId`, id = `ID_QUESTION` (`CompanionNotifications.kt:343`, cancel `:282`) | tag = `push.eventId` (= alertId), id = `ID_LIFECYCLE` = 1003 (`CompanionNotifications.kt:215, 383`) |\n| Watch | `questionId.hashCode()` (`QuestionNotifier.kt:134`, cancel `:59-61`) | `\"lifecycle:$eventId\".hashCode()` (`LifecycleAlertPresentation.kt:81`, notify `LifecycleNotifier.kt:80, 120`) |\n\nYes — a later push could target and cancel a specific earlier one. The alertId is already the notification identity on both surfaces (PROTOCOL.md §13.4: \"That same id is the notification's identity on the phone and on the watch\"). `LifecycleNotifier` has **no** `cancel` function — only `notify` (`wear/notify/` grep: `QuestionNotifier.cancel` exists, `LifecycleNotifier` has none). `CompanionNotifications` has no `cancelLifecycle` (only `retract`, `cancelLostContact` at `:278`).\n\n**Watch dismiss path**: no lifecycle-dismiss Wear path exists. `WearPaths` is closed — `WearProtocol.kt:41-78`; `LIFECYCLE` (`:77`) is one-way notify-only, and its doc explicitly forbids reusing `QUESTION_RESOLVED` for it (`:69-76`). Watch listener `when(event.path)` has no lifecycle-cancel branch — `CompanionWearListenerService.kt:46-57`.\n\n## 5. FCM collapse keys / data-message cancellation\n\n- `collapse_key` is **mandatory** and asserted `=== data.i` — `push.ts:419-423`, built at `push.ts:429-441`. Applies to v1 and v2 alike.\n- Retraction reuses the question's collapse key so an undelivered original queued at FCM is *replaced* rather than delivered-then-cancelled — `push.ts:1108-1113`, PROTOCOL.md §13.3.\n- Data-only, no `message.notification` block; envelope key set closed to `[\"token\",\"android\",\"data\"]` and android to `[\"priority\",\"ttl\",\"collapse_key\"]` — `push.ts:307-308`.\n- No other cancellation pattern (no `apns`, no `webpush`, no FCM \"delete notification\" API use).\n- Dedicated test file exists for the question path: `packages/host-service/src/companion/push-retract.test.ts`. No lifecycle-retraction test.\n\n---\n\n## Verdicts\n\n| Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **question-phone** | **EXISTS** | `k:\"r\"` push + `manager.cancel(questionId, ID_QUESTION)` + foreground sweep backstop |\n| **question-watch** | **EXISTS** | phone relays `QUESTION_RESOLVED` → `QuestionNotifier.cancel`; plus tap/dismiss/answer-confirmed cancels |\n| **lifecycle-phone** | **ABSENT** | `superseded` never leaves the host. Nothing cancels `(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` |\n| **lifecycle-watch** | **ABSENT** | No Wear path, no `LifecycleNotifier.cancel`. PROTOCOL explicitly says the phone cannot retract the wrist copy |\n\n### Minimal-fit additions if you want lifecycle retraction\n\nEach mirrors an existing pattern exactly; no new concepts.\n\n**A. Host → phone (v2 retract kind)**\n1. Add `\"c\"` to `PUSH_KINDS_BY_VERSION[\"2\"]` — `push.ts:305`. v2's key set `[\"v\",\"k\",\"i\",\"w\",\"x\"]` needs no change (no `n`), unlike v1's retract which had to carry `n:\"0\"`.\n2. Add `buildLifecycleRetractPushData` beside `buildLifecyclePushData` (`push.ts:523`), stamping `x = now + RETRACT_TTL_MS` — same (RETRACT-TTL) reasoning as `buildRetractPushData` (`push.ts:481`), *not* the alert's original expiry.\n3. Add `PushSender.sendLifecycleRetraction(alertId, workspaceId)` enqueued on `enqueueOrdered(alertId, …)` — the chain is already keyed by `string` for exactly this (`push.ts:1406-1411`). Same `collapse_key` (= alertId) then overtakes an undelivered original for free.\n4. `lifecycle-alerts.ts`: keep a bounded `delivered` map (alertId → workspaceHandle, sentAtMs) mirroring `push.ts`'s `sent` map, and have `supersede` (`:429-446`) fire the retraction for `state === \"sent\"` entries rather than only deleting/flagging. This is where `superseded` stops being purely internal.\n\n**B. Phone client**\n5. `PushKind` + `routePush` gain a `LIFECYCLE_RETRACT` branch (`PushRouting.kt:57-68` shape) → `notifications.cancelLifecycle(eventId)` = `manager.cancel(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` — one line beside `retract` at `CompanionNotifications.kt:281`.\n6. Release the `SeenLifecycleEvents` claim for that id (`LifecycleRouting.kt:87` `gate.release`) so a genuinely later redelivery is not swallowed.\n\n**C. Phone → watch**\n7. New `WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS = \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\"` — `WearProtocol.kt:78`, payload `{eventId}` (mirrors `WatchQuestionRequest`, `:496`). Its own path for the reason stated at `WearProtocol.kt:69-76`.\n8. `WatchLink.sendLifecycleDismiss` beside `:81`; `WatchBridge.pushLifecycleDismiss` beside `pushLifecycle`.\n9. Watch: `when` branch (`CompanionWearListenerService.kt:54`) → new `LifecycleNotifier.cancel(context, eventId)` calling `NotificationManagerCompat.from(context).cancel(LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId(eventId))` — byte-for-byte the shape of `QuestionNotifier.cancel` (`:59-61`).\n\n**D. The green-dot problem (item 3) is the real blocker for the useful case**\n\nA/B/C give you retraction on *supersession* (a new work cycle started). They do **not** give you \"user read the chat → cancel the ready alert\", because that signal does not exist outside the renderer. Minimal fit:\n\n- Add a renderer→main→host-service forward at `markTerminalSeen` (`store.ts:250`) or, more narrowly, at `useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:44` (the focus-driven clear only — the sidebar bulk \"mark read\" is a different intent).\n- Route it through a **new** outcome, e.g. `\"seen\"`, in `companionLifecycleFields` (`companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:8-10`) and `CompanionLifecycleEvent.outcome` (`:27`). It must **not** go through `pane-map-hook.ts` — that producer is hook-only by design (`:2380`) and mints a fresh `producerEventId` per invocation; a renderer clear needs its own id or the sink's dedupe window (`alreadyApplied`, `lifecycle-alerts.ts:495`) will mis-handle it.\n- In `record()` (`lifecycle-alerts.ts:525`), treat `\"seen\"` like `\"progress\"`: call `supersede(hostTerminalId, \"seen\")`, which with change A.4 now also retracts delivered alerts.\n\nNote the design tension worth surfacing before building: `types.ts:524-529` and `push.ts:500-511` both argue the ready alert is a fact about a past instant that does not stop being true. \"User opened the chat\" is the one input that genuinely falsifies *\"there is something waiting for you to review\"* — so this is an argued change to a stated invariant, not a gap-fill.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>134945</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>55</tool_uses><duration_ms>273052</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"20e6591a-43c4-426b-bb49-c7d2b60208ef","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:03:44.119Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"20e6591a-43c4-426b-bb49-c7d2b60208ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5c9UQEhca8h2JUNpmXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"output_tokens":3054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":551},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3054,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d1c1b30d-cf17-4c2f-92ff-09074c15e36f","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:04:24.101Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d1c1b30d-cf17-4c2f-92ff-09074c15e36f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5c9UQEhca8h2JUNpmXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retraction mapping is back — good news and one real gap:\n\n- **Question notifications already retract end-to-end today** (answer/clear on desktop → retract push → phone cancels → watch cancels, plus a foreground sweep backstop). Nothing to build there; just E2E-verify.\n- **Finished/error notifications have zero retraction** — deliberately, per the current protocol (\"a finished alert doesn't stop being true\"). Your requirement overrides that: needs a new v2 retract push kind, a phone cancel branch, a new Wear dismiss path, and a watch cancel function — all mirroring the question path's existing shapes.\n- **The \"you read the chat\" signal never leaves the renderer** — the green-dot clear lives in renderer state with no forwarding. Needs a renderer → main → host-service forward as a new `\"seen\"` lifecycle outcome that triggers the retraction.\n\nFinalizing the plan's retraction section with those specifics:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"output_tokens":3054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":551},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3054,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"acee6782-75b9-462f-9f67-713bd449a32d","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:04:27.762Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"acee6782-75b9-462f-9f67-713bd449a32d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5c9UQEhca8h2JUNpmXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VGauahNE8Sc1sGPUTmoeAd","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md","old_string":"### 8. Retraction (both repos — details pending machinery exploration)\n- Desktop detects clear events: question answered/cleared; green dot cleared (chat read). Forward to host-service alongside the existing lifecycle event flow.\n- Host-service sends a retraction push targeting the original alert id (`i`) / question handle.\n- Phone cancels the matching posted notification (keyed by id/tag) and relays a dismiss to the watch over the Wear Data Layer; watch cancels its notification.\n- Retraction is best-effort: a failed/undelivered retraction never blocks anything and the notification still expires per existing TTL. A retraction for an unknown/never-posted notification is a silent no-op.\n- If existing machinery already covers part of this (question path, `superseded`), extend it rather than duplicating.","new_string":"### 8. Retraction (grounded in verified machinery, 2026-08-16 exploration)\n\n**Question alerts: retraction already EXISTS end-to-end — do not rebuild.** `k:\"r\"` push (`push.ts:481`), choke point `onSettled → sender.cancelPending` (`index.ts:601-616`), phone `PushRouting.kt:58-62` → `CompanionNotifications.retract` + watch relay `QUESTION_RESOLVED` → `QuestionNotifier.cancel`, foreground sweep backstop. E2E-verify only.\n\n**Lifecycle (`g`/`e`) alerts: retraction is ABSENT on both surfaces and the current protocol forbids it deliberately** (`push.ts:500-511`, PROTOCOL §13.3 \"Lifecycle alerts are not retracted\"). This plan overrides that invariant by explicit user requirement — rewrite those statements, don't work around them. Build, mirroring the question path's exact shapes:\n\nA. **Host → phone (v2 retract kind `\"c\"`):**\n   - Add `\"c\"` to `PUSH_KINDS_BY_VERSION[\"2\"]` (`push.ts:305`); v2 key shape works unchanged.\n   - `buildLifecycleRetractPushData` beside `buildLifecyclePushData` (`push.ts:523`), `x = now + RETRACT_TTL_MS` (same (RETRACT-TTL) reasoning as `push.ts:481`, NOT the alert's original expiry).\n   - `PushSender.sendLifecycleRetraction(alertId, workspaceId)` on `enqueueOrdered(alertId, …)` (`push.ts:1406`); same `collapse_key` (= alertId) so an undelivered original gets replaced at FCM for free.\n   - `lifecycle-alerts.ts`: bounded `delivered` map (alertId → handle, sentAtMs); `supersede` (`:429-446`) fires retraction for `state === \"sent\"` entries instead of only flagging. Retraction is best-effort; TTL (6h) remains the backstop; unknown-id retraction is a silent no-op (matches `push.ts:1905` pattern).\n   - NOTE: retract kind is v2 (works against the CURRENT phone app) — independent of the v3 names schema. But ship together; phone-first install rule (§3) covers both.\n\nB. **Phone:** `PushKind.LIFECYCLE_RETRACT` branch in `routePush` (`PushRouting.kt:57-68` shape) → `manager.cancel(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` (one line beside `CompanionNotifications.kt:281`); release the `SeenLifecycleEvents` claim (`LifecycleRouting.kt:87`) so a later genuine redelivery isn't swallowed.\n\nC. **Phone → watch:** new `WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS = \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\"` (own path — `WearProtocol.kt:69-76` forbids reusing `QUESTION_RESOLVED`), payload `{eventId}`; `WatchLink.sendLifecycleDismiss` / `WatchBridge.pushLifecycleDismiss`; watch `when` branch (`CompanionWearListenerService.kt:54`) → new `LifecycleNotifier.cancel` via `LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId(eventId)` — byte-for-byte the `QuestionNotifier.cancel` shape.\n\nD. **Green-dot clear signal (the trigger for the useful case):** the clear lives ONLY in renderer zustand — `markTerminalSeen` (`stores/v2-notifications/store.ts:250-276`), callers: focus-clear (`useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:35-46`), sidebar mark-read (`useV2NotificationStatus.ts:94-105`), resync (`resyncAgentStatus.ts:361`). Rule: **notification lifetime mirrors the green dot** — ANY `markTerminalSeen` that actually drops a `review` entry forwards a clear. Implementation:\n   - Renderer → main → host-service forward at the `markTerminalSeen` site (fire only when a review entry was actually removed).\n   - New outcome `\"seen\"` in `companionLifecycleFields` (`companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:8-10`) + `CompanionLifecycleEvent.outcome` (`:27`). MUST NOT route through `pane-map-hook.ts` (hook-only producer by design, `:2380`); needs its own event id so the sink dedupe window (`alreadyApplied`, `lifecycle-alerts.ts:495`) behaves.\n   - `record()` (`lifecycle-alerts.ts:525`): treat `\"seen\"` like `\"progress\"` → `supersede(hostTerminalId, \"seen\")`, which with A now retracts delivered alerts.\n\nE. **Tests:** extend `push-retract.test.ts` pattern with a lifecycle-retract twin; supersede-fires-retract; seen-outcome plumbing; phone/watch cancel paths; retract-for-unknown-id no-op."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"output_tokens":3054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":551},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3054,"cache_read_input_tokens":93562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8b2002f8-bb72-4759-b032-42422ab005a3","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:04:50.805Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"8b2002f8-bb72-4759-b032-42422ab005a3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cc09ac32-25b9-44fd-847a-3dd71d9c2c0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VGauahNE8Sc1sGPUTmoeAd","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"61a29d6d-8139-460c-8dc6-1464eaa06250","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:04:51.144Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md","oldString":"### 8. Retraction (both repos — details pending machinery exploration)\n- Desktop detects clear events: question answered/cleared; green dot cleared (chat read). Forward to host-service alongside the existing lifecycle event flow.\n- Host-service sends a retraction push targeting the original alert id (`i`) / question handle.\n- Phone cancels the matching posted notification (keyed by id/tag) and relays a dismiss to the watch over the Wear Data Layer; watch cancels its notification.\n- Retraction is best-effort: a failed/undelivered retraction never blocks anything and the notification still expires per existing TTL. A retraction for an unknown/never-posted notification is a silent no-op.\n- If existing machinery already covers part of this (question path, `superseded`), extend it rather than duplicating.","newString":"### 8. Retraction (grounded in verified machinery, 2026-08-16 exploration)\n\n**Question alerts: retraction already EXISTS end-to-end — do not rebuild.** `k:\"r\"` push (`push.ts:481`), choke point `onSettled → sender.cancelPending` (`index.ts:601-616`), phone `PushRouting.kt:58-62` → `CompanionNotifications.retract` + watch relay `QUESTION_RESOLVED` → `QuestionNotifier.cancel`, foreground sweep backstop. E2E-verify only.\n\n**Lifecycle (`g`/`e`) alerts: retraction is ABSENT on both surfaces and the current protocol forbids it deliberately** (`push.ts:500-511`, PROTOCOL §13.3 \"Lifecycle alerts are not retracted\"). This plan overrides that invariant by explicit user requirement — rewrite those statements, don't work around them. Build, mirroring the question path's exact shapes:\n\nA. **Host → phone (v2 retract kind `\"c\"`):**\n   - Add `\"c\"` to `PUSH_KINDS_BY_VERSION[\"2\"]` (`push.ts:305`); v2 key shape works unchanged.\n   - `buildLifecycleRetractPushData` beside `buildLifecyclePushData` (`push.ts:523`), `x = now + RETRACT_TTL_MS` (same (RETRACT-TTL) reasoning as `push.ts:481`, NOT the alert's original expiry).\n   - `PushSender.sendLifecycleRetraction(alertId, workspaceId)` on `enqueueOrdered(alertId, …)` (`push.ts:1406`); same `collapse_key` (= alertId) so an undelivered original gets replaced at FCM for free.\n   - `lifecycle-alerts.ts`: bounded `delivered` map (alertId → handle, sentAtMs); `supersede` (`:429-446`) fires retraction for `state === \"sent\"` entries instead of only flagging. Retraction is best-effort; TTL (6h) remains the backstop; unknown-id retraction is a silent no-op (matches `push.ts:1905` pattern).\n   - NOTE: retract kind is v2 (works against the CURRENT phone app) — independent of the v3 names schema. But ship together; phone-first install rule (§3) covers both.\n\nB. **Phone:** `PushKind.LIFECYCLE_RETRACT` branch in `routePush` (`PushRouting.kt:57-68` shape) → `manager.cancel(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` (one line beside `CompanionNotifications.kt:281`); release the `SeenLifecycleEvents` claim (`LifecycleRouting.kt:87`) so a later genuine redelivery isn't swallowed.\n\nC. **Phone → watch:** new `WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS = \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\"` (own path — `WearProtocol.kt:69-76` forbids reusing `QUESTION_RESOLVED`), payload `{eventId}`; `WatchLink.sendLifecycleDismiss` / `WatchBridge.pushLifecycleDismiss`; watch `when` branch (`CompanionWearListenerService.kt:54`) → new `LifecycleNotifier.cancel` via `LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId(eventId)` — byte-for-byte the `QuestionNotifier.cancel` shape.\n\nD. **Green-dot clear signal (the trigger for the useful case):** the clear lives ONLY in renderer zustand — `markTerminalSeen` (`stores/v2-notifications/store.ts:250-276`), callers: focus-clear (`useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:35-46`), sidebar mark-read (`useV2NotificationStatus.ts:94-105`), resync (`resyncAgentStatus.ts:361`). Rule: **notification lifetime mirrors the green dot** — ANY `markTerminalSeen` that actually drops a `review` entry forwards a clear. Implementation:\n   - Renderer → main → host-service forward at the `markTerminalSeen` site (fire only when a review entry was actually removed).\n   - New outcome `\"seen\"` in `companionLifecycleFields` (`companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:8-10`) + `CompanionLifecycleEvent.outcome` (`:27`). MUST NOT route through `pane-map-hook.ts` (hook-only producer by design, `:2380`); needs its own event id so the sink dedupe window (`alreadyApplied`, `lifecycle-alerts.ts:495`) behaves.\n   - `record()` (`lifecycle-alerts.ts:525`): treat `\"seen\"` like `\"progress\"` → `supersede(hostTerminalId, \"seen\")`, which with A now retracts delivered alerts.\n\nE. **Tests:** extend `push-retract.test.ts` pattern with a lifecycle-retract twin; supersede-fires-retract; seen-outcome plumbing; phone/watch cancel paths; retract-for-unknown-id no-op.","originalFile":"# (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) — companion alerts name their chat\n\n## Goal / approved UX (user-decided, do not re-litigate)\n\nEvery companion phone/watch alert — ready-for-review (`g`), agent-error (`e`), and blocked-question — identifies its chat:\n\n- **Title:** `<Project name> · <Workspace name>` (e.g. `PX V1 apps · super simplify`)\n- **Body:** `<Tab name> — <event text>` (e.g. `Claude Resume — finished, ready for review`)\n- Tab name **omitted when the workspace has only one tab** (body then just event text).\n- **Watch shows the same text as the phone.**\n- Expanded notification shows the same names (automatic with title/body).\n- **Names travel as PLAINTEXT keys inside the FCM push** — user explicitly waived the Google-visibility concern for these three names (\"i dont care if google sees it\", confirmed via AskUser 2026-08-16). Notification is self-contained — full names even if the PC is asleep/unreachable when it lands. Question text and all other free text remain banned from pushes; only project/workspace/tab names are waived.\n- Fallback: name keys absent/malformed → today's exact generic strings. Never drop or delay the alert.\n- **Trigger invariant (user FYI, 2026-08-16):** the \"finished\" notification fires exactly when the sidebar dot would turn GREEN (ready-for-review) — i.e. the existing `g` alert semantics. This feature changes WHAT alerts say, never WHEN they fire.\n- **Retraction (user requirement, 2026-08-16):** when the cause clears on desktop, the phone AND watch notifications must retract (auto-dismiss):\n  - blocked-question alert → retract when the question is answered or cleared (any surface);\n  - ready/finished alert → retract when the green dot clears (user reads/opens the chat).\n  Mechanism to be grounded in the existing retraction machinery (exploration in progress — see §8).\n\n## Current state (verified by exploration)\n\n- Push is opaque 5-key `PushDataV2` (`packages/host-service/src/companion/types.ts:1356`): `v,k,i,w,x`. No terminal handle, no names. Text composed on-device from `k` alone (`superset-companion/app-phone/.../CompanionNotifications.kt:221`, `app-watch/.../LifecycleAlertPresentation.kt:50`).\n- Hard privacy rule `push.ts:5-8`: no free text ever in FCM; enforced by throwing `assertPushDataSafe` (`push.ts:345`), value pattern `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,43}$` (`config.ts:288`), 160-byte cap (`config.ts:286`), closed per-version key set (`push.ts:298`).\n- Host-service CAN resolve project+workspace names from `hostWorkspaceId` at mint time: `HostDbReader.findWorkspace` (`read-api.ts:191`), `listProjects` (`read-api.ts:182`); lifecycle manager already holds a `HostDbReader` (`companion/index.ts:702`).\n- Real tab titles exist ONLY in desktop main renderer state (`apps/desktop/src/main/lib/notifications/utils.ts:73`, priority `tab.userTitle > tab.name > pane.name`); `host.db` has no terminal title (`read-api.ts:694`).\n- Alert mint/send: `lifecycle-alerts.ts:448` / `:388`; retry backoff 30s→15min; broadcast per registered device (`push.ts:1600`).\n- Companion app is sibling repo `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion` (Kotlin: `app-phone`, `app-watch`, `core`, normative `PROTOCOL.md`). Phone relays to watch over Wear Data Layer `/companion/v1/lifecycle` (`WearProtocol.kt:77`), 60 KiB cap.\n\n## Changes — repo 1: fork-superset-windows-arm64\n\n### 1. Desktop → host-service tab-title plumbing\nDesktop main pushes per-terminal display context to host-service so it is available at alert send time:\n`{ hostTerminalId → { tabTitle: string, workspaceTabCount: number } }`\n- Source: renderer `tabsState` already mirrored into desktop main (`main.ts:360`); title priority per `notifications/utils.ts:73`.\n- Transport: extend the existing desktop→host-service companion-lifecycle sink path (`packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/notifications/companion-lifecycle-sink.ts`) or a sibling endpoint; keep host-side store in memory keyed by terminal id (staleness acceptable: names are a snapshot).\n- The omit-tab decision belongs to the client: send `tabTitle` + `workspaceTabCount`; phone omits tab when count < 2.\n\n### 2. Plaintext names in push (`PushDataV3`)\n- New closed key set `v:\"3\"`: existing `k,i,w,x`, plus:\n  - `t` — opaque terminal handle via `deriveHandle`\n  - `pn` — project name (plaintext)\n  - `wn` — workspace name (plaintext)\n  - `tn` — tab title (plaintext, optional)\n  - `tc` — workspace tab count (digits)\n- Name values: UTF-8, length-budgeted (truncate + ellipsis, e.g. ≤64 chars each), no control chars/newlines.\n- `assertPushDataSafe`: `pn/wn/tn` exempt from `PUSH_VALUE_PATTERN` but bounded length and control-char-free; all other keys keep existing rules. Raise `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` to fit (still ≪ FCM 4096).\n- **Deliberately rewrite the `push.ts:5-8` privacy rule** (explicit owner decision, 2026-08-16): project/workspace/tab names may ride pushes in plaintext; question text, option text, file paths, and all other free text remain banned. The assertion still throws on any other free-text key.\n- Name resolution at each send/retry (fresh snapshot): `findWorkspace` + `listProjects` + new tab-title store. Any name unresolvable → omit that key; phone falls back per-field. Resolution failure must NOT block or fail the alert.\n- Blocked-question pushes gain the same name keys (and `t` if absent) under the same rules.\n\n### 3. Rollout ordering (hard requirement)\nOld phone app silently ignores unknown `v` → shipping host v3 first kills all alerts. **Phone/watch app must be updated and installed BEFORE the desktop/host build.** Phone app v-next accepts both v2 and v3. No dual-send.\n\n### 4. Gates / hygiene\n- `FEATURES.md`: add `(ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES)` marker + companion-bridge row update; marker gate must stay green.\n- Tests (host-service): v3 schema assertions incl. name-key bounds + control-char rejection; name-resolution fallback tiers; question-push parity; tab-title store update/eviction.\n- Host-service/repair logs must not log name values (log key presence only).\n- `/simplify` before commit; `/code-review` low; commit conventional; push main; full Windows ARM64 GH build; install only on explicit user authorization.\n\n## Changes — repo 2: superset-companion\n\n### 5. Phone\n- `LifecyclePush.kt`: accept `v:\"2\"` AND `v:\"3\"`; parse `t`, `pn`, `wn`, `tn`, `tc`; on ANY malformed field → generic path for that field (never crash, never drop).\n- `CompanionNotifications.kt` compose:\n  - ready: title `P · W`, body `T — finished, ready for review` (no tab: `Finished — ready for review`)\n  - error: title `P · W`, body `T — stopped on an error` (no tab: `Stopped on an error`); keep channels/vibration semantics\n  - question: same title pattern; body prefixes tab before the existing question presentation\n  - fallback: byte-for-byte today's strings.\n- Question-alert path gets the same treatment wherever its notification is composed.\n\n### 6. Watch\n- Extend `WatchLifecycleAlert` (`WearProtocol.kt:360`) with the name fields (60 KiB cap trivially satisfied). Watch renders identical text; missing fields → current generic strings. Old watch ignores unknown fields.\n\n### 7. Protocol\n- `PROTOCOL.md`: normative v3 section — key set, name-key bounds, fallback ladder, v2 coexistence, rollout note, explicit record of the owner's plaintext-names waiver, retraction semantics.\n\n### 8. Retraction (both repos — details pending machinery exploration)\n- Desktop detects clear events: question answered/cleared; green dot cleared (chat read). Forward to host-service alongside the existing lifecycle event flow.\n- Host-service sends a retraction push targeting the original alert id (`i`) / question handle.\n- Phone cancels the matching posted notification (keyed by id/tag) and relays a dismiss to the watch over the Wear Data Layer; watch cancels its notification.\n- Retraction is best-effort: a failed/undelivered retraction never blocks anything and the notification still expires per existing TTL. A retraction for an unknown/never-posted notification is a silent no-op.\n- If existing machinery already covers part of this (question path, `superseded`), extend it rather than duplicating.\n\n## Verification\n- Unit tests both repos (incl. Kotlin parse/fallback).\n- E2E on installed build with a FRESH emulator identity (never the physical phone's identity): trigger a real ready alert → notification title/body carry correct names; v2-only simulated push → generic fallback; single-tab workspace → tab omitted; watch relay carries names; answering the question on desktop retracts the phone+watch question notification; opening the ready chat (green dot clears) retracts the ready notification.\n- Alert TRIGGER timing unchanged — ready alert fires exactly on green-dot transitions, as today.\n- Existing invariants untouched: pairing/auth, nonce replay, protocol 0 read-only, question path, (ANSWER-FRAME-PACING).\n\n## Open items for architects\n- Best transport for tab-title plumbing (reuse lifecycle sink vs new tRPC route) and eviction/staleness policy.\n- Exact name length budgets (UTF-8; emoji in tab titles; FCM data values are UTF-8 strings — confirm byte-vs-char budgeting).\n- Whether question pushes share `buildLifecyclePushData` or have a separate builder needing parallel edits.\n- Phone app build/install flow for the user (how is superset-companion currently built/installed?).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":74,"oldLines":13,"newStart":74,"newLines":30,"lines":[" ### 7. Protocol"," - `PROTOCOL.md`: normative v3 section — key set, name-key bounds, fallback ladder, v2 coexistence, rollout note, explicit record of the owner's plaintext-names waiver, retraction semantics."," ","-### 8. Retraction (both repos — details pending machinery exploration)","-- Desktop detects clear events: question answered/cleared; green dot cleared (chat read). Forward to host-service alongside the existing lifecycle event flow.","-- Host-service sends a retraction push targeting the original alert id (`i`) / question handle.","-- Phone cancels the matching posted notification (keyed by id/tag) and relays a dismiss to the watch over the Wear Data Layer; watch cancels its notification.","-- Retraction is best-effort: a failed/undelivered retraction never blocks anything and the notification still expires per existing TTL. A retraction for an unknown/never-posted notification is a silent no-op.","-- If existing machinery already covers part of this (question path, `superseded`), extend it rather than duplicating.","+### 8. Retraction (grounded in verified machinery, 2026-08-16 exploration)"," ","+**Question alerts: retraction already EXISTS end-to-end — do not rebuild.** `k:\"r\"` push (`push.ts:481`), choke point `onSettled → sender.cancelPending` (`index.ts:601-616`), phone `PushRouting.kt:58-62` → `CompanionNotifications.retract` + watch relay `QUESTION_RESOLVED` → `QuestionNotifier.cancel`, foreground sweep backstop. E2E-verify only.","+","+**Lifecycle (`g`/`e`) alerts: retraction is ABSENT on both surfaces and the current protocol forbids it deliberately** (`push.ts:500-511`, PROTOCOL §13.3 \"Lifecycle alerts are not retracted\"). This plan overrides that invariant by explicit user requirement — rewrite those statements, don't work around them. Build, mirroring the question path's exact shapes:","+","+A. **Host → phone (v2 retract kind `\"c\"`):**","+   - Add `\"c\"` to `PUSH_KINDS_BY_VERSION[\"2\"]` (`push.ts:305`); v2 key shape works unchanged.","+   - `buildLifecycleRetractPushData` beside `buildLifecyclePushData` (`push.ts:523`), `x = now + RETRACT_TTL_MS` (same (RETRACT-TTL) reasoning as `push.ts:481`, NOT the alert's original expiry).","+   - `PushSender.sendLifecycleRetraction(alertId, workspaceId)` on `enqueueOrdered(alertId, …)` (`push.ts:1406`); same `collapse_key` (= alertId) so an undelivered original gets replaced at FCM for free.","+   - `lifecycle-alerts.ts`: bounded `delivered` map (alertId → handle, sentAtMs); `supersede` (`:429-446`) fires retraction for `state === \"sent\"` entries instead of only flagging. Retraction is best-effort; TTL (6h) remains the backstop; unknown-id retraction is a silent no-op (matches `push.ts:1905` pattern).","+   - NOTE: retract kind is v2 (works against the CURRENT phone app) — independent of the v3 names schema. But ship together; phone-first install rule (§3) covers both.","+","+B. **Phone:** `PushKind.LIFECYCLE_RETRACT` branch in `routePush` (`PushRouting.kt:57-68` shape) → `manager.cancel(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` (one line beside `CompanionNotifications.kt:281`); release the `SeenLifecycleEvents` claim (`LifecycleRouting.kt:87`) so a later genuine redelivery isn't swallowed.","+","+C. **Phone → watch:** new `WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS = \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\"` (own path — `WearProtocol.kt:69-76` forbids reusing `QUESTION_RESOLVED`), payload `{eventId}`; `WatchLink.sendLifecycleDismiss` / `WatchBridge.pushLifecycleDismiss`; watch `when` branch (`CompanionWearListenerService.kt:54`) → new `LifecycleNotifier.cancel` via `LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId(eventId)` — byte-for-byte the `QuestionNotifier.cancel` shape.","+","+D. **Green-dot clear signal (the trigger for the useful case):** the clear lives ONLY in renderer zustand — `markTerminalSeen` (`stores/v2-notifications/store.ts:250-276`), callers: focus-clear (`useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:35-46`), sidebar mark-read (`useV2NotificationStatus.ts:94-105`), resync (`resyncAgentStatus.ts:361`). Rule: **notification lifetime mirrors the green dot** — ANY `markTerminalSeen` that actually drops a `review` entry forwards a clear. Implementation:","+   - Renderer → main → host-service forward at the `markTerminalSeen` site (fire only when a review entry was actually removed).","+   - New outcome `\"seen\"` in `companionLifecycleFields` (`companion-lifecycle-sink.ts:8-10`) + `CompanionLifecycleEvent.outcome` (`:27`). MUST NOT route through `pane-map-hook.ts` (hook-only producer by design, `:2380`); needs its own event id so the sink dedupe window (`alreadyApplied`, `lifecycle-alerts.ts:495`) behaves.","+   - `record()` (`lifecycle-alerts.ts:525`): treat `\"seen\"` like `\"progress\"` → `supersede(hostTerminalId, \"seen\")`, which with A now retracts delivered alerts.","+","+E. **Tests:** extend `push-retract.test.ts` pattern with a lifecycle-retract twin; supersede-fires-retract; seen-outcome plumbing; phone/watch cancel paths; retract-for-unknown-id no-op.","+"," ## Verification"," - Unit tests both repos (incl. Kotlin parse/fallback)."," - E2E on installed build with a FRESH emulator identity (never the physical phone's identity): trigger a real ready alert → notification title/body carry correct names; v2-only simulated push → generic fallback; single-tab workspace → tab omitted; watch relay carries names; answering the question on desktop retracts the phone+watch question notification; opening the ready chat (green dot clears) retracts the ready notification."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b2002f8-bb72-4759-b032-42422ab005a3","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
