{"parentUuid":"464852ef-8dd2-4175-85cf-70a38acc2b5d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5dKjJa8caGT1yZi1Dj6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Opus verdict in: same direction, needs changes — it confirms most of Fable's corrections independently (closed key sets forbid optional keys; retract branch placement; claim-don't-release; retraction storm; no HostDbReader on the manager) and adds fresh load-bearing findings: cold-start resync would mass-retract phone alerts if the seen-forward hooks the store choke point (must hook the two user-intent sites instead), a superseded-mid-flight alert currently lands and never retracts, and FCM's 900s message TTL silently undercuts retraction for phones offline longer than 15 minutes.\n\nTwo genuine divergences between Fable and Opus to settle once Sol reports:\n1. **Question-alert names:** Fable migrates question pushes to v3 with names embedded (self-contained even when the PC is unreachable); Opus keeps the frozen v1 question push untouched and adds names to the sealed fetch only (zero risk to the proven retraction/dedupe path, but an unreachable-PC question notification stays generic).\n2. **Retract push version:** v2 (Fable) vs v3-only (Opus) — v3-only is cleaner since phone-first install is mandatory regardless.\n\nWaiting on Sol's verdict, then I'll reconcile all three into the final plan."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5611,"cache_read_input_tokens":111765,"output_tokens":1845,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5611,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1845,"cache_read_input_tokens":111765,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5611,"cache_creat