{"parentUuid":"98ed7728-41d3-4524-b5b0-ce548fac00aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5eUHEHvQ5vQ7YzzVHWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14417,"cache_read_input_tokens":119505,"output_tokens":5899,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4910},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14417,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5899,"cache_read_input_tokens":119505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14417},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"713234c1-9487-441e-b255-00cb896d8964","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:36:01.347Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"713234c1-9487-441e-b255-00cb896d8964","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5eUHEHvQ5vQ7YzzVHWj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three verdicts are in and they converge on the big things. Reconciling now — the material decisions:\n\n- **Unanimous:** per-(version,kind) closed push schemas with v1/v2 frozen; retract kind `c` lives in v3 only (an old phone would refuse a v2 `c`); on retract the phone must *tombstone* the event id, never release it (else FCM redelivery resurrects a cleared notification); one retraction per alert via a `retracted` state (else every later agent turn re-broadcasts); names resolved fresh inside `send()` on every retry; the seen-signal hooks the two user-intent sites (pane focus + sidebar mark-read), not the store choke point — Opus proved hooking the store would mass-retract your phone alerts on every desktop cold start; renderer talks tRPC straight to host-service (desktop main never had the terminal↔tab mapping at all).\n- **Majority (Fable+Sol) on the one real split:** question alerts also go v3 with names embedded in the push — so even the unreachable-PC contentless question notification is named. Question *retraction* stays on the proven v1 path, untouched.\n- **Sol-only findings adopted:** retract pushes currently would inherit a 15-minute FCM TTL against a 24-hour intent (fixed with per-message TTL — also repairs a latent gap in today's question retraction); a watch that's disconnected when the dismiss arrives needs a persisted retry queue flushed on reconnect; phone and watch generic wording differs today, so the phone now composes one canonical title/body and the watch renders it literally (your \"same text\" answer); deterministic alert IDs so retraction survives a host-service restart.\n- **Overriding Sol on one point (with Fable+Opus):** all v3 keys always present with `\"\"` meaning absent — the existing exact-equality validators on both sides keep working.\n\nWriting the normative blueprint to disk, then launching implementation:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14417,"cache_read_input_tokens":119505,"output_tokens":5899,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4910},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14417,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5899,"cache_read_input_tokens":119505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14417},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ef114402-44a5-4eb0-8eb2-de3bc20abf5b","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:36:11.390Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
