{"parentUuid":"c044ce41-567b-49e9-9f21-cef770d00b5e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14948665 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c35f05ea-6e39-4e8c-a4be-a544db4c1757","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:36:15.442Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"c35f05ea-6e39-4e8c-a4be-a544db4c1757","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5eb8pDsHbtpXp2xM4mF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BXpzihDY3Ln7zaffhoixcd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\FINAL.md","content":"# (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) — FINAL normative spec (post triple-review reconciliation, 2026-08-16)\n\nReconciled from three independent architect reviews (Fable, Opus, Sol) of PLAN.md.\nThis file is NORMATIVE for both repos. PLAN.md holds the approved UX background.\n\nRepos:\n- FORK  = C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\n- COMP  = C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\n\n## 0. Approved UX (fixed — do not re-litigate)\n\n- Title: `<project> · <workspace>` (e.g. `PX V1 apps · super simplify`).\n- Body: `<tab> — <event text>` when tab context applies; else event text alone.\n- Tab shown only when the workspace has ≥2 tabs AND a tab title resolved.\n- Applies to ready (`g`), error (`e`), and blocked-question alerts.\n- Watch shows the SAME text as the phone (phone composes once, watch renders literally).\n- Names are PLAINTEXT in the FCM push — explicit owner waiver recorded 2026-08-16\n  (\"i dont care if google sees it\", re-confirmed via AskUser). ONLY project,\n  workspace, and tab names are waived. Question text, option text, file paths and\n  all other free text remain BANNED from pushes.\n- Trigger timing is UNTOUCHED: alerts fire exactly when the sidebar dot would turn\n  green (ready) / today's error rule. No context fetch, capability check, or\n  retraction logic may enter mint predicates, presence gating, or curation.\n- Retraction: question notifications already retract (existing v1 `r` path — keep\n  byte-for-byte). NEW: lifecycle notifications retract on phone AND watch when the\n  green dot clears (user reads the chat) or the alert is superseded. This\n  deliberately overrides PROTOCOL.md's \"lifecycle alerts are not retracted\"\n  invariant — rewrite that prose, don't layer over it.\n- Fallback wording: the current PHONE generic strings become canonical on BOTH\n  devices (deliberate change to watch fallback wording; \"same text\" requires it).\n\n## 1. Wire schema v3 (normative)\n\nClosed key sets per (version, kind). Exact-equality validation retained on both\nsides: ALL keys of a set are ALWAYS present; `\"\"` means \"absent\" for context\nfields. (Overrides Sol's optional-key proposal — keeps `assertClosedKeySet` and\nKotlin closed-set logic structurally unchanged.)\n\n- v3 `q` (blocked question): `[v,k,i,w,n,x,t,pn,wn,tn,tc]` — `t` may be `\"\"`\n  (pre-upgrade fence rows with null terminal id).\n- v3 `g` / `e` (lifecycle alert): `[v,k,i,w,x,t,pn,wn,tn,tc]`.\n- v3 `c` (lifecycle retract): `[v,k,i,w,x,t]` — no names.\n- v1 (`q`,`r`) and v2 (`g`,`e`) FROZEN byte-for-byte. Question settlement still\n  emits v1 `r` through the existing choke point (FORK companion/index.ts:588-616).\n  v2 gains NOTHING (current phone refuses unknown v2 kinds — LifecyclePushTest.kt:77-81).\n\nValue rules (host `PUSH_VALUE_RULES_BY_VERSION` + phone parser mirror):\n- `v`=\"3\"; `k`∈{q,g,e,c}; `i`,`w` existing opaque pattern; `t` opaque or `\"\"`;\n  `x` 13 digits; `n` same semantics as v1 `n`.\n- `pn`,`wn`,`tn`: UTF-8, ≤256 bytes each, may be `\"\"`. Sanitizer is TOTAL (can\n  never throw / never fail a send): trim outer whitespace; strip C0/C1 controls +\n  U+2028/U+2029 + newlines; truncate on code-point boundary (never split a\n  surrogate pair; TS: iterate code points, never `slice`; Kotlin: measure with\n  `toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8).size`, never `String.length`), reserving 3 bytes\n  for U+2026 ellipsis when truncated.\n- `tc`: decimal digits (≥1) or `\"\"`.\n- Caps PER VERSION: v1/v2 keep `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES` 160 (config.ts:286 —\n  the leak tripwire must not weaken); v3 data cap 2048; whole-message 4096 check\n  retained (push.ts:396-411).\n- Keep names out of every log, error, exception, and `toString()` (COMP\n  LifecyclePush.kt:54-55 pattern). Log key PRESENCE only. Pin the exempt-key list\n  {pn,wn,tn} in a test that enumerates it (privacy blast-radius guard).\n\n`collapse_key` stays `= data.i` for all kinds (retract overtakes an undelivered\noriginal at FCM for free).\n\nFCM envelope TTL: `buildEnvelope` currently hardcodes 900s `PUSH_TTL_MS`\n(push.ts:429-440). Retract sends (`r` AND `c`) must use `RETRACT_TTL_MS` (24h,\nconfig.ts:229-251) as the Android TTL — per-message TTL parameter. This also\nrepairs the existing latent question-retraction gap. Alert sends keep 900s.\n\n## 2. Text composition (canonical, single implementation on phone: COMP core AlertNotificationText.kt)\n\nContextual mode iff `pn≠\"\"` AND `wn≠\"\"` (all-or-generic; no partial ladders):\n- title = `pn · wn`\n- tab prefix iff `tn≠\"\"` AND `tc≥2`\n- ready body: `tn — finished, ready for review` / no-tab: `Finished — ready for review`\n- error body: `tn — stopped on an error` / no-tab: `Stopped on an error`\n- question: title = `pn · wn`; body = existing fetched (or contentless) body,\n  prefixed `tn — ` only in multi-tab case.\nFallback (any core name missing/malformed): canonical generic = current phone\nstrings byte-for-byte (CompanionNotifications.kt:219-235 for lifecycle; existing\nquestion strings). Malformed OPTIONAL context field ⇒ treat as `\"\"`, never reject\na structurally valid alert.\nSession workspaces (projectId null, read-api.ts:140-151): `pn` = the authoritative\n\"Sessions\" label (session-project.ts:29-48) — so contextual mode still engages.\nWatch renders relayed `notificationTitle`/`notificationBody` literally\n(new fields on `WatchQuestion`, `WatchQuestionOversize`, `WatchLifecycleAlert`,\nall with kotlinx defaults for old-peer compat). Add a lightweight Wear message for\nthe contentless question path (today it never notifies the watch —\nCompanionMessagingService.kt:236-283).\n\n## 3. Tab/workspace context plumbing (FORK)\n\n- NO desktop-main involvement, NO Electron IPC, NO pane-map-hook or lifecycle-sink\n  changes for context. Renderer owns the truth: terminal panes are\n  `pane.kind===\"terminal\"` + `pane.data.terminalId` (renderer v2-notifications\n  store.ts:1173-1180); layouts for ALL workspaces already live-queried in\n  V2NotificationController.tsx:76-135; title precedence per useTabTitle.ts:34-59,\n  reuse resolveDashboardSidebarTabTitle + terminalRuntimeRegistry.getTitle.\n- New PROTECTED tRPC mutations on the companion router (trpc/router/companion/\n  companion.ts — desktop-only authed surface; protectedProcedure trpc/index.ts:102):\n  - `companion.syncAlertContexts({workspaceId, tabCount, terminals:[{terminalId, tabTitle?}]})`\n    — one hydrated workspace snapshot at a time; called from\n    HostNotificationSubscriber (holds hostUrl + reconnect epoch, :35-118): send on\n    mount/layout/live-title change (hash-guarded, debounced) + every resync epoch.\n    SERIALIZE calls per workspace (an older snapshot must not overwrite a newer).\n  - `companion.markLifecycleSeen({workspaceId, terminalId, seenThroughAt})` (see §4).\n- Host side: new `push-context.ts` — bounded process-local `AlertContextRegistry`\n  owned by CompanionBridge (LRU ≈512 workspaces / snapshot size caps); validates\n  workspace+terminal DB relationships (originWorkspaceId) before atomic replace;\n  empty terminal array evicts; cleared on bridge stop; duplicate terminal\n  appearance with DIFFERING titles ⇒ omit `tn`, log ids only.\n- Name resolution: NEW dep injected at the composition root (companion/index.ts:693-708\n  — note LifecycleAlertManagerDeps has NO db today, lifecycle-alerts.ts:177-185).\n  Resolve project+workspace from host.db + tab from registry INSIDE `send()`\n  (lifecycle-alerts.ts:383-399) — fresh on every retry. NEVER cache names in held\n  records. Question path: extend `ArmedQuestion` to retain raw host terminal/\n  workspace ids (currently dropped, push.ts:1298-1318; fence already persists\n  them, push-fence.ts:30-50; reconstruction omits them, push.ts:1951-1987) and\n  resolve at the existing due point (push.ts:1711-1886). Question builder\n  (`buildQuestionPushData` push.ts:443-470) and lifecycle builder (:499-563) stay\n  SEPARATE — parallel edits.\n\n## 4. Retraction (FORK + COMP)\n\nHost:\n- Deterministic alert IDs: hash `(terminalId, kind, occurredAtMs of the FINAL\n  outcome event)` instead of cycle-start `previousEventAtMs`\n  (lifecycle-alerts.ts:187-203,448-466) — lets `markLifecycleSeen` recompute a `g`\n  id after host restart with no schema change. Mint predicates and dedupe\n  behavior must be pinned unchanged by tests. One-time cutover limitation:\n  pre-upgrade notifications can't be retracted post-restart (accepted).\n- `markLifecycleSeen`: revalidate DB relationship, derive the `g` id, send v3 `c`\n  on the existing per-id chain (push.ts:1398-1413). Repeated calls harmless;\n  unknown/restarted id still sends no-op-safe `c`.\n- `supersede` (lifecycle-alerts.ts:424-446) state handling:\n  - `held` → delete (no send, as today);\n  - `sending` → flag; if FCM later ACCEPTS it, `markDelivered` (:317-321) must\n    enqueue `c` behind that exact send (today the flag is silently dropped —\n    alert lands and never retracts);\n  - `sent` → enqueue `c` once, transition to NEW state `retracted`, KEEP the row\n    until TTL prune (deleting re-opens re-mint, comment :479-489). No separate\n    \"delivered map\" — the `alerts` map already retains sent rows (:252-265).\n  - Storm guard: repeated `progress` after `retracted` fires NOTHING further\n    (pin with a test).\n- Seen signal (renderer): fire ONLY from the two user-intent sites —\n  useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:35-46 (focus-clear) and\n  useV2NotificationStatus.ts:89-105 (sidebar mark-read) — and ONLY when\n  `markTerminalSeen` actually removed a `review` entry (make it return a boolean,\n  store.ts:250-276). NEVER from the store choke point: resyncAgentStatus\n  cold-start seeding (:352-363) would mass-retract phone alerts on every desktop\n  restart. Resync MAY repeat the mutation when persisted\n  `terminalSeenAt >= binding.lastEventAt` (restart repair path). NO new outcome in\n  the hook sink; do not touch companion-lifecycle-sink.ts / notifications.hook /\n  pane-map-hook.ts.\n\nPhone (COMP):\n- `c` routes via lifecycle dispatch (CompanionPush.parse → routeLifecyclePush,\n  LifecyclePush.kt:101-121, LifecycleRouting.kt:134) — NOT `routePush`\n  (v1-question-only, PushRouting.kt:56-70). Branch runs BEFORE claim/post flow.\n- On `c`: durably SUPPRESS the eventId FIRST (new `SeenLifecycleEvents.suppress`\n  — insert/retain; NEVER `release`, which re-admits a late FCM redelivery of the\n  original, SeenLifecycleEvents.kt:53-77 + its test :74-93), then\n  `cancel(eventId, ID_LIFECYCLE)` via a method INSIDE CompanionNotifications\n  (ID_LIFECYCLE is private, :383), then persist+attempt watch dismissal.\n  Handles c-before-g, c-after-g, duplicate c, late g redelivery. `release` stays\n  only for the existing failed-post rollback (LifecycleRoutingTest.kt:107-157).\n- `setTimeoutAfter(max(1, expiresAt-now))` on phone AND watch lifecycle\n  notifications (neither builder has one today) so TTL-pruned host state can't\n  leave an immortal notification.\n\nWatch (COMP):\n- New `WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS = \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\"` payload\n  `{eventId}` (own path — WearProtocol.kt:69-76 forbids reuse of\n  QUESTION_RESOLVED). Watch branch in CompanionWearListenerService (when-block\n  :47-57) → new `LifecycleNotifier.cancel` via\n  `LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId(eventId)` (:81), mirroring\n  `QuestionNotifier.cancel` (:59-61). Never relay `c` as a WatchLifecycleAlert.\n- Dismissal must be EVENTUAL, not one-shot (WatchLink returns NoWatchPaired when\n  disconnected, WatchLink.kt:87-106): new bounded (256-entry, 24h expiry)\n  SharedPreferences pending-dismissal queue (`PendingLifecycleDismissals.kt`),\n  persisted BEFORE sending, entry cleared only after ALL connected-node sends\n  succeed, flushed on watch hello (reconnect seam WatchBridge.kt:383-393). Prune\n  expired first; at capacity fail/log loudly, never silently drop a live\n  dismissal.\n\n## 5. Rollout / install order (HARD GATE)\n\n1. COMP first: implement + full Gradle unit suite\n   (`:core:test :app-phone:testDebugUnitTest :app-watch:testDebugUnitTest`), then\n   `./gradlew :app-phone:assembleRelease :app-watch:assembleRelease` — signing\n   from `~/.superset/companion/keystore/signing.properties`\n   (app-phone/build.gradle.kts:37-58 throws if missing); BOTH apps same key +\n   applicationId or the Data Layer silently delivers nothing. Bump versionCode\n   AND versionName in BOTH modules (currently 1 / 0.1.0). Verify both APK cert\n   SHA-256s match. Install (with explicit user authorization) WATCH FIRST, then\n   phone, `adb install -r`, never uninstall. New apps must keep working against\n   the still-old host (v1/v2 untouched incl. question retraction).\n2. Then FORK host + renderer changes, tests, FEATURES.md, /simplify, lint,\n   commit, push main, full Windows ARM64 GH build. Old phone + new host = alerts\n   silently vanish ⇒ phone-first is a release GATE. No dual-send.\n\n## 6. Gates / docs\n\n- FEATURES.md: new `(ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES)` marker whose tokens ROOT IN THE\n  RENDERER FILES TOO (existing lifecycle marker only guards desktop main —\n  a silent upstream takeover of store.ts/V2NotificationController.tsx must red\n  the gate). Update the companion-bridge row (500ms text etc. untouched). Marker\n  must exist in-tree in the SAME commit as the manifest row.\n- Rewrite push.ts:3-8 privacy doctrine (waiver, scope, date) and PROTOCOL.md\n  (§13 v3 per-kind sets, byte budgets, composition, retraction override incl.\n  deleting \"lifecycle alerts are not retracted\" prose at ~:2180 and ~:2034-2077,\n  suppression semantics, rollout order, waiver record).\n- ci-repair.sh already freezes `packages/host-service/src/companion*` against\n  unattended repair (:65-74,145-159) ⇒ local test coverage must be strong.\n\n## 7. Tests (minimum)\n\nFORK: per-(version,kind) schema incl. always-present/\"\" rules + exempt-list\nenumeration; v1/v2 builders byte-identical (golden); UTF-8 truncation vectors\n(emoji, combining, surrogate boundary, U+2028/9, C0/C1); per-version caps;\nretract envelope TTL 24h (r and c); lifecycle manager held/sending/sent/\nretracted races incl. superseded-mid-flight and storm guard; deterministic\nrestart id; repeated seen idempotent; retry name freshness; ArmedQuestion id\nretention through fence reconstruction; registry bounds/atomic replace/eviction/\nrelationship validation; markTerminalSeen boolean semantics; no name values in\nany log/error (assert on thrown messages).\nCOMP: v3 parse (strict structural, lenient context) golden vectors shared with\nhost; composition matrix (contextual/generic × tab/no-tab × q/g/e); suppress\ntombstone semantics (c-before-g, duplicate c, late g); pending-dismissal\npersistence/expiry/capacity; watch literal rendering + dismiss branch; v1/v2\nvectors UNCHANGED.\n\n## 8. Out of scope\n\nDB schema/migrations; durable host alert state; renderer title persistence\nacross full outage; capability negotiation; store distribution / Android CI;\nquestion-settlement semantics; any change to WHEN alerts fire; deep-links on `t`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6000,"cache_read_input_tokens":133922,"output_tokens":6577,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6577,"cache_read_input_tokens":13