{"parentUuid":"3d5f0b4a-592a-42f7-b646-bbbaf091a4b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5ehGbCmpg8jx8i5bK8s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Zae5DT3t1ua5T8hZouShp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement companion app v3 (Android)","name":"impl-android","prompt":"You are implementing the Android/Wear half of the (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) feature.\n\nNORMATIVE SPEC (read both fully before writing code):\n- C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\FINAL.md  (normative; sections 0,1,2,4,5,7 are yours)\n- C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md   (UX background)\n\nWork in: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion (Kotlin, modules core / app-phone / app-watch, normative PROTOCOL.md). Do NOT commit — leave changes in the working tree for my review. Do NOT touch the fork repo except reading the two spec files.\n\nScope (COMP side only):\n1. core: v3 push parsing per FINAL.md §1 — closed key sets per (version,kind), all keys always present, \"\" = absent for context fields; strict structural validation, LENIENT per-context-field degradation (malformed context field → \"\"); v1/v2 parsers preserved byte-for-byte (their tests must pass unchanged); names never in logs/toString/exceptions.\n2. core: canonical AlertNotificationText composer per FINAL.md §2 (contextual iff pn&&wn; tab prefix iff tn && tc>=2; fallback = current PHONE generic strings byte-for-byte, which become canonical for both devices).\n3. Phone: route v3 q/g/e/c per FINAL.md §4 — c handled in lifecycle dispatch (NOT routePush), suppress-tombstone-first (new SeenLifecycleEvents.suppress; NEVER release on retract; release stays only for the failed-post rollback), cancelLifecycle method inside CompanionNotifications, setTimeoutAfter on lifecycle notifications, pending watch-dismissal queue (PendingLifecycleDismissals.kt, bounded 256 / 24h, persist-before-send, clear only after all connected sends succeed, flush on watch hello), value-free logs.\n4. Phone→watch: precomposed notificationTitle/notificationBody fields (kotlinx defaults for old-peer compat) on WatchQuestion, WatchQuestionOversize, WatchLifecycleAlert; new WearPaths.LIFECYCLE_DISMISS \"/companion/v1/lifecycle/dismiss\" {eventId}; lightweight Wear message for the contentless question path (today it never notifies the watch — CompanionMessagingService.kt:236-283).\n5. Watch: render relayed title/body literally; dismiss branch → new LifecycleNotifier.cancel via LifecycleAlertPresentation.notificationId; setTimeoutAfter; canonical fallback strings (= phone's).\n6. PROTOCOL.md: normative v3 section per FINAL.md §6 — rewrite (do not layer over) the \"lifecycle alerts are not retracted\" prose (~line 2180 and ~2034-2077); record the plaintext-names waiver + date + scope; byte budgets; suppression semantics; rollout order.\n7. Bump versionCode AND versionName in BOTH app-phone and app-watch build.gradle.kts (currently 1 / 0.1.0 → 2 / 0.2.0).\n8. Tests per FINAL.md §7 COMP list. Run the full unit suite: `./gradlew :core:test :app-phone:testDebugUnitTest :app-watch:testDebugUnitTest` (bash; JAVA_HOME may need Android Studio's JBR — check existing docs/gradle.properties; if a toolchain is missing, investigate and report rather than skipping). ALL tests must pass, including the untouched v1/v2 golden vectors.\n9. Do NOT build release APKs and do NOT install anything — that happens later with explicit user authorization.\n\nFile-level guidance from the architects is embedded in FINAL.md with file:line references — verify each against the real code before editing (lines may have drifted). Follow existing code style/idioms exactly. Fail loud, no defensive swallowing except where FINAL.md explicitly requires lenient context-field degradation.\n\nReport back: files changed, test run output summary (pass/fail counts), any spec deviations you had to make and why, anything unresolved.","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6675,"cache_read_input_tokens":139922,"output_tokens":3918,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":313},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6675,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3918,"cache_read_input_tokens":139922,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6675},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ea286951-d5fa-4dfb-9c7c-52639c6d9643","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:38:05.908Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
