oot and called INSIDE send() (fresh per retry, never cached in held records), supersede state machine (held→delete; sending→flag + markDelivered enqueues c when a superseded in-flight send lands; sent→enqueue c once + new \"retracted\" state kept until TTL; storm guard: nothing further after retracted), restart-safe markLifecycleSeen (recompute g id, no-op-safe c for unknown ids).\n4. Question path: extend ArmedQuestion to retain raw host terminal/workspace ids incl. through fence reconstruction (push.ts:1298-1318, push-fence.ts:30-50, push.ts:1951-1987); resolve names at the existing due point; question settlement keeps emitting v1 r UNCHANGED.\n5. New PROTECTED tRPC mutations on the companion router (trpc/router/companion/): syncAlertContexts (serialized per workspace, bounds-validated) and markLifecycleSeen. Do NOT touch companion-lifecycle-sink.ts, notifications.hook, or pane-map-hook.ts.\n6. Renderer (apps/desktop/src/renderer): pure alertContexts extraction lib under V2NotificationController (terminal panes = pane.kind===\"terminal\" + pane.data.terminalId; title precedence per useTabTitle.ts / resolveDashboardSidebarTabTitle + terminalRuntimeRegistry.getTitle; duplicate-appearance policy), snapshot sync from HostNotificationSubscriber (hash-guarded, debounced, serialized, resent on resync epoch), markTerminalSeen returns whether it actually removed a review entry, seen-mutation fired ONLY from useClearActivePaneAttention and useV2NotificationStatus mark-read sites (NEVER the store choke point — resync cold-start seeding must not retract), resync repair resend per FINAL.md §4.\n7. FEATURES.md: add (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) marker with tokens rooting in BOTH host-service and the renderer files (store.ts / V2NotificationController area), update the companion-bridge row prose. Same commit discipline: marker tokens must exist in-tree.\n8. Tests per FINAL.md §7 FORK list. Also run existing companion test suite (bun test for packages/host-service companion tests) and th