{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:30:13.435Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Done. All changes left uncommitted in the worktree.\n\n## Files changed\n\n**Host-service — wire (v3)**\n- `packages/host-service/src/companion/types.ts` — `PushDataV3Question` / `PushDataV3Lifecycle` / `PushDataV3LifecycleRetract`, unioned into `PushData`; v1/v2 untouched.\n- `packages/host-service/src/companion/config.ts` — `PUSH_DATA_HARD_CAP_BYTES_V3 = 2048` (v1/v2 keep 160), `PUSH_NAME_MAX_BYTES = 256`.\n- `packages/host-service/src/companion/push.ts` — privacy doctrine rewritten with the waiver + scope + date; `PUSH_DATA_KEYS_BY_VERSION_KIND` (per-kind), `PUSH_VALUE_RULES_BY_VERSION`, exported `PUSH_NAME_EXEMPT_KEYS`, per-version cap; total `sanitizePushName`; per-message envelope TTL derived from the frame (`r` and `c` → `RETRACT_TTL_MS`); v3 `buildQuestionPushData` / `buildLifecyclePushData` (separate builders) + new `buildLifecycleRetractPushData`; `buildEnvelope` exported; `ArmedQuestion` retains raw `hostTerminalId`/`hostWorkspaceId` (incl. through fence reconstruction); `resolveAlertContext` dep called at the fire/due point; `sendLifecycleRetraction` on the existing per-id chain.\n\n**Host-service — context + retraction**\n- `push-context.ts` (new) — bounded `AlertContextRegistry` (LRU 512, per-workspace terminal/title caps, DB `originWorkspaceId` validation, atomic replace, empty-evicts, duplicate-differing-title → no `tn`, value-free diagnostics) + `PushAlertContext`.\n- `lifecycle-alerts.ts` — alert id hashed from the FINAL outcome instant; injected `resolveContext` called inside `send()` (fresh per retry, never cached); new `retracted` state; `supersede` held→delete / sending→flag / sent→retract-once / retracted→nothing; `markDelivered` retracts a superseded in-flight send that lands; `markLifecycleSeen` (revalidates, recomputes the `g` id, no-op-safe `c` with a tombstone for unknown ids).\n- `registry.ts` — alert-context + lifecycle-seen sinks (presence-store pattern: never throw for the off state).\n- `companion/index.ts` — registry owned by the bridge (built before the sender, cleared on stop), `resolveAlertContext` resolving project/workspace off `host.db` (Sessions label for `project_id NULL`) + tab off the registry, wired into both consumers.\n- `trpc/router/companion/companion.ts` — PROTECTED `syncAlertContexts` (bounds-validated, serialized per workspace) and `markLifecycleSeen`.\n\n**Renderer**\n- `V2NotificationController/lib/alertContexts.ts` (new, pure) — extraction + hash.\n- `V2NotificationController/lib/companionAlertSync.ts` (new) — hash-guarded/debounced/serialized sync, per-host forget on reconnect, workspace→host map, `reportTerminalSeen`.\n- `HostNotificationSubscriber.tsx` — sync on mount/layout/live-title change and every resync epoch; publishes the workspace→host map.\n- `stores/v2-notifications/store.ts` — `markTerminalSeen` returns whether it removed a `review` entry.\n- `useClearActivePaneAttention.ts`, `useV2NotificationStatus.ts` — the only two seen-mutation sites, gated on that boolean.\n- `resyncAgentStatus.ts` — restart repair resend, explicitly excluding cold-start seeding.\n- `FEATURES.md` — `(ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES)` row + 7 marker lines rooted in host-service **and** the renderer (store.ts + V2NotificationController); companion-bridge row prose updated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun test src/companion` — **332 pass / 0 fail** (23 files). New: `push-schema.test.ts`, `push-context.test.ts`, `push-armed-context.test.ts`, `push-v3-golden.test.ts`, plus lifecycle retraction/id/freshness suites.\n- Renderer — **46 pass / 0 fail** (store + controller lib).\n- Marker gate under bash — **All 160 feature markers present.**\n- Biome (lint + format) on every touched path — **0 diagnostics**.\n- `tsc --noEmit`: host-service clean except one pre-existing error (`curation-gates.test.ts:341`, `remoteAnswer` optionality — untouched code); desktop shows no errors in any file I touched.\n\n**Golden vectors**: `push-v3-golden.test.ts` mirrors `PushV3Test.kt`'s literals byte-for-byte — all three key sets, every key always present with `\"\"` for absent, `collapse_key = data.i` on all four kinds, `c` on the 24 h TTL, and the 256-byte boundary (64×🚀 accepted, +1 char truncated rather than dropped).\n\n## Spec deviations\n\n1. **v1/v2 \"golden builder\" test** — FINAL §7 asks for byte-identical v1/v2 builders. Per §3 both builders were *edited* to v3, so there is no v2 builder left to pin. I pinned instead: `buildRetractPushData` (v1 `r`) byte-for-byte, the v1 160-byte cap, and v1's refusal of a smuggled name. `lifecycle-push.test.ts`'s old v2-shape assertion was updated to v3 — that is the deliberate change, not drift.\n2. **Per-message TTL** — derived from `data.k` inside `buildEnvelope` rather than passed as a parameter. Stronger: a caller cannot pair a retraction with the wrong TTL.\n3. **`markLifecycleSeen` only retracts `g`** — reading a chat does not un-kill a failed agent, so `e` alerts stand. FINAL §4 says \"derive the `g` id\", so this matches, but it is an explicit behavioural choice worth your eye.\n4. **`test-setup.ts` polyfill added** (out of the stated scope) — the v2 store persists to `window.sessionStorage`, which the desktop test setup never provided, so `store.test.ts` was failing wholesale before my change. Adding the polyfill fixes 10 pre-existing failures alongside my 4 new tests.\n5. **Title precedence** — `useTabTitle.ts` does not exist at the path FINAL §3 cites. I used the real ladder (`resolveDashboardSidebarTabTitle` + `terminalRuntimeRegistry.getTitle`): tab rename &gt; pane rename &gt; live terminal title &gt; nothing. A tab that would only resolve to the word \"Terminal\" sends `\"\"` rather than a placeholder.\n6. **Live-title subscription** — `terminalRuntimeRegistry.onTitleChange` calls `getOrCreateEntry`, which *creates* a runtime entry. I subscribe only where `has(terminalId)` is already true; a terminal opened later re-runs the effect via the layout change.\n\n## Unresolved / for your attention\n\n- **Rollout gate**: v3 is now the only shape the host emits for questions and lifecycle alerts. An old phone against this host = alerts silently vanish. Phone-first install remains a hard gate (FINAL §5).\n- **PROTOCOL.md** was not touched — it lives in the companion repo, which was out of my scope.\n- The pre-existing `curation-gates.test.ts:341` type error is unrelated but will show in any `typecheck` you run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>466445</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>247</tool_uses><duration_ms>3084625</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
