{"parentUuid":"7c0320d0-f61d-4e47-96ec-e60867dfcff9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5ik4yzxd7sjkKoNnWjr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fork half is complete too — 332 host-service tests + 46 renderer tests passing, marker gate green (160 markers), lint clean, and its golden-vector test mirrors the Kotlin one byte-for-byte. Its deviations are sound (notably: reading a chat retracts only `g` alerts — an error alert shouldn't vanish just because you looked; it clears on the next work cycle instead, which matches your green-dot rule).\n\nNow the adversarial review pass — two reviewers, each covering both repos plus cross-repo wire consistency:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_read_input_tokens":156809,"output_tokens":3124,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3124,"cache_read_input_tokens":156809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d6efddb0-1f8b-4397-80d4-89ff08204965","timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:30:58.116Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d6efddb0-1f8b-4397-80d4-89ff08204965","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5ik4yzxd7sjkKoNnWjr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S8afjWcBFz3Wykb15s3MCU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Code review both repos (Opus)","name":"rev-opus","prompt":"Adversarial code review of the uncommitted (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) implementation across TWO working trees:\n\n1. FORK worktree: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3 — review `git diff` vs main (branch worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3; includes new untracked files — use `git status` + `git diff` + read new files).\n2. COMPANION repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion — uncommitted working-tree changes (`git status` / `git diff` vs HEAD).\n\nNormative spec: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\PLAN.md and (overriding) tmp\\alert-context-names\\FINAL.md in the main fork checkout.\n\nReview dimensions, in priority order:\n1. CROSS-REPO WIRE CONSISTENCY — the host golden-vector test (push-v3-golden.test.ts) vs Kotlin PushV3Test.kt: key sets, always-present-\"\"-absent semantics, value rules, byte budgets/truncation, TTLs, collapse_key. Any mismatch = BLOCKER.\n2. Correctness of the retraction state machine (held/sending/sent/retracted, superseded-mid-flight, storm guard, deterministic ids, markLifecycleSeen idempotency + unknown-id tombstone) and the phone tombstone semantics (suppress-before-cancel, never release on retract, c-before-g / duplicate c / late g redelivery), pending watch-dismissal queue (persist-before-send, all-connected-success clearing, hello flush, capacity fail-loud).\n3. Trigger-timing invariant: NOTHING may change when alerts fire — mint predicates, presence gating, curation, question due-point. Verify the diffs cannot alter timing.\n4. Privacy: no name values in any log/error/exception/toString on either side; exempt-key list pinned; v1/v2 caps and value rules unweakened; question text still never in a push.\n5. Renderer: seen-mutation only from the two intent sites; cold-start resync cannot mass-retract; sync serialization (older snapshot cannot overwrite newer); no touch of pane-map-hook/lifecycle-sink/notifications.hook.\n6. Regression risk to existing proven paths: v1 question push + retraction byte-identical; (ANSWER-FRAME-PACING) untouched; existing tests not weakened (check test diffs for deleted/loosened assertions).\n7. Conventions, fail-fast rules (no defensive swallowing beyond the spec's total sanitizer + no-op-safe retracts), type safety.\n\nVerify every finding against the actual code before reporting. Rank BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and a concrete failure scenario. Also report a short \"verified sound\" list for the load-bearing properties above. Read-only — do not fix anything.","subagent_type":"code-reviewer-opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_read_input_tokens":156809,"output_tokens":3124,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3124,"cache_read_input_tokens":156809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3360},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2723eda3-2ccc-4444-be46-ad53f1d282e0","timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:31:13.849Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b