{"parentUuid":"47651f89-3710-47ad-8ac7-643bd6f1a777","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5kcG5G4scgsLr44LUHi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sol's final report: one blocker (surrogate handling mismatch between host sanitizer and Kotlin parser) and seven majors — most confirmed against real code with concrete failure paths. One I'm ruling on rather than fixing: the \"question bodies must be identical on watch\" finding. Your \"same as phone\" answer was about the context names, and those *are* identical on both surfaces; relaying full question text into a watch notification would get silently clamped at ~1024 chars, which is the exact defect the watch app's design forbids. Keeping the per-surface question body (with identical title + tab prefix) stands as an accepted, documented deviation.\n\nEverything else will be fixed. Waiting for Opus's report so the fix batch covers the union, then dispatching fixes to both implementation agents."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3457,"cache_read_input_tokens":164443,"output_tokens":1289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1034},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":164443,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5f11c5ae-0781-4aa7-bd4a-a5b55f3c9425","timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:55:32.025Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":