{"parentUuid":"2e14466b-c5de-47af-bf5f-62ba64843b8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5kwuvreNrxix3yELxbb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LuBFz3Ket8HRJLcJRpypEs","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Two adversarial reviews (Opus + Sol) are back on your worktree. FIX-FIRST findings assigned to you — fix all of these in the same worktree, then rerun the affected tests + lint + marker gate and report back:\n\n1. BLOCKER — push.ts sanitizePushName (~:445-469): passes unpaired UTF-16 surrogates; Kotlin AlertContext.isRenderable rejects them. Drop lone surrogates in the strip loop (code point whose single UTF-16 unit is D800–DFFF → treat name as degraded to \"\" to MATCH Kotlin's behavior — check AlertContext.kt:113-135 in the companion repo and mirror its exact boundary: Kotlin degrades the whole field, so degrade the whole field, don't just strip the unit). Port the Kotlin surrogate vectors into push-schema.test.ts / push-v3-golden.test.ts.\n\n2. MAJOR — alert-id mismatch (lifecycle-alerts.ts:823 vs renderer): markLifecycleSeen recomputes the g id from renderer `binding.lastEventAt`, which ALSO advances on events carrying no lifecycle outcome (e.g. SessionStart — pane-map-hook leaves lifecycle_outcome null but terminalAgentStore.recordEvent still moves lastEventAt; pinned by statusTransitions.test.ts:144). Result: retraction targets an id no phone holds, real notification never retracted, plus a wasted blind c broadcast. Fix BOTH ends: (a) renderer sends the review SOURCE's occurredAt (`sources[key].occurredAt` — the stamp of the event that set the review axis), not binding.lastEventAt; (b) host-side, before falling back to the recomputed-id tombstone path, scan the live `alerts` map for a `sent` `g` with matching hostTerminalId and retract THAT id (recomputed id remains the restart fallback only). Add a test reproducing the SessionStart-advances-lastEventAt scenario.\n\n3. MAJOR — resyncAgentStatus.ts:403: the `preEntry !== undefined` guard makes the restart-repair branch unreachable in exactly its documented case (markTerminalSeen deletes the review entry). Fix per the reviewer's bounded suggestion: drive repair off the condition the clearing branch at ~:393 already computes (replayed state is review AND seenAt >= row.lastEventAt), keep the !seedColdStart exclusion, and bound it (per-epoch cap) so an unguarded resync can't broadcast one c per read terminal. Also honor the mutation's accepted result.\n\n4. MAJOR — companionAlertSync.ts:96-109: sets sentHash after ANY successful tRPC response even when host returns {accepted:false} (real at startup: tRPC listener starts before async bridge registration). Set sentHash only when accepted === true; treat accepted:false as unsent with a bounded retry / readiness-triggered resync.\n\n5. MAJOR — alertContexts.ts:101-119: split-tab title resolved per-terminal instead of once per tab. Resolve ONE title per tab using the sidebar title-pane precedence (including active non-terminal panes and the active terminal's live title), assign that same title to every terminal in the tab; emit no title when the split has no honest single title pane.\n\n6. MAJOR/MINOR — companion.ts:427 / lifecycle-alerts.ts:798: markLifecycleSeen never revalidates terminal↔workspace against host.db (FINAL §4 requires it; the registry path does it at push-context.ts:244-248). Add the same findTerminal originWorkspaceId check (in the index.ts lifecycleSeen wrapper or the router), drop the signal with an id-only log on mismatch/absence.\n\n7. MINOR — HostNotificationSubscriber.tsx:268: effects keyed on unstable `workspacesById` identity; cleanup calls releaseAlertContextSync wiping sentHash + debounce on every layout tick. Key on the derived `workspacesKey` string (the resync effect already does), release only on true unmount.\n\n8. MINOR — push-schema.test.ts:367: raw NUL/SOH bytes make the file binary to ripgrep (nightly-merge/gate agents can't read it). Replace with \"\u0000\u0001\" escapes.\n\n9. MINOR — stale comments: index.ts:1904-1907 still claims arm-time ids never reach FCM (they now feed t/pn/wn/tn); lifecycle-alerts.ts:717-732 alreadyApplied comment still describes the old previous-event-stamp id input. Rewrite both.\n\nReviewers verified sound (do NOT churn these): wire golden vectors, retraction state machine, tombstone semantics, trigger timing, privacy exempt-list pinning, seen-site gating, v1/v2 freezing. Don't touch anything outside these fixes. Report: per-finding fix summary, test/lint/gate results.","summary":"Dispatch review fixes to fork agent","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"Two adversarial reviews (Opus + Sol) are back on …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":176462,"output_tokens":2540,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2540,"cache_read_input_tokens":176462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c6fd2f85-7d06-40bd-a586-b178eb388c02","timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:00:01.298Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
