{"parentUuid":"610c6ea5-f686-47d6-abab-6381cfbd163a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5kwuvreNrxix3yELxbb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HBNANzgYK6gcebuZnopRiN","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Two adversarial reviews (Opus + Sol) are back. Three findings assigned to you in C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion — fix, rerun the Gradle unit suite, and report back:\n\n1. MAJOR — AlertNotificationText.kt:11: Kotlin data class generated toString() exposes project/workspace/tab-derived notification text. Replace with a custom redacted toString() exposing only safe presence/shape flags, following the existing AlertContext/LifecyclePushData pattern.\n\n2. MAJOR — WearProtocol.kt (~:290): WatchQuestion, WatchQuestionOversize, WatchQuestionContentless, WatchLifecycleAlert retain generated toString() now that they carry notificationTitle/notificationBody — stringifying prints names (and, where present, question-derived text). Give every name-bearing Wear envelope a redacted custom toString() (identifiers/kinds/field-presence only), same pattern.\n\n3. MINOR — WatchBridge.kt:309: at pending-queue capacity, pushLifecycleDismiss returns Refused WITHOUT attempting the Data Layer send — dropping a dismissal a currently-connected watch would have taken, in favor of 256 older ones. Fix: still attempt deliverDismissal(eventId) when enqueue is refused, returning a result that distinguishes \"sent but not persisted\" from \"neither\" (or evict the oldest to make room — pick whichever fits the existing result-type idiom better and say which you chose).\n\nNOT a defect (my ruling, do not change): per-surface question bodies (your deviation #1) stand — the reviewer flagged it but the watch's ~1024-char silent clamp justifies it; it's now recorded in FINAL.md §8. Everything else the reviewers verified sound — don't churn beyond these three fixes. Report: per-finding fix summary + test results.","summary":"Dispatch review fixes to Android agent","to":"impl-android","type":"message","recipient":"impl-android","content":"Two adversarial reviews (Opus + Sol) are back. Th…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":176462,"output_tokens":2540,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2540,"cache_read_input_tokens":176462,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c4b74b44-3187-429d-8d22-8ad9d567dcac","timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:00:09.752Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
