{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:20:21.686Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LuBFz3Ket8HRJLcJRpypEs</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 9 findings fixed and verified. Changes remain uncommitted in the worktree.\n\n## Per-finding\n\n**1. BLOCKER — lone surrogates (`push.ts`)** — Added `hasLoneSurrogate`, a deliberate UTF-16 **index walk** mirroring `AlertContext.isRenderable` (`AlertContext.kt:113-135`) unit for unit. Checked on the **raw** value before stripping/truncation, and it degrades the **whole field to `\"\"`** — not strips the unit — because Kotlin's `name()` refuses such a name outright. Stripping would have shipped a name the phone accepts while the two ends disagreed about its text. (`for...of` was the trap: it yields a lone surrogate as an ordinary code point, so the defect passed straight through.) Kotlin's vectors ported into `push-schema.test.ts` (all 6 lone-surrogate shapes + well-formed-pair control) and a cross-end assertion in `push-v3-golden.test.ts` (one bad field costs one field).\n\n**2. MAJOR — alert-id mismatch** — Both ends:\n- *Renderer*: both seen sites now read the **review entry's `occurredAt`** (the stamp of the event that set the review axis) before `markTerminalSeen` deletes it, and send that. `binding.lastEventAt` still drives the seen mark itself — unchanged.\n- *Host*: `findLiveReadyAlert` scans the live map for this terminal's `g` alert **first**; the recomputed hash is now the restart-only fallback. My new test caught that matching only `sent` still let a **held** alert fall through to a blind broadcast, so it matches **any** state (`sent` preferred, else newest) — knowing anything about the terminal is enough to prove the hash is unnecessary; `retractById` then does the right thing per state.\n- Three regression tests: the SessionStart-advances-`lastEventAt` scenario, no-blind-broadcast-while-held, and no cross-terminal mismatching.\n\n**3. MAJOR — unreachable resync repair** — Hoisted the clearing branch's own predicate into `replayedReviewAlreadySeen` and drove the repair off it. The `preEntry !== undefined` guard was self-defeating exactly as reported (the user's own `markTerminalSeen` deletes the entry). Capped at `MAX_SEEN_REPAIRS_PER_RESYNC = 10` per epoch with `seenRepairsSent`/`seenRepairsSkipped` in the logged result; `!seedColdStart` retained.\n\n**4. MAJOR — `accepted:false` treated as sent** — `sentHash` is now recorded **only** on `accepted === true`. Anything else schedules a bounded readiness retry (1s/2s/4s, max 3), and a reconnect resets the budget via `forgetAlertContextSyncsForHost`. `reportTerminalSeen` reads its result too and logs an id-only diagnostic when unconsumed (deliberately not retried — it's one moment's event, and the resync repair path owns re-offering it).\n\n**5. MAJOR — split-tab title** — New `resolveTabTitle` resolves **once per tab** and hands the same title to every terminal in it. Precedence: tab rename &gt; title-pane rename &gt; title-pane's live terminal title (only when that pane *is* the terminal) &gt; nothing. A non-terminal active pane now names the tab (\"Changes\"), rather than borrowing a terminal's name for a pane nobody is on. Four tests, incl. the previously-wrong per-terminal divergence.\n\n**6. MAJOR/MINOR — missing DB revalidation** — The `lifecycleSeen` wrapper in `index.ts` now runs the same `findTerminal().originWorkspaceId` check the registry does, dropping mismatches with an id-only log. Deliberately fails **closed** here (unlike the alert path's fail-open rules): the cost of dropping is a notification lingering; the cost of acting wrongly is retracting an alert for a chat nobody read.\n\n**7. MINOR — effect churn** — Derived `workspaceIds` from `workspacesKey`'s first segment and keyed both effects on it, so `releaseAlertContextSync` runs on genuine unmount/membership change instead of every layout tick. Layouts come off a ref. Note: I avoided `biome-ignore` here — the lint was right both times (first that the map was a real dependency, then that the key had become unused), so the deps are now honest rather than suppressed.\n\n**8. MINOR — binary test file** — `push-schema.test.ts:367` raw NUL/SOH replaced with `\\u0000\\u0001`. Verified zero remaining raw control bytes; the file is ripgrep-readable again.\n\n**9. MINOR — stale comments** — `index.ts` armPush: \"None of it goes to FCM\" corrected (the ids are read at fire time to resolve names; the ids themselves still never cross the wire, only the resulting names, and `transcriptPath`/`toolUseId` stay local). `lifecycle-alerts.ts` `alreadyApplied`: rewritten for the outcome-instant id input — same-instant re-deliveries now collapse, but a re-stamped POST still mints two ids, which is what the producer id is for.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Host companion suite: 339 pass / 0 fail** (23 files) — was 332, +7 from the new regression tests.\n- **Renderer: 49 pass / 0 fail** (5 files).\n- **Biome** (lint + format, CRLF-normalised) on every touched path: **0 diagnostics, no suppressions added**.\n- **Marker gate** under bash: **All 160 feature markers present.**\n- **tsc**: desktop — no errors in any touched file; host-service — only the pre-existing `curation-gates.test.ts:341` (`remoteAnswer` optionality, untouched code).\n\nNothing outside the 9 findings was changed; the verified-sound areas (golden vectors, retraction state machine, tombstone semantics, trigger timing, exempt-list pinning, seen-site gating, v1/v2 freeze) are untouched except where a finding required it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>535746</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>77</tool_uses><duration_ms>1220370</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"dequeue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:20:21.691Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91"}
