{"parentUuid":"90cbbfca-21dd-4ba5-891b-b0868fd528ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5oats8CaEpgujN3Mp4U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Opus's verification is in. Reconciling the two rounds: three findings overlap, one conflicts. My rulings:\n\n- **Conflict resolved in Opus's favor:** Sol wants the tab-title resolver to match the sidebar for non-terminal panes (diff → \"Changes\", file → basename, browser → host). Opus correctly flags that file basenames and URLs are exactly the free text your plaintext waiver does *not* cover — only project/workspace/tab names. Derived pane names stay off the wire; an explicitly renamed tab still names it. Recording as a privacy-scoped deviation.\n- **To fix (round 2, all renderer/host-edge):** the repair path's pane-visible blind spot; repair-cap rotation so rows 11+ aren't starved forever; the stale retry timer that can overwrite a newer accepted snapshot; the lost layout-change sync trigger (tab counts go stale in exactly the multi-tab case the feature targets); and Opus's sharpest catch — a blind retract broadcast for terminals that never alerted, which would erode the phone's 64-slot dedupe window on every reconnect; fixed host-side by proving-nothing-to-retract when the host has been up since before the seen instant."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5378,"cache_read_input_tokens":195039,"output_tokens":2331,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1527},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5378,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2331,"cache_read_input_tokens":195039,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5378},