{"parentUuid":"d224ae68-a779-4f75-be37-ae1bbab3a6c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5qbH9oQSNHJUAv95YF3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sol's final round disagrees with Opus's SHIP — four new majors, and they're real: the sharpest is that the title-listener subscription keys the runtime registry by terminal ID while V2 runtimes are keyed by pane ID, silently creating a shadow entry that could sync empty tab titles. Plus a remaining snapshot-ordering race, the eviction case genuinely breaking proof-of-absence (Opus saw it as a comment issue; Sol showed the swallowed-retraction path), and the cooldown marking repairs done before the host accepted them. Dispatching the full union — with a requirement for focused tests on the three files that keep churning, since that's why these keep slipping through:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2435,"cache_read_input_tokens":213937,"output_tokens":2840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1047},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2435,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2840,"cache_read_input_tokens":213937,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2435},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"cbb7eb56-e3ee-4703-bd61-e916e23ef7b9","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:00:51.618Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"cbb7eb56-e3ee-4703-bd61-e916e23ef7b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5qbH9oQSNHJUAv95YF3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0165sPSSVtdtcuNWyWZ62TKL","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Round 3 — final verification split: one reviewer SHIP, one found 4 new MAJORs. Union of remaining findings; fix all, and this round ADD FOCUSED TESTS for companionAlertSync, resyncAgentStatus repair, and the subscriber listener lifecycle — these three files have churned three rounds precisely because they have no tests.\n\n1. MAJOR — HostNotificationSubscriber.tsx:335: title-listener subscription uses the registry's DEFAULT instance keyed by terminalId, but V2 terminal runtimes are keyed by PANE id — TerminalPane mounts (terminalId, pane.id). `has(terminalId)` may pass but `onTitleChange(terminalId,...)` CREATES a separate (terminalId, terminalId) default entry: real title events never reach the listener, and the empty shadow entry can make a later layout tick sync tn:\"\". Fix: carry pane ids through listener reconciliation; subscribe/read the exact (terminalId, pane.id) runtime; never create default entries (use a has/get that doesn't getOrCreate).\n\n2. MAJOR — companionAlertSync.ts:131: equal-to-sentHash fast path ignores an older pending/in-flight send that can still land afterward. Scenario: sentHash=C; queue A; queue C again before A completes → C call early-returns; A accepted; completion correctly refuses to record A as current but leaves sentHash=C and queues nothing → host stuck on A forever, future C suppressed. Fix: track the hash/generation actually applied by every completion; when an accepted completion is not the current desired, enqueue desired; take the equal-hash fast path only when no older queued/in-flight op can land afterward.\n\n3. MAJOR — lifecycle-alerts.ts:895 proof-of-absence vs eviction (both reviewers, different grades): evictOldest can delete an unexpired `sent` row (silently — :323-337 logs only held/sending) or a `sending` row whose FCM send later succeeds; map absence then isn't proof and a real phone alert is abandoned with no trace. Fix: (a) track whether any unexpired row has ever been evicted (e.g. latestUnexpiredEvictionAtMs); proof-of-absence requires startedAtMs <= seenThroughAt AND no such eviction could cover this terminal (a global flag disabling the silent return after any unexpired eviction is acceptable — evictions at 512 live alerts are near-impossible in practice, so correctness beats precision); (b) log sent/retracted evictions loudly with the alert id and fix the \"costs nothing\" comment at :317-337 plus the \"logs loudly\" claim at :923-926. Tests: evicted-sent case, sending-evicted-then-accepted case.\n\n4. MAJOR — resyncAgentStatus.ts:509: cooldown marks a terminal repaired immediately after the fire-and-forget call — an accepted:false (documented transient during host/bridge startup) or transport rejection still inserts the key, skipping the needed repair for 30 min. Fix: reportTerminalSeen returns acceptance; markRepaired only on accepted:true; failed attempts get a SHORT retry cooldown (or attempt cursor) so rotation is preserved without labeling failure as repaired.\n\n5. MINOR — resyncAgentStatus.ts:110 (both reviewers): cooldown map has no hard cap — 513+ fresh entries grow past the stated 512. After age pruning, evict oldest-first down to the bound.\n\n6. MINOR — resyncAgentStatus.ts:455: `statuses: {}` also suppresses wasAwaitingPermission — a turn-end that arrived while a permission was pending counts as wouldRaiseReview though the real transition shows no green (contained by fix 3's gating: warm host drops silently; restarted host costs one blind c). Fix: pass a synthetic statuses entry when the row indicates pending permission if that info is available on the row; otherwise document the wider report set honestly in the comment.\n\nThen: rerun ALL affected tests incl. the new focused suites, lint, marker gate. Report per-item + test counts. Do not churn anything the reviewers confirmed (the durable eligibility predicate, membership/layout effect split shape, desired-at-fire-time retry, privacy rewrite).","summary":"Dispatch round-3 fix union to fork agent","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"Round 3 — final verification split: one reviewer …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2435,"cache_read_input_tokens":213937,"output_tokens":2840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1047},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2435,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2840,"cache_read_input_tokens":213937,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2435},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"9d45c881-16c9-4fde-ad46-060928c7ef24","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:01:09.682Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
