{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:19:43.664Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0165sPSSVtdtcuNWyWZ62TKL</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All six fixed, three test suites added. Changes remain uncommitted in the worktree.\n\n## Per-item\n\n**1. MAJOR — listener subscribed to a shadow registry entry** — Verified the exact mechanism in `terminal-runtime-registry.ts`: `onTitleChange` → `getOrCreateEntry(terminalId, instanceId = terminalId)` mints the `(terminalId, terminalId)` default, and `getPrimaryEntry` then *prefers* that empty default — so `getTitle` starts answering `undefined` for everyone, not just the listener. Fixes:\n- New non-creating `terminalRuntimeRegistry.hasInstance(terminalId, instanceId)`.\n- New `collectTerminalPaneRefs(layout)` → `(terminalId, paneId)` pairs.\n- `GetTerminalTitle` now takes `(terminalId, paneId)`; the title pane's own id is threaded through `resolveTabTitle`, so live titles are read instance-exact.\n- Listener reconciliation extracted to `subscribeTerminalTitleListeners`, which checks `hasInstance` then subscribes with the pane id. No path can create an entry.\n\n**2. MAJOR — equal-hash fast path ignored an older in-flight send** — The fast path now requires a *quiet* workspace (`pending === null &amp;&amp; timer === null &amp;&amp; inFlight === 0`), and every accepted completion reconciles: if its hash is not the current `desired`, it clears `sentHash` **and** enqueues `desired` rather than leaving nobody to push it. `inFlight` is tracked around the chained mutation. The A/C inversion is a regression test that fails against the old code (C early-returns, A lands, nothing re-queues C).\n\n**3. MAJOR — eviction vs proof-of-absence** — (a) `unexpiredEvictionAtMs` latches whenever an *unexpired* row of any state is evicted, and proof-of-absence now requires `live === null &amp;&amp; startedAtMs &lt;= seenThroughAt &amp;&amp; unexpiredEvictionAtMs === null`. Coarse and global, as you allowed — at 512 live alerts a cheap wrong answer (a blind `c` the phone drops) beats an abandoned real notification. (b) `evictOldest` now logs **every** unexpired eviction loudly with the alert id and state; the \"sent/retracted is only a tombstone and costs nothing\" comment is gone (a `sent` row is the only record that can retract a live notification; a `retracted` row is the re-mint guard), and the \"HONEST LIMIT\" paragraph in `markLifecycleSeen` is rewritten since the limit no longer exists. Tests: evicted-sent, sending-evicted-then-accepted, and proof-disabled-after-eviction.\n\n**4. MAJOR — cooldown recorded before the answer** — `reportTerminalSeen` now returns `Promise&lt;boolean&gt;` (never rejects). The repair records the attempt only once resolved: accepted → 30 min, `accepted:false` or transport failure → 60 s. Counters are `seenRepairsSent`/`Skipped`/`Deferred`.\n\n**5. MINOR — unbounded cooldown map** — After age pruning, the map is trimmed **oldest-first** to `MAX_REPAIR_COOLDOWN_ENTRIES` (512), so 513 fresh entries can no longer sit above the bound.\n\n**6. MINOR — `statuses: {}` hid `wasAwaitingPermission`** — When `row.pendingPermission === true` a synthetic `permission` entry is passed, so a turn-end that landed on a pending permission is correctly *not* eligible. `pendingPermission === null` (host could not read its markers) stays in the wider set, documented honestly and contained by #3's gating.\n\n## New focused suites (the three churned files)\n\n| Suite | Tests | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `companionAlertSync.test.ts` | 18 | wire shape, debounce, hash guard, refused/thrown hashes not recorded, **A/C inversion**, retry-sends-latest, retry cancellation, reconnect/host-change re-send, release, `reportTerminalSeen` acceptance/rejection/validation |\n| `resyncAgentStatus.test.ts` | 13 | **the visibility-suppressed headline case**, not-read-through, no-seen-mark, non-green event, pending-permission, foreign workspace, cap+defer, **rotation across epochs**, accepted vs unconsumed vs rejected cooldowns, per-host keying |\n| `terminalTitleListeners.test.ts` | 10 | subscribes by pane id, **never addresses a non-existent runtime**, exact-pair check (a live sibling instance does not authorise), one listener per pane, non-terminal panes ignored, multi-layout, full teardown, event forwarding |\n\nTwo narrow test seams were added for #4/#5 (`__peekRepairCooldownForTest`, `__REPAIR_COOLDOWNS_FOR_TEST`, `__resetRepairCooldownsForTest`) because the 30-min vs 60-s distinction is otherwise unobservable within a test's lifetime; `MAX_STATE_ENTRIES` is now exported so the eviction tests cannot drift from it.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Host companion suite: 345 pass / 0 fail** (23 files) — +3 eviction/proof tests.\n- **Renderer: 89 pass / 0 fail** (8 files) — was 49 across 5; +40 across 3 new suites.\n- **Biome** (lint + format) across all touched paths incl. the registry: **0 diagnostics**, no suppressions.\n- **Marker gate** (bash): **All 160 present.**\n- **tsc**: desktop — no errors in any touched file; host-service — only the pre-existing `curation-gates.test.ts:341`.\n\nNothing the reviewers confirmed was touched: the durable eligibility predicate, the membership/layout effect split, desired-at-fire-time retries, and the privacy rewrite are all unchanged in substance — #6 only *narrowed* the eligibility predicate, and #1's extraction moved the listener loop into a tested helper without altering the split.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>649181</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>54</tool_uses><duration_ms>1113968</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
