{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:34:13.873Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Fixed and verified. Changes remain uncommitted in the worktree.\n\n## The finding\n\nConfirmed both halves before fixing:\n- `layout.tsx:292` — `V2NotificationController` is an **earlier sibling** of `Outlet`, so its effect runs first on the commit that adds a pane.\n- `TerminalPane.tsx:153-163` — the runtime is created in the pane's own effect via `terminalRuntimeRegistry.mount(terminalId, container, appearance, terminalInstanceId)`, which changes no layout state.\n\nSo `hasInstance(terminalId, paneId)` was correctly false at reconciliation, the pair was skipped, and nothing ever brought it back. The pane-key fix made the *check* correct but left the *lifecycle* one-shot.\n\n## Fix\n\n**`terminal-runtime-registry.ts`** — added `onInstanceRegistered(cb)`, a read-only observer notified from `getOrCreateEntry` **after** the entry is fully registered (so an observer calling `hasInstance`/`onTitleChange` for that pair sees it). Listener throws are caught and logged — an observer must never break terminal creation. The no-default-entry guarantee is untouched: this path creates nothing, and `hasInstance` remains the only existence check.\n\n**`terminalTitleListeners.ts`** — reconciliation now keeps a **waiting list** of exact pairs whose runtime did not exist. When the registry announces one, it installs the title listener against that exact `(terminalId, paneId)` and fires `onTitleChange()` once — the runtime that just registered may already carry a title the reconciliation pass could not read, which is what makes the context sync fire. The instance observer is only subscribed when something is actually pending, and teardown clears the waiting list plus every listener, including ones installed late.\n\n## Count reconciliation\n\nSol was right — the file had **9** tests, not 10; my previous report miscounted. It now has **17** (9 original + 8 new), and the totals below are recomputed from actual runs rather than carried forward.\n\nNew tests in the `pending instances` block:\n- **the exact sequence**: pair absent at reconciliation → `registerInstance` with *no* layout change → exact `(terminal-1, pane-1)` listener installed → sync fired once;\n- title changes forwarded through a late-installed listener;\n- a non-pending instance (different terminal, and same terminal under a different pane) installs nothing;\n- each pending pair subscribes exactly once across a remount;\n- present pairs subscribe immediately while only missing ones wait;\n- the instance observer exists only when something is pending;\n- teardown before the instance arrives installs nothing;\n- teardown after a late install still unsubscribes it.\n\nAlso fixed two more literal NUL bytes that had been written into `terminalTitleListeners.ts` and its test (same ripgrep-binary hazard as round 2's `push-schema.test.ts`) — both now use `\\u0000`.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Renderer: 97 pass / 0 fail** (8 files) — `terminalTitleListeners` 9 → 17.\n- **Host companion suite: 345 pass / 0 fail** (23 files) — unchanged.\n- **`src/renderer/lib/terminal`: 308 pass / 3 fail** — the 3 (`launchCommandInPane` ×2, `writeCommandsInPane`) are **pre-existing**; I verified by stashing only the registry change and re-running: byte-identical failures with and without it.\n- **Biome** (lint + format) across all touched paths: **0 diagnostics**.\n- **Marker gate** (bash): **All 160 present.**\n- **tsc**: desktop — no errors in any touched file; host-service — only the long-standing `curation-gates.test.ts:341`.\n\nNothing else was touched; items 2-6 and the earlier confirmed work are unchanged.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>678407</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>34</tool_uses><duration_ms>552933</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
