ists.\n- `titleUnsubscribes: Map&lt;pairKey, () =&gt; void&gt;` — the *current* teardown per pair.\n- `install(ref)` calls the recorded teardown first, then subscribes against the exact `(terminalId, paneId)` — so a re-announcement **replaces** rather than stacks (and after a dispose the stale teardown is harmlessly inert).\n- The observer is armed whenever `desired` is non-empty, not only when something is missing; any announcement for a desired pair re-installs and fires the sync.\n- Teardown stops the observer, runs every recorded teardown, and clears both maps.\n\nThe no-default-entry guarantee is unchanged: `hasInstance` is still the only existence check and nothing on this path can create an entry.\n\n## Test double corrected\n\nThe fake registry now models the real lifecycle rather than a convenient one:\n- `registerInstance` announces **only on real creation**; an existing pair returns early and announces nothing (matching `getOrCreateEntry`).\n- `disposeInstance` deletes the key **and clears that pair's live listeners** (matching `disposeEntry` + `disposeTransport`).\n- `fireTitle` reaches only listeners attached to the runtime live *right now* — so \"the listener was reinstalled\" is a behavioural assertion, not bookkeeping.\n\nThat also retired the misleading \"remount subscribes once\" test, which had announced a still-existing pair twice; it is now an explicit assertion that re-announcing a live pair is a no-op.\n\n## New tests (`disposed and recreated runtimes`)\n\n- **the required regression**: present initially → subscribed and live (`fireTitle` syncs) → `disposeInstance` (`fireTitle` now syncs nothing) → exact recreation **with no layout change** → listener reinstalled, sync fired, and the new listener verified live;\n- several dispose/recreate cycles leak nothing (each install replaces; exactly one live at teardown);\n- only the recreated pair is re-subscribed, not its neighbours;\n- a recreation of a pair the layouts never wanted is ignored;\n- after teardown, recreation installs nothing.\n\nPlus the observer-arming assertion was inverted to match the fix: it is now armed whenever anything is desired (present or not), and only skipped when the layouts want no terminals at all.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Renderer: 103 pass / 0 fail** (8 files); `terminalTitleListeners` 17 → **23**.\n- **Host companion suite: 345 pass / 0 fail** (23 files) — unchanged.\n- **`src/renderer/lib/terminal`: 308 pass / 3 fail** — the same 3 pre-existing failures (`launchCommandInPane` ×2, `writeCommandsInPane`), confirmed unrelated last round by stashing the registry change.\n- **Biome** (lint + format) across all touched paths: **0 diagnostics**.\n- **Marker gate** (bash): **All 160 present.**\n- **tsc**: desktop — no errors in any touched file; host-service — only the long-standing `curation-gates.test.ts:341`.\n\nNo other behaviour was touched; the registry's `onInstanceRegistered` and `hasInstance` additions are unchanged from the previous round.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>678459</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>22</tool_uses><duration_ms>438659</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"3966894c-042e-47a2-8631-e85c732cb6af","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:44:08.566Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
