{"parentUuid":"202fcace-a468-421e-a519-defe5459fb5e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a309a21121f4ead3f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Fo4mud4MnLZmQfA7FsPwq2</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a309a21121f4ead3f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review: altitude angle\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Review complete. Both trees read end-to-end (fork host+renderer diffs, companion Kotlin diffs, all new files, FINAL.md rulings). Overall verdict: the mechanism-level design is sound — the registry-as-display-cache, single composition point in `:core`, tombstone suppression, retraction-as-own-type, and proof-of-absence latch are all at the right depth and match FINAL.md. Findings below are expression/mechanism altitude only; none change semantics.\n\n## Findings — FORK\n\n1. **`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\routes\\_authenticated\\components\\V2NotificationController\\lib\\companionAlertSync.ts:320-352`** — two stacked doc comments on `reportTerminalSeen`; first is a stale earlier draft. Cost: the dead block says `seenThroughAt` is \"the binding's `lastEventAt`\" while the live block (and the code) say \"the review entry's `occurredAt`\" — a reader can land on the wrong rule for exactly the subtlety the 4 review rounds fixed. Deeper form: delete the first block.\n\n2. **`...\\lib\\resyncAgentStatus.ts:80-81`** — stray doubled `/**` opener above `REPAIR_COOLDOWN_MS`. Cost: malformed JSDoc; review-round artifact. Fix: drop the inner `/**`.\n\n3. **`...\\lib\\companionAlertSync.ts:53-215`** — sync state machine carries `desired` + `pending` + `timer` + `inFlight` + `chain` where `pending` is always identical to `desired` when set (every caller writes both, line 137/161), and the accepted-but-desired-moved branch (189-201) re-implements a work loop by recursive self-call. Cost: three coordination fields whose safety (`isQuiet` guard, \"retry must read desired\") is enforced by comments rather than structure. Deeper same-semantics shape: dirty-loop reducer — `{desired, sentHash, debounceTimer, running, retries, retryTimer}`; after debounce, a single loop `while hash(desired)!==sentHash → send desired`. Kills `pending`, the `inFlight` counter, the recursion, and makes \"a retry can only push toward current truth\" true by construction. Debounce, hash guard, backoff, and forget-on-reconnect all keep their exact behavior.\n\n4. **`...\\lib\\resyncAgentStatus.ts:100-140`** — cooldown entries store `{at, cooldownMs}` and every reader recomputes age (`isInRepairCooldown`, the expiry prune). Deeper form: store one number, `retryEligibleAtMs` (`now + cooldown`); check becomes `nowMs &lt; until`, prune becomes `until &lt;= nowMs`, and the accepted/failed distinction stays a single ternary at write time. Same semantics incl. the backwards-clock fail-toward-repair. (The cap+cooldown+rotation trio itself is fine — no simpler mechanism gives the same rotation guarantee.)\n\n5. **`...\\hooks\\useV2NotificationStatus\\useV2NotificationStatus.ts:104-133` + `...\\useClearActivePaneAttention\\useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:46-71`** — the two user-intent sites duplicate the identical ~20-line ritual: read review entry by source key → capture `occurredAt` → `markTerminalSeen` → report only if `clearedReview &amp;&amp; reviewAt !== null`. Cost: the read-before-delete ordering and the \"review occurredAt, not binding lastEventAt\" rule are pinned in two places; one site can drift. Deeper form: one helper (e.g. `markSeenAndReportRead({workspaceId, terminalId, lastEventAt})` in `companionAlertSync.ts`) called from both sites — keeps \"only the two user-intent sites call it\" intact and FINAL.md §4's boolean-returning `markTerminalSeen` untouched. (The richer alternative — `markTerminalSeen` returning the removed entry's `occurredAt` — would delete the pre-read entirely but deviates from §4's stated boolean signature, so the helper is the deviation-free move.)\n\n6. **`...\\components\\HostNotificationSubscriber\\HostNotificationSubscriber.tsx` (workspaceIds `useMemo`)** — recovers the workspace-id array by string-parsing the serialized `workspacesKey` (`split(\"|\")[0].split(\",\")`). Cost: silent coupling to the key's print format; a separator change in the key builder breaks membership registration invisibly. Deeper form: memoize the id array where the key is composed and derive the key from the array (single source), passing both down.\n\n7. **`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\registry.ts:174-316`** — third and fourth hand-rolled copies of the singleton-sink pattern (`set` throw-if-other / `clear` compare-and-null / `record` try-catch-log): mirror-change, alert-context, lifecycle-seen. Cost: ~80 duplicated lines; each new bridge capability re-copies the same registration discipline. Deeper form: generic `createBridgeSlot&lt;T&gt;(name, onErrorMessage)` returning `{set, clear, invoke}`; the three sinks become one-liners with identical semantics (presence/bridge slots differ enough to leave alone).\n\n8. **`...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\lifecycle-alerts.ts` — `supersede()` (~line 656) vs `retractById()` (~line 674)** — both walk the same per-state transition ladder (held→delete, sending→flag, sent→retracted+fire, retracted→noop) as separate hand-written copies. Cost: FINAL.md §4's supersession/storm-guard semantics live in two places; an edit to one ladder (e.g. a logging change, a new state) can miss the other. Deeper form: one `retractExisting(alert, reason)` transition function applied by both; `retractById` keeps only its unique no-row tombstone branch.\n\n9. **`...\\push.ts:2167` + `...\\lifecycle-alerts.ts` (`resolveContextSafely` ×2)** — two identical try/catch→null wrappers around the same injected resolver, both fed `resolveAlertContext` from `index.ts`. Deeper form: make the resolver total at the composition root (wrap once in `index.ts`, inject the already-safe function) and delete both consumer-side wrappers. Same failure policy, one copy.\n\n10. **`...\\push.ts` — `contextKeys()` vs `buildLifecycleRetractPushData()`** — the `t` normalization expression (`typeof handle === \"string\" &amp;&amp; LIFECYCLE_ID_PATTERN.test(handle) ? handle : \"\"`) is duplicated verbatim. Micro: extract `opaqueHandleOrEmpty(handle)`.\n\n11. **`...\\lifecycle-alerts.ts` — `unexpiredEvictionAtMs`** — declared as a timestamp but only ever null-checked; the time value is never read or logged. Micro: a boolean `hasEvictedUnexpired` states the actual mechanism (a process-wide latch), removing the implication that recency matters.\n\n## Findings — COMPANION\n\n12. **`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\protocol\\Push.kt` (`parseV3`) + `LifecyclePush.kt` (`LifecyclePushData.parseV3`, `LifecycleRetractPushData.parseV3`)** — the `t` handling (`requireOpaqueOrEmpty` then `if empty \"\" else Ids.requireOpaque16`) is written out three times. Micro: a shared `terminalIdOrEmpty(data, label)` beside the existing file-level `expiry` helper. Same strictness.\n\nOtherwise the companion tree is **clean at altitude**: text composition is genuinely single-sourced in `AlertNotificationPresentation`, the retraction is a distinct type exactly as §8 rules, `PushEnvelope` was refactored into shared halves rather than forked, the tombstone (`suppress` vs `release`) and `PendingLifecycleDismissals` are principled single mechanisms rather than guard stacks, and the watch renders relayed text literally with old-peer fallbacks.\n\n**Explicitly examined and NOT flagged** (a deeper same-semantics shape does not exist): the repair cap+cooldown+rotation trio as a mechanism (only its entry encoding, #4); the proof-of-absence latch (`startedAtMs` + live-map + eviction latch is the minimal honest evidence model short of durable state, which is out of scope); the `superseded` flag alongside the state enum (FINAL.md §4 specifies it); per-version rule tables in `push.ts` (wire schema frozen; the \"name rule ⇒ exempt list\" double-check is a deliberate pinned privacy guard); `retractById`'s fabricated tombstone fields (a discriminated-union `HeldAlert` would cost more than it saves given the map's uniform consumers).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>192189</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>330369</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:52:37.053Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3e9e5854-5444-4aa9-a9bd-ef07ac18b109","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:52:37.053Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3e9e5854-5444-4aa9-a9bd-ef07ac18b109","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a76f62abae280edf8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a76f62abae280edf8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review: reuse angle\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Review complete. Scope: (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) uncommitted changes in both trees, reuse angle only. Overall the change reuses well (PushEnvelope helpers, `AlertNotificationPresentation` shared by phone+watch, `resolveV2AgentStatusTransition`, `deriveHandle`, `enqueue`/`broadcast`, caps imported not re-declared). Findings:\n\n**Strong (existing helper explicitly exists to prevent this copy)**\n\n1. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:439` — new `hasLoneSurrogate()` re-implements exported `findUnpairedSurrogate()` at `packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\keystrokes.ts:752`. That helper's doc says verbatim: *\"Exported because `/v1/message` types text into the same terminals through a different writer and must not have a second, drifting copy of this rule.\"* push.ts is now that second drifting copy. Cost: two surrogate-walk implementations of one protocol rule in one package. Fix: `findUnpairedSurrogate(value) !== null` — identical semantics (both do the same high/low index walk; `isWellFormed` is unavailable at lib ES2022, which is why the helper exists).\n\n2. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3\\apps\\desktop\\test-setup.ts:~141` — new `mockSessionStorage` is a line-for-line copy of `mockLocalStorage` (lines 112–126, same file). Cost: 14 duplicated lines of Storage stub. Fix: extract local `createMockStorage(): Storage` factory, call twice.\n\n**Moderate**\n\n3. Companion repo `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\protocol\\AlertContext.kt:113` — `isRenderable()` re-implements `SemanticText.firstUnpairedSurrogate` (Answer.kt:72) plus `SemanticText.firstControlChar`'s C0/DEL/C1 set (Answer.kt:54), adding only U+2028/2029. Both are `private` in `SemanticText`, so the fix is exposing them (`internal`) and composing, keeping only the 2028/2029 check local. Behavior-preserving — same walks, same sets — so the frozen golden vectors and FINAL.md §8 rulings are untouched. Cost: second copy of the §0.3 control-char table and the surrogate walk in the same `core.protocol` package.\n\n4. `C:\\...\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\routes\\_authenticated\\components\\V2NotificationController\\lib\\alertContexts.ts:147` — `titlePaneOf()` duplicates `getTitlePane()` in `...\\useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceTabChips\\utils\\resolveDashboardSidebarTabTitle\\resolveDashboardSidebarTabTitle.ts:16` (\"only pane → active pane → none\"; the code comment even says \"the sidebar's rule verbatim\"). Types differ (`Tab&lt;unknown&gt;` Record vs descriptor array), so reuse needs a small shared generic over `{id}[] + activePaneId`; worth doing because the two ladders must stay in sync and only a comment enforces it today. (Not the derived-title ladder — FINAL.md §8 correctly keeps that unshared for privacy.)\n\n5. `C:\\...\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\routes\\_authenticated\\components\\V2NotificationController\\lib\\companionAlertSync.ts:34` — `log()` is the 4th copy of the `ndots()` JSON-console-info logger (identical