{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:53:29.238Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a947b5f582af77e0c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a947b5f582af77e0c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Simplify review: simplification angle\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings — simplification only, both trees reviewed in full. Ordered by payoff. Wire schema, golden vectors, and the four deliberate mechanisms untouched.\n\n**Fork worktree** (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3`)\n\n1. `...\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\routes\\_authenticated\\components\\V2NotificationController\\lib\\companionAlertSync.ts:320-352` — **duplicate JSDoc block**. Two near-identical doc comments stacked back-to-back on `reportTerminalSeen` (lines 320-332 superseded by 333-352; older one says \"binding's `lastEventAt`\", newer says \"review entry's `occurredAt`\"). Leftover from a review round; the stale copy states the *wrong* stamp. Delete lines 320-332.\n\n2. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\trpc\\router\\companion\\companion.ts:284-307` — **`serializePerWorkspace` serialises synchronous work**. `recordCompanionAlertContexts` → registry `sync()` is fully synchronous (`sync(input): AlertContextSyncResult`, no await inside `work`). A promise chain over sync work cannot change ordering vs calling directly in handler order — ~25 lines + a chain Map guarding an interleaving that cannot occur. Simpler: call `recordCompanionAlertContexts(...)` directly in the mutation; drop the chain. (If a future async sink is anticipated, that belongs with the type change that makes it async.)\n\n3. `...\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\hooks\\host-service\\useV2NotificationStatus\\useV2NotificationStatus.ts:103-133` and `...\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\routes\\_authenticated\\_dashboard\\v2-workspace\\$workspaceId\\hooks\\useClearActivePaneAttention\\useClearActivePaneAttention.ts:46-75` — **copy-paste seen-and-report block ×2**. Both do: read review entry by source key → capture `occurredAt` if `status===\"review\"` → `markTerminalSeen` → guard `!clearedReview || reviewAt === null` → `reportTerminalSeen`. ~25 lines each incl. duplicated rationale comments; a third call site would fork the logic again. Simpler: one exported helper (e.g. `markTerminalSeenAndReportRead({workspaceId, terminalId, lastEventAt})` in `companionAlertSync.ts` or beside the store) holding the read-before-delete ordering and the comment once.\n\n4. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\lifecycle-alerts.ts:644-666` vs `683-708` — **`supersede` and `retractById` duplicate the same 4-state transition** (held → delete + identical log line; sending → `superseded: true`; sent → `retracted` + `fireRetraction`; retracted → no-op), ~22 lines twice. Divergence risk on the next state added. Simpler: extract `retireAlert(alert, reason)` applying the transition to one alert; `supersede` loops it, `retractById` calls it for the known-id branch (tombstone branch stays as is).\n\n5. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:365-397` — **`PUSH_VALUE_RULES_BY_VERSION` per-version nesting is derivable**. Rules never vary by version for any key (v/k/i/w/n/x = `\"opaque\"` everywhere; t/pn/wn/tn/tc exist only on v3). Membership per version+kind is already enforced by `PUSH_DATA_KEYS_BY_VERSION_KIND` + `assertClosedKeySet`. Simpler: one flat `PUSH_VALUE_RULES: Record&lt;string, PushValueRule&gt;`; the `rule === undefined` throw and the exempt-key cross-check keep working unchanged; ~25 lines saved. (`push-schema.test.ts` pins only `PUSH_NAME_EXEMPT_KEYS`, not this table — no test weakened.)\n\n6. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:2167-2181` and `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\lifecycle-alerts.ts:561-583` — **`resolveContextSafely` duplicated in both consumers**. `index.ts` builds ONE `resolveAlertContext` and hands it to both; each consumer re-wraps it in an identical try/catch→null+log. Simpler: wrap once in `index.ts` (a resolver that never throws) and drop both consumer wrappers — semantics (\"resolver throw costs the names, never the notification\") unchanged, just enforced at the source.\n\n7. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\registry.ts:235-324` — **3rd and 4th copy of the sink-slot boilerplate**. `alertContextSink` + `lifecycleSeenSink` each repeat the set/clear/record-with-catch pattern already present for the mirror-change sink (~30 lines per slot). Simpler: `createSinkSlot&lt;TIn, TOut&gt;(name, failureLogLine)` factory returning `{set, clear, record}`; each slot becomes ~4 lines, identity checks and never-throw semantics preserved.\n\n8. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:732-757` vs `912-940` — **`t`-handle sanitising expression duplicated**: `typeof handle === \"string\" &amp;&amp; LIFECYCLE_ID_PATTERN.test(handle) ? handle : \"\"` appears in `contextKeys` and again in `buildLifecycleRetractPushData`. Extract `sanitizeTerminalHandle(handle)`. Same file, minor: `(context.tabCount as number)` casts ×2 in `contextKeys` — assign `const tc = context.tabCount` and narrow with `typeof tc === \"number\"` instead of casting.\n\n**Companion repo** (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion`)\n\n9. `core\\...\\protocol\\Push.kt:122-146`, `LifecyclePush.kt:112-133`, `LifecyclePush.kt:186-204` — **optional-terminal-id parse triplicated, with a redundant check inside each copy**. All three do: `requireOpaqueOrEmpty(t)` then `if (t.isEmpty()) \"\" else Ids.requireOpaque16(t, \"…\")`. `requireOpaque16` (exact 22 chars + charset) subsumes the pattern check for non-empty values, so the `requireOpaqueOrEmpty` line is dead weight in each copy. Simpler: one shared `Ids.optionalOpaque16(value, field)` (empty → `\"\"`, else `requireOpaque16`); drop the pre-check. Client validation stays strictly as strong.\n\n10. `core\\...\\protocol\\Push.kt:149-155` vs `LifecyclePush.kt:211-213` — **private `expiry(data)` helper duplicated across the two parser files** (LifecyclePush's takes a label, Push's hardcodes it). Move one `expiry(data, label)` into `PushEnvelope` next to `required`. Same-scale nit: `Push.kt` `OPAQUE_KEYS_V3 = KEYS` is a pure alias — use `KEYS` directly or keep only if the name earns its line.\n\n11. `core\\...\\protocol\\AlertNotificationText.kt:58-76` — **`lifecycle()` `when` duplicates the tab/no-tab shape per kind**. Simpler: select the `(tabBody, plainBody)` pair by kind, then one `if (context.namesTab)`; halves the branch body. Wording constants unchanged.\n\nClean / no action: `push-context.ts` registry, `alertContexts.ts`, `terminalTitleListeners.ts`, `PendingLifecycleDismissals.kt`, `routeLifecycleRetract`, watch notifier changes, `WearProtocol` redacted `toString`s (pinned by test), test-only seams in `resyncAgentStatus.ts` (all consumed by its test), the `workspacesKey`-derived `workspaceIds` memo (identity rationale is real), and the `buildQuestion`/`pushQuestion` `AlertContext.NONE` defaults (both default call sites exist).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249569</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>48</tool_uses><duration_ms>402419</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
