eck keep working unchanged; ~25 lines saved. (`push-schema.test.ts` pins only `PUSH_NAME_EXEMPT_KEYS`, not this table — no test weakened.)\n\n6. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:2167-2181` and `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\lifecycle-alerts.ts:561-583` — **`resolveContextSafely` duplicated in both consumers**. `index.ts` builds ONE `resolveAlertContext` and hands it to both; each consumer re-wraps it in an identical try/catch→null+log. Simpler: wrap once in `index.ts` (a resolver that never throws) and drop both consumer wrappers — semantics (\"resolver throw costs the names, never the notification\") unchanged, just enforced at the source.\n\n7. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\registry.ts:235-324` — **3rd and 4th copy of the sink-slot boilerplate**. `alertContextSink` + `lifecycleSeenSink` each repeat the set/clear/record-with-catch pattern already present for the mirror-change sink (~30 lines per slot). Simpler: `createSinkSlot&lt;TIn, TOut&gt;(name, failureLogLine)` factory returning `{set, clear, record}`; each slot becomes ~4 lines, identity checks and never-throw semantics preserved.\n\n8. `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\push.ts:732-757` vs `912-940` — **`t`-handle sanitising expression duplicated**: `typeof handle === \"string\" &amp;&amp; LIFECYCLE_ID_PATTERN.test(handle) ? handle : \"\"` appears in `contextKeys` and again in `buildLifecycleRetractPushData`. Extract `sanitizeTerminalHandle(handle)`. Same file, minor: `(context.tabCount as number)` casts ×2 in `contextKeys` — assign `const tc = context.tabCount` and narrow with `typeof tc === \"number\"` instead of casting.\n\n**Companion repo** (`C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion`)\n\n9. `core\\...\\protocol\\Push.kt:122-146`, `LifecyclePush.kt:112-133`, `LifecyclePush.kt:186-204` — **optional-terminal-id parse triplicated, with a redundant check inside each copy**. All three do: `requireOpaqueOrEmpty(t)` then `if (t.isEmpty()) \"\" else Ids.requireOpaque16(t, \"…\")`. `requireOpaque16` (exact 22 chars + charset) subsumes the pattern check for non-empty values, so the `requireOpaqueOrEmpty` line is dead weight in each copy. Simpler: one shared `Ids.optionalOpaque16(value, field)` (empty → `\"\"`, else `requireOpaque16`); drop the pre-check. Client validation stays strictly as strong.\n\n10. `core\\...\\protocol\\Push.kt:149-155` vs `LifecyclePush.kt:211-213` — **private `expiry(data)` helper duplicated across the two parser files** (LifecyclePush's takes a label, Push's hardcodes it). Move one `expiry(data, label)` into `PushEnvelope` next to `required`. Same-scale nit: `Push.kt` `OPAQUE_KEYS_V3 = KEYS` is a pure alias — use `KEYS` directly or keep only if the name earns its line.\n\n11. `core\\...\\protocol\\AlertNotificationText.kt:58-76` — **`lifecycle()` `when` duplicates the tab/no-tab shape per kind**. Simpler: select the `(tabBody, plainBody)` pair by kind, then one `if (context.namesTab)`; halves the branch body. Wording constants unchanged.\n\nClean / no action: `push-context.ts` registry, `alertContexts.ts`, `terminalTitleListeners.ts`, `PendingLifecycleDismissals.kt`, `routeLifecycleRetract`, watch notifier changes, `WearProtocol` redacted `toString`s (pinned by test), test-only seams in `resyncAgentStatus.ts` (all consumed by its test), the `workspacesKey`-derived `workspaceIds` memo (identity rationale is real), and the `buildQuestion`/`pushQuestion` `AlertContext.NONE` defaults (both default call sites exist).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>249569</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>48</tool_uses><duration_ms>402419</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:53:29.238Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5698251-7bf5-458c-87ed-3cc7573786e5","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:53:29.238Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset