{"parentUuid":"625b6c14-30d1-4f2d-998e-3503338aa68f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce5udWE8i9CgE43iGx1hv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHmbu56uTD3tD4Fns7J2vw","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"/simplify results — apply these in the worktree. Rules: behavior identical, all suites stay green, golden vectors byte-identical, don't weaken tests; if an item breaks a test asserting real behavior, REVERT that item and report it skipped.\n\nAPPLY (fork):\n1. push.ts hasLoneSurrogate → delete it and use exported findUnpairedSurrogate from companion/keystrokes.ts:752 (`!== null`) — that helper's doc explicitly forbids a second drifting copy. Golden/surrogate tests must stay byte-identical.\n2. companionAlertSync.ts:320-332 — delete the stale duplicate JSDoc block (it states the WRONG stamp: binding lastEventAt vs review occurredAt).\n3. resyncAgentStatus.ts:80-81 — remove stray doubled `/**` opener.\n4. apps/desktop/test-setup.ts — extract createMockStorage(): Storage factory; use for both mockLocalStorage and mockSessionStorage.\n5. Extract one exported helper markTerminalSeenAndReportRead({workspaceId, terminalId, lastEventAt}) (in companionAlertSync.ts) holding the read-review-occurredAt-before-delete ritual; call from BOTH intent sites (useV2NotificationStatus, useClearActivePaneAttention). Keeps \"only two user-intent sites\" — they both call the one helper.\n6. lifecycle-alerts.ts — extract retireAlert(alert, reason) for the shared 4-state transition; supersede loops it, retractById uses it for the known-id branch (tombstone branch unchanged).\n7. push.ts:365-397 — flatten PUSH_VALUE_RULES_BY_VERSION to one flat PUSH_VALUE_RULES map (rules never vary by version; membership already enforced by PUSH_DATA_KEYS_BY_VERSION_KIND). Keep the rule-undefined throw + exempt-key cross-check.\n8. resolveContextSafely — wrap ONCE at the index.ts composition root (inject an already-total resolver); delete both consumer-side wrappers (push.ts:2167, lifecycle-alerts.ts:561).\n9. registry.ts — in-file generic createSinkSlot factory; collapse the two new sink slots (alert-context, lifecycle-seen) to it. Leave presence/bridge slots alone.\n10. push.ts — extract sanitizeTerminalHandle(handle); replace both copies; replace the two `as number` tabCount casts with typeof narrowing.\n11. companion.ts serializePerWorkspace — registry sync() is fully synchronous, so the promise chain guards an interleaving that cannot occur: call the sink directly, drop the chain (~25 lines). If any test pins the chain's existence (not behavior), update that test's mechanism only.\n12. Efficiency — HostNotificationSubscriber: (a) key the listener-subscription work on a memoized stable fingerprint of the pane-ref set (pair keys joined) so listener churn happens only when the set changes; (b) in syncAlertContexts, cache last paneLayout REF per workspace and skip unchanged ones before extract+hash; (c) debounce the title-change → syncAlertContexts trigger ~250ms trailing so redraw bursts don't extract N workspaces per event.\n13. companionAlertSync.ts — compute the snapshot hash ONCE per snapshot at queueAlertContextSync entry; carry {snapshot, hash} through desired/pending.\n14. resyncAgentStatus.ts — compute wouldRaiseReview + syntheticStatuses lazily only when alreadyReadThrough && !seedColdStart; cooldown entries store a single retryEligibleAtMs (now+cooldown) instead of {at, cooldownMs} (same backwards-clock fail-toward-repair).\n15. read-api.ts — add prepared findProject(id) point statement; use in resolveAlertContext instead of listProjects().find() per send.\n16. push-context.ts sync() — replace per-terminal findTerminal loop with ONE query (terminal ids by origin_workspace_id → Set membership); same rejection semantics.\n17. HostNotificationSubscriber — derive the workspace-id ARRAY first and build workspacesKey FROM it (stop string-parsing the key with split(\"|\")).\n18. lifecycle-alerts.ts — unexpiredEvictionAtMs is only null-checked: rename to boolean hasEvictedUnexpired.\n\nSKIPPED (deliberate, do not do): dirty-loop reducer rewrite of the sync state machine (structural rewrite of just-verified code); sharing titlePaneOf with the sidebar util and consolidating the ndots logger copies (both touch upstream-owned files — merge surface); generalizing evictOldest across pairing/question-store (verified files).\n\nThen: rerun host companion + renderer suites, lint, marker gate, tsc. Report per-item applied/reverted + final counts.","summary":"Apply simplify findings in fork worktree","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"/simplify results — apply these in the worktree. …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6500,"cache_read_input_tokens":253234,"output_tokens":4774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6500,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4774,"cache_read_input_tokens":253234,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6500},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7d096568-0155-4051-a633-40d0e7195429","timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:54:22.699Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
