{"parentUuid":"8d400b36-a0e4-4046-a01b-e2f5327f1f38","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6NERpxzVB7cWdSuUjwr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UEvvGvj8xjKPTe1NWU8HNx","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"New user-approved requirement before install: ONE-BUZZ-UNTIL-READ for `g` alerts. Live evidence: overnight, one long-running chat minted 16 distinct g alerts (~15min apart, each turn-end while away) = 16 stacked buzzing notifications on v0.1.0. Approved semantics: a chat that finishes again while its previous finished-notification is UNREAD updates that notification silently; reading the chat (retract) resets, so the next finish buzzes fresh.\n\nYour fork-side change (worktree, then I'll re-merge):\n1. lifecycle-alerts.ts: thread the supersede REASON through retireAlert. For a `sent` `g` being retired because a NEW WORK CYCLE started on the terminal (record() outcome \"progress\"): transition sent→retracted WITHOUT fireRetraction — the row is kept for dedupe, the phone notification stays standing and the NEXT g for that terminal will replace it in place (phone keys g notifications by terminal handle now). All other retraction triggers keep firing the c frame: outcome \"session-end\" (chat gone → clear it), markLifecycleSeen (user read), and the superseded-mid-flight markDelivered path (fire c only when the supersede reason was session-end; progress → silent retire there too). `e` alerts unchanged.\n2. Update the affected lifecycle-alerts tests: progress-supersede of sent g fires NO retraction (new test), session-end still fires, seen still fires, storm guard unchanged (retracted stays inert).\n3. No wire change: v3 g/c already carry `t`. No renderer change.\n4. Rerun host companion suite + lint + marker gate. Report.\n\nContext note: this makes the earlier \"supersession retracts delivered alerts\" behavior conditional on reason — deliberate user-approved trigger change recorded in FINAL.md.","summary":"Dispatch one-buzz-until-read host change","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"New user-approved requirement before install: ONE…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":310127,"output_tokens":5261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":461,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5261,"cache_read_input_tokens":310127,"cache_creation_input_tokens":461,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":461},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"efe1f883-b908-4866-a14a-50c96033293b","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:43:31.794Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
