{"parentUuid":"f494ad58-a1fd-4c3e-b8a2-06bb971f87c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6NERpxzVB7cWdSuUjwr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014gx5mN3d1T7x5woRGq2c3D","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"New user-approved requirement before install: ONE-BUZZ-UNTIL-READ for `g` alerts. Live evidence: overnight, one long-running chat produced 16 distinct g alerts (one per turn-end while away) = 16 stacked buzzing notifications on v0.1.0. Approved semantics: a repeat finish of a chat whose finished-notification is still unread updates it SILENTLY in place; after a retract (user read the chat), the next finish is a fresh notification and buzzes. `e` (error) alerts keep current per-event behavior.\n\nYour companion-side change (C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion):\n1. Phone `g` notifications: key by TERMINAL — tag = push `t` when non-empty, else fall back to eventId (t can be \"\" only on the q kind in practice, but stay total); `setOnlyAlertOnce(true)` so an in-place replacement doesn't re-buzz. Maintain a small per-tag \"shown\" record {eventId, expiresAtMs} (in-memory + prefs like SeenLifecycleEvents so it survives process death). Ordering guard: if an incoming g's x (expiry, monotone with mint time) is OLDER than the shown record's, skip posting (stale out-of-order delivery) — still claim its eventId. Claims/suppression stay keyed by eventId exactly as now.\n2. `c` handling: cancel the terminal-tagged notification ONLY when the retracted eventId == that tag's shown eventId (a c for an older cycle must not kill a newer notification); always tombstone the eventId as now. c with t=\"\" → legacy cancel by eventId tag.\n3. Watch: mirror the same identity — add optional terminal field (kotlinx default) to WatchLifecycleAlert and the dismiss payload; watch g notification id keyed by terminal when present (else eventId), same only-alert-once + shown-record + ordering guard semantics; e unchanged. Old-peer defaults keep both directions parseable.\n4. PROTOCOL.md §13.5: document one-buzz-until-read (terminal-keyed identity, silent replace, ordering guard, read-resets-buzz).\n5. Tests: silent in-place replacement; fresh-buzz after cancel; stale-ordering skip; c-matching-shown cancels / c-stale only tombstones; process-death survival of the shown record; v1/v2 and existing suites untouched.\n6. Rerun full Gradle suite; then rebuild both release APKs (assembleRelease). Report per-item + counts + APK paths.","summary":"Dispatch one-buzz-until-read companion change","to":"impl-android","type":"message","recipient":"impl-android","content":"New user-approved requirement before install: ONE…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":310127,"output_tokens":5261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":461,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5261,"cache_read_input_tokens":310127,"cache_creation_input_tokens":461,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":461},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3be0a190-3ede-4e76-af68-d2c9dacb333b","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:43:43.500Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
