next finish buzzes fresh. Host: progress-supersede of a sent `g`","+  retires WITHOUT firing `c` (row kept); session-end and read still fire `c`.","+  `e` alerts keep per-event behavior. Trigger-timing invariant amended by","+  explicit user decision (evidence: 16 stacked buzzes overnight from one","+  orchestration chat on v0.1.0).","+"," - QUESTION bodies remain per-surface (phone = question text, watch = count +","   source): relaying full question text into a watch notification is silently","   clamped by Android at ~1024 chars — the exact defect the watch design forbids."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b3dddaab-ba21-4837-89e3-1489666456c8","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
