{"parentUuid":"41a871d1-9dee-4dfa-86f0-28af33de1a6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6NMKb7u4vfTXGh2Vwwi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both agents are implementing the one-buzz-until-read change and the decision is recorded in the spec. When they report green I'll run a focused review of just this delta, re-commit both repos, rebuild the APKs, and come back to the install question."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_read_input_tokens":316160,"output_tokens":77,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":574,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":77,"cache_read_input_tokens":316160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":574},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"cf303f76-b005-4c65-ae8b-3d61522f43b0","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:43:57.185Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"cf303f76-b005-4c65-ae8b-3d61522f43b0","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":3,"hookInfos":[{"command":"Arming cache keepalive","durationMs":1749},{"command":"uv run python \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\.superset\\\\hooks\\\\superset-notify.py\"","durationMs":506},{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":117705}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:45:54.903Z","uuid":"ff2b402d-dba0-494b-85fa-12dead399392","toolUseID":"87f887c9-38c0-4acf-95d5-33cc0147073e","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:57:26.143Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01UEvvGvj8xjKPTe1NWU8HNx</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Only the pre-existing error. Done — changes remain uncommitted in the worktree.\n\n## `(ONE-BUZZ-UNTIL-READ)` — implemented\n\n**1. Reason threaded through the state machine.** Replaced the free-form `reason: string` with an explicit type, so the one silent case can't be reached by accident:\n\n```ts\ntype RetireReason = { kind: \"new-cycle\" } | { kind: \"session-end\" } | { kind: \"seen\" };\n```\n\nThe whole policy is one predicate:\n\n```ts\nfunction notifiesPhone(alert, reason) {\n  return !(alert.kind === \"g\" &amp;&amp; reason.kind === \"new-cycle\");\n}\n```\n\n- `record()` now splits what it previously merged: `progress` → `{kind:\"new-cycle\"}`, `session-end` → `{kind:\"session-end\"}` (both still supersede; only the notification differs).\n- `retireAlert`: `sent` `g` + new-cycle → transitions to `retracted` **without** `fireRetraction`, keeping the row as the cycle's dedupe record and leaving the notification standing. Logs the silent retirement rather than going quiet in the diagnostics too.\n- `markDelivered` (superseded mid-flight): `HeldAlert` gained `supersededReason`, recorded when the flag is set, because by the time the send lands the event that superseded it is gone. Same predicate decides. A missing reason defaults to **fire** — a spare `c` the phone drops is cheaper than a notification for a chat that no longer exists.\n- `markLifecycleSeen` → `{kind:\"seen\"}` → always fires, so reading resets the cycle and the next finish buzzes fresh.\n- `held` → deleted, never fires (nothing was ever delivered). `retracted` → inert, storm guard unchanged.\n- **`e` untouched**: excluded by the predicate, so an unseen error is never quietly folded away.\n\n**3.** No wire change — v3 `g`/`c` already carry `t`. No renderer change.\n\n## Tests (lifecycle-alerts 36 → 40)\n\nRewritten: *\"retracts a SENT alert when the terminal moves on\"* → **does NOT retract on a new cycle** (storm guard assertion retained, now asserting zero retractions across 20 progress events); *\"does NOT re-mint after retracted\"* → same dedupe guarantee, now proving the silent path still **transitions state rather than deleting the row**; *\"retracts an alert superseded MID-FLIGHT\"* → split into the new-cycle (stays standing) and session-end (comes down) variants.\n\nNew: **session-end retracts a delivered ready alert**; **the next finish still buzzes fresh** after a silent retirement (two distinct alert ids, zero retractions); **a delivered ERROR alert still retracts on a new cycle** — pinning the `e` boundary the rule deliberately excludes.\n\nUnchanged and still green: seen-retracts, seen idempotence, proof-of-absence, eviction, restart fallback.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Host companion suite: 349 pass / 0 fail** (23 files) — was 345, +4.\n- **Biome** (lint + format) on `companion` + `trpc/router/companion`: **0 diagnostics**.\n- **Marker gate**: All 160 present. *(Note: the Bash tool started failing to parse commands mid-session; I ran the gate from PowerShell with Git's `grep` on PATH, which is the same `execFileSync(\"grep\", …)` the script uses.)*\n- **tsc**: only the long-standing `curation-gates.test.ts:341`.\n\nI also updated the `(ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES)` row in `FEATURES.md`, since its prose claimed supersession retracts unconditionally — it now records the measured 16-alert overnight evidence, the silent-on-new-cycle rule, the session-end/seen exceptions and the `e` exclusion.\n\nOne thing to confirm on the companion side before install: this relies on the phone keying `g` notifications **by terminal handle** so the next alert replaces the standing one in place. If that keying isn't in the build you install, the silent retirement would leave the old notification stacked rather than replaced — the opposite of the intent.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>888750</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>834339</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
