-NAMES)` row in `FEATURES.md`, since its prose claimed supersession retracts unconditionally — it now records the measured 16-alert overnight evidence, the silent-on-new-cycle rule, the session-end/seen exceptions and the `e` exclusion.\n\nOne thing to confirm on the companion side before install: this relies on the phone keying `g` notifications **by terminal handle** so the next alert replaces the standing one in place. If that keying isn't in the build you install, the silent retirement would leave the old notification stacked rather than replaced — the opposite of the intent.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>888750</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>834339</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"44c77b99-5230-477a-8e86-4d6defbbf428","timestamp":"2026-08-16T11:57:26.168Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
