{"parentUuid":"2a8ef710-778d-4448-97e5-573e97efe16c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6PtLcN7UNHu3t1EAxcV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LGAhgLPcSz8fofqvVMJbHK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"One more focused verification round — a new user-approved behavior change (ONE-BUZZ-UNTIL-READ) was implemented AFTER your SHIP verdict, in both repos (uncommitted deltas on top of the committed feature). Review ONLY this delta; verdict SHIP or FIX-FIRST.\n\nSemantics (user-approved, recorded in FINAL.md §8): a repeat `g` finish for a chat whose finished-notification is unread replaces it silently; reading retracts and resets so the next finish buzzes; session-end still retracts; `e` per-event unchanged. Evidence: 16 stacked buzzes overnight from one chat on v0.1.0.\n\nFORK worktree (C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3, uncommitted): lifecycle-alerts.ts typed RetireReason {new-cycle|session-end|seen}; notifiesPhone predicate (silent ONLY for g+new-cycle); sent g + new-cycle → retracted WITHOUT fireRetraction (row kept); supersededReason recorded for mid-flight (missing reason defaults to FIRE); session-end/seen always fire; e excluded. Tests 345→349.\n\nCOMPANION (C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion, uncommitted): :core LifecycleAlertIdentity.key — READY keyed t:<terminal> when t non-empty else event; ERROR always e:<event> (prefixed keyspaces); setOnlyAlertOnce silent replace; persisted shown-record {key, eventId, expiresAtMs} bounded 64; ordering guard: older-x g not posted but KEEPS its dedupe claim (LifecyclePost {POSTED|SUPERSEDED|BLOCKED} — superseded never relayed to watch, claim retained); c does two cancels: event-keyed unconditionally + terminal-keyed only when the shown record says that event is showing (match via record, covers c with t=\"\" for a terminal-keyed alert); watch mirrors the same :core rule + store; PendingLifecycleDismissals carries terminal, old 2-field rows decode as no-terminal; PROTOCOL §13.5.6. Tests 341→364 (same 2 pre-existing env failures).\n\nProbe hardest: (1) the implementing agent's own flag — shown-record vs FCM dedupe-window (SeenLifecycleEvents) are two persisted eventId-keyed stores with different lifetimes; find any divergence that re-buzzes a read chat or silences an unread one (eviction from one but not the other, process death between writes, claim-kept-but-not-shown then user reads → next finish must buzz but c for the superseded event...); (2) cross-repo semantic agreement: host silently retires on new-cycle assuming the NEXT g replaces in place — verify the phone's replace actually happens for every path the host stays silent on (incl. mid-flight supersede landing late); (3) the retraction-match race and equal-x boundary; (4) e/g keyspace isolation; (5) no regression to claims/tombstones/proof-of-absence.","summary":"Sol review of one-buzz delta","to":"rev-sol","type":"message","recipient":"rev-sol","content":"One more focused verification round — a new user-…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":319035,"output_tokens":1413,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1413,"cache_read_input_tokens":319035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"867d70a2-c463-4e51-bdc4-380931dcb0f5","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:04:23.231Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d