{"parentUuid":"d3863f1e-5cf1-4d5c-99f4-41b55bfe1c48","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"Building the companion-alert upgrade: notifications now name the project/workspace/tab, retract when you read the chat, and buzz once per unread chat. Final review of that last change is running; next is your go-ahead to install watch and phone apps.","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:10:20.492Z","uuid":"9b783ba4-4d86-4f3d-8292-3c654e0b63c8","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"9b783ba4-4d86-4f3d-8292-3c654e0b63c8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49e6820d-ef30-49de-83ed-bc1cde735b88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"on the left where it says sessions... just checking that if I press X on that row that it sends it to the recycled bin for sessions and also I need access to the recycle bin. currently there's no option to open or show the recycle bin"},"uuid":"a4c1f7d3-5530-4288-acac-e61709d5f462","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:13:48.377Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"a4c1f7d3-5530-4288-acac-e61709d5f462","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\AGENTS.md","snippet":"1\t<!-- ===================================================================== -->\n2\t<!-- FORK MAINTENANCE (khairm Windows ARM64 fork). Everything ABOVE the -->\n3\t<!-- divider is about maintaining this fork; everything BELOW is upstream  -->\n4\t<!-- superset's own developer guide, unchanged, for working on the app.    -->\n5\t<!-- ===================================================================== -->\n6\t\n7\t# superset-windows-arm64 — Windows ARM64 fork maintenance\n8\t\n9\tThis repo is a **vendored fork** of [superset-sh/superset]: the full upstream\n10\tsource with our Windows ARM64 + feature changes committed on top, plus CI that\n11\tbuilds a native **Windows ARM64** one-click NSIS installer. The fork is the\n12\tsource of truth; we track upstream by **merging its deltas**, not by\n13\tre-applying changes. `.fork/upstream-baseline.txt` records the upstream\n14\t`desktop-v*` tag the baseline currently sits on.\n15\t\n16\t## Setup / architecture (high level)\n17\t\n18\t- **Build (deterministic steps, self-repairing).** `.github/workflows/build-arm64.yml`\n19\t  orchestrates a bounded attempt/repair loop `(BUILD-REPAIR)`: the actual build\n20\t  steps (install → compile → materialize the win-arm64 native closure\n21\t  (`scripts/materialize-native-closure.sh`: libsql/tokenizers/node-pty) →\n22\t  package the installer → verify packaged natives are ARM64 → publish) live in\n23\t  `.github/actions/arm64-build/action.yml` as thin shims over `scripts/*.sh`.\n24\t  A failed attempt triggers an Opus 5 (`claude-opus-5`, effort high) repair job\n25\t  that reads the failed log, fixes the checked-out tree, and pushes to the\n26\t  repair branch (nightly candidate / dispatched branch); the next attempt\n27\t  builds that exact sha so every deterministic gate re-runs. Max 3 attempts /\n28\t  2 repairs, then fail loud. Repairs may never change the app version or touch\n29\t  `FEATURES.md` (`scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` gates marker survival).\n30\t- **Nightly merge.** `.github/workflows/nightly-merge.yml` (02:13 UTC): when\n31\t  upstream publishes a newer `desktop-v*` tag, git merges it; Opus 5 resolves\n32\t  conflicted files, then a `(MERGE-ADAPT)` proactive port pass adapts fork-only\n33\t  callers to cleanly-merging upstream API refactors. Deterministic gates follow\n34\t  (FEATURES.md marker survival, dependency/lock consistency, `(REFERR-GATE)`\n35\t  cannot-find-name check), then a bounded `(MERGE-SEMANTIC-GATE)` review →\n36\t  adapt → fresh-review loop (max 3 reviews / 2 repairs). Green all the way =\n37\t  build (with its own repair loop), publish the Release, advance the baseline\n38\t  to the BUILT sha; ANY unrepaired failure hard-aborts with the baseline\n39\t  untouched → fix locally with the maintainer and re-baseline. A\n40\t  `rehearse=true` dispatch replays a night's merge half with zero side effects.\n41\t  A night blocked ONLY by `(AI-UNAVAILABLE)` attempted nothing, so it concludes\n42\t  GREEN (no email) as a loud no-op with build/advance skipped — until\n43\t  `AI_UNAVAILABLE_STREAK_THRESHOLD` (3) consecutive such nights, which fails RED.\n44\t- **Key files.** `FEATURES.md` (feature manifest + fenced `markers` block the\n45\t  gates parse), `.fork/upstream-baseline.txt`,\n46\t  `scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` (REFERR gate),\n47\t  `scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` (standalone marker gate),\n48\t  `scripts/ci-repair.sh` (build-repair engine),\n49\t  `scripts/ai-run.sh` ((AI-UNAVAILABLE) classification + shared Claude CLI wrapper),\n50\t  `scripts/ai-streak.sh` ((AI-UNAVAILABLE) green no-op + consecutive-outage\n51\t  escalation, counter on `refs/meta/ai-unavailable-streak`),\n52\t  `scripts/check-override-consistency.mjs`, `scripts/resolve-release-age.mjs`,\n53\t  companion native packages `github.com/khairm/libsql-windows-arm64` +\n54\t  `github.com/khairm/tokenizers-windows-arm64`.\n55\t\n56\t## Non-negotiables\n57\t\n58\t- **Whole feature set or fail loud** — every `FEATURES.md` marker survives a\n59\t  merge or the run aborts; never ship a partial fork.\n60\t- **v2-only, forever** — the v2 cloud/host-service stack is pinned on; never v1.\n61\t- **One version, ever** — exactly one Release per upstream version, tagged\n62\t  `desktop-v<version>`, rebuilt in place; no betas/prereleases.\n63\t- **No build-time type/test gate except `(REFERR-GATE)`** — the tree carries\n64\t  accepted type debt; only cannot-find-name diagnostics fail the build.\n65\t  Validate + e2e locally before relying on a release.\n66\t- **Everything is AI-touchable** (needs `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`): the nightly\n67\t  merge resolves/ports/reviews, and the build self-repairs via `(BUILD-REPAIR)`.\n68\t  Workflow YAML self-repair additionally needs the `WORKFLOW_PUSH_TOKEN` secret\n69\t  (fine-grained PAT, Contents+Workflows write) and only takes effect the NEXT\n70\t  run — workflow files are frozen once a run starts, which is why all step\n71\t  logic lives in `.github/actions/` + `scripts/` (repairable mid-run).\n72\t  Rate-limited/unparsable AI output aborts rather than ships.\n73\t\n74\t## Custom features / overrides\n75\t\n76\t`FEATURES.md` is the authoritative manifest (descriptions + marker tokens).\n77\tIn brief:\n78\t\n79\t- **Native Windows ARM64 packaging** — one-click installer; ARM64 node-pty,\n80\t  libsql, tokenizers; renderer CORS for `superset-app://`.\n81\t- **Window controls** — native `titleBarOverlay` is the sole min/max/close on\n82\t  Windows, theme-matched; upstream's duplicates hidden.\n83\t- **Windows behaviour fixes** — skip quit-confirm; cmd.exe fallback;\n84\t  force-foreground; hidden-window watchdog; WebGL first-paint recovery; Wispr\n85\t  Flow accessibility/paste fix; fast non-blocking startup.\n86\t- **Agent status dots (Claude + Codex)** — per-terminal + workspace-rollup dot:\n87\t  red = needs input, yellow = working (incl. subagents/teammates/compaction/\n88\t  codex-companion holds), green = ready for review, blue = shell/background/\n89\t  cloud activity; precedence red > yellow > blue > green. All surfaces (tab,\n90\t  pane header, sidebar row + agent chips, rollup, kanban card) derive from one\n91\t  per-source primitive with independent latched axes; hook-driven via\n92\t  `superset-notify.py` POSTs with self-healing markers and persistence across\n93\t  renderer reloads; companion phone/watch alerts cover blocked questions,\n94\t  ready-for-review, and terminal-agent failures.\n95\t- **Auto-resume** — after an API failure, idle Claude terminals re-send\n96\t  automatically (bounded retries/budget, default-on, away-detection).\n97\t- **Recycle Bin** — every delete entry point soft-deletes (30-day display\n98\t  window); permanent delete only from inside the bin.\n99\t- **Non-git / multi-repo workspaces** — open any folder (non-git or multi-repo)\n100\t  as a plain workspace.\n101\t- **Multi-repo branch workspaces** — group N git repos under one project row;\n102\t  its \"+\" fans a branch out as worktrees per member (all-or-nothing, adoption\n103\t  on resume, editable membership, loud partial-state failures).\n104\t- **Workspace branch label** — branch name top-right in the tab bar; click\n105\t  copies.\n106\t- **Thread snooze / archive** — timed Snooze (auto-returns) + sticky Archive in\n107\t  revealable sidebar sections.\n108\t- **Sidebar** — pinned > active > idle tier sort with stable manual drag order;\n109\t  hover freezes re-sorting.\n110\t- **Terminal links** — plain click copies a URL/path; Ctrl/Cmd+click opens.\n111\t- **Agent-hook bash-wrap** — Gemini/Cursor `.sh` hooks run via Git-for-Windows\n112\t  bash.\n113\t- **Kanban board** — device-local board of every sidebar project's branches +\n114\t  Queued and final Completed columns, custom columns, deadlines, per-column\n115\t  date filters, promote-to-branch drag, sidebar Mark completed for active\n116\t  worktrees, frozen completed records, append-only daily JSON backups under\n117\t  `~/.superset/backups/kanban/`.\n118\t\n119\t## Live footguns (do NOT repeat)\n120\t\n121\t- No synchronous/blocking fs on the main thread at startup — the renderer's\n122\t  `superset-app://` loader starves and the window stays blank for minutes.\n123\t- Never re-enable xterm `screenReaderMode` (Wispr Flow regression); the build\n124\t  hard-fails if it is truthy in a renderer bundle.\n125\t- Never let `ws` load native bufferutil/utf-8-validate in the host-service —\n\n... [207 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9082deae-c057-40c5-a46a-a3a2ef007dfd","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:13:48.376Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
