{"parentUuid":"5081e25b-ce88-4406-8be9-38e033f26064","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6QftnstybMnw91gsySh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0162tfkKV4LN3SSWs56Hie6G","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore sessions delete + recycle bin UI","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (main checkout — note there may be uncommitted-unrelated worktrees; work only in the main checkout). This fork has a \"Recycle Bin\" feature: \"every delete entry point soft-deletes (30-day display window); permanent delete only from inside the bin\" (FEATURES.md). Search breadth: very thorough.\n\nQuestions:\n1. The sidebar has a \"Sessions\" section (session workspaces — projectId null, the \"Sessions\" project). When the user presses the X on a session row: trace the exact handler — does it route through the Recycle Bin soft-delete, or hard-delete/archive/something else? File:line for the X button, its handler, and the delete path it calls.\n2. Where is the Recycle Bin implementation? Find: the store/data model (categories — projects? workspaces? sessions? kanban?), the soft-delete entry points that exist today, the 30-day display window logic, permanent-delete logic, and the FEATURES.md marker name for it.\n3. Where is the Recycle Bin UI (the view showing binned items + restore/permanent-delete), and what entry points OPEN it today (menu item, button, command palette, settings, keyboard shortcut, route)? The user reports there is currently NO visible way to open it — verify whether an entry point exists but is hidden/broken, or genuinely none was ever built.\n4. What UI surface patterns exist for adding an entry point: sidebar footer buttons, section header context menus (the Sessions/Projects section headers), app menu, command palette registry, settings pages — file:line for each pattern nearest the sidebar.\n5. Does the bin cover session workspaces as a category at all? If sessions were never a bin category, say so explicitly.\n\nReturn concise findings with file:line, a verdict per question, and the smallest-change options for (a) ensuring the Sessions X soft-deletes to the bin, (b) adding an open-recycle-bin entry point consistent with existing patterns.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3688,"cache_read_input_tokens":323507,"output_tokens":1394,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3688,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":323507,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3688,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3688},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"70ecad22-0c5c-4afb-bc09-7eaabc096473","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:14:41.970Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
