{"parentUuid":"f2623632-4f0b-4d32-9dd5-906cf21dd59e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49e6820d-ef30-49de-83ed-bc1cde735b88","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6s2zcmS8Q7kC7y6yc6q16","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Resuming agent a4b4acd\",\"resumedAgentId\":\"a4b4acd04792ec9a3\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"a4b4acd04792ec9a3\",\"name\":\"a4b4acd04792ec9a3\",\"ref\":\"062019\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"327507e9-2706-4fc9-ba77-f3f9e0d38a09","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:19:35.908Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Resuming agent a4b4acd","resumedAgentId":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","pin":{"id":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","name":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","ref":"062019"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2623632-4f0b-4d32-9dd5-906cf21dd59e","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"327507e9-2706-4fc9-ba77-f3f9e0d38a09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6QzuY46AbSnV2Hy94eV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013CyodpKCB4NRBUNL2tSVsN","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Sol FIX-FIRST on the one-buzz delta: 4 MAJORs, 2 yours (companion). Coordinated design decisions are FIXED (wire amendment allowed — v3 unshipped; fork host is being changed in lockstep):\n\nWIRE AMENDMENT: v3 `g` gains REQUIRED key `gx` = the alert's outcome instant, occurredAtMs (13 digits, monotonic per terminal across cycles). v3 `c` gains REQUIRED `gx` = the generation being retired. v3 `g`'s `t` is now REQUIRED non-empty (host guarantees it independent of display-name resolution). q/e unchanged. Update PushV3Test golden vectors accordingly.\n\nYour fixes (Sol #4 + wire):\n1. Replace the shown-record ordering/cancel logic with GENERATION semantics: shown record stores {key, eventId, gx, expiresAtMs}. Posting guard: skip posting a g whose gx < shown gx for that terminal key (claim still consumed). Replacement: gx >= shown → post (silent in-place via setOnlyAlertOnce as now).\n2. Cancel rule for terminal-keyed g: cancel when shown gx <= c.gx (NOT exact-event match) — this fixes the watch-relay-failure divergence (watch shows g1, phone posted g2, relay failed, user reads → c(g2).gx >= g1.gx → watch cancels g1 correctly). Keep exact-event cancellation for e and event-keyed rows; keep genuinely-stale-c protection via the gx comparison itself. Tombstoning by eventId unchanged.\n3. Thread gx through the watch relay: WatchLifecycleAlert + WatchLifecycleDismiss gain gx (kotlinx defaults for old-peer decode); watch shown-record + cancel logic uses the same :core rule (extend LifecycleAlertIdentity/ShownLifecycleAlerts — one implementation both devices, as you built).\n4. PendingLifecycleDismissals entries carry gx (old rows decode as gx=0 → cancels nothing newer — safe).\n5. Process-death/commit-failure divergence (part of Sol #4): the gx rule already heals most of it (a later c or g with higher gx corrects the surface); ensure a failed shown-record commit still posting is at worst one extra buzz, never a stuck notification — document the residual in PROTOCOL §13.5.6 honestly.\n6. Tests: the exact Sol watch scenario (g1 shown on watch, g2 relay failed, c(g2) cancels g1); gx-stale c only tombstones; gx posting guard incl. equal boundary; old-peer decode of gx-less dismissals; golden vectors with gx + required t.\n\nThen rerun the full Gradle suite and rebuild both release APKs; verify certs match as before. Report per-item + counts + APK paths.","summary":"Dispatch one-buzz round-2 companion fixes","to":"impl-android","type":"message","recipient":"impl-android","content":"Sol FIX-FIRST on the one-buzz delta: 4 MAJORs, 2 …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":329024,"output_tokens":4772,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2055},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1988,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4772,"cache_read_input_tokens":329024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1988,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1988},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"def5ec68-8d97-49ea-9d93-a3cedb38c346","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:19:48.620Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
