{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:23:01.287Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab7bc04d52fcbd1b8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\ab7bc04d52fcbd1b8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore sessions delete + recycle bin UI\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Verdicts\n\n**Q1 — Sessions X: it DOES route through the soft-delete, but the item then falls into a void.**\n\n- X button: `apps/desktop/src/renderer/routes/_authenticated/_dashboard/components/DashboardSidebar/components/DashboardSidebarWorkspaceItem/components/DashboardSidebarExpandedWorkspaceRow/DashboardSidebarExpandedWorkspaceRow.tsx:442-471` (`aria-label=\"Close workspace\"`, `HiMiniXMark`, → `onCloseWorkspaceClick()` at :448).\n- Wiring: `DashboardSidebarWorkspaceItem.tsx:367-373` — `sectionState === \"deleted\" ? handleDeletePermanently : handleDelete`. A session row has `sectionState === undefined` → `handleDelete`.\n- Handler: `useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceItemActions.ts:194-196` → `deleteWorkspace(workspaceId, projectId)` with `projectId === null` for sessions.\n- Soft-delete: `useDashboardSidebarState.ts:759-829` — sets `sidebarState.deletedAt = Date.now()`, `isHidden = true`, clears archive/snooze/completed. Lossless; no worktree/branch touched.\n\nSo it soft-deletes correctly. The break is downstream: `useDashboardSidebarData.ts:410-458` buckets it into `deletedSidebarWorkspaces`, and the ONLY consumer is the project-tree loop at `:898-904` (`projectsById.get(workspace.projectId)` → `continue` on null). Snoozed/archived get a session partition (`:704`, `:710`); **deleted does not**. Net effect: X on a session = row disappears permanently with no bin, no restore, no trace in UI.\n\nTwo latent defects worth noting:\n- `deleteWorkspace(workspaceId, projectId?: string)` (`:760`) is called with `string | null` from two sites (`useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceItemActions.ts:195`, `V2WorkspaceRow.tsx:158`) under `strict: true` (`tooling/typescript/base.json:18`) — accepted type debt.\n- No-local-state-row fallback (`:787-798`) refuses when `resolvedProjectId` is falsy → a session with no local row silently console.errors. In practice sessions always have a local row (`isAutoIncludedLocalMainWorkspace` requires `projectId !== null`, `sidebarVisibility.ts:46`), so the update path runs.\n\n**Q2 — Recycle Bin implementation.** Marker: `(RECYCLE-BIN)`, `FEATURES.md:72`.\n\n- Data model: no separate store. It's a **field**, `sidebarState.deletedAt`, on `v2WorkspaceLocalState` — `dashboardSidebarLocal/schema.ts:185`; per-project reveal flags `showDeleted` / `deletedCollapsed` at `schema.ts:31-32`; per-kanban-column `showRecycleBin` / `recycleBinCollapsed` at `schema.ts:655-656`, defaults `:750-751`.\n- Bucket classifier: `sidebarVisibility.ts:109-113` (`isWorkspaceDeleted`), `:147-176` (`getWorkspaceSidebarBucket`, deleted checked FIRST at :156).\n- 30-day window: `recycleBinRetention/recycleBinRetention.ts:4` (`DEFAULT_RECYCLE_BIN_RETENTION_DAYS = 30`), clamp `:22-30`, store `:46-68` (zustand persist, key `recycle-bin-retention`). Filter fn: `sidebarVisibility.ts:186-193` (`isWithinRecycleBinWindow`). Display-only — nothing auto-purges. Applied in `DashboardSidebarStateSection.tsx:106-117` and `useKanbanData.ts:671-677`.\n- Soft-delete entry points today: sidebar row X (above); sidebar row context menu Delete (`DashboardSidebarWorkspaceItem.tsx:297-301`, item at `DashboardSidebarWorkspaceContextMenu.tsx:424-431`); command palette \"Delete &lt;ws&gt;\" + `CLOSE_WORKSPACE` hotkey (`commandPalette/modules/workspace/commands.tsx:74-84` → `ui/DeleteWorkspaceMount/DeleteWorkspaceMount.tsx:38`); kanban card Delete (`KanbanCard.tsx:345,416` → `useKanbanActions.ts:617`); workspaces list row (`V2WorkspaceRow.tsx:157-159`); dead-worktree page (`WorkspaceMissingWorktreeState.tsx:44-47`). **Exception:** multi-select bulk \"Delete N Workspaces\" (`DashboardSidebarWorkspaceBulkContextMenu.tsx:109-113` → `useBulkWorkspaceDelete/bulkWorkspaceDelete.ts:25-51`) is a HARD git destroy, not a bin move.\n- Permanent delete: `useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceItemActions.ts:144-152` → `destroy-workspace-intent` → `commandPalette/ui/DestroyWorkspaceMount/DestroyWorkspaceMount.tsx`; bulk \"Empty Recycle Bin\" `useDashboardSidebarProjectSectionActions.ts:301-370` (`workspaceCleanup.destroy` per item, mains skipped at :321).\n- Settings: `settings/behavior/.../BehaviorSettings.tsx:300-330`, registry id `BEHAVIOR_RECYCLE_BIN_RETENTION` `settings-search.ts:31,151,628`.\n\n**Q3 — There IS no dedicated bin view/route; an entry point exists but only on project rows.**\n\n- The \"view\" is an inline collapsible section: `DashboardSidebarStateSection.tsx` variant `\"deleted\"` (copy `:50-54`, restore/empty menu `:141-162`, \"Show all\" footer `:176-186`). Per-row Restore = `LuRotateCcw` button `:402-406`; \"Restore\" / \"Delete permanently\" in row context menu `DashboardSidebarWorkspaceContextMenu.tsx:349-367`.\n- Opened by: **right-click a project row → \"Show Recycle Bin\"** — `DashboardSidebarProjectContextMenu.tsx:109-114`, wired `DashboardSidebarProjectSection.tsx:187,194-196`, section config `:119-128`. Kanban equivalent: right-click column → \"Show Recycle Bin\", `KanbanColumn.tsx:204-217`, section `:339-368`.\n- No route, no app-menu item, no command-palette command, no keyboard shortcut, no sidebar footer button. So the user's report is half right: not hidden/broken, but the only affordance is an undiscoverable project-row context menu, defaulting off (`schema.ts:31` `showDeleted: false`) — and for Sessions there is genuinely nothing.\n\n**Q4 — Nearest UI surface patterns.**\n\n- Sessions section header context menu (closest analogue): `DashboardSidebarSessionsContextMenu.tsx:30-44` (two items: Show snoozed / Show archived).\n- Project row context menu: `DashboardSidebarProjectContextMenu.tsx:100-116`.\n- Projects section header: `DashboardSidebarWorkspacesHeader.tsx:55-127` — no context menu; has an \"Add project\" dropdown button (`:84-98`).\n- Sessions header \"+\" button pattern: `DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx:125-137`.\n- Sidebar footer button row: `DashboardSidebar.tsx:532-571` (OrganizationDropdown, NotificationBusPill, UpdatesPill, Settings button `:549-570` → `navigate({to:\"/settings/account\"})`).\n- Sidebar header buttons (Kanban/Workspaces/Automations): `DashboardSidebarHeader.tsx:143-190`.\n- Command palette registry: `commandPalette/modules/navigation/commands.tsx:8-50` (CommandProvider shape), providers assembled in `commandPalette/modules/index.ts`; intent-store + globally-mounted UI pattern in `ui/DeleteWorkspaceMount`, `ui/DestroyWorkspaceMount`.\n- Settings page + search registry: `BehaviorSettings.tsx:300`, `settings-search.ts:628`.\n- Electron app menu: `apps/desktop/src/main/lib/menu.ts:229-230`.\n\n**Q5 — No. Sessions were never a bin category. Explicitly:**\n`SidebarSessionLifecycleVariant = \"snoozed\" | \"archived\"` (`buildDashboardSidebarProjects.ts:237`) and `SidebarInactiveWorkspaceInput` (`:231-235`) carries `snoozeUntil` / `snoozeLaunchId` / `archivedAt` but **no `deletedAt`**. `DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx:74-109` has exactly two `stateSections`. `V2UserPreferences` has 4 session flags (`schema.ts:422-425`, defaults `:454-457`) — no `showDeletedSessions`. Kanban is also out (sessions never bind to a card — `DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx:36-37`). Bin categories today = project-scoped worktree/branch workspaces only (sidebar per project + kanban per column). Mains are excluded by design (`(MASTER-ARCHIVE-ONLY)`, `FEATURES.md:71`).\n\n## Smallest-change options\n\n**(a) Sessions X → a real bin.** The delete already works; add the missing lane (mirrors snoozed/archived exactly, 5 edits):\n1. `useDashboardSidebarData.ts` ~`:714` — add `const { sessions: sessionDeletedRows, projectScoped: projectDeletedRows } = useMemo(() =&gt; partitionSidebarWorkspacesBySession(deletedSidebarWorkspaces), [...])`; change `:898` to loop `projectDeletedRows`.\n2. `buildDashboardSidebarProjects.ts:231-237` — add `deletedAt: number | null` to `SidebarInactiveWorkspaceInput`, widen the variant union to include `\"deleted\"` (sort by `deletedAt` DESC), and pass `deletedAt` through in `buildDashboardSidebarInactiveSessionWorkspaces` (`:271-290`) — `DashboardSidebarStateSection.tsx:111` reads it.\n3. `schema.ts:422-425` + `:454-457` — add `showDeletedSessions` / `deletedSessionsCollapsed` booleans (bounded singleton; the existing comment at `:415-421` already covers the rationale).\n4. `DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx:83-109` — third `stateSections` entry `variant:\"deleted\"`, `title:\"Recycle Bin\"`, `onRestoreAll` = map `restoreWorkspace` over the rows, optional `onEmptyBin`.\n5. `DashboardSidebarSessionsContextMenu.tsx:38-41` — third item \"Show/Hide Recycle Bin\" with `LuTrash2`, copying `DashboardSidebarProjectContextMenu.tsx:109-114`.\nAlso fix `useDashboardSidebarState.ts:760` signature to `projectId?: string | null` and let the fallback accept an explicit `null` for sessions (removes the type debt + the no-local-row refusal).\n\n**(b) Open-the-bin entry point, consistent with existing patterns** — cheapest first:\n- Zero-new-surface: the Sessions header menu item from step 5 above + the existing project-row item. Matches the fork's own reveal-toggle idiom exactly.\n- One command-palette command (~15 lines, no new UI): add to `commandPalette/modules/navigation/commands.tsx` a `\"nav.recycleBin\"` command with `Trash2Icon` that flips `showDeleted` on every sidebar project (`toggleProjectSectionFlag`) + the new session flag, then scrolls the sidebar. Same provider shape as `:29-36`.\n- If a persistent affordance is wanted: a trash icon button in the sidebar footer row `DashboardSidebar.tsx:532-571`, next to the Settings button (`:549-570`) — same `Tooltip` + `size-8` button pattern — toggling the same flags. Avoid a new route: no bin route exists and the bin is per-project data, so a global view would need a new aggregation layer.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>164452</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>68</tool_uses><duration_ms>470628</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
