{"parentUuid":"4b1b45ea-d52d-4fe3-a218-6c671df1b716","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6RNmkrHVBSwuf2omsPy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Explorer's verdict on your two points:\n\n1. **The X on a session row does soft-delete** — the data is preserved with a deletion timestamp — **but deleted sessions then fall into a void**: the Sessions section was never given a Recycle Bin lane (only project rows have one), so the row just vanishes from the UI with no way to see or restore it. Your instinct was right.\n2. **Bin access today is genuinely undiscoverable**: the only way in is right-clicking a *project* row → \"Show Recycle Bin\" (off by default). No button, no menu, no command, and nothing at all for Sessions.\n\nI'll add the missing Sessions bin lane (restore + permanent delete, same as projects get). One bonus find: the multi-select bulk \"Delete N Workspaces\" does a **hard git destroy**, bypassing the bin — violating the fork's own every-delete-soft-deletes rule. UX decisions:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4975,"cache_read_input_tokens":337211,"output_tokens":1261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":451},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4975,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":337211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4975},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d818990d-e6ea-4dd4-b53e-ffe2bd4c69e7","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:23:47.791Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Pro