{"parentUuid":"d4c72ca0-3aea-44fe-beab-07036944c252","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6RVkfp2QFodHSbNFaEU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TRrqUcWTwqGxh5n1j8Z2rE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement sessions recycle bin","isolation":"worktree","model":"opus","name":"impl-bin","prompt":"Implement (RECYCLE-BIN-SESSIONS) in this fork worktree (Windows ARM64 Superset fork). User-approved scope, exploration already done — file:line references below were verified minutes ago.\n\nProblem: the sidebar Sessions section's X soft-deletes (sets sidebarState.deletedAt via useDashboardSidebarState.ts:759-829) but deleted sessions fall into a void — useDashboardSidebarData.ts buckets them into deletedSidebarWorkspaces whose only consumer is the project-tree loop (:898-904) which `continue`s on null projectId. Snoozed/archived sessions get partitions (:704, :710); deleted does not. Also: multi-select bulk \"Delete N Workspaces\" (DashboardSidebarWorkspaceBulkContextMenu.tsx:109-113 → useBulkWorkspaceDelete/bulkWorkspaceDelete.ts:25-51) HARD-destroys, violating the fork's (RECYCLE-BIN) invariant \"every delete entry point soft-deletes\".\n\nApproved changes:\nA. Sessions Recycle Bin lane (mirror the snoozed/archived idiom exactly):\n1. useDashboardSidebarData.ts (~:714): partition deletedSidebarWorkspaces via partitionSidebarWorkspacesBySession; project-scoped rows keep feeding the :898 loop; session rows feed the new lane.\n2. buildDashboardSidebarProjects.ts:231-237: add `deletedAt: number | null` to SidebarInactiveWorkspaceInput; widen SidebarSessionLifecycleVariant to include \"deleted\" (sort by deletedAt DESC); pass deletedAt through buildDashboardSidebarInactiveSessionWorkspaces (:271-290) — DashboardSidebarStateSection.tsx:111 reads it for the 30-day window filter.\n3. dashboardSidebarLocal/schema.ts: add showDeletedSessions / deletedSessionsCollapsed to V2UserPreferences (:422-425) + defaults (:454-457), default hidden/collapsed like the project flags (:31-32).\n4. DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx:83-109: third stateSections entry variant:\"deleted\", title \"Recycle Bin\", with per-row Restore + context-menu Restore/Delete-permanently working as they do for project rows (DashboardSidebarStateSection variant \"deleted\" already renders these — verify sessions' null projectId flows through restore + destroy paths; fix where it doesn't, loudly not silently).\n5. DashboardSidebarSessionsContextMenu.tsx:38-41: add \"Show Recycle Bin\"/\"Hide Recycle Bin\" toggle item (LuTrash2), copying DashboardSidebarProjectContextMenu.tsx:109-114. This is the ONLY new entry point — user explicitly declined a footer button and a command-palette command; do not add those.\n6. Type-debt fix: useDashboardSidebarState.ts:760 deleteWorkspace signature accepts `projectId?: string | null`; the no-local-row fallback (:787-798) must accept explicit null for sessions instead of refusing via console.error.\nB. Bulk delete → soft delete: useBulkWorkspaceDelete/bulkWorkspaceDelete.ts:25-51 (and its menu label if it says destroy) becomes a loop over the same deleteWorkspace soft-delete used by single rows; permanent destroy remains only inside the bin (\"Empty Recycle Bin\" / per-row Delete permanently, useDashboardSidebarProjectSectionActions.ts:301-370). Keep main-workspace exclusions ((MASTER-ARCHIVE-ONLY) FEATURES.md:71) exactly as the single-delete path treats them.\nC. FEATURES.md: update the (RECYCLE-BIN) row prose to cover sessions + bulk soft-delete; if the row's marker tokens don't root in the sessions files you touch, add token(s) so a silent upstream takeover reds the gate. Marker gate must stay green (run under PowerShell with git's grep on PATH if Bash is broken: node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs).\nD. Tests: follow the repo's co-located test idiom for the files you touch (buildDashboardSidebarProjects has tests? check; add coverage for: session deleted partition + 30-day window, restore round-trip, bulk soft-delete not destroying, deleteWorkspace null-projectId path). Run the touched renderer suites (bun test with apps/desktop/test-setup.ts preload), bun run lint on touched paths (Biome, 0 diagnostics incl. warnings), tsc on touched files.\n\nRules: fail fast and loud; no defensive fallbacks; match surrounding idiom; DO NOT touch packages/host-service, V2NotificationController, or anything the (ALERT-CONTEXT-NAMES) work owns. Do not commit — leave the worktree for my review. Report: per-item summary, test/lint/gate results, anything unresolved.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":342186,"output_tokens":2271,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":292},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1404,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":342186,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1404},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"f805a1bc-cf1b-43d7-ae61-9c26ed3dd194","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:25:38.508Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
