{"parentUuid":"07b3a1fd-0807-43c6-a257-7d9600026d74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6SPXzmEmRcSXPaga9m4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VWjj6Bk9ViJjpbsEzkxFgM","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Companion side has finalized the gx wire — your host implementation must byte-match these vectors (PushV3Test.kt in the companion repo is the shared golden source):\n- g = [v,k,i,w,x,gx,t,pn,wn,tn,tc], t REQUIRED NON-EMPTY, gx REQUIRED 13-digit.\n- e = UNCHANGED: [v,k,i,w,x,t,pn,wn,tn,tc], NO gx, t may be \"\" — g and e no longer share a key set, and each closed set refuses the other's extra key (an e carrying gx must throw).\n- c = [v,k,i,w,x,gx,t], gx REQUIRED.\n- q untouched.\n- CRITICAL normative rule (PROTOCOL §13.5.1): gx is the OUTCOME INSTANT (occurredAtMs of the event that set ready) — NEVER derived from anything send-shaped (not x, not send time, not mint-processing time): presence gating can send an earlier finish later, and a send-derived gx silently recreates the ordering bug. Store the outcome instant on HeldAlert at mint and emit it verbatim on g and on every c for that alert; blind restart c uses seenThroughAt (same instant, renderer-supplied).\nMirror the refusal vectors too: ready alert missing t, ready alert missing gx, error carrying gx, retraction missing gx. Continue with your standing/outstanding-ready work and report per usual.","summary":"Relay final gx wire facts to fork agent","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"Companion side has finalized the gx wire — your h…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2164,"cache_read_input_tokens":347241,"output_tokens":820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":212},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard"