{"parentUuid":"34a47994-b376-4dee-8b8c-deda5e3cfbf9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cf3bd592-9676-465e-aff4-2baba6f8f4d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a91ec5448000b24ae</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a91ec5448000b24ae.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement sessions recycle bin\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Done. Worktree left uncommitted for review.\n\n## Per item\n\n**A1 — deleted bucket partitioned** (`useDashboardSidebarData.ts:716-724, :909, :1017, :1065-1080, :1100`). `deletedSidebarWorkspaces` now splits via `partitionSidebarWorkspacesBySession`; project rows feed the project-tree loop (`projectDeletedRows`), session rows build `deletedSessionWorkspaces` (variant `\"deleted\"`), returned from the hook and threaded through `DashboardSidebar.tsx`.\n\n**A2 — builder** (`buildDashboardSidebarProjects.ts`). `SidebarInactiveWorkspaceInput.deletedAt: number | null`; `SidebarSessionLifecycleVariant` widened to `\"deleted\"`; `deletedAt` passed through the decorated row; sort is now a 3-way (snoozed→wake asc, archived→archivedAt desc, deleted→deletedAt desc).\n\n**A3 — prefs schema** (`dashboardSidebarLocal/schema.ts`). `showDeletedSessions` / `deletedSessionsCollapsed` added to `v2UserPreferencesSchema`, `DEFAULT_V2_USER_PREFERENCES`, and `SESSION_SECTION_FLAGS` (so the boolean read-heal covers them). Both default false = hidden, expanded when revealed — identical to the project flags.\n\n**A4 — sessions lane** (`DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx`). Third `stateSections` entry: variant `\"deleted\"`, title `Recycle Bin`, Restore-all loops `restoreWorkspace`. Verified the null-projectId paths flow: per-row Restore (`handleRestore` → `restoreWorkspace(id)`) and context-menu Delete permanently (`useDestroyWorkspaceIntent` → `DestroyWorkspaceMount` → `DashboardSidebarDeleteDialog`) are both projectId-free, and the retention/\"Show all\" filter in `DashboardSidebarStateSection` already keys off `workspace.deletedAt`. **Not implemented:** section-level \"Empty Recycle Bin\" for sessions (`onEmptyBin` is optional; the project version duplicates host-destroy plumbing in `useDashboardSidebarProjectSectionActions`). Scope only required per-row destroy — flagging as a deliberate gap.\n\n**A5 — toggle** (`DashboardSidebarSessionsContextMenu.tsx`): third item, `LuTrash2`, \"Show/Hide Recycle Bin\". No footer button, no palette command.\n\n**A6 — type debt** (`useDashboardSidebarState.ts:761-800`): `deleteWorkspace(id, projectId?: string | null)`; the host record is resolved once, and the insert path uses the new pure `resolveSoftDeleteProjectId(explicit, hostProjectId)` (in `sidebarMutations.ts`) so an explicit null is honoured instead of hitting the old \"projectId unresolvable\" refusal. That refusal branch is now unreachable and removed (the record is guaranteed by the type guard above).\n\n**B — bulk delete → soft delete.** Both bulk entry points (context menu `DashboardSidebarWorkspaceBulkContextMenu` **and** the selection toolbar `DashboardSidebarBulkActions`, which shared the same dialog) now call the new `useBulkWorkspaceSoftDelete` → pure `executeBulkWorkspaceSoftDelete`, which loops the same `deleteWorkspace` used by single rows; mains are skipped and stay selected. **Deviation to review:** with no caller left, I deleted the dead hard-destroy stack — `components/DashboardSidebarBulkDeleteDialog/**` (dialog, failures pane, `useBulkWorkspaceDelete`, `bulkWorkspaceDelete.ts` + its test) and `hooks/useBulkWorkspaceDeleteDialog/**`. Keeping the dialog would have lied (\"removes every selected worktree from disk\", uncommitted-work inspection, force retries) about a lossless soft delete. In-bin rows are not bulk-selectable (state sections pass no `onSelectionClick`), so no permanent-destroy capability is reachable-but-lost beyond bulk destroy itself.\n\n**C — FEATURES.md.** `(RECYCLE-BIN)` prose now covers bulk soft-delete; new row `(RECYCLE-BIN-SESSIONS)`. Three new marker lines rooted narrowly (sessions section dir, `dashboardSidebarLocal/schema.ts`, `useBulkWorkspaceSoftDelete` dir) so an upstream takeover of those files reds the gate.\n\n**D — tests.** Added: session-bin partition, deletedAt-DESC ordering + carried `deletedAt`, retention-window behaviour over built rows (`buildDashboardSidebarProjects.test.ts`); bucket precedence for a deleted session + 30-day window edges (`sidebarVisibility.test.ts`); `resolveSoftDeleteProjectId` explicit-null/fallback cases (`sidebarMutations.test.ts`); soft-delete-not-destroy + main-skip (`bulkWorkspaceSoftDelete.test.ts`); new prefs defaults (`schema.test.ts`).\n\n## Results\n- Tests: `bun test` over DashboardSidebar + useDashboardSidebarState + CollectionsProvider → **160 pass / 1 fail**. The failure (`removeProjectFromSidebarState &gt; clears the pin on a kept main-workspace row`) **is pre-existing** — reproduced identically on the clean main checkout; it's stale vs (REMOVE-STICKY) tombstoning mains.\n- Biome: `check` over the three touched dirs → **0 diagnostics**. Note `--write` also auto-fixed one unrelated pre-existing import-order violation in `DashboardSidebarExpandedWorkspaceRow.tsx` (2 lines) — kept, since lint treats it as an error; revert if you want the diff strictly scoped.\n- tsc (`apps/desktop`): no diagnostics in any file I touched; **no REFERR-class codes anywhere**. Baseline had 2 errors in `useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceItemActions.ts` (lines 166, 195) — line 195 (`deleteWorkspace`) is now fixed.\n- Marker gate: `node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` → **All 156 feature markers present**, including the three new ones.\n\n## Unresolved / for your call\n1. **`snoozeWorkspace` has the identical bug**, untouched (out of scope): signature is `projectId?: string` (TS2345 at `useDashboardSidebarWorkspaceItemActions.ts:166`) and its no-local-row fallback refuses an unresolvable projectId — so snoozing a session that has no local-state row silently no-ops, same class as the delete bug just fixed.\n2. Session Recycle Bin has no \"Empty Recycle Bin\" (see A4).\n3. Deleting the bulk destroy stack (see B) — the one place I went beyond \"modify\".\n4. `bun install --frozen-lockfile` was run in the worktree to get tests running (`node_modules` was absent); `bun.lock` unchanged. The desktop `install:deps` postinstall step failed non-fatally on Windows, which is why unrelated files (pty-daemon, route pages) show tsc noise here that main doesn't.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>287600</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>155</tool_uses><duration_ms>1413642</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a91ec5448000b24ae</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a91ec5448000b24ae</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"4d0f5819-f53d-40a0-bd37-1a54cbea423d","timestamp":"2026-08-16T12:49:45.223Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
