yout.tsx:281-290`), so the hook is legal there.\n- New test `tools/delete-workspace.test.ts` (4 cases): soft-deletes each id and marks it recoverable; refuses a main loudly while still deleting the rest (asserts the main was never passed to the soft delete); all-refused → `success:false`; a thrown soft delete becomes a per-item error. The fake ctx exposes *only* `softDeleteWorkspace`, so a regression reaching for a destroy mutation fails to compile and to run.\n\n## 2. MINOR — bulk core honours the hook's refusals (FIXED)\n- `deleteWorkspace` now returns `boolean`: `false` on **both** refusal paths (unresolvable host record/type, main), `true` after the insert/update.\n- `executeBulkWorkspaceSoftDelete` takes `softDelete: (w) =&gt; boolean` and returns `{ softDeletedIds, skippedMainIds, refusedIds }`; only `softDeletedIds` reaches `onDeleted`, so a refused row stays selected and visible in the active lane. Doc comment states the contract.\n- Tests updated + new case \"keeps a row the state hook refused out of the deleted set\".\n\n## 3. MINOR — session \"Delete permanently\": TRACED, verdict **safe, kept**\nRead `packages/host-service/src/trpc/router/workspace-cleanup/workspace-cleanup.ts` end to end. Sessions are a first-class branch, not an unhandled case:\n- `inspect:149` — reads worktree state with `ignoreInitialCommit: local.type === \"session\"`.\n- `runDestroy:299` — preflight explicitly includes sessions: `if (!input.force &amp;&amp; local &amp;&amp; (project || local.type === \"session\"))`.\n- `runDestroyPhases:465-489` — `if (local?.type === \"session\")`: removes the session folder with `rm -rf`, **but only when `isInsideSessionsRoot(worktreePath)`**; outside the managed sessions root it pushes a warning and skips (non-destructive). A failed `rm` throws `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`, which un-archives the row (`:388-391`) — retryable, not orphaned.\n- Teardown (`:346`) requires `local &amp;&amp; project` → skipped for sessions. Legacy cloud delete (`:573`) explicitly skipped for sessions. Branch delete needs `project`/`repoGitEnv` → no-op.\n- Existing upstream coverage pins it: `packages/host-service/test/workspace-cleanup.test.ts:695` (\"session destroy archives the row like any other workspace\", asserts `success` + a single `deleted` event) and `:718` (\"the archive commit point applies to sessions too\"), both with `projectId: null, type: \"session\"`.\n\nSo \"Delete permanently\" stays on session bin rows. **I did not add a host-service test** — the task's standing rule is \"DO NOT touch packages/host-service\"; say the word and I'll add a third case there pinning the sessions-root guard (folder outside the root → warning, no removal), which is the one session sub-path with no direct test.\n\n## 4. MINOR — `archiveWorkspace` (FIXED)\nWidened to `projectId?: string | null`, routed through the shared `resolveSidebarRowProjectId`, and the collapsing `??` + falsy refusal replaced by a narrow fail-loud (`projectId === undefined &amp;&amp; hostWorkspace === null`). `RemoveFromSidebarMount.tsx:36` already passed `string | null`, so \"Remove from Sidebar\" on a session with no local-state row now archives instead of silently doing nothing. Matching test added (\"lets a project-less row archive instead of refusing it\"). All three lifecycle inserts (delete/snooze/archive) now share one resolver.\n\n## FEATURES.md\n`(RECYCLE-BIN)` prose extended to cover the remote-agent command and the refused-row-stays-selected rule. New marker root `(RECYCLE-BIN) → .../AgentHooks/hooks/useCommandWatcher/tools` so an upstream takeover of the tool reds the gate (token present in both `delete-workspace.ts` and `types.ts`).\n\n## Gate results\n- **Tests**: 187 pass / 1 fail across 24 files (DashboardSidebar + useDashboardSidebarState + CollectionsProvider + AgentHooks). The single failure is the pre-existing `removeProjectFromSidebarState &gt; clears the pin on a kept main-workspace row`, reproduced on clean `main` earlier — stale vs (REMOVE-STICKY), untouched by this work.\n- **Biome**: 213 files checked, **0 diagnostics**.\n- **tsc**: **zero** diagnostics in every touched path (DashboardSidebar, useDashboardSidebarState, dashboardSidebarLocal, AgentHooks) and **zero** REFERR-class codes.\n- **Marker gate**: `All 157 feature markers present`.\n\n## Two observations, not fixed (your call)\n1. `list_workspaces` (same remote tool set) reads the v1 electron list and has no view of `deletedAt`, so a binned workspace still appears to the remote agent after `delete_workspace`. Harmless — a repeat delete is idempotent (refreshes `deletedAt`) — but the agent can't tell it already deleted it. Filtering would need a new ctx accessor over `v2WorkspaceLocalState`.\n2. The physical `electronTrpc.workspaces.delete` remains reachable from two **v1** screens (`WorkspaceInitializingView`, v1 `DeleteWorkspaceDialog`). The fork is v2-only, so these are dead paths in practice; flagging since the invariant is \"every delete entry point\".\n\nNothing committed — worktree left for review.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>358335</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>473604</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a91ec5448000b24ae</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a91ec5448000b24ae</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"8c3774d8-a394-41e3-bbe1-fc65150577d5","timestamp":"2026-08-16T13:20:38.711Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
