{"parentUuid":"ad59061f-ac82-45b0-aecd-b53dafe2b478","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6W9JSWWy2cEKNgGXnJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sol confirmed the standing-state and identity fixes clean but found three more ordering defects — the most serious being that a delayed read-report can retract a *newer, unread* finish. Dispatching:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1701,"cache_read_input_tokens":379068,"output_tokens":1119,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":123},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1119,"cache_read_input_tokens":379068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d005dff2-f88f-4cb3-ba99-32cb4aa3ecc7","timestamp":"2026-08-16T13:26:11.840Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d005dff2-f88f-4cb3-ba99-32cb4aa3ecc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6W9JSWWy2cEKNgGXnJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CXehs1AoETGwrVbhZzPLio","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Sol FIX-FIRST round 3 on one-buzz: 3 MAJORs, all fork-side (companion verified clean). Fix, add the named tests, rerun suites/lint/markers, report.\n\n1. notifications.ts:263 — raw Date.now() as every lifecycle instant → gx not monotonic per terminal under clock backstep (NTP step-back): finish B minted with gx < shown A → both devices reject B as superseded; post-restart read emits c(gx=B) which can't retire A; renderer thinks accepted and drops repair evidence → stale card until 6h timeout. Fix: mint a per-terminal MONOTONIC lifecycle instant — max(Date.now(), lastInstantForTerminal+1) — persisted/derivable across restart via the same binding state the deterministic id path uses; use it consistently for event storage, alert ids, g.gx and c.gx. Cross-side clock-backstep test.\n\n2. lifecycle-alerts.ts:1122 — markLifecycleSeen ignores its seenThroughAt boundary when any live ready row exists: delayed read-of-A arriving after B was delivered retracts B — work the user NEVER read. Fix: findLiveReadyAlert selects only rows with outcomeAtMs <= seenThroughAt; retire the newest ELIGIBLE generation; later held/sending/sent rows untouched; blind-restart path unchanged (already bounded by seenThroughAt). Test: A-read arrives after B delivery → B stands, A (if still live) retires.\n\n3. companionAlertSync.ts:405 (+ resyncAgentStatus.ts:650 same defect) — report completion clears outstandingReadyAt[terminalId] unconditionally: if finish B lands while A's report is in flight, A's .then deletes B's outstanding record → later Start clears B's green → opening the chat reports nothing → B stuck until expiry. Fix: compare-and-clear — both callbacks pass the reported generation and clear only when the stored record is <= the acknowledged seenThroughAt. Test: newer finish arriving before an older report resolves keeps its record.\n\nThese interlock: fix 1's monotonic instant is what makes fix 2's <= boundary and fix 3's compare-and-clear sound. Don't churn the verified-clean list (standing escalation, reason upgrades, alert-owned identity, replay restoration, cap/rotation, golden vectors).","summary":"Dispatch one-buzz round-3 ordering fixes","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"Sol FIX-FIRST round 3 on one-buzz: 3 MAJORs, all …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1701,"cache_read_input_tokens":379068,"output_tokens":1119,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":123},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1119,"cache_read_input_tokens":379068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8180fc86-6080-41d1-a47f-33a701a779b3","timestamp":"2026-08-16T13:26:21.978Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
