{"parentUuid":"d913272c-a442-4cee-a250-56aaf34ed418","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6XEccAMA1hq5epVHtG7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MbKpPWt4TTgBxgwxSQJpB1","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"One-buzz round-3 fixes applied (fork worktree agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3, uncommitted). Verify your 3 MAJORs, final verdict SHIP or FIX-FIRST:\n1. notifications.ts: exported pure nextLifecycleInstantMs(nowMs, prev) = now>prev ? now : prev+1, anchored on the PERSISTED binding's lastEventAt read before stamping (survives restart, per-terminal not global, forward jumps honoured); one instant flows to bus broadcast, recordEvent, capture sink, lifecycle sink. Tests: step-back 5000→5001; forward jump; no-history; second terminal unaffected; corrected instant reaches binding + broadcast.\n2. lifecycle-alerts.ts: findReadAlerts(hostTerminalId, seenThroughAt) — only outcomeAtMs <= seenThroughAt, newest-generation-first (ordering by generation, total per terminal given fix 1); markLifecycleSeen retires EVERY covered generation (standing fires its one c, held deleted silently, retracted inert) — rationale: the visible card may be an older standing row while the newest covered row was only held. Blind-restart unchanged; proof-of-absence = \"nothing this read covers\". Tests: delayed A-read after B delivery → one c(gx=2000), B untouched, later read retires B; read older than only row → nothing; standing A + held B both retired.\n3. clearOutstandingReady(terminalId, acknowledgedThroughAt) compare-and-clear (<=); both callbacks pass what they reported. Tests at store + helper level incl. mid-report finish surviving the older ack.\nSuites: host 387/0 (25 files), renderer 1619 pass/10 pre-existing-unrelated, markers 160, biome clean.\nProbe: retire-every-covered-generation — any way a delayed old read fires a c that cancels the CURRENT terminal-keyed notification on device? (phone cancels tag when shown.gx <= c.gx — c carries the OLD alert's gx, shown is newer → survives; confirm.) Monotonic anchor vs the outstanding-record instants and deterministic ids staying consistent. Restart with clock still behind the persisted lastEventAt.","summary":"Sol final verdict on round-3 fixes","to":"rev-sol","type":"message","recipient":"rev-sol","content":"One-buzz round-3 fixes applied (fork worktree age…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":394807,"output_tokens":1049,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":97},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":394807,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"080cb1cb-952c-411d-af56-074c72e493b7","timestamp":"2026-08-16T13:40:39.824Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
