{"parentUuid":"8b0d13e6-e784-4223-b322-78fa8f8a7ff2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6XRXzesrX1PEhwiifPz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01De59oQmmG9HXUrcaphXhDQ","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Sol round-4 verdict: everything clean EXCEPT one MAJOR — the proof-of-absence epoch.\n\nlifecycle-alerts.ts:419: startedAtMs is raw Date.now() while generations are now per-terminal monotonic — a restart during a wall-clock backstep (restart at 4000, persisted A sent at corrected gen 5000) records startedAtMs=4000, so a read at seenThroughAt=5000 hits the silent proof branch (:1111-1153) instead of blind-retracting: A stands on devices until timeout, and accepted:true wipes the renderer's repair evidence. Same false proof when a later gen 5001 is held post-restart (filtered as newer; A still wrongly proven absent).\n\nFix per Sol: put the proof epoch on the SAME per-terminal logical timeline — at manager start, snapshot each persisted binding's lastEventAt and define that terminal's proof boundary as strictly AFTER it (proof valid only for seenThroughAt > snapshot[terminal] AND no live/standing row covers it; terminals with no snapshot use the conservative default of no-proof → blind c). Alternatively disable proof wherever restart ordering can't be established. Required test: restart-at-4000 / persisted-A-at-5000 / read-at-5000 → blind c(gx=5000) fires. Also cover the held-5001-post-restart variant.\n\nEverything else is verified clean — touch nothing beyond this. Rerun host suite + markers, report.","summary":"Dispatch proof-epoch timeline fix","to":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","type":"message","recipient":"a4b4acd04792ec9a3","content":"Sol round-4 verdict: everything clean EXCEPT one …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":398770,"output_tokens