{"parentUuid":"0daedaa7-3970-4503-8985-8f34268b08f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0273ed08-720a-4f5b-bef3-9308e54ad1a1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4b4acd04792ec9a3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01De59oQmmG9HXUrcaphXhDQ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\a4b4acd04792ec9a3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement fork host+renderer v3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Round 4 MAJOR fixed — the proof epoch is now on the same per-terminal logical timeline as the generations it reasons about.\n\n## The fix (`lifecycle-alerts.ts`)\n\nNew required dep `proofEpochs: (() =&gt; Iterable&lt;{hostTerminalId, lastEventAtMs}&gt;) | null`, read **once** at construction into `proofEpochByTerminal`. Proof-of-absence moved out of the inline condition into one predicate:\n\n```\ncanProveAbsence(terminalId, seenThroughAt) =\n  !proofDisabled\n  &amp;&amp; !hasEvictedUnexpired\n  &amp;&amp; startedAtMs &lt;= seenThroughAt\n  &amp;&amp; (epoch === undefined ? !clockIsBehindPersistedTimeline\n                          : seenThroughAt &gt; epoch)\n```\n\n- **Per-terminal epoch.** With monotonic instants this process's first stamp for a terminal is `epoch + 1` at the earliest, so `seenThroughAt &lt;= epoch` means the generation belongs to a **predecessor** — its row died with that process, silence is ignorance, blind `c`. Sol's scenario (start 4000, persisted A at 5000, read at 5000) now fails `5000 &gt; 5000` and broadcasts.\n- **`clockIsBehindPersistedTimeline`** — any persisted instant `&gt;= startedAtMs` is the backstep signature, so terminals with *no* epoch row (nothing to compare against) also lose the proof while that holds. Without it the same false proof leaks through any terminal whose binding row didn't survive. In the ordinary restart (all persisted instants below start) this is `false` and nothing changes — the blind-broadcast guard is untouched.\n- **Failure is conservative, not fatal.** `null` (no restart evidence) disables proof outright; a throwing epoch read logs `could not read the lifecycle proof epoch…` and disables it, rather than killing bridge start. A blind `c` the phone drops is the safe failure; a swallowed retraction is not.\n\nComposition root (`companion/index.ts`) supplies it from `hostDb.listBindings()` — which has no `ended_at` filter, so ended sessions' `last_event_at` counts too.\n\n## Tests (`lifecycle-alerts.test.ts`, new describe, 7 added → 57 pass)\n\n- **Required case**: restart at 4000 / persisted A at 5000 / read at 5000 → blind `c` with `alertId = readyAlertIdFor(5_000)` and `gx = 5_000`.\n- **Held-5001 variant**: same restart, this process mints 5001 (held, present), read at 5000 → the newer row is filtered out and the blind `c` for 5000 still fires.\n- Proof is still claimed for `seenThroughAt = 5_001` (a generation only this process could have minted).\n- One terminal's epoch cannot silence another terminal's read (per-terminal, not a global floor).\n- Unknown-terminal behaviour both ways: timeline ahead of the clock → blind; timeline behind (ordinary restart) → silence preserved.\n- `proofEpochs: null` → no proof; epoch read throws → logged loudly and no proof.\n\n`setup()` gained `startAtMs`, `proofEpochs`, `epochThrows` seams; every existing test defaults to an empty snapshot, i.e. unchanged behaviour.\n\n## Verification\n\n- host `bun test src/companion src/trpc/router/notifications`: **394 pass / 0 fail** (25 files; lifecycle-alerts 50→57).\n- host typecheck: only the pre-existing `curation-gates.test.ts(341)`.\n- biome 2.4.2 `--line-ending=crlf` over the touched dirs: clean (two format fixes applied to `lifecycle-alerts.test.ts` and `index.ts`; the 11 errors a repo-wide `packages/host-service/src` run reports are pre-existing and in files I never touched, e.g. `trpc/router/workspaces/workspaces.ts`).\n- marker gate: **All 160 feature markers present.**\n- FEATURES.md updated with the bounded proof epoch.\n\nNothing outside this finding was touched; renderer files are unchanged this round. Still uncommitted — 19 files modified in the worktree.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>332810</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>37</tool_uses><duration_ms>722188</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a4b4acd04792ec9a3</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"30635e89-08c4-45ef-b6d8-8e8a6d9e026e","timestamp":"2026-08-16T13:55:05.464Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
