{"parentUuid":"6511f4e2-b51b-45f1-b027-13774a0caefd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce6ZQmk6YgdKCRbwTqbVk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EnFThogEgx6fyqzswMLYvA","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Final pre-install review found 2 companion findings — fix both, rerun suite, rebuild APKs, verify certs, report:\n\n1. app-watch LifecycleNotifier: shownAlerts(context) constructs a fresh ShownLifecycleAlerts per call, so @Synchronized locks a per-call instance — concurrent Data Layer notify + dismiss race the SharedPreferences read-filter-write and can lose a shown record or resurrect a just-retracted row. Fix like the phone: one shared instance (watch-side DI/singleton object) so the lock is real.\n\n2. app-phone CompanionNotifications.cancelLifecycle: cancels tag LifecycleAlertIdentity.eventKey(eventId) (\"e:\"+id), but cards posted by the CURRENTLY INSTALLED v0.1.0 used raw eventId as tag (and have no setTimeoutAfter, so they linger until manually swiped). Fix: cancel BOTH tags — the new key AND the legacy raw eventId — in cancelLifecycle (and anywhere else a cancel targets lifecycle cards), with a one-line comment naming the v0.1.0 upgrade edge. Cheap, removes the one-time stale-card window entirely.\n\nThen: full Gradle suite, assembleRelease both, cert check. Report counts + paths.","summary":"Dispatch final two companion fixes","to":"impl-android","type":"message","recipient":"impl-android","content":"Final pre-install review found 2 companion findin…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1448,"cache_read_input_tokens":409136,"output_tokens":985,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":337},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1448,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"