{"parentUuid":"b123c3dc-7e8f-413a-96c0-f7a18637de87","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce741N821PjZg8Rrc4i88","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The map is complete and there's a clean path: the phone app already hard-codes the tunnel hostname — the *only* thing a fresh install lacks is one secret that today can only cross the LAN. So the design is: a **code-based pairing flow over the tunnel** — desktop shows a short code, phone types it, the existing proven crypto handshake runs over TLS through Cloudflare, no LAN involvement at all. Two notes on your ask:\n\n- I'm making it **8 digits** shown as `1234-5678` (not 6): typed exactly the same way, but with the brute-force budget of 3 attempts per 2-minute window it makes a guess essentially impossible. QR-on-LAN stays as a second option.\n- The pairing endpoint will be reachable only with a pairing-scoped access token baked into your app — not open to the internet — and only while a window you opened is live.\n\nDispatching both implementation agents now:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"output_tokens":6542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6542,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b1d39861-80c1-41c4-ac89-b72aeeb6d3ca","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:24:44.357Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"b1d39861-80c1-41c4-ac89-b72aeeb6d3ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce741N821PjZg8Rrc4i88","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PNDW7GS2auGZdo5wYkWr2P","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement remote code pairing (fork)","isolation":"worktree","model":"opus","name":"impl-pair-fork","prompt":"Implement (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) — fork side — in this worktree of the Windows ARM64 Superset fork. NOTE: the Bash tool may be broken on this machine (malformed system profile) — use PowerShell; for grep-dependent scripts put C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin on PATH.\n\nProblem: companion pairing is QR + LAN-only (pairing.ts LAN listener :47611; PROTOCOL.md §4.1 makes LAN a hard requirement). The user's network blocks phone→PC LAN traffic, so pairing is impossible. The phone app already hard-codes the public tunnel origin (superset.khaira.family → Cloudflare Access → cloudflared → 127.0.0.1:47610); a fresh install lacks ONLY the CF service-token secret, deliverable today only via the LAN handshake.\n\nFIXED ARCHITECTURE (decided, do not re-litigate):\nAdditive \"remote code pairing\": desktop shows an 8-digit code (rendered \"1234-5678\"); phone types it; the EXISTING X25519+HKDF kex/confirm handshake (pairing.ts:355-396 derivePairingKeys, transcript :294, confirm MAC :665, sealed step-4 :688-740) runs over the tunnel with the 8-digit code as the low-entropy HKDF input, domain-separated from the QR flow (new transcript/HKDF labels, e.g. \"superset-companion/pair/v2-remote\"). Security posture (document honestly): online-only grinding, 3-bad-MAC burn, 5 confirm cap, single-use, 120s window, one window at a time, endpoint 404 when no remote window is open, reachable only via a NEW pairing-scoped Cloudflare Access service token (second Access application covering /v1/pair/* only; its client-id+secret will be embedded in the phone APK — accepted). Step-4 sealed response delivers the MAIN CF secret + bridge config exactly as the QR flow does. QR/LAN flow stays byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nYour scope:\n1. packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts: remote window variant — openRemotePairing(): 8-digit CSPRNG code (crypto.randomInt-style, never logged anywhere, never in errors), returns {code, expiresAtMs, pairingRef}; shares single-window/burn/attempt-cap machinery with the LAN variant (one active window TOTAL across both kinds); handshake handlers reusing derivePairingKeys with code as the pairingCode input under the new domain-separation labels.\n2. packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts: routes /v1/pair/kex + /v1/pair/confirm on the main 47610 listener, OUTSIDE handleSealed (unsealed), gated: (a) reject unless a REMOTE window is open (404 identical to unknown-path), (b) Access JWT validation for these two paths accepts ONLY the new pairing token identity (separate aud/common_name config — new config entries beside the existing ones, config.ts:21-37 pattern), while every other path keeps requiring the MAIN token exactly as today (path-scoped validator, fail closed both directions: pairing token must NOT authorize any other path), (c) strict per-source rate limit mirroring pairing.ts:524-567.\n3. trpc/router/companion: openRemotePairing mutation + extend pairingState so the dialog can show phase/countdown for either kind.\n4. Desktop renderer PairDeviceDialog.tsx (:363-379 render area, phase machine :64-82 + countdown :185-198 reusable): add a \"Pair with code\" mode toggle — big grouped code \"1234-5678\", countdown, retry button; CompanionPairingSetting.tsx copy updated (\"works from anywhere\" for code mode). Match existing UI idiom; no new deps.\n5. Config: new settings for pairing-token aud + CN (+ client-id passthrough if the bridge needs it), sourced the same way the existing Access config is; absent config = remote pairing disabled loudly (openRemotePairing throws a clear message telling the user the CF pairing app isn't configured), LAN flow unaffected.\n6. PROTOCOL.md is in the COMPANION repo — out of your scope; the companion agent owns it. But update FEATURES.md: new (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) row + markers rooting in pairing.ts/http.ts/PairDeviceDialog; and the fork's own docs if any reference LAN-only pairing.\n7. Tests (mirror existing pairing test idiom): window single-use/burn/expiry shared across kinds; only-one-window; 404-when-closed; path-scoped token acceptance matrix (pairing token on /v1/pair/* ok, pairing token on /v1/tree rejected, main token on /v1/pair/* rejected); code never appears in any log/error (assert on messages); HKDF domain separation (QR-flow vectors unchanged byte-for-byte — golden); full handshake happy path with an 8-digit code; wrong-code burn after 3.\n8. Run: host companion suite (bun test), scoped biome lint, tsc on touched files, marker gate (node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs with git grep on PATH). All green.\n\nRules: never log or persist the code in plaintext beyond the window's lifetime; fail fast; match existing style; DO NOT touch the QR/LAN flow's wire bytes or PROTOCOL claims about it; do not commit — leave the worktree for review. Report per-item + test results + the exact config keys the user's CF setup step must fill.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"output_tokens":6542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6542,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5b14a85d-07a7-4985-9902-24d13143cca6","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:25:11.982Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"5b14a85d-07a7-4985-9902-24d13143cca6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce741N821PjZg8Rrc4i88","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PQK3NipaSdVFyjYEDwLL4t","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement remote code pairing (phone)","model":"opus","name":"impl-pair-phone","prompt":"Implement (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) — phone side — in C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion (Kotlin; app-phone/app-watch/core; PROTOCOL.md is normative and lives here). NOTE: Bash may be broken on this machine — use PowerShell for shell work; Gradle runs fine from PowerShell.\n\nProblem + FIXED ARCHITECTURE (decided): companion pairing is QR + LAN-only and the user's network blocks phone→PC LAN. Additive remote flow: desktop shows an 8-digit code (\"1234-5678\"); user types it in the phone app; the EXISTING X25519+HKDF kex/confirm handshake (core/.../pairing/PairingClient.kt:50-208, KeyDerivation) runs over the PUBLIC TLS origin (CompanionConstants PUBLIC_ORIGIN, already compiled in) through a NEW pairing-scoped Cloudflare Access service token (its client-id+secret WILL be embedded in the app as constants beside ACCESS_CLIENT_ID — accepted decision; add clearly-named constants with placeholder values and a comment that the real values come from the CF pairing app setup), with the 8-digit code as the low-entropy HKDF input under NEW domain-separation labels (\"superset-companion/pair/v2-remote\" — coordinate: the fork agent is implementing the same labels; PROTOCOL.md is the meeting point, write the labels there normatively). Sealed step-4 delivers the MAIN CF secret + bridge config exactly as the QR flow. QR/LAN flow stays byte-for-byte unchanged (PairingUri host restrictions untouched for the QR path).\n\nYour scope:\n1. core pairing: PairingClient remote variant — TLS OkHttp client (NOT the CLEARTEXT one, standard ConnectionSpec), targets PUBLIC_ORIGIN /v1/pair/kex + /v1/pair/confirm with the pairing service-token headers; same kex/confirm steps; code (digits only, 8) replaces pc as the HKDF input under the v2-remote labels; NO fp verification in this flow (TLS to the pinned hostname is the authenticity anchor — document that in PROTOCOL §4 amendment); store identity + main CF secret from the sealed response exactly as the QR flow (SecureCompanionStore path unchanged).\n2. app-phone UI: PairingScreen (ui/pairing/PairingScreen.kt:78-196, Unpaired/Scanning branch :165-192) gains a \"Enter code instead\" affordance → 8-digit entry (auto-grouping 1234-5678, digits keyboard, paste-tolerant), submit → pairFromCode wired through CompanionShell (:177-186 pairFromQr sibling) + BridgeCompanionRepository (:890-910). Loading/countdown/error states.\n3. PairingState (phone/model/PairingState.kt:47-91): new error codes — CODE_WRONG (bad code/MAC), CODE_BURNED (window burned after 3), WINDOW_CLOSED (404), NETWORK (origin unreachable) — each with a human message that tells the user the next step (\"check the code and the window on your desktop\", \"open a new pairing window\", etc.). Never echo the entered code in errors or logs.\n4. PROTOCOL.md: amend §4 normatively — new §4.x \"Remote code pairing\": the v2-remote labels, transcript, 8-digit code semantics (online-only grinding, burn/attempt caps, single-use, 120s, one window), the pairing-scoped Access token reachability model, TLS-as-authenticity-anchor (no fp), the explicit statement that §4.3's \"no PAKE needed\" rationale does NOT apply to the short code and what compensates (window+burn+token-scoped reachability), and that LAN QR remains unchanged. Fix §4.1's \"LAN is a hard requirement, no degraded path\" claim.\n5. Tests: remote handshake happy-path against a fake server (mirror existing pairing tests); v2-remote HKDF/label vectors (write them as shared golden literals the fork side can mirror — put the vectors IN the test file with clear byte values); wrong-code → CODE_WRONG; 404 → WINDOW_CLOSED; QR-flow tests untouched and green; code-not-in-logs assertion.\n6. Run the full Gradle unit suite (same 2 pre-existing env failures are acceptable). Do NOT build APKs yet (constants need real CF values first). Do not commit.\n\nReport per-item + test counts + the exact constant names the CF setup must fill + the golden vector values for the fork side.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"output_tokens":6542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6542,"cache_read_input_tokens":453433,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"04025513-4dc6-420f-a5e4-384e9f0bc522","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:25:33.954Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"5b14a85d-07a7-4985-9902-24d13143cca6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"45ca7d09-fa99-4b80-ba22-acddca00d9ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNDW7GS2auGZdo5wYkWr2P","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a6c0cf0431904f59f (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a6c0cf0431904f59f', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a6c0cf0431904f59f.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"a5b79c27-4b6f-4c11-b655-a0cd523ac740","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:26:22.175Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a6c0cf0431904f59f","description":"Implement remote code pairing (fork)","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","prompt":"Implement (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) — fork side — in this worktree of the Windows ARM64 Superset fork. NOTE: the Bash tool may be broken on this machine (malformed system profile) — use PowerShell; for grep-dependent scripts put C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin on PATH.\n\nProblem: companion pairing is QR + LAN-only (pairing.ts LAN listener :47611; PROTOCOL.md §4.1 makes LAN a hard requirement). The user's network blocks phone→PC LAN traffic, so pairing is impossible. The phone app already hard-codes the public tunnel origin (superset.khaira.family → Cloudflare Access → cloudflared → 127.0.0.1:47610); a fresh install lacks ONLY the CF service-token secret, deliverable today only via the LAN handshake.\n\nFIXED ARCHITECTURE (decided, do not re-litigate):\nAdditive \"remote code pairing\": desktop shows an 8-digit code (rendered \"1234-5678\"); phone types it; the EXISTING X25519+HKDF kex/confirm handshake (pairing.ts:355-396 derivePairingKeys, transcript :294, confirm MAC :665, sealed step-4 :688-740) runs over the tunnel with the 8-digit code as the low-entropy HKDF input, domain-separated from the QR flow (new transcript/HKDF labels, e.g. \"superset-companion/pair/v2-remote\"). Security posture (document honestly): online-only grinding, 3-bad-MAC burn, 5 confirm cap, single-use, 120s window, one window at a time, endpoint 404 when no remote window is open, reachable only via a NEW pairing-scoped Cloudflare Access service token (second Access application covering /v1/pair/* only; its client-id+secret will be embedded in the phone APK — accepted). Step-4 sealed response delivers the MAIN CF secret + bridge config exactly as the QR flow does. QR/LAN flow stays byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nYour scope:\n1. packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts: remote window variant — openRemotePairing(): 8-digit CSPRNG code (crypto.randomInt-style, never logged anywhere, never in errors), returns {code, expiresAtMs, pairingRef}; shares single-window/burn/attempt-cap machinery with the LAN variant (one active window TOTAL across both kinds); handshake handlers reusing derivePairingKeys with code as the pairingCode input under the new domain-separation labels.\n2. packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts: routes /v1/pair/kex + /v1/pair/confirm on the main 47610 listener, OUTSIDE handleSealed (unsealed), gated: (a) reject unless a REMOTE window is open (404 identical to unknown-path), (b) Access JWT validation for these two paths accepts ONLY the new pairing token identity (separate aud/common_name config — new config entries beside the existing ones, config.ts:21-37 pattern), while every other path keeps requiring the MAIN token exactly as today (path-scoped validator, fail closed both directions: pairing token must NOT authorize any other path), (c) strict per-source rate limit mirroring pairing.ts:524-567.\n3. trpc/router/companion: openRemotePairing mutation + extend pairingState so the dialog can show phase/countdown for either kind.\n4. Desktop renderer PairDeviceDialog.tsx (:363-379 render area, phase machine :64-82 + countdown :185-198 reusable): add a \"Pair with code\" mode toggle — big grouped code \"1234-5678\", countdown, retry button; CompanionPairingSetting.tsx copy updated (\"works from anywhere\" for code mode). Match existing UI idiom; no new deps.\n5. Config: new settings for pairing-token aud + CN (+ client-id passthrough if the bridge needs it), sourced the same way the existing Access config is; absent config = remote pairing disabled loudly (openRemotePairing throws a clear message telling the user the CF pairing app isn't configured), LAN flow unaffected.\n6. PROTOCOL.md is in the COMPANION repo — out of your scope; the companion agent owns it. But update FEATURES.md: new (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) row + markers rooting in pairing.ts/http.ts/PairDeviceDialog; and the fork's own docs if any reference LAN-only pairing.\n7. Tests (mirror existing pairing test idiom): window single-use/burn/expiry shared across kinds; only-one-window; 404-when-closed; path-scoped token acceptance matrix (pairing token on /v1/pair/* ok, pairing token on /v1/tree rejected, main token on /v1/pair/* rejected); code never appears in any log/error (assert on messages); HKDF domain separation (QR-flow vectors unchanged byte-for-byte — golden); full handshake happy path with an 8-digit code; wrong-code burn after 3.\n8. Run: host companion suite (bun test), scoped biome lint, tsc on touched files, marker gate (node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs with git grep on PATH). All green.\n\nRules: never log or persist the code in plaintext beyond the window's lifetime; fail fast; match existing style; DO NOT touch the QR/LAN flow's wire bytes or PROTOCOL claims about it; do not commit — leave the worktree for review. Report per-item + test results + the exact config keys the user's CF setup step must fill.","outputFile":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a6c0cf0431904f59f.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b14a85d-07a7-4985-9902-24d13143cca6","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
