{"parentUuid":"eb8274a2-80d7-44f5-9000-d3d9b7f45f13","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce74FmHgof8gFZ2iZke3N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G3D7N7jEmSDeDeUkgtbpT9","name":"PowerShell","input":{"command":"$c = Get-Content \"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\SETUP.md\" | Out-String; $i = $c.IndexOf(\"Access\"); $c.Substring($i, [Math]::Min(2600, $c.Length - $i)); Get-ChildItem \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.config\\cf\" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object FullName","description":"Read SETUP.md Access section and cf config contents"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_read_input_tokens":466696,"output_tokens":357,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":466696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ca27cb41-a9c6-4793-8300-b3c843c1df98","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:27:17.670Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"ca27cb41-a9c6-4793-8300-b3c843c1df98","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"45ca7d09-fa99-4b80-ba22-acddca00d9ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3D7N7jEmSDeDeUkgtbpT9","type":"tool_result","content":"Access being\r\nconfigured. Access is now in place (below), so the only remaining precondition is the bridge itself:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\ncloudflared service install\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Cloudflare Access — DONE and VERIFIED\r\n\r\n`superset.khaira.family` now sits behind Access, reachable only by one service token.\r\n\r\n| Thing | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Service token name | `superset-companion-phone` |\r\n| Client id | `c6d1295b4ed520de15de3446b9ec736b.access` |\r\n| Client secret | **not here** — `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access.json` |\r\n| Token duration | Non-expiring (`forever`; nominal expiry 2126) |\r\n| Application | `superset-companion-bridge` (self-hosted) |\r\n| Application AUD | `40d388403c3555b6fdc75302c99c24dffa5503fa5ac2a8f7774f30ac221ccf29` |\r\n| Team domain | `khairm.cloudflareaccess.com` |\r\n| Policy | `phone-service-token` — **Service Auth only** (`non_identity`), include = that one token |\r\n\r\nThe application carries exactly **one** policy. There is no identity policy and no allow-all rule, so\r\nno human login can reach the host — only a caller holding the token. The bridge still validates the\r\nAccess JWT itself against the AUD and team domain above, rather than trusting the edge, because a\r\npolicy misconfiguration could otherwise let requests through.\r\n\r\n**Files:**\r\n- `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access.json` — **the client secret**, plus ids, AUD and team\r\n  domain. Same class as the FCM key: outside this repo, ACL-restricted to your user account only.\r\n  Never copy it in here. The client id above is safe to record; the secret is not.\r\n\r\n**Verified working, not assumed.** Two live requests to `https://superset.khaira.family/`:\r\n\r\n| Request | Status | Means |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| No headers | **403** | Access refuses anonymous callers |\r\n| `CF-Access-Client-Id` + `CF-Access-Client-Secret` | **530** | Passed Access, then hit the missing tunnel |\r\n\r\nThe 530 is the *good* result here — it is the tunnel-not-running signal from the taxonomy above,\r\nwhich proves the request got past Access to the tunnel layer. Denial without the token plus 530 with\r\nit is exactly the shape a correct configuration produces.\r\n\r\nSet up through the Zero Trust dashboard's own authenticated API, driven from the browser session —\r\nno manual clicking. One gotcha: `GET`s from the page work as-is, but every mutating call is blocked\r\nby Cloudflare's WAF with a 403 challenge page unless it carries the dashboard's own\r\n`X-Cross-Site-Security: dash` header. Blocked attempts fail at the edge and create nothing, so the\r\nretry was safe.\r\n\r\n## Not started\r\n\r\nThe app itself. No Gradle project, no Ko\r\n\r\nFullName\r\n--------\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\completions\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\config.json\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\completions\\cf.bash","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"eb400a0e-cda7-45ef-9102-b0f474998bac","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:27:21.808Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Access being\r\nconfigured. Access is now in place (below), so the only remaining precondition is the bridge itself:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\ncloudflared service install\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Cloudflare Access — DONE and VERIFIED\r\n\r\n`superset.khaira.family` now sits behind Access, reachable only by one service token.\r\n\r\n| Thing | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Service token name | `superset-companion-phone` |\r\n| Client id | `c6d1295b4ed520de15de3446b9ec736b.access` |\r\n| Client secret | **not here** — `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access.json` |\r\n| Token duration | Non-expiring (`forever`; nominal expiry 2126) |\r\n| Application | `superset-companion-bridge` (self-hosted) |\r\n| Application AUD | `40d388403c3555b6fdc75302c99c24dffa5503fa5ac2a8f7774f30ac221ccf29` |\r\n| Team domain | `khairm.cloudflareaccess.com` |\r\n| Policy | `phone-service-token` — **Service Auth only** (`non_identity`), include = that one token |\r\n\r\nThe application carries exactly **one** policy. There is no identity policy and no allow-all rule, so\r\nno human login can reach the host — only a caller holding the token. The bridge still validates the\r\nAccess JWT itself against the AUD and team domain above, rather than trusting the edge, because a\r\npolicy misconfiguration could otherwise let requests through.\r\n\r\n**Files:**\r\n- `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access.json` — **the client secret**, plus ids, AUD and team\r\n  domain. Same class as the FCM key: outside this repo, ACL-restricted to your user account only.\r\n  Never copy it in here. The client id above is safe to record; the secret is not.\r\n\r\n**Verified working, not assumed.** Two live requests to `https://superset.khaira.family/`:\r\n\r\n| Request | Status | Means |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| No headers | **403** | Access refuses anonymous callers |\r\n| `CF-Access-Client-Id` + `CF-Access-Client-Secret` | **530** | Passed Access, then hit the missing tunnel |\r\n\r\nThe 530 is the *good* result here — it is the tunnel-not-running signal from the taxonomy above,\r\nwhich proves the request got past Access to the tunnel layer. Denial without the token plus 530 with\r\nit is exactly the shape a correct configuration produces.\r\n\r\nSet up through the Zero Trust dashboard's own authenticated API, driven from the browser session —\r\nno manual clicking. One gotcha: `GET`s from the page work as-is, but every mutating call is blocked\r\nby Cloudflare's WAF with a 403 challenge page unless it carries the dashboard's own\r\n`X-Cross-Site-Security: dash` header. Blocked attempts fail at the edge and create nothing, so the\r\nretry was safe.\r\n\r\n## Not started\r\n\r\nThe app itself. No Gradle project, no Ko\r\n\r\nFullName\r\n--------\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\completions\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\config.json\r\nC:\\Users\\khair\\.config\\cf\\completions\\cf.bash","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca27cb41-a9c6-4793-8300-b3c843c1df98","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
