{"parentUuid":"0d98c7cc-a8bd-42fb-89cc-2cf7e390e911","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ba57bbb8-e40b-48ac-b001-13956f64ad9f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6c0cf0431904f59f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01PNDW7GS2auGZdo5wYkWr2P</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a6c0cf0431904f59f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement remote code pairing (fork)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>(REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) fork side: implemented, all gates green, nothing committed. Worktree `.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f`.\n\n## Per item\n\n1. **`packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts`** — `openRemotePairing(deps)` mints 8 CSPRNG digits (`randomInt(0,1e8)`, zero-padded, uniform), returns `{ code, expiresAtMs, pairingRef, kind, closed, toJSON, close }`; `toJSON` exposes only kind/ref/expiry, and the `code` getter throws 410 once closed. **One window slot shared across both kinds** — QR-vs-code, code-vs-code, code-vs-QR all collide with 409. Burn / 5-confirm cap / expiry / single-use / kex-junk machinery is the existing code reached through the same handlers. New `PairingProfile` (LAN + REMOTE) carries salt prefix, transcript prefix, three HKDF labels and the step-4 AAD path; `derivePairingKeys` / `buildPairingTranscript` are profile-driven with the prefix defaulting to the QR flow, so no existing caller changed.\n2. **`http.ts`** — `/v1/pair/kex` + `/v1/pair/confirm` on 47610, outside `handleSealed`. Order: pairing-validator-or-404 → Access JWT (pairing identity only) → pre-auth bucket → window-or-bodyless-404 (403 `pair_code_burned` inside a 60 s memo) → `cf-connecting-ip` required → 4 KiB bounded read → handler. Per-source cap 32/window over 32 evicting buckets. `pairingAccessValidator` is a required-but-nullable dep; every other path keeps the main validator untouched.\n3. **tRPC** — `companion.openRemotePairing` → `{ code, expiresAtMs }`; `pairingState` gained `pairingKind: \"lan\" | \"remote\"`; `CompanionBridge.openRemotePairing()` added.\n4. **Renderer** — `PairDeviceDialog` mode toggle, flow keyed on mode; code mode renders `1234-5678` big/tabular/non-selectable with the same countdown and phases; secret is one discriminated union, dropped on unmount; verdicts ignored unless the window kind matches. `CompanionPairingSetting` + settings-search copy updated. No new deps.\n5. **Config** — new `cloudflare-access-pairing.json`, read at start. Absent → code flow off, QR untouched, `openRemotePairing` throws naming the file; present-but-wrong → throws at start-up.\n6. **FEATURES.md** — new row + 6 markers (pairing.ts, http.ts, config.ts, index.ts, trpc/router/companion, PairDeviceDialog). No other fork doc asserts LAN-only pairing.\n7. **Tests** — new `remote-pairing.test.ts`, 22 tests: pinned QR goldens (schedule, 117-byte transcript, prefix-default equivalence), the Android client's frozen v2-remote vectors reproducing **byte-for-byte**, domain-separation inequality, one-window, closed-window unreachable, bodyless 404 (no window / no pairing app), 400 without `cf-connecting-ip`, full happy path (stored K_dev == phone's, sealed step-4 opens under K_s2c), same envelope failing under the LAN AAD path, `pair_bad_key_agreement`, 3-strike burn + memo 403, code absent from console/logger/error bodies/`JSON.stringify`, and an Access matrix with real RS256 tokens vs a test JWKS.\n8. **Gates** — `bun test src/companion` **397 pass / 0 fail**; marker gate **\"All 171 feature markers present\"**; Biome lint/assist clean on all touched paths; tsc clean in every file I touched (remaining errors are pre-existing debt: `curation-gates.test.ts`, node-pty, windsurf, V2Workspace). Formatter complaints are the worktree's pre-existing CRLF checkout and hit untouched files identically.\n\n## Config the CF setup must fill\n\n`~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access-pairing.json`:\n```json\n{ \"app_aud\": \"&lt;64-char lowercase hex AUD of the NEW pairing Access app&gt;\",\n  \"client_id\": \"&lt;pairing service token client id, ends in .access&gt;\",\n  \"team_domain\": \"khairm.cloudflareaccess.com\" }\n```\nStart-up rejects it if `app_aud` isn't 64 hex, `client_id` doesn't end `.access`, `team_domain` differs, or either value equals the MAIN application's. The pairing token's **secret is deliberately not a field** — the desktop only validates JWTs; the secret lives in the APK. The Access app must cover `/v1/pair/*` only. Restart host-service after writing it.\n\n## Deviations (deliberate)\n\n- Adopted the companion agent's frozen labels (`superset-companion/pair/v2-remote`, `sc/v2-remote …`, 124-byte transcript) rather than my draft; vectors verified identical on both runtimes.\n- Three new wire codes (`pair_code_wrong`, `pair_code_burned`, `pair_bad_key_agreement`); LAN codes untouched. Added a 60 s burn memo.\n- Access validation runs *before* the window check (spec listed 404 first) — fail-closed on identity; difference is only observable to a valid pairing-token holder.\n- Source attribution is `cf-connecting-ip`, absence refused (the socket peer behind the tunnel is always loopback).\n- **I pushed back on the phone side's kex shape**, which carried the code in the request body. Cloudflare terminates the TLS, so that would have handed the edge a pairable code and voided the MITM argument. They agreed and dropped it, plus a kex-side burn rule that junk could have used to destroy a legitimate window.\n\n## Unresolved\n\nNothing committed; the second Access application doesn't exist yet, so the remote flow is OFF on this machine and end-to-end with a real phone is untested by construction. `bun install` was run here (worktree had no `node_modules`); `bun.lock` unchanged. The honest weakness — 8 digits ≈ 26.6 bits, online-only, ≤3 guesses in 10⁸ per user-opened window — is written into pairing.ts's header and the FEATURES.md row rather than left implicit.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>394761</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>207</tool_uses><duration_ms>2892442</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"86e33c02-979e-4263-aa9d-789123b63a72","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:13:41.790Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
