{"parentUuid":"fd364b20-cc9c-4695-bbd0-6413750e87fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce781XCS5yqwfTTU8sAMk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JxWVpJD76NgqvSompAvEt7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Security review remote pairing (Sol)","name":"rev2-sol","prompt":"Adversarial SECURITY review (correctness second) of the uncommitted (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) implementation. Read-only. Findings ranked BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line + concrete attack scenario, plus a verified-sound list. Bash may be broken on this machine (malformed system profile) — use PowerShell; rely on reported suite numbers where you cannot run (fork: 397/0 companion suite; phone: 422 tests / 2 pre-existing env failures).\n\nTrees:\n1. FORK worktree C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f (uncommitted; git status/diff + read new files): packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts (remote 8-digit window variant, PairingProfile domain separation), http.ts (/v1/pair/kex + /v1/pair/confirm unsealed on 47610, pairing-scoped Cloudflare Access validation, per-source rate buckets, 60s burn memo), companion config (cloudflare-access-pairing.json fail-closed handling), trpc/router/companion (openRemotePairing), renderer PairDeviceDialog code mode, FEATURES.md, remote-pairing.test.ts.\n2. COMPANION C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion (uncommitted): core/.../pairing/RemotePairingHandshake.kt (TLS client, v2-remote labels, code never transmitted — proven only via macPhone at confirm), PairingCode, app-phone PairingScreen code entry, RemotePairingErrorMapping, PROTOCOL.md §4.9, RemotePairingVectorsTest (frozen cross-runtime vectors).\n\nDesign (user-approved, do NOT re-litigate the concept): 8-digit code pairing over the public Cloudflare tunnel; existing X25519+HKDF kex/confirm with the code as HKDF input, domain-separated (salt prefix \"superset-companion/pair/v2-remote\", labels \"sc/v2-remote …\", 124-byte transcript, step-4 AAD \"/v1/pair/confirm\"); APK-embedded pairing-scoped CF Access service token = reachability only; one window slot across QR+code kinds; 120s, single-use, 3-bad-confirm-MAC burn, 5-confirm cap; sealed step-4 delivers the main CF secret; QR/LAN flow byte-frozen (goldens pinned).\n\nAttack checklist:\n1. AUTH/PATH SCOPING (http.ts): can the pairing token reach anything besides the two pair endpoints — path normalization (/v1/pair/../tree), casing, trailing slash, query, double-encoding, method variance? Can the MAIN token hit /v1/pair/*? Anything bypassing handleSealed? Does the RS256 access-matrix test pin the negative cases?\n2. GRINDING/STATE: 3-strike burn airtight across kex/confirm interleavings, concurrency, close/reopen races? One-window 409 race-free? DoS: junk kex, bucket exhaustion, or the burn memo locking out legitimate pairing?\n3. CRYPTO: domain separation complete vs LAN (labels/salt/transcript/AAD vs the pinned vectors); code appears nowhere on wire/logs/errors/URLs/tRPC beyond the dialog; MITM at the CF edge (who legally reads TLS) limited to online guessing — pPub/dPub swap, step-4 replay, cross-window splicing? AAD path binding \"/v1/pair/confirm\" vs LAN \"/pair/confirm\".\n4. SECRET HANDLING: code lifetime in renderer memory; never persisted/logged either side (verify the no-code-in-logs tests cover every emission path); main CF secret delivery unchanged.\n5. CONFIG FAIL-CLOSED: missing/wrong cloudflare-access-pairing.json (start-up rejection, must-differ-from-MAIN check); phone REPLACE_ME constructor guard.\n6. REGRESSION: QR/LAN flow byte-identical (goldens), sealed transport untouched, alert/question paths untouched.\nReport via SendMessage to me (team-lead) when done.","subagent_type":"code-reviewer-sol"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens