{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"bd408ee7-97e6-453e-9bb4-d503e1971970","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"manual","preTokens":494542,"postTokens":8844,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":6135211,"durationMs":165973,"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"5e76ac0b-6f84-4d5f-a66f-56fc9e85253f","anchorUuid":"202fe799-8f2c-44bf-a39f-29356c996a88","tailUuid":"bd408ee7-97e6-453e-9bb4-d503e1971970"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"202fe799-8f2c-44bf-a39f-29356c996a88","uuids":["5e76ac0b-6f84-4d5f-a66f-56fc9e85253f","818c72d7-348a-4392-ac14-e62143d5ea9e","2dac7461-5b23-4f2f-928e-c436637106d6","7f5dd1a8-df1b-492e-ac06-dfd01d5b2320","0faa9d95-6614-4d70-9175-40f7a76a17e4","4d9c4216-56eb-4106-8da4-085901f4a83f","bd408ee7-97e6-453e-9bb4-d503e1971970"],"allUuids":["5e76ac0b-6f84-4d5f-a66f-56fc9e85253f","818c72d7-348a-4392-ac14-e62143d5ea9e","2dac7461-5b23-4f2f-928e-c436637106d6","7f5dd1a8-df1b-492e-ac06-dfd01d5b2320","0faa9d95-6614-4d70-9175-40f7a76a17e4","4d9c4216-56eb-4106-8da4-085901f4a83f","bd408ee7-97e6-453e-9bb4-d503e1971970"]}},"uuid":"3e205f1b-97a0-42d3-b95a-222ccd01453b","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:09.322Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3e205f1b-97a0-42d3-b95a-222ccd01453b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ee64123d-b41f-4856-87f1-39b9c86ab024","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Request A — Named companion alerts (delivered, shipped):** \"The companion app now tells me when a chat has finished, but it doesn't tell me which chat. It should tell me the name on the left, for example: the name of the project (e.g. PX V1 apps), the name of the worktree/space (eg super simplify), the tab name (if there are multiple tabs) (eg Claude Resume). These should be in the notification, and if I open that up I can see them there too. Make sense? asksuer tool always to perfect the ux\"\n   - UX decisions (AskUserQuestion): title = `Project · Workspace`, body = `Tab — <event>`; tab omitted when only one tab; applies to ALL alert types (finished/error/question); watch shows same text as phone.\n   - Delivery: user initially chose sealed-in-push, then said **\"i dont care if google sees it fyi\"** → re-asked → **plaintext names in the FCM push**. Scope of waiver: ONLY project/workspace/tab names. Question text, option text, file paths and all other free text remain BANNED from pushes.\n   - Two follow-up FYIs: \"FYI I'm only expecting the notification for completed chat for when a green dot would appear in the left hand bar\" and \"Also on phone and watch if I clear the question or read the completed chat (green dot) then those notifications should retract too\".\n\n   **Request B — One buzz per unread chat (delivered, shipped):** \"why am I getting an agent finished notification every 15 minutes... should be once per finish event per chat?\" Investigation found 16 distinct `g` alerts overnight from one chat. User chose \"One buzz until read (Recommended)\": a repeat finish while the previous notification is unread updates it silently; reading retracts and resets so the next finish buzzes fresh.\n\n   **Request C — Sessions Recycle Bin (delivered, shipped):** \"on the left where it says sessions... just checking that if I press X on that row that it sends it to the recycled bin for sessions and also I need access to the recycle bin. currently there's no option to open or show the recycle bin\". UX decisions: bin opened via the **Sessions context menu** only (user declined footer button and command palette); bulk multi-select delete converted to **soft-delete**.\n\n   **Request D — Code-based pairing (IN PROGRESS, BLOCKED):** After the release-key re-pair failed repeatedly (\"failing - I nkeep getting couldnt reach the desktop join the same wifi and try again .... can't we do 6 digit code or something\"), user instructed: **\"rebuild to allow 6 digit code instead of QR -\"** then **\"fuck this you're wasting my time\"**. I chose 8 digits (rendered `1234-5678`) for entropy, over the public Cloudflare tunnel, keeping QR/LAN as a second option.\n\n   **Ship sequencing intent:** \"start the desktop build and have it to ready to install\", \"Then when thats in motion ask me about companion installations\", \"both now on wireless debugging\".\n\n   Standing operational rules: work on main, never force-push; ship only through the full GitHub Windows ARM64 workflow, never hot-patch the installed app; `/simplify` before commit on production code; `/code-review` per batch; scratch in `tmp/` only; AskUserQuestion for every decision; install only on explicit authorization.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Windows ARM64 Electron/Superset vendored fork; Bun/Turbo monorepo; host-service companion bridge\n   - FCM v1 data-only pushes with closed per-(version,kind) key sets; `collapse_key = data.i`\n   - v3 wire: `q`=[v,k,i,w,n,x,t,pn,wn,tn,tc]; `g`=[v,k,i,w,x,gx,t,pn,wn,tn,tc] (t required non-empty, gx required); `e`=[v,k,i,w,x,t,pn,wn,tn,tc] (separate closed set, no gx); `c`=[v,k,i,w,x,gx,t]. All keys always present; `\"\"` = absent. v1/v2 frozen.\n   - `gx` = the OUTCOME instant (occurredAtMs), never send-derived; per-terminal monotonic via `nextLifecycleInstantMs(now, prev) = now > prev ? now : prev + 1`\n   - Host alert states: held / sending / sent / **standing** (silently superseded, still on devices) / retracted\n   - Proof-of-absence: `canProveAbsence` = !proofDisabled && !hasEvictedUnexpired && startedAtMs<=seenThroughAt && (epoch===undefined ? !clockIsBehindPersistedTimeline : seenThroughAt>epoch)\n   - Phone tombstones (`SeenLifecycleEvents.suppress`, never `release` on retract); generation-based post/cancel (`shown.gx <= c.gx` retires)\n   - Renderer outstanding-ready records (not cleared by `Start`), compare-and-clear on acknowledged generation\n   - Cloudflare Access service tokens + tunnel (`superset.khaira.family` → cloudflared → 127.0.0.1:47610); bridge independently validates `Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion`\n   - Pairing crypto: X25519 + HKDF; LAN profile labels `sc/v1`; new remote profile `superset-companion/pair/v2-remote`, labels `sc/v2-remote …`, 124-byte transcript, step-4 AAD `/v1/pair/confirm`\n   - PAKE (SPAKE2+/OPAQUE) — NOT implemented; this is the crux of the open blocker\n   - FEATURES.md marker gate (165→171 markers), REFERR gate, Biome, scoped tsc\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **`tmp/alert-context-names/FINAL.md`** (fork main checkout) — normative spec for the alert work; §0 UX + waiver, §1 wire schema, §2 text composition, §3 context plumbing, §4 retraction, §5 rollout, §6 gates, §7 tests, §8 accepted deviations (per-surface question bodies; g-only retraction on seen; `c` as its own Kotlin type; non-terminal panes name a tab only via explicit rename because derived names are free text outside the waiver; ONE-BUZZ amendment incl. `gx`).\n\n   **`packages/host-service/src/companion/push.ts`** — privacy doctrine rewritten with the waiver; `PUSH_DATA_KEYS_BY_VERSION_KIND`, flat `PUSH_VALUE_RULES`, `PUSH_NAME_EXEMPT_KEYS` = {pn,wn,tn}; total `sanitizePushName` (uses shared `findUnpairedSurrogate` from keystrokes.ts; degrades whole field to `\"\"`); `buildLifecycleRetractPushData`; per-message envelope TTL (r and c → RETRACT_TTL_MS 24h).\n\n   **`packages/host-service/src/companion/lifecycle-alerts.ts`** — `RetireReason = {kind:\"new-cycle\"|\"session-end\"|\"seen\"}`; `notifiesPhone(alert, reason) = !(alert.kind === \"g\" && reason.kind === \"new-cycle\")`; `retireAlert`; `findReadAlerts(hostTerminalId, seenThroughAt)` (only outcomeAtMs <= seenThroughAt, retires every covered generation); `proofEpochs` dep. This file was corrupted by a PowerShell `Set-Content -NoNewline` and byte-verified reconstructed (998 lines).\n\n   **`packages/host-service/src/companion/push-context.ts`** (new) — bounded `AlertContextRegistry` (LRU 512, DB relationship validation, atomic per-workspace replace).\n\n   **Renderer:** `V2NotificationController/lib/alertContexts.ts` (one title per tab), `companionAlertSync.ts` (desired/sentHash/retry, `markTerminalSeenAndReportRead`), `resyncAgentStatus.ts` (repair with cooldown+rotation), `terminalTitleListeners.ts` (desired-pair map + `onInstanceRegistered` observer), `stores/v2-notifications/store.ts` (`markTerminalSeen` returns boolean; `outstandingReadyAt`).\n\n   **Companion repo:** `core/.../protocol/AlertNotificationText.kt`, `AlertContext.kt`, `core/.../notify/ShownLifecycleAlerts.kt`, `LifecycleAlertIdentity` (t:/e: prefixed keyspaces), `PendingLifecycleDismissals.kt`, `WearProtocol.kt` (redacted toStrings on all name-bearing envelopes incl. WatchQuestionItem/Option), `app-phone/.../SeenLifecycleEvents.kt` (`suppress`), `PROTOCOL.md` §13.5.x.\n\n   **Recycle bin:** `DashboardSidebarSessionsSection.tsx` (variant \"deleted\" lane), `DashboardSidebarSessionsContextMenu.tsx` (\"Show Recycle Bin\"), `useBulkWorkspaceSoftDelete/`, `sidebarMutations.ts` (`resolveSidebarRowProjectId` shared by delete/snooze/archive), `AgentHooks/.../tools/delete-workspace.ts` + `types.ts` (delete mutation handle REMOVED from ToolContext — type-enforced containment).\n\n   **New pairing work (UNCOMMITTED):**\n   - Fork worktree `.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f`: `pairing.ts` `openRemotePairing()` (8 CSPRNG digits, one window slot shared across kinds, `PairingProfile` LAN/REMOTE); `http.ts` `/v1/pair/kex` + `/v1/pair/confirm` outside handleSealed, gate order pairing-validator-or-404 → Access JWT (pairing identity only) → pre-auth bucket → window-or-bodyless-404 (403 `pair_code_burned` in a 60s memo) → `cf-connecting-ip` required → 4KiB bounded read; new error codes `pair_code_wrong`, `pair_code_burned`, `pair_bad_key_agreement`; `remote-pairing.test.ts` 22 tests; 397 pass/0 fail; 171 markers.\n   - Companion repo: `core/.../pairing/RemotePairingHandshake.kt` (TLS OkHttp, pairing Access headers, no fp check, code never transmitted — proven only via `macPhone` at confirm); `PairingScreen.kt` 8-digit entry; `RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt` (403 branched by body: `pair_code_burned` vs `access_denied`→ACCESS_REFUSED); `PROTOCOL.md` §4.9; `RemotePairingVectorsTest.kt` frozen vectors (PRK 2c1a1522…, K_dev f3d417c6…, macPhone f360a3dc…, transcript 124 bytes); 422 tests / 2 pre-existing env failures.\n   - Config the CF setup must fill: phone `CompanionConstants.kt` `PAIRING_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID` + `PAIRING_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET` (both `REPLACE_ME…`, constructor throws while placeholder); desktop `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access-pairing.json` `{app_aud, client_id, team_domain}` (secret deliberately absent; start-up rejects if it names the MAIN app).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **AskUserQuestion `preview` rejected** (\"disabled by user policy\") → re-issued with label/description only.\n   - **Alert review rounds (all fixed):** lone-surrogate host/Kotlin mismatch (BLOCKER); alert-id derived from `binding.lastEventAt` which advances on non-lifecycle events; resync repair unreachable behind `preEntry !== undefined`; `sentHash` set on `accepted:false`; per-terminal split-tab titles; missing DB revalidation on markLifecycleSeen; unstable `workspacesById` effect key; raw NUL/SOH making a test file binary to ripgrep; stale comments; Kotlin `toString` leaking names; queue-capacity dismissal drop; blind `c` broadcast eroding the phone's 64-slot dedupe window; registry keyed by terminalId instead of paneId (shadow entry); listener lifecycle gaps (late creation, dispose+recreate).\n   - **One-buzz review rounds (all fixed):** silent retirement occupying `retracted` so later session-end/seen could never retract; identity taken from the nullable context resolver; outstanding-ready cleared by `Start`; non-monotonic `Date.now()` breaking gx ordering; `markLifecycleSeen` retracting newer unread work; unconditional outstanding clear; proof epoch on wall clock.\n   - **/simplify reverts (agents pushed back correctly):** fork kept `resolveContextSafely` at both consumers (a test injects a throwing resolver directly into `createPushSender`); Android kept `requireOpaqueOrEmpty` pre-check (its error message is the pinned leak signal).\n   - **lifecycle-alerts.ts corruption** by `Set-Content -NoNewline` → byte-verified reconstruction; I independently sanity-checked the file.\n   - **Merge blocked** by uncommitted AI-streak CI work in main; user said \"bring it all in as well - that work is done include it in your commits/pushes\"; by re-check the other session had committed it (172f50ab6a), so the merge proceeded cleanly.\n   - **Bash tool broken** on this machine (malformed system profile; every command dies in the wrapper). Verified user's `.bashrc`/`.bash_profile` are intact — it's the tool wrapper. Workaround: PowerShell, with `C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin` on PATH for grep-dependent gate scripts.\n   - **`INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`**: installed v0.1.0 was debug-signed (cert `bcf6465…`, CN=Android Debug); v0.2.0 is release-signed (`b1ecb33be027b2010ae051acd596c1fe77896c5bb6cf24736cad55f6aa5e2d75`). User chose \"Release key + re-pair\" → uninstall+install both devices to v0.2.0.\n   - **adb devices dropped** mid-install → `adb kill-server`/`start-server` rediscovered both.\n   - **Final code-review findings (fixed):** watch `shownAlerts(context)` built per call so `@Synchronized` locked nothing; phone/watch could not cancel v0.1.0-posted cards (tag/id formula changed) → cancel both legacy and new identities.\n   - **Reviewer agents crashed:** rev2-opus died on \"Fable 5's safeguards flagged this message\"; rev2-sol died on \"flagged for possible cybersecurity risk\" — my adversarial-attack-framed brief tripped content classifiers.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Shipped three features end-to-end with multi-round adversarial review: named alerts (v3 plaintext names), retraction on read, one-buzz-until-read, and the sessions recycle bin (including removing a physical-destroy path from the remote agent tool by deleting the mutation handle from `ToolContext`). Merged to main (`8ffd5c6fca`), pushed, built (run 31952224483, attempt-1 green), released `desktop-v1.20.2` (installer sha `2CBFD22502D1902E070BD1D7A32BCE5B8F4C4FE056120687B38C37E7DD5A10CA`), installed and verified by grepping app.asar. Companion v0.2.0 installed on Pixel Watch 4 and Pixel 10 Pro Fold.\n\n   **Open problem:** re-pairing fails. Diagnosis showed the desktop side is healthy (47611 listening, firewall rules present, LAN self-test OK, network profile Public) — the phone simply cannot reach the PC over this network. User demanded a code-based flow. Implemented 8-digit remote pairing over the tunnel; both halves complete, mutually verified, frozen cross-runtime vectors reproduced byte-for-byte on both runtimes.\n\n   **NEW BLOCKER (unresolved), from rev2-sol:** `RemotePairingHandshake.kt:163-195` accepts an unauthenticated server X25519 key and sends `macPhone`; desktop `pairing.ts:530-579,884-905` treats the code as an HKDF tail. A TLS-terminating active edge (Cloudflare terminates the TLS) can substitute `pPub` toward the desktop and `dPub` toward the phone, learn the phone-side DH secret and transcript, then brute-force all 10^8 codes **offline** against `macPhone` (plain HKDF/HMAC-SHA256) and submit only the correct MAC — the 3-strike/5-confirm limits never see the guesses. It becomes paired and can decrypt the sealed step-4 carrying the main CF secret. Sol's stated fix: a real augmented/balanced PAKE (OPAQUE/SPAKE2+) or an authenticated desktop key channel — raw X25519 + a low-entropy PSK is not sufficient. This matches the earlier architecture exploration: option A (PAKE) is the only design preserving the protocol's security claims; option B (what was built) is the cheap-but-weaker path.\n\n   Also noted by rev2-sol: the companion working tree/HEAD `835c283…` is ahead of its `origin/main` `e16c218…` (my local commits are unpushed — expected, the companion repo was never pushed this session).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"The companion app now tells me when a chat has finished, but it doesn't tell me which chat. It should tell me the name on the left, for example: - the name of the project (e.g. PX V1 apps) - the name of the worktree/space (eg super simplify) - the tab name (if there are multiple tabs) (eg Claude Resume) These should be in the notification, and if I open that up I can see them there too. Make sense? asksuer tool always to perfect the ux\"\n   - AskUser answers: \"Context in title (Recommended)\"; \"Omit tab (Recommended)\"; \"All alert types (Recommended)\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"how can it not be embedded in the notification?\"; then \"Sealed in push (Recommended)\"; watch \"Same as phone (Recommended)\"\n   - **\"i dont care if google sees it fyi\"**\n   - AskUser answer: \"Plaintext names (Recommended)\"\n   - \"FYI I'm only expecting the notification for completed chat for when a green dot would appear in the left hand bar\" / \"Also on phone and watch if I clear the question or read the completed chat (green dot) then those notifications should retract too\" / \"continue sorry\"\n   - \"why am I getting an agent finished notification every 15 minutes... should be once per finish event per chat?\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"One buzz until read (Recommended)\"\n   - \"on the left where it says sessions... just checking that if I press X on that row that it sends it to the recycled bin for sessions and also I need access to the recycle bin. currently there's no option to open or show the recycle bin\"\n   - AskUser answers: \"Sessions context menu (Recommended)\"; \"Soft-delete (Recommended)\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"bring it all in as well - that work is done include it in your commits/pushes\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"start the desktop build and have it to ready to install\"\n   - \"Then when thats in motion ask me about companion installations\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"both now on wireless debugging\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"Release key + re-pair (Recommended)\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"Install now (Recommended)\" (desktop)\n   - \"installed bro\"\n   - AskUser answer: \"failing - I nkeep getting couldnt reach the desktop join the same wifi and try again .... can't we do 6 digit code or something - does it need to be this complex with a QR code especially since has to be same wifi to pair (i check phone and laptop defo on same wifi)\"\n   - \"where am I opening the window in the desktop or phone?!\"\n   - \"I had opened and the 2 minutes elapsed shall I do it again?\"\n   - AskUser answer: **\"rebuild to allow 6 digit code instead of QR -\"**\n   - **\"fuck this you're wasting my time\"**\n   - \"what are we working on now?\" (with instruction to produce a summary only)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Resolve the pairing BLOCKER** — the 8-digit remote pairing as built is offline-crackable by a TLS-terminating edge. Needs a PAKE (SPAKE2+/OPAQUE, requiring hash-to-curve on both runtimes) or an authenticated desktop-key channel, or the feature must not ship.\n   - Re-run the security review (both reviewers crashed on content classifiers; the brief must be re-worded away from attack framing).\n   - Create the second Cloudflare Access application scoped to `/v1/pair/*` + its service token; fill `PAIRING_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID`/`PAIRING_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET` in the APK and `~/.superset/companion/cloudflare-access-pairing.json` on the desktop (client_id must match exactly in both places or every attempt returns 403).\n   - Commit/push the pairing work (both trees uncommitted); push the companion repo (local `835c283` is ahead of `origin/main` `e16c218`).\n   - Rebuild + install APKs and desktop after the above; then the actual re-pair, which is still outstanding — until it completes, phone/watch receive no alerts.\n   - Known accepted gap: the shipped alert features are installed but unverified end-to-end on the real phone precisely because pairing is broken.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request I was running an adversarial security review of the uncommitted (REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) work in two trees (fork worktree `agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f`, companion repo). Both implementation halves reported complete and mutually verified: fork 397 tests/0 fail, 171 markers, path-scoped Access matrix with real RS256 tokens; phone 422 tests/2 pre-existing env failures, 45 new, frozen vectors reproduced byte-for-byte across runtimes.\n\n   rev2-sol then reported a **verified BLOCKER** before dying: \"A TLS-terminating active edge can replace pPub toward desktop and dPub toward phone, know the phone-side DH secret/transcript, and brute-force all 10^8 ASCII codes OFFLINE against macPhone (plain HKDF/HMAC-SHA256), then submit only the correct desktop-side MAC, become paired, and decrypt sealed step 4/main CF secret. Three-strike/5-confirm limits never see the guesses. Fix requires a real augmented/balanced PAKE (e.g. OPAQUE/SPAKE2+) or an authenticated desktop key channel, not raw X25519+low-entropy PSK.\"\n\n   Both reviewer agents (rev2-opus, rev2-sol) then failed with API content-safety errors triggered by my attack-framed review brief. No fix has been dispatched for the blocker yet; nothing about the pairing work is committed.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Surface the blocker to the user and get a decision, because it changes scope materially and the user has already expressed frustration at time spent. Specifically: the 8-digit code flow as built is not safe to ship — Cloudflare terminates the TLS, so an attacker positioned there could crack the code offline and steal the pairing. The realistic options are (a) implement SPAKE2+/OPAQUE so a short code is genuinely safe (large: new curve dependency on both runtimes plus new cross-runtime vectors), (b) ship a long random code that is typed/pasted rather than 8 digits (small, keeps the existing crypto sound), or (c) drop remote pairing and fix LAN reachability instead. This is directly in line with the user's most recent explicit request — \"rebuild to allow 6 digit code instead of QR -\" — and the review that was running when the summary was requested, whose verdict was: \"Fix requires a real augmented/balanced PAKE (e.g. OPAQUE/SPAKE2+) or an authenticated desktop key channel, not raw X25519+low-entropy PSK.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"202fe799-8f2c-44bf-a39f-29356c996a88","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:07.608Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49