{"parentUuid":"47f5e2f1-9c88-4e2a-a72c-f6789f3a7563","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\bxz1rtn4p.output","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\bxz1rtn4p.output","content":"build 31952224483: in_progress:\nbuild 31952224483: completed:success\n\n[exited with code 0]\n","numLines":5,"startLine":1,"totalLines":5}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\6e3543cc-ec14-446a-a214-ee9f89274f0a\\tasks\\bxz1rtn4p.output"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dbe33dc5-aa52-4689-a9c3-50d6b79dd10f","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:07.623Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"dbe33dc5-aa52-4689-a9c3-50d6b79dd10f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-onebuzz.txt","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-onebuzz.txt","content":"feat(companion): one buzz per unread chat, generation-ordered retraction\n\n(ONE-BUZZ-UNTIL-READ) A chat that finishes again while its previous\nfinished-notification is unread now updates it silently in place;\nreading the chat retracts and resets, so the next finish buzzes fresh.\nEvidence: one long-running chat produced 16 stacked buzzing alerts\novernight on v0.1.0.\n\n- v3 wire (pre-ship amendment, lockstep with companion v0.2.0): g gains\n  required gx (the outcome instant) and required non-empty t; c gains\n  required gx; e unchanged as its own closed set (e carrying gx throws)\n- per-terminal MONOTONIC lifecycle instants (nextLifecycleInstantMs,\n  anchored on the persisted binding) feed event storage, alert ids,\n  g.gx and c.gx - clock backsteps can no longer strand notifications\n- host alert state machine gains `standing` (silently superseded, still\n  on devices): sent -> standing on a new cycle (no retract frame),\n  escalating to exactly one c on read or session-end; in-flight\n  supersede reasons upgrade\n- g identity (t, gx) comes off the alert row; display-name resolution\n  failing can degrade names but never identity\n- reads are bounded by their own instant: markLifecycleSeen retires\n  every generation <= seenThroughAt and never newer unread work\n- renderer keeps an outstanding-ready record per terminal that Start\n  does not clear, with generation-aware compare-and-clear, so reading\n  a now-running chat still retracts its notification\n- proof-of-absence epoch moved onto the per-terminal logical timeline\n  (restart during a clock backstep now blind-retracts instead of\n  falsely proving absence)\n\nAdversarially reviewed across 4 rounds (Sol/Opus), all findings fixed.\nShips with superset-companion v0.2.0 (watch first, then phone, before\nthis host build - older apps silently ignore v3).\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"displayPath":"tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-onebuzz.txt"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"68fb3d44-2a05-4dce-b415-a36b3f151e31","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:07.616Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"68fb3d44-2a05-4dce-b415-a36b3f151e31","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\AGENTS.md","displayPath":"AGENTS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"290ee244-c19f-44cd-b491-7c37eef65ad7","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:08.457Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"290ee244-c19f-44cd-b491-7c37eef65ad7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-bin.txt","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-bin.txt","content":"feat(desktop): sessions recycle bin, bulk soft-delete, lifecycle null-project fixes\n\n(RECYCLE-BIN-SESSIONS) The sidebar Sessions section gains a Recycle Bin\nlane: deleted sessions now partition into a revealable \"Recycle Bin\"\nstate section (30-day display window, deletedAt DESC) with per-row\nRestore and Delete permanently, toggled via \"Show Recycle Bin\" in the\nSessions context menu. Previously the X on a session row soft-deleted\ninto a void - the row vanished with no UI to see or restore it.\n\n(RECYCLE-BIN) hardening:\n- bulk multi-select delete converted from a physical git destroy to the\n  same lossless soft delete as single rows (mains skipped and kept\n  selected; host-refused rows stay selected); the dead hard-destroy\n  dialog stack is removed\n- the remote agent-command delete_workspace tool now soft-deletes via\n  the same path; its physical-delete mutation handle is removed from\n  ToolContext entirely, so no tool can compile a path to a destroy;\n  mains refused loudly per (MASTER-ARCHIVE-ONLY)\n- deleteWorkspace/snoozeWorkspace/archiveWorkspace accept\n  projectId: string | null through one shared resolveSidebarRowProjectId\n  (explicit null honoured for sessions; silent no-op refusals removed;\n  fail-loud narrowed to genuinely unresolvable)\n\nSession permanent-delete verified safe end-to-end in host\nworkspace-cleanup (sessions are a first-class destroy branch: dirty\npreflight opted in, rm gated by isInsideSessionsRoot, failures\nun-archive and rethrow).\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}},"displayPath":"tmp\\alert-context-names\\commit-msg-bin.txt"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ae4649e2-24e0-4079-b9e3-aa08b73a0a00","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:07.617Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"ae4649e2-24e0-4079-b9e3-aa08b73a0a00","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"agent_listing_delta","addedTypes":["architect-fable","architect-opus","architect-sol","claude","code-reviewer-fable","code-reviewer-opus","code-reviewer-sol","codex:codex-rescue","entire-search","Explore","feature-dev:code-architect","feature-dev:code-explorer","feature-dev:code-reviewer","general-purpose","project-structure-validator","sol","statusline-setup","understand-anything:architecture-analyzer","understand-anything:article-analyzer","understand-anything:assemble-reviewer","understand-anything:domain-analyzer","understand-anything:file-analyzer","understand-anything:graph-reviewer","understand-anything:knowledge-graph-guide","understand-anything:project-scanner","understand-anything:tour-builder"],"addedLines":["- architect-fable: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- architect-opus: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- architect-sol: Designs implementation architectures: analyzes existing codebase patterns, then delivers a blueprint — files to create/modify, component design, data flow, build sequence, risks, alternatives. Read-only: never edits code. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)","- code-reviewer-fable: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- code-reviewer-opus: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- code-reviewer-sol: Adversarial code review of diffs/commits/PRs: correctness, security, data integrity, conventions. Verifies each finding before reporting, ranks BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and concrete failure scenario. Read-only: never fixes. (Tools: Bash, Glob, Grep, Read, LSP, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- codex:codex-rescue: Proactively use when Claude Code is stuck, wants a second implementation or diagnosis pass, needs a deeper root-cause investigation, or should hand a substantial coding task to Codex through the shared runtime (Tools: Bash)","- entire-search: Search Entire checkpoint history and transcripts with `entire search --json`. Use proactively when the user asks about previous work, commits, sessions, prompts, or historical context in this repository. (Tools: Bash)","- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: \"medium\" for moderate exploration, \"very thorough\" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- feature-dev:code-architect: Designs feature architectures by analyzing existing codebase patterns and conventions, then providing comprehensive implementation blueprints with specific files to create/modify, component designs, data flows, and build sequences (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- feature-dev:code-explorer: Deeply analyzes existing codebase features by tracing execution paths, mapping architecture layers, understanding patterns and abstractions, and documenting dependencies to inform new development (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- feature-dev:code-reviewer: Reviews code for bugs, logic errors, security vulnerabilities, code quality issues, and adherence to project conventions, using confidence-based filtering to report only high-priority issues that truly matter (Tools: Glob, Grep, LS, Read, NotebookRead, WebFetch, TodoWrite, WebSearch, KillShell, BashOutput)","- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)","- project-structure-validator: Validates project structure against co-location and architecture patterns defined in AGENTS.md (Tools: All tools)","- sol: General-purpose subagent running on Codex GPT-5.6 Sol via the claude-all gateway. Use for heavy implementation, deep debugging, second-opinion reviews, or any Task the orchestrator wants executed by GPT-5.6 Sol instead of a Claude model. Accepts any prompt a general-purpose agent would. (Tools: All tools)","- statusline-setup: Use this agent to configure the user's Claude Code status line setting. (Tools: Read, Edit)","- understand-anything:architecture-analyzer: Analyzes a codebase's file structure, summaries, and import relationships to identify\nlogical architectural layers and assign every file to exactly one layer. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:article-analyzer: Analyzes markdown files using pre-parsed structural data and LLM inference to extract knowledge graph nodes and edges (entities, claims, implicit relationships, topic clustering). (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:assemble-reviewer: Reviews the output of merge-batch-graphs.py for semantic issues the script\ncannot catch. Recovers dropped nodes/edges and fills cross-batch gaps. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:domain-analyzer: Analyzes codebases to extract business domain knowledge — domains, business flows, and process steps. Produces a domain-graph.json that maps how business logic flows through the code. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:file-analyzer: Analyzes batches of source files to produce knowledge graph nodes and edges.\nExtracts file structure, functions, classes, and relationships using a two-phase\napproach: structural extraction script followed by LLM semantic analysis. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:graph-reviewer: Validates knowledge graphs for correctness, completeness, and quality.\nRuns systematic checks and renders approval or rejection decisions. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:knowledge-graph-guide: Use this agent when users need help understanding, querying, or working\nwith an Understand-Anything knowledge graph. Guides users through graph\nstructure, node/edge relationships, layer architecture, tours, and\ndashboard usage. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:project-scanner: Scans a codebase directory to produce a structured inventory of all project files,\ndetected languages, frameworks, import maps, and estimated complexity. (Tools: All tools)","- understand-anything:tour-builder: Designs guided learning tours through codebases, creating 5-15 pedagogical steps\nthat teach project architecture and key concepts in logical order. (Tools: All tools)"],"removedTypes":[],"isInitial":true,"showConcurrencyNote":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8739e522-8b2b-40ee-8a5b-06608476c158","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:56:08.458Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
