{"parentUuid":"b8c965ef-695d-464d-a187-7b4c5ed697d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_08a0eb4ae2cdd0fd016a82325528d4819180836d1537f900d5","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37239,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":884,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Progress update\n\n### Completed and shipped\n- **Named phone/watch alerts**: project, workspace, and tab names are included.\n- **One buzz per unread finished chat**: repeat finishes update silently until the chat is read.\n- **Notification retraction**: reading a finished chat or clearing a question removes its phone/watch notification.\n- **Sessions Recycle Bin**: session delete is recoverable, bulk delete is soft-delete, with restore and permanent-delete controls.\n- **Desktop release `desktop-v1.20.2`** built successfully, published, installed, and verified.\n- **Companion v0.2.0** is installed on the Pixel phone and watch.\n\n### Current blocker\n- The phone and watch are still **not paired**, so real alerts cannot yet be tested end-to-end.\n- I built and tested an **8-digit remote pairing flow** as an alternative to the failing same-Wi-Fi QR flow.\n- Security review found that design unsafe: because Cloudflare handles the connection, a compromised connection layer could test every short code privately and gain pairing access.\n- I stopped it at the review gate. **The unsafe pairing code has not been committed, pushed, or shipped.**\n\n### Remaining work\n1. Replace the short-code security design with a protocol specifically built to protect short pairing codes.\n2. Repeat security review and full tests.\n3. Configure the separate Cloudflare pairing route.\n4. Build and install the updated desktop and companion apps.\n5. Complete real phone/watch pairing and verify alerts end-to-end.\n6. Push the companion source, which is currently only local.\n\n**Bottom line:** the alert and Recycle Bin features are complete; secure remote pairing is the only major unfinished piece, and phone/watch alerts remain unverified until that pairing succeeds."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"9d782b3b-f27f-4942-97e5-9011a036fde9","timestamp":"2026-08-16T21:57:58.614Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
