{"parentUuid":"c01fbc7e-0f09-414b-894c-7790c1bab501","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_056e6bb85450738f016a8238b601888191a4f454a65680bd34","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":74240,"output_tokens":2122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_j9w82QiBgEd6qFMMmgV5g9re","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","name":"desktop-srp-opus","description":"Implement desktop SRP pairing","prompt":"You own task #2. Implement the approved SRP-6a remote pairing replacement in place at:\nC:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\nThis worktree contains an uncommitted X25519+8-digit-HKDF prototype. Replace only the remote code pairing cryptography; preserve QR/LAN v1 byte-for-byte and preserve the already-built UI, Access-path enforcement, limits, state machine, error mapping, and step-4 envelope unless the SRP wire requires a targeted change. Do not commit or push.\n\nNormative architecture approved by 3 Fable reviews:\n- SRP-6a, RFC 5054 3072-bit safe-prime group, SHA-256. Desktop is server; phone is client. Fixed identity ASCII `sc/v3 remote-pair`; password is exactly 8 ASCII digits; fresh 16-byte pairSalt per pairing window.\n- x = H(salt || H(I || ':' || P)); v = g^x mod N. Window retains code for display, salt, verifier; drops them on close. Never transmit code, x, verifier, or another offline-checkable code derivative.\n- Kex request remote wire version 2: fixed-width 384-byte base64url A plus existing bounded metadata. Kex response: pid, fixed-width 384-byte B, pairSalt, server time. Remote v1 refused with pair_version_unsupported; no fallback/coexistence. LAN remains v1.\n- Fresh random b (>=256 bits), B, u, S, and derived keys PER ACCEPTED KEX CANDIDATE, never per window and never reused. Candidate stores only B and derived keys/transcript inputs needed for confirm; erase references to b/S as soon as derived. Retransmitted kex replaces the candidate.\n- k = H(PAD(N) || PAD(g)) matching BC/RFC behavior; u = H(PAD(A) || PAD(B)); B=(k*v+g^b) mod N; S=(A*v^u)^b mod N. PAD/I2OSP is exactly 384-byte unsigned big-endian. Validate API boundaries before derivation: decoded A must be exactly 384 bytes, 0<A<N, and reject A in {1,N-1} plus A mod N==0; reject u==0. Fail loud as pair_bad_key_agreement. Use Node built-ins only; no third-party Node crypto.\n- Key schedule: HKDF-Extract salt = ASCII `superset-companion/pair/v3-srp` || pairSalt; IKM=PAD(S). Labels exactly `sc/v3-srp device ` (trailing space)||pid||deviceId, `sc/v3-srp confirm-phone`, `sc/v3-srp confirm-desktop`. Transcript exactly ASCII `sc/v3-srp` || pid(16) || deviceId(16) || PAD(A)(384) || PAD(B)(384) || pairSalt(16). Confirm/HMAC role separation, charge-before-verify, burn-after-3, caps, persist-before-seal, AAD `/v1/pair/confirm`, sealed main credentials, and deviceId checks stay intact. Do not replace transcript MACs with RFC M1/M2.\n- Keep one window/120s/single-use/404 closed/5 confirm attempts/source limits/burn memo. Keep (PAIR-META-UNAUTHENTICATED) behavior and markers.\n- Remote protocol labels must be wholly v3-srp; delete v2-remote crypto labels to prevent downgrade. Keep LAN goldens.\n- Implement pure, tight SRP server math in a dedicated module if that best matches style. Parameterize enough to test RFC 5054 Appendix B 1024/SHA-1 independently even though production is 3072/SHA-256. Use constant-time MAC comparisons. Document unavoidable BigInt non-zeroization/timing limitation honestly, not as a security claim.\n- Tests: exact RFC Appendix B anchor; deterministic production-profile golden vectors with injected a/b or supplied A inputs; boundary/canonical rejection A=0,1,N-1,N,N+..., u=0 if injectable; wrong code; tampered B/transcript; retransmit replacement; per-candidate distinct B; full HTTP Access matrix still green; LAN v1 vectors unchanged; proof the edge transcript cannot validate a code without an online run should be a property/assertion grounded in the protocol, not a misleading brute force test.\n- Update FEATURES.md marker description and any authoritative host comments/spec references. Preserve all markers and run feature marker gate, targeted tests, lint, and scoped type checks. Do not claim broad typecheck if accepted repository debt fails elsewhere.\n\nCoordinate directly with agent `companion-srp-opus`: agree exact constants, wire field names, and publish deterministic golden inputs/outputs to them as soon as stable. Review their reported vectors against yours. If a Fable detail conflicts with actual mature SRP/BC behavior, fail loud and message me before improvising. Follow AGENTS.md and global rules. Keep task #2 in_progress on any unresolved failure; mark completed only when implementation and tests are genuinely done, then send a concise report with files, tests, vectors, and deviations."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"1f78f558-3c15-4387-acd3-442e64dc1c2d","timestamp":"2026-08-16T22:25:43.326Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"1f78f558-3c15-4387-acd3-442e64dc1c2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_056e6bb85450738f016a8238b601888191a4f454a65680bd34","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":74240,"output_tokens":2122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_6pyC8IX0gcMNkKBKxNv7SkJP","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","name":"companion-srp-opus","description":"Implement Android SRP pairing","prompt":"You own task #3. Implement the matching approved SRP-6a remote pairing replacement in place at:\nC:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\nThis repo contains uncommitted phone/UI/protocol work for the blocked X25519+8-digit-HKDF prototype and is ahead of origin with prior alert commits. Replace only the remote code pairing cryptography; preserve QR/LAN pairing byte-for-byte, the 8-digit UI, existing error handling, push registration, Access headers, and secure storage. Do not commit, push, build/install APKs, or expose secret values.\n\nNormative architecture approved by 3 Fable reviews:\n- SRP-6a RFC 5054 3072-bit group + SHA-256. Phone is SRP client; desktop is server. Fixed identity ASCII `sc/v3 remote-pair`; password exactly 8 ASCII digits; pairSalt 16 bytes from desktop.\n- Use current latest stable `org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on` lightweight API (`org.bouncycastle.crypto.*`) for SRP6Client / SRP6StandardGroups; pin exact version in version catalog. NEVER register BC as a JCE provider. Verify actual API before coding. Use one SRP6Client per handshake. Generate fresh a/A per user submit.\n- Kex request remote wire version 2: A as fixed-width 384-byte unsigned big-endian base64url plus existing metadata. Kex response: pid, B fixed 384 bytes, pairSalt, serverTimeMs. Remote v1 refused; no fallback. LAN stays v1.\n- Validate boundaries before SRP: B decoded exactly 384 bytes, 0<B<N; reject B in {1,N-1} and B mod N==0; reject u==0. Map bad values to BAD_KEY_AGREEMENT/fail loud without accepting credentials.\n- Let BC generate A and calculate raw S only. Do not use BC calculateSessionKey/evidence methods. Convert S to exact 384-byte unsigned big-endian PAD.\n- Production key schedule: HKDF-Extract salt = ASCII `superset-companion/pair/v3-srp` || pairSalt; IKM=PAD(S). Labels exactly `sc/v3-srp device ` (trailing space)||pid||deviceId, `sc/v3-srp confirm-phone`, `sc/v3-srp confirm-desktop`. Transcript exactly ASCII `sc/v3-srp` || pid(16)||deviceId(16)||PAD(A)(384)||PAD(B)(384)||pairSalt(16). Keep macPhone first, sealed step-4 AAD `/v1/pair/confirm`, AES-GCM open, macDesktop constant-time check, deviceId check, and storage semantics. Never substitute RFC M1/M2.\n- Delete v2-remote crypto labels/codepaths; remote payload v2 only. Never transmit the code or a code-derived verifier. Preserve all existing limits/errors and the code countdown semantics.\n- Tests: verify BC profile behavior; RFC 5054 Appendix B via parameterized helper if feasible; frozen deterministic cross-runtime production-profile vectors from desktop agent; honest run via MockWebServer; wrong code, tampered B/transcript, B=0,1,N-1,N,wrong length, u=0 where feasible, version refusal, code absence from logs/stack traces, QR/LAN tests unchanged. Update PROTOCOL.md §4.9 to describe SRP honestly, including limits (BigInteger timing/non-zeroization, SRP maturity tradeoff), and keep all existing Access/error/state documentation.\n- Run full Gradle unit suites and targeted tests. Distinguish the two known pre-existing CrossRuntimeDifferentialVectors20260729Test environment failures if they remain; do not hide new failures.\n\nCoordinate directly with agent `desktop-srp-opus`: agree exact constants/wire names and consume the desktop deterministic golden vector set; independently recompute and compare every value. If actual BC behavior differs from the plan, message me and the desktop agent before adapting. Follow repo AGENTS/global rules, keep Entire enabled. Keep task #3 in_progress on unresolved failures; mark completed only when implementation/tests are done, then report files, dependency/version, tests, vectors, and deviations."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"23ea9b7c-1b25-4bac-a1a7-591462cb6594","timestamp":"2026-08-16T22:25:43.426Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
