bits), B, u, S, and derived keys PER ACCEPTED KEX CANDIDATE, never per window and never reused. Candidate stores only B and derived keys/transcript inputs needed for confirm; erase references to b/S as soon as derived. Retransmitted kex replaces the candidate.\n- k = H(PAD(N) || PAD(g)) matching BC/RFC behavior; u = H(PAD(A) || PAD(B)); B=(k*v+g^b) mod N; S=(A*v^u)^b mod N. PAD/I2OSP is exactly 384-byte unsigned big-endian. Validate API boundaries before derivation: decoded A must be exactly 384 bytes, 0<A<N, and reject A in {1,N-1} plus A mod N==0; reject u==0. Fail loud as pair_bad_key_agreement. Use Node built-ins only; no third-party Node crypto.\n- Key schedule: HKDF-Extract salt = ASCII `superset-companion/pair/v3-srp` || pairSalt; IKM=PAD(S). Labels exactly `sc/v3-srp device ` (trailing space)||pid||deviceId, `sc/v3-srp confirm-phone`, `sc/v3-srp confirm-desktop`. Transcript exactly ASCII `sc/v3-srp` || pid(16) || deviceId(16) || PAD(A)(384) || PAD(B)(384) || pairSalt(16). Confirm/HMAC role separation, charge-before-verify, burn-after-3, caps, persist-before-seal, AAD `/v1/pair/confirm`, sealed main credentials, and deviceId checks stay intact. Do not replace transcript MACs with RFC M1/M2.\n- Keep one window/120s/single-use/404 closed/5 confirm attempts/source limits/burn memo. Keep (PAIR-META-UNAUTHENTICATED) behavior and markers.\n- Remote protocol labels must be wholly v3-srp; delete v2-remote crypto labels to prevent downgrade. Keep LAN goldens.\n- Implement pure, tight SRP server math in a dedicated module if that best matches style. Parameterize enough to test RFC 5054 Appendix B 1024/SHA-1 independently even though production is 3072/SHA-256. Use constant-time MAC comparisons. Document unavoidable BigInt non-zeroization/timing limitation honestly, not as a security claim.\n- Tests: exact RFC Appendix B anchor; deterministic production-profile golden vectors with injected a/b or supplied A inputs; boundary/canonical rejection A=0,1,N-1,N,N+..., u=0 if injectable; wrong code; tampered B/transcript; retransmit replacement; per-candidate distinct B; full HTTP Access matrix still green; LAN v1 vectors unchanged; proof the edge transcript cannot validate a code without an online run should be a property/assertion grounded in the protocol, not a misleading brute force test.\n- Update FEATURES.md marker description and any authoritative host comments/spec references. Preserve all markers and run feature marker gate, targeted tests, lint, and scoped type checks. Do not claim broad typecheck if accepted repository debt fails elsewhere.\n\nCoordinate directly with agent `companion-srp-opus`: agree exact constants, wire field names, and publish deterministic golden inputs/outputs to them as soon as stable. Review their reported vectors against yours. If a Fable detail conflicts with actual mature SRP/BC behavior, fail loud and message me before improvising. Follow AGENTS.md and global rules. Keep task #2 in_progress on any unresolved failure; mark completed only when implementation and tests are genuinely done, then send a concise report with files, tests, vectors, and deviations.","teammate_id":"desktop-srp-opus@session-db223e0d","agent_id":"desktop-srp-opus@session-db223e0d","agent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","name":"desktop-srp-opus","color":"red","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-db223e0d","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1f78f558-3c15-4387-acd3-442e64dc1c2d","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
