{"parentUuid":"c94ac9cb-ce06-4dba-8775-75dfd4fd30f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_0098df1fac730020016a8259ce9a3481918f28fd6ed72c8583","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":150016,"output_tokens":2815,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_wR1oi9MRxBDuPx0uXUo6rk1k","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"desktop-srp-opus","summary":"Apply deduplicated simplify fixes","message":"Phase 2 of required /simplify: apply the deduplicated behavior-preserving fixes below in your existing worktree. Do not commit/push. Rerun full companion tests, target Electron timing, Biome, marker, REFERR, and scoped tsc; report each applied/skipped item with reason.\n\nAPPLY:\n1) Fix the measured 2.4s/event-loop DH constructor waste in srp.ts. DO NOT cache/reuse one mutable DiffieHellman object after setPrivateKey: it would retain the latest x/b secret indefinitely. Prefer a fresh predefined native group object per exponentiation (investigate getDiffieHellman('modp15'), verify its prime exactly equals production N, and use computeSecret(base) so generator=2 is irrelevant even for base g=5) or another built-in native path that avoids primality checks and drops key object refs after each synchronous call. Prove math vs pure BigInt and benchmark under ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. If no safe native path exists, stop and report rather than retaining secrets. On top, use native path for v^u if clean.\n2) Replace wipe variants with one wipeAllPairingKeys helper; skip buffer.some scan when observer null.\n3) Remove dead/redundant discriminants/state: PairingProfile.kind, duplicated OpenPairingWindow.kind, RemoteBurnMemo.pairingRef; move remoteRequestCounts onto RemotePairingSessionState only.\n4) Keep LAN/remote transcript builders structurally separate and hardcode their byte-frozen prefixes inside each; share only one fixed-length concatenation loop/helper. Remove optional/caller-supplied transcriptPrefix and its no-op test.\n5) Extract shared bounded per-source charging logic. More importantly, stop inserting arbitrary public IPs into the authenticated bridge preauthBuckets. At the pair-host boundary, after exact route+source and live-window lookup but BEFORE body read/crypto, charge the remote window's bounded per-source table exactly once; inner handlers must not double-charge and direct calls must not bypass. Closed-window scans allocate nothing. Preserve body cap, 32-source/32-request bounds, and tests.\n6) Consolidate JSON response header/body construction so no-store cannot drift.\n7) Remove redundant SRP A%N check; strict 1<A<N-1 remains.\n8) Use c.req.path and pre-lowercased constants in host gate.\n9) Use @superset/ui ToggleGroup/ToggleGroupItem for the QR/code selector. Unify or centrally map the renderer vocabulary so the poll cannot repeat an inline qr/code↔lan/remote ternary. Remove PairingSecret.mode if provably derivable from remounted mode prop.\n10) Remove sealed-body copy if Response accepts the original bytes without type/zeroization issue.\n11) Consolidate the authoritative open-window guard in pairing.ts and remove index.ts duplicate prechecks if user-visible fail-loud behavior/messages stay identical.\n12) Move the BRIDGE_PUBLIC_HOST-vs-PAIRING_PUBLIC_HOST invariant to a module-load assertion and remove the unreachable loader branch, while KEEPING the JSON host value + requireEqual drift check (the config intentionally names the audited host; do not reduce it to a mere existence flag).\n\nSKIP, but report: generic common window factory (too invasive for cleanup); changing publicPairHost to boolean (loses config drift assertion); removing lookup/burned/fetch/wipe test seams without a clearly equivalent test path; injecting all pairing module state through BridgeHttpServer (singleton is current architecture); optional new confirm wire error code/UX split (safe current message, avoid protocol churn); companion LAN helper/OkHttp cleanup (outside this desktop diff and deferred to correctness review).","type":"message","recipient":"desktop-srp-opus","content":"Phase 2 of required /simplify: apply the deduplic…"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3a5b0f5e-8634-4e23-ac81-d713d17e867c","timestamp":"2026-08-17T00:47:11.030Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
