{"parentUuid":"b5d59e6a-a6f2-49ee-9b99-74645aec5105","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f8141793-8631-4728-a4bf-e5704c00de39","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_GIeUZNhiZ4lASFDDGwtPtLRx","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the ID below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagent_id: srp-runtime-fable-1@session-db223e0d\nname: srp-runtime-fable-1\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"7426ad77-8fb9-4951-86de-d11241289e5f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T01:05:05.514Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"Read-only urgent architecture decision. Inspect current SRP code in C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\srp.ts and pairing caps/state. Production is Windows ARM64 Electron/BoringSSL. Measured: createDiffieHellman(custom RFC5054 3072 prime,g=5) costs 2.3-2.8 seconds EACH due primality check; getDiffieHellman('modp15') has same prime but no setPrivateKey and same constructor cost; PKCS8/SPKI crypto.diffieHellman works Node but Electron throws unsupported; actual native exponent is ~1ms; pure JS BigInt modpow is 4-8ms. Current design calls native at window open for verifier and per new kex for g^b/S, so public traffic can block event loop for seconds each. A cached mutable DH object is forbidden because it retains last x/b secret. Worker preserves huge CPU DoS. Proposed fix: pure BigInt for secret exponents, with x only at local window open, fresh b per candidate, exact retries cached/no recompute, 16 live candidates, network jitter; document non-constant-time limitation and add a hard per-window expensive-kex computation cap. Assess whether this is acceptable against a hostile TLS edge and public callers, whether timing across fresh b can enable offline code validation, and exact safeguards/cap/tests. Recommend a decision; no edits.","teammate_id":"srp-runtime-fable-1@session-db223e0d","agent_id":"srp-runtime-fable-1@session-db223e0d","agent_type":"architect-fable","model":"fable","name":"srp-runtime-fable-1","color":"cyan","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-db223e0d","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5d59e6a-a6f2-49ee-9b99-74645aec5105","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"7426ad77-8fb9-4951-86de-d11241289e5f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Design secure short-code pairing","description":"Have Fable architecture agents independently assess and challenge a secure remote short-code pairing design across desktop host-service, Android phone, Cloudflare Access, and the existing protocol. Produce a concrete implementation plan that removes offline code guessing.","activeForm":"Designing secure short-code pairing","status":"completed","blocks":["3","2"],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Implement desktop pairing protocol","description":"Use an Opus agent to implement the approved secure pairing protocol in the fork worktree, preserving fail-loud behavior, API-boundary validation, feature markers, and tests.","activeForm":"Implementing desktop pairing protocol","owner":"desktop-srp-opus","status":"completed","blocks":["4"],"blockedBy":["1"]},{"id":"3","subject":"Implement companion pairing protocol","description":"Use an Opus agent to implement the matching secure pairing protocol in the Android companion repository, with frozen cross-runtime vectors and phone UI/error handling.","activeForm":"Implementing companion pairing protocol","owner":"companion-srp-opus","status":"completed","blocks":["4"],"blockedBy":["1"]},{"id":"4","subject":"Review and simplify pairing changes","description":"Run required simplify workflow after production edits, then Fable/Opus adversarial review of both repositories. Fix every confirmed issue and rerun tests.","activeForm":"Reviewing and simplifying pairing changes","status":"in_progress","blocks":["5"],"blockedBy":["2","3"]},{"id":"5","subject":"Ship and verify companion pairing","description":"Commit and push both repositories, configure the Cloudflare pairing route and credentials, run the official Windows ARM64 build, build/install phone and watch apps, complete pairing, and verify named alerts/retraction/one-buzz end to end.","activ