{"parentUuid":"426cc585-7795-4a1a-aae1-88465eafac66","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_0d8652ea11fbb44c016a8260aa30788191840229dbeaf6fe7d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":165376,"output_tokens":627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_iVGUOiGMZCdkYBpFbFYtfBjL","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"desktop-srp-opus","summary":"Implement final BigInt safeguard ruling","message":"Final Fable ruling converged: implement pure BigInt fixed-4-bit-window secret modpow; NO native DH, worker, cached crypto object, exponent blinding, or response jitter. Exact requirements:\n- fixed 64 nibbles over a zero-padded 32-byte exponent; always 4 squarings + 1 multiply per window; 16-entry table; table[0]=N+1n (full-width representative of 1) so zero nibbles are not a cheap multiply. Use for g^x and both b exponentiations. Keep plain srpModPow only for public u.\n- fresh one-use b and exact retry cache unchanged.\n- RemotePairingSessionState monotone MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW=64 counter, charged immediately before a genuinely new srpServerHandshake; cached exact retries, refused rewrites, begin floods, confirms do not charge. 65th -> 429 pair_rate_limited + loud warn. Counter never evicted/reset within window.\n- Delete nativeModPow/createDiffieHellman entirely. Rewrite honest-limit/security comments.\n- Deterministic tests: fixed-window equals naive on production + RFC groups/random/single-bit/zero-nibble exponents; Appendix B through fixed path; injectable operation counter proves identical square/multiply counts for low/high Hamming weights; table[0] full-width/correct; 64 cap, 65th refusal, cached retry after cap, confirm after cap, refused rewrite free; static no createDiffieHellman regression if appropriate. No wall-clock timing assertions.\nRationale: x is local-before-window and fixed-window already removes count leakage, so 100-250ms blinding adds no practical remote protection; jitter adds complexity and carries no security claim. Finish all remaining Phase 2 items/gates and report.","type":"message","recipient":"desktop-srp-opus","content":"Final Fable ruling converged: implement pure BigI…"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5cdb17f9-2993-44a7-8c0a-aeda9918bebb","timestamp":"2026-08-17T01:15:40.405Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
