whose user text is \"Pairing failed to verify. Nothing was stored.\" — the documented deliberate unnamed-failure bucket per `RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:17-18`, mirroring pre-existing `pairFromQr` at lines 922-924. Not a violation.\n- **FEATURES.md marker discipline** (fork `AGENTS.md`, \"add a marker row here in the same commit\") — feature row plus 7 fenced-block entries added; `(REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING)` verified literally present in all 7 named paths (`pairing.ts` 27, `http.ts` 10, `config.ts` 10, `index.ts` 6, `srp.ts` 1, `trpc/router/companion/companion.ts` 3, `PairDeviceDialog.tsx` 1). `scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` will pass.\n- **Test co-location + runner** — `srp.test.ts` / `remote-pairing.test.ts` sit beside their sources in the flat `packages/host-service/src/companion/` layout and import `bun:test`, matching all 20+ sibling tests. Kotlin tests mirror their package paths under `src/test/java/`.\n- **Package manager / Next.js proxy.ts / drizzle** — no npm/yarn/pnpm invocation, no `middleware.ts`, nothing under `packages/db/drizzle/`.\n- **Gradle version catalog** — `bouncycastle = \"1.85.2\"` added to `[versions]` with resolution date and consumed via `libs.bouncycastle.bcprov`, matching the file's stated convention.\n- **Plan/doc placement** — no `*_PLAN.md` added; existing ones are in `docs/` and `plans/done/`.\n- **Fork footguns** — no `screenReaderMode`, no new sync fs on the desktop main-thread startup path (the one `existsSync` is in host-service `config.ts`, a separate process, matching the pre-existing `readJsonFile`), no `.github/workflows` changes, no agent-hook `.sh` edits.\n\n**Verdict: SHIP** (Conventions angle only — the single finding is MINOR and non-blocking).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>112679</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>55</tool_uses><duration_ms>307304</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T02:09:08.531Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a22f69ede33f6ccf8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_zCE9V3s5gLcebRYuAfRlJKv9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a22f69ede33f6ccf8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace pairing across files\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Bash unusable this session (shell init syntax error) — no `git`, `bun test`, `tsc`, or gradle runs. Findings from Read/Grep tracing plus the materialized diffs.\n\n```\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts:1215\nDefect: SRP candidate is pinned to the CF-Connecting-IP of its `begin` request for its whole life, but the remote flow is three separate HTTP connections from a mobile client.\nFailure: Phone POSTs `/v1/pair/begin` over Wi-Fi (or a CGNAT pool address), Wi-Fi drops / carrier reassigns the pool IP before `/v1/pair/kex` or `/v1/pair/confirm`. `assertCandidateSource` → `refuseCandidateRewrite` → 400 `pair_wrong_peer`. Phone maps it (RemotePairingHandshake.kt:382 → RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:30) to `PairingError.WRONG_PEER`, text \"Something else answered instead of the desktop. Refused.\" — an MITM accusation for an ordinary handoff. Retry mints a new deviceId, re-charges `MAX_KEX_PER_SOURCE`, and the exact network the code flow exists to serve (mobile data) is the one that hits it.\nFix: Bind the candidate to the deviceId only, or admit a source change on a candidate that has not yet completed kex; if the binding stays, map it to a distinct wire code so the phone can say \"your network changed, try again\" instead of WRONG_PEER.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\build.gradle.kts:43\nDefect: `bcprov-jdk18on` added to a module consumed by a release build with `isMinifyEnabled = true`, and no `-dontwarn`/keep rules were added anywhere.\nFailure: `app-phone/build.gradle.kts:50` enables R8; bcprov-jdk18on carries references to classes absent on Android (`javax.naming.*`, `java.awt.*`, `java.lang.management.*` from its JCE/PKIX halves) and ships no consumer-proguard rules. R8 treats missing classes as build errors, so `assembleRelease` fails with \"Missing class …(referenced from: org.bouncycastle…)\". `app-phone/proguard-rules.pro` (13 lines) and `core/consumer-rules.pro` (17 lines) contain no BC entry. Debug builds pass, so this surfaces only when the release APK is cut. Not executed — gradle unavailable this session.\nFix: Add `-dontwarn org.bouncycastle.**` plus the specific missing-class suppressions to `core/consumer-rules.pro`, and run one release assemble before merge.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\PairingCode.kt:20\nDefect: `digitsOrNull`/`takeDigits` accept Unicode digits via `Char.isDigit()`, but `passwordBytes` (line 46) encodes `US_ASCII`.\nFailure: User on a Devanagari/Arabic-Indic IME (or pasting from an app that normalises to them) enters `१२३४५६७८`. `isDigit()` accepts all 8 → `digitsOrNull` returns them → `passwordBytes` encodes US_ASCII → every char becomes `0x3F` `?`. SRP `x` is computed over `\"sc/v3 remote-pair:????????\"`, `macPhone` fails, desktop returns 401 `pair_code_wrong`. UI shows the correct-looking digits and says \"Check the code and type it again\"; three tries burn the 120 s window. Same asymmetry on the desktop, which mints ASCII only.\nFix: Filter on `it in '0'..'9'` in both `digitsOrNull` and `takeDigits`, and fail loud on any non-ASCII digit rather than silently substituting.\n\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt:232\nDefect: Every `EnvelopeException` from opening the step-4 body is reported as `CODE_WRONG` (\"type it again\"), but by the time that body exists the desktop has already verified `macPhone`, persisted the device record and consumed the window.\nFailure: Any AAD/envelope drift — e.g. `CompanionConstants.PROTOCOL_CURRENT` moving off the desktop's frozen `PROTOCOL_VERSION_AT_PAIRING = 1` (pairing.ts:261), or an edge that alters the `application/octet-stream` body — makes `SealedEnvelope.open` fail on every remote pairing. Phone tells the user \"That code wasn't accepted… type it again\"; the retype hits a consumed window (404 → WINDOW_CLOSED) and can never succeed, while the desktop holds a paired device record and a stored key the phone does not have. `pairedDeviceCount()` counts the phantom. This is the exact failure the desktop's own AAD note (pairing.ts:1626-1630) records from an earlier revision, reintroduced with a message that points the user at the wrong thing.\nFix: Distinguish \"the desktop accepted us but its reply would not open\" from \"the code was wrong\" — a dedicated failure (nothing to retype, re-pair from the desktop) and, on the desktop side, a way to reap a record whose confirm response was never consumed.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt:113\nDefect: The typed 8-digit code is held in `rememberSaveable`, so it is written into the Activity saved-instance-state Bundle.\nFailure: User types the code, backgrounds the app. Android serialises the Bundle into the system's saved task state, which survives process death and can be written to disk for the task record. The secret the desktop treats as never-persisted (pairing.ts:484-489, \"MUST NOT be logged, persisted…\") then outlives its 120 s window in system storage, retrievable well after the window closed. `submittedAtMs` on line 119 leaks the attempt timing the same way.\nFix: Hold `digits` in plain `remember` (accepting re-entry after process death) or in a ViewModel field that is cleared on `onCleared`, and drop it from saved state.\n\n[MINOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\http.ts:886\nDefect: `readBoundedBody` throws `CleartextError`, so oversized/invalid bodies on the public pairing host answer with the MAIN bridge's error envelope, not the pairing hop's `{code}` shape that `pairingJsonResponse` (line 698) claims to be the only one.\nFailure: A phone (or scanner) POSTs &gt;4 KiB or a non-numeric `content-length` to `/v1/pair/kex`. Response is `{code:\"body_too_large\", serverTimeMs, retryAfterMs}` with 413. `RemotePairingHandshake.FAILURE_BY_WIRE` has no `body_too_large` and `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` has no 413, so it falls through to the default `PairingFailure.BAD_MAC` → \"Pairing failed to verify. Nothing was stored.\" Also publishes the authenticated surface's error vocabulary and clock on the unauthenticated public host.\nFix: Catch `CleartextError` inside `handleRemotePairRequest` and re-emit through `pairingErrorResponse` with a `PairingErrorCode`, so the pairing hop has exactly one response shape.\n```\n\nChecked and clean: SRP-6a arithmetic agreement desktop↔BouncyCastle (`k`, `x`, `u` padded-pair hashing, `S = (A·v^u)^b` vs `(B−k·v)^(a+u·x)`, PAD width 384 both sides); HKDF salt prefixes, info labels and the 825-byte `sc/v3-srp` transcript byte-for-byte across repos; wire JSON field names/versions (`v:2`, `A`/`B` `@SerialName`, begin/kex/confirm shapes); error-code vocabulary desktop `PairingErrorCode` ↔ Kotlin `PairingFailure.wire`; host-isolation gate (`routeByHost`, comma/port/root-dot normalisation, pair-paths-404-on-main and inverse, `publicPairHost === null` fail-closed, the `PAIRING_PUBLIC_HOST !== BRIDGE_PUBLIC_HOST` load-time assert); one-window-process-wide slot and its teardown hook; single-use/burn/consumed ordering and the synchronous prefix that makes concurrent confirms safe; key zeroization paths (`wipeAllPairingKeys`, `zeroKexSession`, eviction, `completePairing` finally); counter-0 nonce reservation; QR/LAN path bytes unchanged; tRPC boundary returning `{code, expiresAtMs}` explicitly rather than through the secret-omitting `toJSON`.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>212614</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>63</tool_uses><duration_ms>663737</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
