airDeviceDialog/components/ModeToggle/`. Cost: `PairDeviceDialog.tsx` now holds three components (`PairDeviceDialog`, `ModeToggle`, `PairingFlow`), so `ModeToggle` cannot be unit-tested or imported without pulling in the whole pairing-flow module — its module-level `pairingOperations` promise queue and the `getHostServiceClientByUrl` import — and there is no co-located test file for the next contributor to extend.\",\n    \"caveat\": \"`PairingFlow` (line 216) was already inline before this change, so the file was already non-conforming. This is an addition to an existing deviation, not a new one — hence MINOR.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nCoverage: `any`/type-safety, validate-at-API-boundaries, fail-fast/no-masking-defaults, FEATURES.md marker discipline (all 7 marker paths verified present), test co-location + `bun:test` runner, package manager / `proxy.ts` / drizzle, Gradle version catalog, plan-doc placement, fork footguns (`screenReaderMode`, main-thread sync fs, `.github/workflows`, agent-hook `.sh`) — all clean. Companion repo has no root `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`; only user-level `C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\CLAUDE.md` governs it, no violation found there.\n\n**Verdict: SHIP** (Conventions angle only).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>114473</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>55</tool_uses><duration_ms>436113</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
