ately before srpServerHandshake (pairing.ts:239-255, 1057), with exact-retry short-circuit; MAC grinding is bounded per-window by confirmAttempts(5)/PAIRING_MAX_BAD_MACS(3); memory is bounded by MAX_KEX_SESSIONS=16 evict-with-zeroing. Log-spam half of the claim is inverted: the console.warn fires only on refusal at cap, so the refund produces FEWER warn lines, not unbounded ones. Residual exposure is cheap request handling (&lt;=4 KiB body, JSON parse, map lookups) inside a 120 s human-opened window, which the module header already declares an accepted limitation ('A distributed flood can still make this process busy'), and the refund itself is documented as deliberate at pairing.ts:1296-1299. Verified by reading pairing.ts (1275-1347, 210-363, 960-1140, 2270-2373) and http.ts (713-893); no independent global request counter exists, which is the one real gap, but it does not reach a shipping defect.\"}</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>51679</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>10</tool_uses><duration_ms>115915</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
