le the LAN window is still live and 0.0.0.0:47611 still bound; and the stop() teardown step `close: () =&gt; state?.pairing?.close()` (index.ts:1142) also no-ops, leaving a listening pairing socket plus its timer alive past bridge stop, and pairing.ts's module-level `openWindow` non-null so a restarted bridge's first openPairing also refuses until the 120s timer fires. companion.ts's `trackedPairingWindow` (companion.ts:199, 422, 461, 482, 498) is read-only in pairingState and never closes the handle, so it is not a mitigating path. Nothing catches, retries, or restores the memo; nothing else can close the window early.\"}</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>91911</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>161030</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
