{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-17T02:41:24.741Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0ebd5c293a60c23d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a0ebd5c293a60c23d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify SRP constant recomputation\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>```json\n{\n  \"candidate\": \"srp.ts:505 — srpComputeK + generator fixed-window table rebuilt per server handshake\",\n  \"verdict\": \"REFUTED\",\n  \"severity\": \"NONE\",\n  \"classification\": \"negligible pure micro-optimization\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"srp\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\\\packages\\\\host-service\\\\src\\\\companion\\\\srp.ts\",\n    \"pairing\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\\\packages\\\\host-service\\\\src\\\\companion\\\\pairing.ts\"\n  },\n  \"call_paths_verified\": [\n    \"pairing.ts:1029 handleRemoteKex -&gt; srpServerHandshake (srp.ts:480). Only production caller. Reached only after: window open, wire version, source key, pid match, candidate exists, source match, canonical A, exact-retry short-circuit (srp.ts:1043-1055), chargeKexComputation (pairing.ts:1057).\",\n    \"srpServerHandshake:505 srpComputeK -&gt; 2x srpPad(384B) + 1 SHA-256 over 768 bytes. Once per handshake.\",\n    \"srpServerHandshake:508 srpSecretModPow(g, b) -&gt; builds table[2..15] = 14 modmuls over constant g.\",\n    \"srpServerHandshake:525 srpSecretModPow(base=A*v^u, b) -&gt; builds 14-modmul table over a PER-CANDIDATE base. Not memoizable, not part of the claim.\",\n    \"pairing.ts:2157 openRemotePairing -&gt; srpComputeVerifier -&gt; srpSecretModPow(g, x): one more g-table, once per 120s window.\"\n  ],\n  \"cost_arithmetic\": {\n    \"per_handshake_total_modmuls\": \"~1050 (2 secret ladders = 2 x 320 = 640; srpModPow(v,u) with 256-bit u ~ 384; two 14-mul tables = 28)\",\n    \"claimed_redundant_work_per_handshake\": \"14 modmuls (g table) + 1 SHA-256 = ~1.3% of one handshake\",\n    \"claimed_900_figure\": \"CORRECT ARITHMETIC, WRONG FRAMING: 14 x MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW(64, pairing.ts:255) = 896. That is a per-WINDOW worst case under a full flood, not per handshake.\",\n    \"wall_clock\": \"Module's own measured figure (srp.ts:307): ~2.8-3.3 ms per ladder (320 modmuls) =&gt; ~9-10 us/modmul; ~10 ms per full kex. Redundant g table = ~0.13 ms/handshake, ~8.4 ms across an entire flooded 120 s window against ~640 ms of legitimately-charged exponentiation. srpComputeK is ~2 us (one SHA-256 over 768 B).\",\n    \"real_phone_path\": \"exactly 1 charged derivation per window =&gt; total saving ~0.13 ms per pairing.\"\n  },\n  \"memoization_assessment\": {\n    \"safe\": \"For the g table and k: yes in principle — g, N, k and g^i mod N are all public constants of the group, and the table build is exponent-independent so caching changes no timing property the module claims (srp.ts:284-320 fixes the OPERATION SEQUENCE, not table setup).\",\n    \"worthwhile\": \"No. ~1.3% of one handshake, ~1.3% of a flood window's CPU. It does not move any bound: MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW=64 and REMOTE_PAIR_REQUESTS_PER_SOURCE already cap main-thread work, and the cap is set by the 640-modmul ladders, not by table setup.\",\n    \"costs_introduced\": [\n      \"Module-level mutable cache contradicts the stated invariant 'this module holds no state / is arithmetic' (srp.ts:23, srp.ts:474); today the only module state is the test-only op counter.\",\n      \"A naive base-keyed memo in srpSecretModPow would also cache the per-candidate A*v^u base — an attacker-controlled, unbounded cache key set inside a 120 s flood window, i.e. a real memory-growth footgun traded for a 1.3% CPU win.\",\n      \"Caching k on the group object weakens the current property that SrpGroup is frozen pure data shared with the test-only 1024/SHA-1 profile.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"clean_areas_checked\": \"SRP handshake call path and its guards (window/version/source/pid/candidate/retry/A-range), MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW monotone charging, table-build cost vs ladder cost, k derivation cost, per-candidate base non-memoizability, timing-shape invariants of srpSecretModPow, state/mutability invariants of srp.ts.\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"DROP — do not report. Pure micro-optimization worth ~0.13 ms per pairing (~1.3% of one kex); implementing it adds module state and an attacker-keyed cache risk for no bound-moving gain.\",\n  \"final\": \"SHIP\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>87855</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>250179</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
