eal residual defect is narrower: ProtocolException is genuinely reachable and mislabelled as PairingError.BAD_MAC. Sources: CompanionJson.decodeFromBytes on begin/kex bodies (RemotePairingHandshake.kt:307-309), Base64Url.decode length mismatch (:151-152, :189, :239), empty Access client secret (:247), non-TLS/unparsable origin (:420, :429), and PairingClient.kt:240 'paired-device record disappeared immediately after being written'. That last one is the worst case: pairing was already persisted by store.persistPairing, yet UI reports BAD_MAC ('codes did not match / nothing stored') -&gt; user-visible state contradicts secure-store state and user retries a code path that cannot succeed. Mitigating: identical pattern already exists at pairFromQr (:922-926), so it is codebase convention, not a new divergence; failure is loud in logcat. Fix (not applied): add an explicit `catch (e: ProtocolException)` mapping to a distinct PairingError (e.g. VERSION_UNSUPPORTED/INTERNAL) before the CompanionException arm, and make PairingClient.kt:240 surface a store-inconsistency error rather than fall into BAD_MAC.\",\n  \"verified_by\": [\n    \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\superset-companion\\\\app-phone\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\family\\\\khaira\\\\supersetcompanion\\\\phone\\\\data\\\\BridgeCompanionRepository.kt:948-994\",\n    \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\superset-companion\\\\core\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\family\\\\khaira\\\\supersetcompanion\\\\core\\\\CompanionException.kt:14-209\",\n    \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\superset-companion\\\\core\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\family\\\\khaira\\\\supersetcompanion\\\\core\\\\pairing\\\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt:110-336\",\n    \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\superset-companion\\\\core\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\family\\\\khaira\\\\supersetcompanion\\\\core\\\\pairing\\\\PairingClient.kt:218-241\",\n    \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\superset-companion\\\\app-phone\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\family\\\\khaira\\\\supersetcompanion\\\\phone\\\\data\\\\RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:20-37\"\n  ],\n  \"clean_areas\": \"typed catch ordering (subclass-before-base, compiles), PairingException-&gt;PairingError mapping exhaustive, key zeroization in handshake finally, timeout handling, no state mutation before failure return\",\n  \"ship_verdict\": \"SHIP\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>39893</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>7</tool_uses><duration_ms>250870</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
