: \"evictOldestKexSessionsIfFull:1341-1342\", \"effect\": \"zeroKexSession then Map.delete — nulled entry unreachable\"},\n    {\"site\": \"clearKexSessions:888-893\", \"effect\": \"zeroKexSession then Map.clear — nulled entries unreachable\"}\n  ],\n  \"reachability_of_line_1051\": {\n    \"reachable\": false,\n    \"reasoning\": \"Only two paths leave keys=null with clientPublic!=null. (a) eviction/clear: entry is removed from state.kexSessions in the same statement pair, so requireRemoteCandidate can never return it. (b) successful confirm: line 1521 nulls keys, then completePairing-&gt;sealPairedResponse sets state.consumed=true at 1569 with NO await between 1521 and 1569 (hmacSha256 at 1544 is sync; first await is deps.onPaired at 1572), so single-threaded JS cannot interleave a kex; any later handleRemoteKex dies at assertWindowOpen (1034) before reaching 1051. Confirmed unreachable.\"\n  },\n  \"claim_accuracy\": {\n    \"co_nullable_and_always_written_together\": \"PARTIAL — true on the write-to-non-null path only. keys is independently nulled at 1521 and 884, so the doc comment at 396-397 ('nullable TOGETHER and are only ever written together') is already inaccurate; the real state machine is begun | kexed | spent, not begun | kexed.\",\n    \"repeated_unreachable_500_checks\": \"OVERSTATED — exactly ONE unreachable check exists (1051, 500 'unknown'). The second narrowing site (handleRemoteConfirm 1479-1488) is genuinely REACHABLE (confirm sent before kex → clientPublic null) and returns 400 pair_wrong_peer, which is correct behaviour, not dead code.\",\n    \"union_would_enforce_invariant\": \"PARTIAL — a discriminated union removes 1051 only if the post-confirm/post-wipe state is modelled as a third variant (or the entry is deleted at 1521/884 instead of nulled). A plain begun|kexed union is not a drop-in; it would also require replacing the Map entry object at kex instead of in-place mutation, and widening the outer KexSession union that LanKexSession shares.\"\n  },\n  \"observable_maintenance_risk\": {\n    \"present\": true,\n    \"magnitude\": \"low\",\n    \"detail\": \"Invariant is enforced by convention (one contiguous 3-line assignment) plus a prose comment, not by types. A future edit that assigns clientPublic before deriving keys resurrects the exact state the 1051 check guards — the retry short-circuit would hand back a B with no confirmable keys. The 500 is a loud fail-fast, consistent with repo rules, and masks nothing today.\"\n  },\n  \"no_bug_found\": true,\n  \"checked_clean\": [\n    \"kex retry short-circuit constant-time A comparison (1043-1054)\",\n    \"commit-all-three ordering vs SrpError/finally zero(privateExponent) (1057-1097)\",\n    \"confirm narrowing + transcript field sourcing (1479-1501)\",\n    \"keys lifetime: wipeAllPairingKeys on all exit paths (874-893, 1341, 1555)\",\n    \"consumed-window atomicity across await boundary (1521 -&gt; 1569)\"\n  ],\n  \"recommended_disposition\": \"Report as MINOR type-modelling note; do not block. If addressed, delete the Map entry (or move to a spent variant) at 1521/884 rather than nulling keys, and only then collapse 1051.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>41942</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>264151</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
