theoretical gap: if SRP6Client.init() threw before generateClientCredentials, password would escape unwiped — init only assigns fields (N, g, digest, random) and cannot realistically throw; negligible, not a finding. Threat/lifetime contract also already documented: the un-wipeable String source is an accepted, bounded limit (120-second pairing window), so heap residue of the low-entropy code is explicitly in-scope-accepted, not an oversight.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>29124</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>27701</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
