es with identical non-zeroizing handling. (3) The file's discipline (ConstantTime.kt:16-22 doc, handshake lines 250/260-261) is explicitly scoped to key material 'as soon as it is dead' — sharedSecret, prk, confirm keys, MACs, transcript — all of which are wiped; the confirm plaintext is neither key material nor dead at return. (4) Observability requires heap-dump/memory-disclosure on the device, where the surviving Strings expose the same secret anyway. Reporting it would be a no-risk-reduction nit and would need SealedTransport plus the whole String-based decode path changed to a byte-oriented secret type to mean anything.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>37184</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>50606</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
