s with identical non-zeroizing handling. (3) The file's discipline (ConstantTime.kt:16-22 doc, handshake lines 250/260-261) is explicitly scoped to key material 'as soon as it is dead' — sharedSecret, prk, confirm keys, MACs, transcript — all of which are wiped; the confirm plaintext is neither key material nor dead at return. (4) Observability requires heap-dump/memory-disclosure on the device, where the surviving Strings expose the same secret anyway. Reporting it would be a no-risk-reduction nit and would need SealedTransport plus the whole String-based decode path changed to a byte-oriented secret type to mean anything.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>37184</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>50606</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T02:42:06.805Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a11f712477b4a5a24</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_TgJaAzavM6omwoiJRreWO8Zi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a11f712477b4a5a24.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify pairing kind typing\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>```json\n{\n  \"candidate\": \"PAIRING_MODES `satisfies` constraint types `pairingKind` as bare `string` instead of host `PairingKind`, so a rename/typo compiles and the poll ignores every verdict\",\n  \"verdict\": \"PLAUSIBLE\",\n  \"severity\": \"MINOR\",\n  \"live_bug\": false,\n  \"file\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\Code Projects\\\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\\\apps\\\\desktop\\\\src\\\\renderer\\\\components\\\\PairDeviceDialog\\\\PairDeviceDialog.tsx\",\n  \"lines\": \"103-120, 363\",\n  \"verified\": {\n    \"inferred_types\": \"`as const satisfies Record&lt;PairingMode, {label: string; pairingKind: string; description: string}&gt;` — `as const` preserves literals, so `PAIRING_MODES.qr.pairingKind` infers `\\\"lan\\\"`, `.code` infers `\\\"remote\\\"`. The `string` constraint widens nothing at the use site; it only removes the compile-time check that the literals are members of the host union. Comparison at line 363 (`state.pairingKind !== PAIRING_MODES[mode].pairingKind`) is `\\\"lan\\\"|\\\"remote\\\"` vs `\\\"lan\\\"|\\\"remote\\\"` today — legal, no TS2367.\",\n    \"typo_would_compile\": \"Confirmed by TS rules, not run: with one entry typo'd (e.g. `\\\"lann\\\"`), the satisfies constraint accepts it (assignable to `string`), and line 363 still compares `\\\"lan\\\"|\\\"remote\\\"` against `\\\"lann\\\"|\\\"remote\\\"` — overlap on `\\\"remote\\\"` means TS2367 does NOT fire. Only a BOTH-entries typo (zero overlap) errors. So the candidate's premise holds: single-site drift is silent.\",\n    \"concrete_drift_today\": \"NONE. Host `PairingKind = \\\"lan\\\" | \\\"remote\\\"` at packages\\\\host-service\\\\src\\\\companion\\\\pairing.ts:521; handles are constructed with `kind: \\\"lan\\\"` (pairing.ts:1999, 2015) and `kind: \\\"remote\\\"` (pairing.ts:2184, 2200); `pairingState` returns `pairingKind = handle.kind` (companion.ts:429). Renderer literals match exactly. No live mismatch.\",\n    \"runtime_consequence_if_drifted\": \"Worse than the candidate states. On mismatch, line 363 returns early on EVERY poll, so `closed-early`/`expired` are never applied. The local countdown (lines 302-316) sets `{kind:\\\"closing\\\"}` at `left &lt;= 0`, and `trackedExpiresAtMs` keeps polling in `closing` — the dialog is stuck on the 'Finishing up…' spinner permanently (lines 423-430), never reaching the expired/closed-early screens with their 'Show a new code' button. Not merely 'ignored until expiry' — a permanent hang requiring dialog close.\",\n    \"import_availability\": \"The candidate's implied fix (`import type { PairingKind }`) is NOT directly available. `packages/host-service/package.json` exports no `./companion` subpath (`.`, `./db`, `./events`, `./git`, `./tunnel`, `./trpc`, `./host-worker`, `./terminal-env`, `./session-project`, `./settings`, `./attachments`, `./router`), and `src/index.ts` does not re-export `PairingKind` (it exports `AppRouter` only, line 29). Renderer gets types via `import type { AppRouter } from \\\"@superset/host-service\\\"` (renderer\\\\lib\\\\host-service-client.ts:1), so the union IS reachable structurally by derivation from the router return type, or the type could be added to the root export.\",\n    \"tests\": \"No test file exists for PairDeviceDialog (dir contains only PairDeviceDialog.tsx, components/QrCode, utils/encodeQrMatrix). Repo-wide, `pairingKind` appears in exactly 2 files (the component and companion.ts) — nothing asserts the qr-&gt;lan / code-&gt;remote mapping. Drift is caught only by manual e2e.\",\n    \"ci_gate_reality\": \"Fork CI runs no typecheck gate (AGENTS.md: 'No build-time type/test gate except (REFERR-GATE)'), so even a hard type error here would not fail the nightly. Value of the tighter constraint is local `bun run typecheck` / review time, not CI.\"\n  },\n  \"why_not_higher\": \"Current literals are provably correct against the host union, no test or caller depends on the weak constraint, and nothing misbehaves at runtime today. This is latent hardening against a future rename, not a defect in the change under review.\",\n  \"recommended_fix_described\": \"Constrain the table against the host's own union rather than `string`: either add `export type { PairingKind } from \\\"./companion/pairing\\\"` to packages\\\\host-service\\\\src\\\\index.ts and use it in the `satisfies` Record, or derive it locally from the router type (e.g. `Extract&lt;Awaited&lt;ReturnType&lt;HostServiceClient[\\\"companion\\\"][\\\"pairingState\\\"][\\\"query\\\"]&gt;&gt;, { pairingKind: string }&gt;[\\\"pairingKind\\\"]`). Separately worth considering: make the line-363 mismatch fail loud (set a `failed` phase) instead of silently returning, so a future kind rename surfaces as an error rather than an eternal 'Finishing up…' spinner.\",\n  \"clean_areas_checked\": \"host `PairingKind` definition and every construction site; `pairingState` return shape and `observedClosedAtMs` memoisation; renderer poll early-return chain (none/expiry-mismatch/kind-mismatch/open); countdown -&gt; closing handover; package export map and renderer import path; test coverage for the mapping.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>58755</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>17</tool_uses><duration_ms>322333</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T02:42:11.459Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4c830d125713f473</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a4c830d125713f473.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify byte concat duplication\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>```json\n{\n  \"candidate\": \"pairing.ts:783 buildHkdfSalt / IKM build / concatFixed duplicate crypto.ts concatBytes + hkdfInfoWithSuffix (drift/offset risk)\",\n  \"verdict\": \"REJECT\",\n  \"severity\": \"none\",\n  \"reason\": \"No defect. All three hand-rolled concatenations are correct: buildHkdfSalt (pairing.ts:783-792) allocates exactly prefix.length + pairSalt.length and writes at 0 and prefix.length; the IKM build (pairing.ts:726-728) allocates z.length + pairingCode.length with matching offsets; concatFixed (pairing.ts:664-678) sizes from a caller-supplied expectedBytes, and out.set() throws RangeError on overflow while a short total throws PairingError(500) — it is STRICTER than crypto.ts concatBytes (crypto.ts:573), which sums lengths and can never assert a total. Reuse is not appropriate either: crypto.ts concatBytes is module-private (not exported; only exported concat-shaped helper is hkdfInfoWithSuffix), so 'reuse' means widening crypto.ts's public surface across the module boundary. hkdfInfoWithSuffix is semantically an HKDF *info* builder (utf8 label || raw id suffixes, pinned by the INTEROP NOTE at crypto.ts:15-43 and used at pairing.ts:810, keys.ts:2281, remote-pairing.test.ts:326); an HKDF-Extract *salt* (ascii prefix || pairSalt) is a different protocol field, and routing it through the info builder would couple two byte-frozen wire constructions that must be free to change independently. Substituting the unasserted concatBytes for concatFixed would also delete the 117-byte / 825-byte transcript total check that the golden vectors rely on — a net loss of safety. Real duplication is ~6 lines of trivially-verified offset arithmetic against a real cross-boundary coupling and a lost invariant; maintenance cost is negligible.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>68364</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>327057</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
