 1041). decodeExact: 4 (pPub 920, deviceId 1163, macPhone 1418, macPhone 1492)\"\n  },\n  \"duplication_is_real\": true,\n  \"pure_preference_refuted\": true,\n  \"maintenance_cost_concrete\": [\n    \"Strictness edits that do NOT live inside base64UrlDecode land in one copy only: e.g. a pre-decode length cap on the raw string, an all-zero/low-entropy reject, a max-input guard against decode DoS, or switching the width check to a range check. handleRemoteKex validates A via decodeClientPublic (1041) and macPhone via decodeExact (1492) inside the SAME pairing exchange, so a one-sided edit yields two different accept/reject surfaces within one handshake.\",\n    \"Error-code drift is the only semantic difference and it is expressed by 6 scattered literals across the two functions rather than one parameter; adding a third code-specific field means a third near-identical copy.\",\n    \"PairingErrorCode (types.ts:433) is a closed union containing both 'unknown' and 'pair_bad_key_agreement', so parameterization is fully type-safe with no widening.\"\n  ],\n  \"simpler_alternative\": {\n    \"shape\": \"function decodeExact(value: unknown, expected: number, code: PairingErrorCode = \\\"unknown\\\"): Uint8Array — single body, throw new PairingError(400, code) at all three gates\",\n    \"call_site\": \"const clientPublic = decodeExact(request.A, SRP_3072_SHA256.widthBytes, \\\"pair_bad_key_agreement\\\");\",\n    \"net\": \"deletes ~15 lines and 6 error literals; keeps the existing doc comment as a call-site note\",\n    \"behavior_change\": \"none — byte-for-byte identical status/code/return for every input\"\n  },\n  \"counterarguments_considered\": [\n    \"Named wrapper aids readability at 1041 — real but preserved by a named const or a 2-line wrapper delegating to the parameterized helper; the current version duplicates the BODY, not just the name.\",\n    \"Doc block justifies the distinct code — justification survives parameterization unchanged.\",\n    \"Out-of-range A is NOT checked here (it is mapped to the same code by the SRP derive catch at 1060-1075), so the wrapper carries no extra validation the helper lacks.\"\n  ],\n  \"not_a_bug\": \"No correctness, security, or data-integrity defect. Divergence is latent, not present.\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"Report as MINOR; non-blocking.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>38304</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>10</tool_uses><duration_ms>341698</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T02:43:24.740Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>adaa91e71613bf277</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\adaa91e71613bf277.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"/code-review Review the complete uncommitted secu…\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts\",\n    \"line\": 2097,\n    \"summary\": \"The process-wide pairing-window slot is claimed only after the LAN listener awaits startup, allowing a concurrent remote open to be overwritten.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Two concurrent tRPC calls open LAN and remote pairing: LAN passes the empty-slot check and awaits server.listen; remote then claims the slot and returns a code; when LAN resumes it overwrites the slot. The displayed remote code receives only 404 responses, and Cancel targets the LAN window instead of the orphaned remote window.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": 1451,\n    \"summary\": \"Opening a second pairing window clears the bridge's only handle before the authoritative opener can reject the request.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"With a pairing window already live, a second open sets current.pairing to null and then pairing.ts throws the one-window error. closePairing and bridge shutdown subsequently see no handle, so the listener and window cannot be closed until the 120-second timer expires.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/superset-companion/core/src/main/java/family/khaira/supersetcompanion/core/pairing/PairingCode.kt\",\n    \"line\": 20,\n    \"summary\": \"The code parser accepts Unicode digits that the SRP password encoder silently replaces with ASCII question marks.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"An Arabic-Indic or Devanagari numeric keyboard enters eight visually valid digits. Char.isDigit accepts them, but US_ASCII encoding produces eight 0x3F bytes, so every SRP attempt fails as a wrong code and repeated attempts can burn the otherwise-correct pairing window.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts\",\n    \"line\": 1330,\n    \"summary\": \"Candidate-table eviction is treated as recoverable even though the Android handshake never automatically begins again.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Four attacker source addresses introduce sixteen candidates after the real phone's begin but before its kex. The phone's candidate is evicted, kex returns pair_wrong_peer, and Android terminates the attempt with a misleading WRONG_PEER error; repeated eviction can consume the phone's four introductions and deny the 120-second window.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts\",\n    \"line\": 1313,\n    \"summary\": \"Evicting the oldest source bucket refunds an exhausted source's per-window request allowance.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A caller exhausts its allowance from source X, cycles through more than 32 source addresses until X is evicted, then returns to X with a fresh counter and repeats. Global crypto and MAC limits remain, but the advertised per-source request bound no longer caps body reads, JSON parsing, map churn, or request volume during the window.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/superset-companion/core/src/main/java/family/khaira/supersetcompanion/core/pairing/RemotePairingHandshake.kt\",\n    \"line\": 232,\n    \"summary\": \"A failure to open the desktop's final sealed response is incorrectly reported as a mistyped code after the desktop has already accepted and stored the device.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"AAD drift, response corruption, or an envelope implementation mismatch causes EnvelopeException after the desktop verifies macPhone, persists the device, and consumes the window. The phone shows CODE_WRONG and asks for another entry into a closed window while the desktop retains a phantom paired record.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/superset-companion/app-phone/src/main/java/family/khaira/supersetcompanion/phone/data/BridgeCompanionRepository.kt\",\n    \"line\": 984,\n    \"summary\": \"Reachable protocol and post-storage consistency failures are collapsed into BAD_MAC even when no MAC failure occurred.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A malformed remote response, invalid decoded field, or a paired record disappearing immediately after persistence raises ProtocolException. The broad CompanionException catch reports BAD_MAC and tells the user verification failed or nothing was stored, potentially contradicting the secure store and sending the user down an ineffective code-retry path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/superset-companion/app-phone/src/main/java/family/khaira/supersetcompanion/phone/ui/pairing/PairingScreen.kt\",\n    \"line\": 320,\n    \"summary\": \"The phone labels a locally invented timeout as time remaining in the server-owned pairing window.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The desktop code has already been visible for 105 seconds when the user submits it on the phone. The UI displays about 119 seconds remaining and starts a fresh 120-second timeout even though the desktop closes the real window 15 seconds later.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts\",\n    \"line\": 38,\n    \"summary\": \"New security documentation claims the public pairing routes require a second Cloudflare Access identity that the implementation explicitly removed.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A maintainer auditing or extending the unauthenticated pairing surface reads the file-level contract and assumes Access authenticates all three pairing routes, although the real controls are only host isolation, SRP, an open window, and rate limits. Subsequent security changes can therefore be evaluated against a protection that does not exist.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts\",\n    \"line\": 885,\n    \"summary\": \"Oversized or malformed pairing bodies bypass the pairing response constructor and expose the main sealed-protocol error format.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A public pairing request with a non-numeric Content-Length or a body over 4 KiB raises CleartextError. The handler emits envelope_invalid or body_too_large with serverTimeMs and without the pairing constructor's no-store header, violating the pairing host's promised PairingErrorCode-only response contract.\"\n  }\n]</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>0</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>152</tool_uses><duration_ms>3043877</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
