exist. `ModeToggle` is used once, by `PairDeviceDialog`, so the rule places it at `PairDeviceDialog/components/ModeToggle/`. Cost: `PairDeviceDialog.tsx` now holds `PairDeviceDialog` + `ModeToggle` + `PairingFlow`, so `ModeToggle` cannot be unit-tested or imported without pulling in the whole pairing flow module (its module-level `pairingOperations` promise queue and `getHostServiceClientByUrl` import), and the next contributor extending the toggle has no co-located test file to add to.\n\n**Caveat on rank:** `PairingFlow` (line 216) was already inline pre-change, so the file was already non-conforming. This is an addition to an existing deviation, not a new one — hence MINOR, not MAJOR.\n\n## Checked and clean\n\n- **`any` / type safety** (AGENTS.md Agent Rule 1) — zero `: any`, `as any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, `biome-ignore` in added lines across both diffs and all untracked files.\n- **Validate at API boundaries** (user `CLAUDE.md` NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE 1) — the public unauthenticated pairing host validates before use: `classifyRequestHost`/`routeByHost` (host+method+path, `secure-pairing-desktop.diff:2284-2329`), bounded body read + `fatal: true` UTF-8 decode + object check before the `as RemotePair*Request` casts, then `assertWireVersion` / `assertSourceKey` / `parseKexMetadata` / `decodeClientPublic` inside `handleRemoteBegin`/`handleRemoteKex`. `openRemotePairing` uses `protectedProcedure`, matching sibling procedures.\n- **Fail fast / no masking defaults** (NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE 2; \"Do not catch unexpected errors just to hide them\", \"no sensible defaults for missing values\") — `loadPublicPairHost`, `requireString`, `requireEqual`, `resolveCompanionPaths` all throw with the offending file and key named. The two bare `catch {}` blocks (desktop diff 2501, 5732) convert malformed input into typed `PairingError`s, not silence. Kotlin `BridgeCompanionRepository.kt:984-987` catch-all logs at `Log.e` and surfaces `PairingError.BAD_MAC`, w