{"parentUuid":"7875b756-b57e-41ad-9121-384297cf8d82","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_02dd4a769161d400016a82ea9614b08191acfe74fe813d2da4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":183456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_pABopyPMp8s6ZcxFMReqhp0A","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"desktop-srp-opus","summary":"Verify and fix desktop review findings","message":"Lockstep /code-review returned desktop findings. Verify each against current post-simplify tree before editing; fix every confirmed item with regression tests, rerun full suite/gates, and report any false positive with concrete proof. Repo files only—do not inspect user shell/profile files.\n1) pairing.ts concurrent LAN open awaits listen before claiming process-wide slot; remote can claim then be overwritten. Make reservation/transition atomic, fail loud, clean reservation on listen failure.\n2) index.ts second open clears current.pairing before authoritative rejection, orphaning live handle. Preserve existing handle on rejected open; only replace after successful authoritative open.\n3) candidate-table eviction before phone kex yields pair_wrong_peer and Android has no automatic safe restart. Coordinate with companion agent on a bounded begin/kex restart or another deterministic recovery; preserve public-DoS honesty and no confirm retry.\n4) source-bucket eviction refunds per-source allowance; ensure a monotone per-window total request/body-parse bound and make documented bounds true without unbounded source memory. Coordinate exact wire behavior with companion if needed.\n5) http.ts file header still claims a second Access identity although public pair host removed it. Correct docs.\n6) oversized/malformed body CleartextError bypasses pairing response/no-store contract. Catch/map at pair-host boundary to closed pairing error shape with no-store; no main sealed-protocol codes.\n7) conventions: move newly added ModeToggle to PairDeviceDialog/components/ModeToggle/ModeToggle.tsx + index.ts per AGENTS.md, preserving ToggleGroup behavior.\nAlso re-verify confirm charging and all host isolation. Do not commit/push.","type":"message","recipient":"desktop-srp-opus","content":"Lockstep /code-review returned desktop findings. …"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"f8f7cb35-4cb2-431e-b15d-97740c3f5471","timestamp":"2026-08-17T11:04:43.994Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"f8f7cb35-4cb2-431e-b15d-97740c3f5471","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"resp_02dd4a769161d400016a82ea9614b08191acfe74fe813d2da4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"codex-gpt-5-6-sol","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":183456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_SrQI9sCWaeBuMDsMX0t8VvRe","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"companion-srp-opus","summary":"Verify and fix Android review findings","message":"Lockstep /code-review returned Android findings. Verify each against current post-simplify tree before editing; fix every confirmed item with regression tests/full aggregate, and report false positives with proof. Repo files only—do not inspect user shell/profile files.\n1) PairingCode accepts Unicode digits via Char.isDigit, then US_ASCII encodes them as '?'. Enforce/normalize the protocol's exact 8 ASCII digits at the earliest UI/core boundary so Unicode input never burns a window; test Arabic-Indic/Devanagari cases.\n2) final sealed-response open failure after desktop accepted/stored device is mapped CODE_WRONG. Wrong code cannot reach 200 sealed response; map to an honest protocol/verification state that tells user to reopen, not retry digits. Test response corruption/AAD drift.\n3) BridgeCompanionRepository broad CompanionException catch maps protocol/post-storage consistency failures to BAD_MAC. Preserve specific failure meaning and avoid claiming nothing stored when that may be false; add mapping tests.\n4) PairingScreen shows a locally started 120s countdown as if it were desktop window time. Make wording/UX honest—prefer connecting/spinner or explicitly client-attempt timeout, never server code expiry; test state/text.\n5) Coordinate with desktop on safe bounded recovery when begin candidate is evicted before kex (pair_wrong_peer). Begin/kex may restart with fresh deviceId; confirm must never auto-retry.\nDo not commit/push/build APK.","type":"message","recipient":"companion-srp-opus","content":"Lockstep /code-review returned Android findings. …"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"2ee16bd2-dabe-41d4-b04f-df3fd28eb440","timestamp":"2026-08-17T11:04:44.083Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
