{"parentUuid":"211375da-38ed-4a49-9c6c-b9891da8ffb2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"82e1d50d-e1a1-476c-a5f7-8416c2b0c1ce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Another Claude session sent a message:\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"desktop-srp-opus\" color=\"red\" summary=\"Reverted to 400 pair_unknown_candidate; 464 pass, gates green\">\nCorrection you both need, stated plainly: my tree DID move to `409 pair_restart_required` after your earlier ruling — I applied it, tested it and reported it green about an hour of work ago. Your re-pin arrived describing my tree as still on `400 pair_unknown_candidate`, which was true at the time you wrote the first ruling but not when you re-pinned. I have now reverted to the re-pinned contract, so the tree matches what you and companion settled on. Nothing was committed at any point, so no bad contract ever left this worktree.\n\nFINAL STATE, re-verified just now\n- `400 {\"code\":\"pair_unknown_candidate\"}` from one throw site (`requireRemoteCandidate`), at kex AND confirm.\n- `pair_restart_required` exists nowhere in the tree — grepped code, tests and FEATURES.md.\n- `pair_wrong_peer` conflict-only; wrong `pid`, wrong source and rewrite each proven to still return it.\n- Body shape pinned on both paths: exactly one `code` key plus `cache-control: no-store`, at kex and at confirm. That is companion's hard dependency, since they read the literal and never the status.\n- Uncharged and no strike, proven by a correct confirm still succeeding after three evicted confirms on top of two real wrong-code strikes.\n- LAN/QR v1 untouched; the literal is pinned to the single remote helper by test.\n\nGATES RERUN after the revert: 464 companion tests pass / 0 fail across 25 files, 172/172 feature markers, `(REFERR-GATE)` clean, Biome clean, scoped tsc clean for the touched files. Nothing committed or pushed.\n\nOne process note, offered once and then dropped: this contract changed direction three times in one hour and each fli