hing calls `dispatcher.executorService.shutdown()` / `connectionPool.evictAll()`. Three retries + a mode switch leaves 4 pools holding live TLS sockets to the pairing host and 4 thread sets on a phone. Every sibling collaborator (`PairingClient`, `SealedTransport` at CompanionCore.kt:96, `EventStreamClient` at :98) is handed the shared `httpClient` — this is the only path that forks it.\nFix: Thread the shared client through: keep `baseClient` as a field on PairingClient and default the param to `RemotePairingHandshake(baseClient = &lt;shared httpClient&gt;)`, or construct the handshake once in CompanionCore alongside `pairingClient()`. Also hoist `random: SecureRandom = SecureRandom()` off the per-call path.\n```\n\n```\n[MAJOR] C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/srp.ts:321\nDefect: `srpSecretModPow` (fixed 64-window ladder, 320 BigInt mulmods of 3072-bit operands) runs synchronously on the host-service event loop, twice per kex (`g^b` and `(A·v^u)^b`, srp.ts:508 and :525), reachable by unauthenticated public requests.\nFailure: Module header measures ~2.8-3.3 ms per exponentiation, ~10 ms per kex on win-arm64. `MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW = 64` (pairing.ts:256) admits 64 new derivations per window, and `REMOTE_PAIR_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW = 1024` (config.ts:234) lets a flood deliver them back-to-back — ~640 ms of contiguous event-loop block inside the 120 s window. That is the same loop serving `/v1/events` WS, `/v1/answer` and push, so a phone answering a blocked question during a pairing flood sees the bridge stall, and the real phone's own kex queues behind the flood's.\nFix: Move the two exponentiations off the loop — a small `worker_threads` pool, or at minimum yield (`setImmediate`) between the B and S exponentiations and between queued kex requests so no single stretch exceeds one request. Do not lower the security bounds to buy this.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/srp.ts:505\nDefect: `srpComputeK(group)` is recomputed inside every `srpServerHandshake`, though `k = H(PAD(N) || PAD(g))` is a constant of the group.\nFailure: Each kex pays two `srpPad` round-trips through `BigInt.toString(16)` -&gt; `padStart` -&gt; `Buffer.from(hex,\"hex\")` (srp.ts:205-219) on the 3072-bit modulus, a SHA-256, and a hex parse back to BigInt — pure repeat work per unauthenticated request, 64× per window under flood, on the same blocked loop as the finding above.\nFix: Memoize `k` per `SrpGroup` (lazily on the frozen group object, or compute it in `defineGroup` and expose it as a readonly field). Same for `srpPad(group, group.N)` / `srpPad(group, group.g)`.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts:1097\nDefect: `pid` is stored only as base64url text and re-decoded per request — `base64UrlDecode(state.pid)` at pairing.ts:1097 (kex), :1528 (confirm) and twice inside `assertPidMatches` (:1808, :1813) — while the raw `pidBytes` already existed at open (`openRemotePairingReserved`, :2275) and was discarded.\nFailure: Every admitted `/v1/pair/*` request pays 2-3 base64 decodes plus allocations for 16 bytes it already had; up to 1024 requests per window. Also makes `assertPidMatches` decode the *server's* own pid on every hostile packet.\nFix: Keep `pidBytes` on `PairingSessionCommon` next to `pid` and compare against it; decode only the caller-supplied value.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts:1356\nDefect: `evictOldestKexSessionsIfFull` full-scans `kexSessions` comparing `createdAtMs` to find the oldest, but candidates are only ever appended, so Map insertion order already puts the oldest first — the scan is redundant. `chargePerSource` in the same file (:1341) already uses the cheap `counts.keys().next()` form.\nFailure: Under a `begin` flood every introduction pays an O(17) scan plus the `Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY` bookkeeping instead of one `keys().next()`; small in absolute terms, but it is redundant work on the public flood path and it diverges from the eviction idiom used 15 lines earlier.\nFix: Take `state.kexSessions.keys().next()` as the eviction victim, matching `chargePerSource`; drop the scan and the `oldestAtMs` tracking.\n```\n\n```\n[MINOR] C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/.claude/worktrees/agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f/apps/desktop/src/renderer/components/PairDeviceDialog/PairDeviceDialog.tsx:253\nDefect: countdown ticks at 250 ms and stores raw `remainingMs`, but the only consumer renders `Math.ceil(remainingMs / 1000)` (line 419) — so 3 of every 4 `setRemainingMs` calls re-render the whole `PairingFlow` subtree for identical output.\nFailure: ~480 renders per 120 s window instead of ~120. `QrCode` memoizes on `value` so the encode is skipped, but React still reconciles the ~2 800-module single `&lt;path&gt;` string and the entire dialog tree 4×/s for the whole window, on top of the 1 s `pairingState` poll (line 325).\nFix: Store `secondsLeft` (integer) rather than `remainingMs` so `setState` is a no-op when unchanged, or tick once per second aligned to the next second boundary.\n```\n\nChecked and found clean: window-slot reservation lifecycle (`reserveWindowSlot`/`claimOrTearDown`/`releaseWindowSlot` — reservation is released on every failure path, timer cleared in `close()`, bridge teardown closes the window via the `unwind` entry at index.ts:1142); all four caps are genuinely bounded (`MAX_KEX_SESSIONS` 16 with wipe-on-evict, `MAX_KEX_PER_SOURCE`/`MAX_KEX_SOURCES` and `remoteRequestCounts` both table-bounded at 32, `remoteRequests`/`kexComputations` monotone); candidate key zeroization on every drop path (`zeroKexSession`/`wipeAllPairingKeys`); `remoteBurnMemo` is a single lazily-expired slot, not a growing table; the 404-with-no-window path allocates nothing; `QrCode` encode is correctly `useMemo`'d on `value`; the Android `produceState` countdown stops emitting once clamped and is cancelled on leave; the frozen `pair_unknown_candidate` / HTTP 400 behaviour at kex/confirm — untouched, no alias or auto-retry suggested.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>179294</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>52</tool_uses><duration_ms>496645</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
