ft` drops ~250 ms/tick → `Object.is(prev,next)` always false → full render + reconcile every tick.\n- `...\\components\\QrCode\\QrCode.tsx:32` not `React.memo` → body re-runs each parent render; `useMemo([value])` with stable `phase.qrUri` spares the ~2800-module encode and returns same `path` reference → no DOM attr writes. Caps cost at React work, not layout/paint → MINOR not MAJOR. Author already noted the pressure at QrCode.tsx:28-30 (\"a visible cost every time the countdown re-renders the dialog\").\n- `aria-live=\"polite\"` (:373-378): identical text → no DOM write → no spurious announcements.\n- Interval lifecycle clean: keyed on `expiresAtMs`, immediate `tick()`, `clearInterval` cleanup (:185-198). No leak, no double-timer.\n\n**Fix (not applied):** keep 250 ms interval for prompt `closing` handoff; quantise the write — `setSecondsLeft(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(left/1000)))` or `setRemainingMs(prev =&gt; Math.ceil(prev/1000) === Math.ceil(left/1000) ? prev : left)`.\n\nChecked clean: interval lifecycle/cleanup, effect keying on `expiresAtMs`, QrCode memoization, poll in-flight guard, absence of other `remainingMs` consumers.\n\nNote: no SendMessage tool in this session — returning verdict here for `code-review` to read.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>29874</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>16574</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:43.411Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa97907abca83ce65</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\aa97907abca83ce65.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify sealed-response honesty\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## CONFIRMED\n\n**File:** `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts`\n**Current line:** 1616 — `const access = await deps.loadAccessToken();` in `sealPairedResponse`. Candidate line accurate, no drift.\n\n**Summary:** `loadAccessToken` runs after `onPaired` already persisted device record + K_dev; its throw is a plain `Error` → HTTP 500 `{\"code\":\"unknown\"}` → phone fallback → `BAD_MAC` → \"Nothing was stored.\" while desktop holds a live paired device.\n\n**Failure scenario:** Remote code pairing, correct code, MAC verifies. `cloudflare-access.json` unreadable/torn/rotated-mismatched at that instant (deleted or rotated since bridge start, AV/backup lock `EACCES`, OneDrive placeholder eviction, partial write during rotation). Then:\n\n1. `pairing.ts:1601` — `state.consumed = true`\n2. `pairing.ts:1604` — `onPaired` commits `deviceStore.create` + `keyStore.put` to disk\n3. `pairing.ts:1616` — throws (`config.ts:786` `readJsonFile` / `requireString` / `requireEqual`, all bare `throw new Error`)\n4. `pairing.ts:2498-2510` — `state.consumed` true → window closed, error rethrown\n5. `http.ts:891-918` — not `PairingError`/`CleartextError` → `pairingErrorResponse(500, \"unknown\")`\n6. `RemotePairingHandshake.kt:408` — `\"unknown\"` not in `FAILURE_BY_WIRE`, `500` not in `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` → `?: PairingFailure.BAD_MAC`\n7. `RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:28` → `PairingError.BAD_MAC` → `PairingState.kt:145` `\"Pairing failed to verify. Nothing was stored.\"`\n\nDamage: orphan paired device + live K_dev on desktop, phone stored nothing, message tells user no cleanup needed → stale record persists unnoticed. Honesty/consistency defect, not corruption or lockout (§4.8 new-deviceId-per-pairing → re-pair works).\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `pairing.ts:1577-1583` — repo states \"`onPaired` writes to disk and `loadAccessToken` reads from it, so **either can throw** for reasons that have nothing to do with this exchange\". Reachability acknowledged; wipe handled, reporting not.\n- `pairing.ts:1560-1564` accepts \"desktop holding a key the phone never received\" as the ordering trade-off; nothing propagates that fact to the phone as a distinct code.\n- `config.ts:782-796`, `888-896` — sync `readFileSync` + strict validation, every failure a plain `Error`.\n- `index.ts:470` validates same file at bridge start → pairing-time throw needs post-start change/transient: rare, not impossible.\n- Against intentionality: `BridgeCompanionRepository.kt:984-991` deliberately routes `ProtocolException` to `PROTOCOL_MISMATCH` not BAD_MAC because \"by the time most of these can fire the desktop has already paired this device, so the claim would be false\". Same invariant; 500 path is the unpatched gap.\n- `RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:17-18` reserves BAD_MAC for \"rejected and **nothing was stored**\" — 500 fallback violates that stated contract.\n- `PROTOCOL.md` §4.9.7 error table has no code for post-persist host failure.\n\n**Frozen contract untouched:** missing candidate stays `pairing.ts:1149` `PairingError(400, \"pair_unknown_candidate\")` → `UNKNOWN_CANDIDATE` → `RESTART_REQUIRED`. Not implicated, no change proposed.\n\n**Fix direction (not applied):** load Access token before `onPaired`, or add a dedicated `PairingError` code for post-persist failure so the phone stops asserting nothing was stored.\n\nNote for `code-review`: no `SendMessage` tool in this session, so this reply is the return channel. Verdict is final; nothing restarted or broadened.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>55875</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>16892</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
