{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:45.565Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>acb422cff09a3381f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_s2NyuYkO56nZoLnCLF5hcXtu</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\acb422cff09a3381f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify protocol AAD pinning\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**CONFIRMED** (latent; not broken today — `PROTOCOL_CURRENT == 1`, so wire currently matches).\n\n```\n[MAJOR] C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt:352\nDefect: pairing-confirm AAD binds moving constant CompanionConstants.PROTOCOL_CURRENT where PROTOCOL.md and the host freeze the byte at 0x01; nothing couples the two.\nFailure: protocol 2 ships → PROTOCOL_CURRENT = 2 (doc comment \"What PROTOCOL.md describes\"; CLIENT_PROTOCOL_MAX derives from it, so a bump is the natural single edit). Phone builds AAD ...||0x00||0x02, host seals with PROTOCOL_VERSION_AT_PAIRING = 1 → GCM tag failure in SealedEnvelope.open on EVERY new pairing (remote + LAN). Remote reports CONFIRM_UNVERIFIED, LAN reports BAD_MAC — indistinguishable from MITM, the exact regression host comment pairing.ts:1652-1662 records as already having happened once. 100% of new pairings dead; existing paired devices unaffected; fails closed, no data loss. No test catches it: RemotePairingHandshakeTest.kt:902 seals the fake confirm with PROTOCOL_CURRENT too (self-consistent, stays green); frozen vectors CrossRuntimeDifferentialVectors20260729Test.kt:218 and :443 hand-build AAD with literal 1 and never call openConfirmEnvelope (also green).\nFix: dedicated frozen constant (e.g. PROTOCOL_VERSION_AT_PAIRING = 1, mirroring the host name, commented \"pairing precedes negotiation — never track PROTOCOL_CURRENT\") at both AAD sites; assert it in the frozen vector test so a future bump fails at build time.\n```\n\nSecond site, same defect: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\PairingClient.kt:273` (LAN `/pair/confirm`).\n\nEvidence\n- `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\PROTOCOL.md:399` — `|| 0x00 || protocolVersion  1 byte, the negotiated protocol (§6); 0x01 before negotiation`; `:968` — `METHOD \"POST\", PATH \"/v1/pair/confirm\", protocolVersion 0x01`. Pairing precedes `hello` → literal, not \"current\".\n- `...\\core\\CompanionConstants.kt:67-73` — `PROTOCOL_BASELINE = 0`, `PROTOCOL_CURRENT = 1`, `CLIENT_PROTOCOL_MAX = PROTOCOL_CURRENT`; nothing marks it frozen. `PROTOCOL.md:3114` enumerates `0`, `1`, ... (designed to grow).\n- `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts:262` — `const PROTOCOL_VERSION_AT_PAIRING = 1;`, sole confirm-seal use at `:1666` via `state.profile.confirmPath` (both flows) → no lockstep with any Android constant.\n- No pin anywhere: `PROTOCOL_CURRENT` occurs only at the two AAD sites, `CLIENT_PROTOCOL_MAX`, `BridgeClient.kt:428`, `SealedTransport.kt:63`, and tests reusing the same constant.\n\nRelated, not the candidate: `...\\core\\transport\\SealedTransport.kt:57-63` documents \"`1` before `hello` (§3.3)\" but initializes `protocolVersion = PROTOCOL_CURRENT` — same shape on the pre-hello default; that axis is legitimately negotiated afterwards.\n\nChecked clean: host confirm-seal path + constant; `EnvelopeAad.forRequest/forResponse/forEventFrame` field order/separators vs §3.3; remote `v` checks (`requireRemoteVersion`, remote `v=2` per PROTOCOL.md:984); §6/§6.1 negotiation baseline; `pair_unknown_candidate` literal untouched (no unsafety shown). Not checked: diff membership of these hunks — Bash aborts on broken shell profile (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching '`), so no `git diff` or test run; source + docs only.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>60462</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>18716</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:46.049Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a156cda089b7159f4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_cxOhqfvnx0gXyk2E0LZXHZ0C</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a156cda089b7159f4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify gateway status mapping\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>VERDICT: **PLAUSIBLE**\n\nLocation (current): `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt:470` (`FAILURE_BY_STATUS`, entries 471-478; BAD_MAC default at line 408).\n\nSummary: Cloudflare gateway statuses (502/504/520-524/530) have no `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` entry and their HTML bodies fail `PairErrorBody` decode, so they fall to the `PairingFailure.BAD_MAC` default → \"Pairing failed to verify. Nothing was stored.\" — verification/no-storage language for a tunnel or origin outage; 503 alone routes to NETWORK.\n\nFailure scenario: desktop shows a pairing code, `cloudflared` is down or nothing is bound on the pairing port → edge returns 530 or 502 with an HTML page (both empirically observed on this tunnel, `SETUP.md:53-65`). Phone shows \"Pairing failed to verify. Nothing was stored.\" Sharper variant: 504/502 on `/v1/pair/confirm` after the desktop already processed confirm and stored the device record → phone asserts \"Nothing was stored\" while the desktop holds a paired device, and gives no \"check your desktop's paired devices\" advice.\n\nEvidence:\n- `RemotePairingHandshake.kt:401-410` — `remoteFailureOf`: unparsable body → `code == null`, `FAILURE_BY_STATUS[502]` null, `?: PairingFailure.BAD_MAC`.\n- `CompanionJson.kt:51-55` — HTML → `ProtocolException`, the only exception caught in `remoteFailureOf`; silent default, no crash.\n- `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` covers 401/403/404/410/429/503 only — no 5xx besides 503.\n- `RemotePairingErrorMapping.kt:28` → `PairingState.kt:145` text; reached via `BridgeCompanionRepository.kt:973-975`. No interception in `PairingClient.pairWithCode` (`PairingClient.kt:218-226`).\n- Same physical outage arriving as `IOException` correctly yields UNREACHABLE (`RemotePairingHandshake.kt:389-397`, per `PROTOCOL.md:1005-1009`); as a status it does not.\n- In-repo convention divergence: `ConnectionClassifier.kt:47-50` calls the 530-vs-502 split \"load-bearing\" (530 = DesktopUnreachable, 502 = SupersetNotRunning) for the same architecture.\n- Honest-claim rule already enforced: `RemotePairingErrorMappingTest.kt:135-152` — BAD_MAC may claim \"Nothing was stored\" only because in the flow raising it, nothing was.\n\nCounter-evidence (why PLAUSIBLE, not CONFIRMED): `PROTOCOL.md:1248-1252` normatively mandates this default — \"Any other non-2xx is a rejection the phone has no name for: it reports 'nothing was stored' and must neither call it unreachable (the endpoint answered) nor blame the code.\" Code matches spec; the weakness is the spec clause, whose \"the endpoint answered\" premise is false for 502/530/504.\n\nFix direction (not applied): map 502/504/520-524/530 → `UNREACHABLE` and amend `PROTOCOL.md` §4.9.7; stop claiming \"Nothing was stored\" for any failure after `confirm` was transmitted. HTTP-400 `pair_unknown_candidate` wire-code-only contract untouched; no automatic retry added.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70193</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>20640</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:46.762Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>add2c8840ff906cd5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_28GTVZizxwm1L0M0Dr86dWd8</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\add2c8840ff906cd5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace pairing cross-file contracts\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Sweep already complete. Final candidates below — unchanged, no re-inspection.\n\n## Tooling caveat\n\nBash tool nonfunctional all session (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''` on every invocation, incl. `echo ok`). No `git diff HEAD` / untracked listing obtainable → candidates derived by reading both working trees directly (Read/Grep/Glob) across the frozen-contract surface. Change-attribution to the diff is inferred, not proven. Finder phase: unverified by design.\n\n## Candidates (6, recall-biased)\n\n**1.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts\n- `line`: 2547\n- `summary`: `chargeRemoteRequest` increments the monotone window total before `chargePerSource` can refuse → per-source-refused requests still spend the global cap.\n- `failure_scenario`: One IP sends 1024 `POST /v1/pair/begin` inside the 120 s window. Requests 1-32 admitted; 33-1024 throw `429 pair_rate_limited` from `chargePerSource` — but each already ran `state.remoteRequests += 1`. `remoteRequests` reaches `REMOTE_PAIR_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW` (32×32=1024). Real phone's first `begin` then hits the ceiling at line 2541 → `429 pair_rate_limited`; PROTOCOL.md §4.9 forbids the phone retrying. Crypto-free junk from a single address rate-limits the legitimate device out of its own window — the invariant config.ts:212-215 and pairing.ts:348-357 both claim holds.\n\n**2.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\SessionViewModel.kt\n- `line`: 360\n- `summary`: `pairFromCode` launches into `viewModelScope` with no in-flight guard; the retained-code \"Try again\" button makes double-fire trivial.\n- `failure_scenario`: Double-tap \"Try again\" (PairingScreen.kt:186, plain `Button`, no enabled-gate; state flips to `Exchanging` only asynchronously). Two concurrent `begin→kex→confirm` runs with two deviceIds. Desktop window is single-use: first `confirm` sets `state.consumed`, second gets `410 pair_window_closed` → `pairingState` (one MutableStateFlow, last writer wins) settles on `Failed(WINDOW_CLOSED)`, overwriting `Paired`, and that branch skips `pushRegistrar.onPairingSucceeded()`. Phone is paired and persisted but shows \"The pairing window closed. Start it again on the desktop.\" with the FCM token never registered → no push ever arrives.\n\n**3.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt\n- `line`: 382\n- `summary`: `response.body.bytes()` buffers every pairing response entirely, uncapped, from an unauthenticated public endpoint.\n- `failure_scenario`: The pairing origin (public Cloudflare host, or anything terminating that hostname) answers `POST /v1/pair/kex` `200` with a multi-hundred-MB body. `bytes()` buffers it all before `Base64Url.decode(kex.bPublic, \"B\")` (line 312, 2-arg — no expected length) and `Srp.decodeGroupElement` can reject → `OutOfMemoryError`, app killed mid-pairing. Asymmetric with the host, which caps at `MAX_PAIR_BODY_BYTES` (4 KiB) in `readBoundedBody` before parsing.\n\n**4.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt\n- `line`: 113\n- `summary`: The typed 8-digit code lives in `rememberSaveable` → written to Android saved-instance-state, so a ~26.6-bit shared secret outlives its 120 s window.\n- `failure_scenario`: User types the code, pairing fails `RESTART_REQUIRED`, app backgrounded. Compose writes `digits` into the Activity `Bundle`; Android persists saved state (recoverable via `onSaveInstanceState` dumps, bugreports, heap capture) with no expiry tied to the desktop window. Post-hoc device access yields a code the desktop deliberately never persists (pairing.ts:490-496 bans logging/persisting it; the desktop zeroes the code bytes at open). Retained-code retry needs the digits in memory only, not in saved state.\n\n**5.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\shell\\CompanionShell.kt\n- `line`: 185\n- `summary`: `onRetry = session::cancelPairing` republishes the existing paired record instead of resetting to entry → an already-paired phone cannot retry a re-pair.\n- `failure_scenario`: Already-paired phone opens PAIRING to re-pair, submits a code, gets a non-resubmittable failure (e.g. `CODE_WRONG`). \"Try again\" (PairingScreen.kt:191-195) clears `digits` and calls `onRetry` → `repository.cancelPairing()` → `publishPairing(pairedRecordOrNull())` → state becomes `PairingState.Paired` with the OLD record. Screen renders \"Paired with &lt;old origin&gt;…\" + Done; the code field never returns. User is told they are paired when the attempt they just made failed, with no in-place route back to entry.\n\n**6.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt\n- `line`: 203\n- `summary`: QR entry's `Failed` branch offers only \"Start again\" wired to `onCancel`, which navigates off the pairing route rather than resetting the scanner.\n- `failure_scenario`: QR pairing fails `UNREACHABLE` (wrong Wi-Fi) — the commonest recoverable QR failure. Only control is \"Start again\" → `onCancel` → `session.cancelPairing()` + `route = CompanionRoute.AGENTS` (CompanionShell.kt:181-184). User is ejected from pairing, must re-navigate Diagnostics → Pair, and the camera permission/scanner is torn down and rebuilt. CODE entry got a reset-in-place path; QR did not.\n\n## Checked, consistent across both repos\n\nSRP domain separation and identity/label/transcript-prefix parity (`sc/v3 remote-pair`, `sc/v3-srp*`, salt prefix); fixed-window ladder guards (`srpSecretModPow` exponent width, `table[0] = N+1`, `srpAssertClientPublic`, `u == 0`, `B mod N == 0`); exact-width I2OSP refusal both sides (`srpBigIntToBytes` / `Srp.pad` / `decodeGroupElement`); `base64UrlDecode`/`decodeWireId` canonicality vs `decodeExact` — no outer-accepts/inner-refuses drift against device-store; the frozen wire contract itself (`400` + parsed body literal `pair_unknown_candidate` on both kex and confirm, exactly one double-quoted occurrence confined to `requireRemoteCandidate`, no `pair_restart_required`, no alias, 400 absent from `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` so status alone can never imply it, no automatic re-begin/re-confirm, `retryOnConnectionFailure(false)`); `requireRemoteCandidate` charging neither a confirm attempt nor a MAC strike, reached only after window/version/source/pid; `pair_wrong_peer` narrowed to rewrite/wrong-source/wrong-pid; LAN v1 vocabulary byte-unchanged; `evictOldestKexSessionsIfFull` oldest-first with `zeroKexSession` wipe; monotone `kexComputations` charged only for genuinely new derivations (cached retry and refused rewrite free); sealed step-4 AAD path/protocol-version parity (`/v1/pair/confirm`, protocol 1) and `PROTOCOL_CURRENT` vs `PAIRING_REMOTE_WIRE_VERSION`; host/Access isolation (`routeByHost` matrix, `normaliseHostHeader`, startup assert that pair host ≠ main host); Unicode digit normalisation (`Character.digit` → ASCII, `passwordBytes` guard, `assertAsciiDigitCode`); `GroupedCodeTransformation` offset mapping; window-slot reserve/claim/release plus both `close()` paths (handle identity check, timer clear, code/salt/verifier/keys destruction, burn memo lifecycle); docs (PROTOCOL.md §4.9.3 normative text matches implementation; FEATURES.md marker table consistent with sibling `(PAIR-*)` markers).\n\n**FIX-FIRST**\n\n(No `SendMessage` tool in this session — `code-review` should read these candidates from this output.)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>182606</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>42784</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:46.786Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8eaf6c26af20d34c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a8eaf6c26af20d34c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Scan pairing diff linewise\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Sweep already complete. Re-emitting final Angle A candidates unchanged; no further inspection performed.\n\n## Scope caveat\nBash tool dead all session — every invocation (`echo hello`, `git --version`) failed in the shell preamble: `/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''`. No `git diff HEAD` / `git status --short` obtainable. Scope reconstructed by reading the remote-pairing surface directly. Untracked-file enumeration and hunk boundaries unverified — treat coverage as file-level, not diff-level.\n\n## Candidates (6, recall-biased, unverified Phase 1)\n\n**1.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts` `line`: 1063\n`summary`: `chargeKexComputation` charged before `A` range validation (which lives inside `srpServerHandshake` → `srp.ts:497`), never refunded on `SrpError`.\n`failure_scenario`: 16 distinct `CF-Connecting-IP` values × 4 `begin`+`kex` pairs (`MAX_KEX_PER_SOURCE`), each `kex` sending a canonical all-zero 384-byte `A` → `decodeClientPublic` passes, charge lands, `srpAssertClientPublic` throws → 64 charges, zero exponentiations, `kexComputations` = `MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW`. Real phone's first `kex` → `429 pair_rate_limited`; phone treats 429 as terminal (§4.9) → user-opened window dead. Exactly the outcome the docblock at 1740 says cannot happen.\n\n**2.** same file `line`: 2547\n`summary`: `state.remoteRequests += 1` executes before `chargePerSource`, so over-cap requests still burn the never-refunded window-wide aggregate.\n`failure_scenario`: One IP sends 1024 `POST /v1/pair/begin`. Requests 33-1024 each increment `remoteRequests`, then throw the per-source 429. Aggregate hits `REMOTE_PAIR_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW` (32×32) → every source, incl. the real phone, refused at 2541. Contradicts the invariant stated at 352-357 and 2522-2534.\n\n**3.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt` `line`: 113\n`summary`: `var digits by rememberSaveable` puts the typed 8-digit secret into Android saved-instance-state, escaping the process.\n`failure_scenario`: User types `12345678`, then rotates / backgrounds / process death on the `Failed(RESTART_REQUIRED)` screen → `digits` serialised into the Activity `Bundle` held by `system_server` for task restore, outliving both the 120 s window and the app process. ~26.6 bits of authenticator outside the boundary `pairing.ts:488-497` mandates. (`submittedAtMs`, line 119, is legitimately saveable; `digits` is not.)\n\n**4.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\data\\BridgeCompanionRepository.kt` `line`: 961\n`summary`: `withTimeout(PAIRING_WINDOW_MS)` can cancel after the desktop persisted the device record; `TimeoutCancellationException` → `WINDOW_CLOSED`, whose text omits the orphan record.\n`failure_scenario`: Confirm reaches desktop → `consumed` set, `onPaired` writes `K_dev` record, sealed 200 delayed by tunnel latency, phone timeout fires. Phone stores nothing, shows \"The pairing window closed. Start it again on the desktop.\" Desktop holds a paired device no phone has a key for; retries mint fresh `deviceId`s → orphan records accumulate. `CONFIRM_UNVERIFIED` (`PairingState.kt:166-169`) gives the correct advice; this path does not.\n\n**5.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt` `line`: 382\n`summary`: `response.body.bytes()` reads the pairing-hop response unbounded, on both 200 and error paths.\n`failure_scenario`: Unauthenticated public host, TLS terminated at the edge. A hostile edge / captive portal / misrouted DNS answer returns 400 with a multi-hundred-MB body; `bytes()` buffers it all before `remoteFailureOf` parses → OOM kill. Desktop bounds bodies at `MAX_PAIR_BODY_BYTES` (`http.ts:936-948`); phone has no counterpart despite every field having a known ceiling (`B` 384 B, `pid`/`pairSalt`, sealed envelope).\n\n**6.** `file`: `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts` `line`: 2369\n`summary`: `remoteBurnMemo` cleared only by `openRemotePairingReserved`; opening a QR/LAN window leaves a stale memo live.\n`failure_scenario`: Remote window burns on three wrong codes → `rememberRemoteBurn()`. Within 60 s the user opens a QR window (`openPairingWindowReserved`, ~2219, never touches the memo). `currentRemotePairing()` returns `null` (kind `\"lan\"`), so `http.ts:833` consults `remoteWindowWasBurned()` → `true` → every internet caller gets `403 pair_code_burned` instead of the bare 404 that \"no remote window\" must be indistinguishable from, and a phone is told a current code is dead.\n\n## Checked clean\nSRP-6a arithmetic + RFC 5054 padding (refuse-not-truncate, `k = H(PAD(N)||PAD(g))`, `u==0` / degenerate-`A` rejection); fixed 4-bit-window ladder op-count invariance and `table[0] = N+1`; cross-runtime label/salt/identity/transcript agreement (`sc/v3-srp`, `superset-companion/pair/v3-srp`, `\"sc/v3 remote-pair\"`, 825-byte transcript, `PAD(S)` IKM); `base64UrlDecode` canonicality (kills the non-canonical-`deviceId` map-key hazard); frozen wire contract — `pair_unknown_candidate` = 400 + parsed-body-only, no alias, no 400 status fallback, no auto-retry, `resubmitsSameCode` gated on user tap; `assertCandidateSource` pinning on `begin` and `kex`; candidate key wiping on every drop path + `completePairing`'s outermost `finally`; `(PAIR-ONE-WINDOW-ATOMIC)` reserve/claim/release/`claimOrTearDown`; host isolation (`classifyRequestHost`, duplicate-`Host`, root-dot, load-time two-host assertion); `cf-connecting-ip` single-value/IP-literal gate; step-4 request-form AAD + reserved nonce counter 0; `PairingCode` Arabic-Indic/fullwidth→ASCII normalisation and `passwordBytes` guard; QR/LAN `sc/v1` bytes unchanged.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**\n\nReply to `code-review` not sent — no SendMessage tool in this session's toolset. Findings above are the deliverable.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>175084</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>41523</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:47.520Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a099f92dbfd042d82</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a099f92dbfd042d82.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify no-window source shape\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>REFUTED\n\n**Candidate as stated:** `packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts:820` — does not contain the described code. That line is `export const ROUTES: Record&lt;SealedPath, SealedRoute&gt; = {` (sealed route table).\n\n**Corrected location of nearest real analog:** `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts:1134-1138`\n\n**Summary:** Every load-bearing identifier is absent. `cf-connecting-ip` → one hit repo-wide, unrelated: `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/apps/marketing/src/lib/email-rate-limit.ts:25`. `routeByHost` → zero hits. `pair_unknown_candidate` → zero hits. Bridge caller identity is Cloudflare Access JWT only (`cf-access-jwt-assertion`, `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/packages/host-service/src/companion/access-jwt.ts:55`); no client-IP header is read anywhere in host-service. No host-based routing, no remote-window existence branch on this listener. Missing-source state unreachable for every caller → provably impossible.\n\n**Real analog, and why it is not the defect:**\n```ts\n// pairing.ts:1130-1138\nif (path === PAIR_PATH_KEX) {\n    const sourceKey = req.socket.remoteAddress;\n    if (sourceKey === undefined || sourceKey.length === 0) {\n        writeJson(res, 400, { code: \"unknown\" satisfies PairingErrorCode });\n        return;\n    }\n```\n- Separate socket: pairing is its own `createServer` on `PAIRING_BIND_HOST:PAIRING_PORT`, LAN, 120 s (`pairing.ts:1063-1087`). Bodyless 404 catch-all belongs to the loopback Hono app (`http.ts:1188`, `app.all(\"*\", (c) =&gt; c.body(null, 404))`). No tunnel/Access hop → no proxy header.\n- No no-window 404 to differ from: window closed → server closed (`pairing.ts:1016-1061`) → TCP refusal, not a 404 body.\n- Literal is `{\"code\":\"unknown\"}` on `req.socket.remoteAddress`, not `pair_unknown_candidate` on a header → frozen-literal constraint untouched.\n- Unobservable: `remoteAddress` is `undefined` only after socket destruction; handler runs post-`readBody` `'end'` on a live socket. Destroyed case → write lands on dead socket, no caller reads it. All other rejections on this listener (405 / 404 / bad-JSON 400 / `pair_version_unsupported`) share the same JSON envelope → no fingerprint added.\n\n**Failure scenario:** none constructible.\n\n**Evidence:** `http.ts:700-960`, `http.ts:1090-1208`, `pairing.ts:409-545`, `pairing.ts:1000-1292` read directly; repo-wide greps for `cf-connecting-ip`, `pair_unknown_candidate`, `routeByHost|pair_unknown|connecting.ip|cf_connecting`; `handleKex`/`handleConfirm` each have exactly one call site (`pairing.ts:1142`, `pairing.ts:1147`).\n\nChecked clean: pairing kex/confirm ordering + charging, candidate-table eviction bounds, sealed route table coverage, bridge auth boundary and 404 catch-all.\n\n**SHIP**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>45237</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>19612</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:26:47.714Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa60a2b4b066b592e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\aa60a2b4b066b592e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify synchronous SRP blocking\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**REFUTED**\n\nVerification was already complete; re-stating the verdict unchanged. No SendMessage tool available in this session, so the verdict is returned here for the `code-review` coordinator.\n\nCorrected path/line: candidate file does not exist — no `packages/host-service/src/companion/srp.ts`, so no `:321`. Actual code in that role:\n- `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts` — `handleKex` line 417, `handleConfirm` line 615\n- `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\crypto.ts:326` — `x25519`\n\nSummary — every premise fails:\n1. No SRP, no 3072-bit modexp. Pairing is X25519 ECDH via Node native `diffieHellman()` (`crypto.ts:326-351`), keys from `generateKeyPairSync(\"x25519\")` (`crypto.ts:353-368`). No bigint math, no `modPow`, no MODP/ffdhe constant, no fixed-window exponentiation anywhere in tree. Per-op cost = native curve25519, tens of microseconds.\n2. Zero asymmetric ops per kex. `handleKex` does window check, `v` check, constant-time pid compare, base64url decode (16 B + 32 B), validation, `Map` insert, O(n&lt;=16) eviction scan. Never calls `x25519`.\n3. The one ECDH sits behind authenticated caps: `handleConfirm` requires matching pid (`:626`) + existing candidate session (`:628`), then `chargeConfirmAttempt` (`:642`, `PAIRING_ATTEMPTS_PER_WINDOW`), with `burnMac` (`:841`) consuming the window at `PAIRING_MAX_BAD_MACS`. Handful of ECDH ops per 120 s window max.\n4. \"64-computation flood\" is arithmetic over storage caps, not crypto caps: `MAX_KEX_SESSIONS = 16` (`:148`), `MAX_KEX_PER_SOURCE = 4` (`:156`), `MAX_KEX_SOURCES = 32` (`:158`). True worst case 128 introductions, each bounded by `MAX_PAIR_BODY_BYTES = 4 * 1024` (`:139`, enforced `readBody` `:1229-1245`) plus `headersTimeout`/`requestTimeout` (`:1066-1067`).\n5. Async boundaries intact. `route` async; confirm-path awaits are real I/O (`deps.onPaired`, `deps.loadAccessToken`, `flushed`). Listener is a separate socket (`0.0.0.0:47611`, 120 s, `:1076`) sharing the loop — immaterial at microsecond-scale per-request work.\n\nLoad -&gt; observable failure: none reproducible. Saturating caps (32 sources x 4 deviceIds x 4 KB bodies in one 120 s window) = ~128 parse/validate requests, no asymmetric crypto, sub-millisecond aggregate CPU. No measurable contiguous stall on bridge/event/answer traffic. Claimed damage needs an exponentiation absent from this codebase.\n\nEvidence: full read of `pairing.ts` (1293 lines); `x25519`/`generateX25519KeyPair`/HKDF region of `crypto.ts`; searches for `modPow|3072|kex|powmod|modexp` in `packages/host-service/src` (hits only in `pairing.ts` comments, `limits.ts:93`, `types.ts:297`, unrelated `terminal.seq-catchup.node-test.ts:719` `\"blob 3072\"`); `srp` in `packages/` (none) and `apps/` (only base64 inside `cursor.svg`); `MODP|ffdhe|srpVerifier|SRP_|modPow|createDiffieHellman` in both trees (no code hits). Caveat: `Bash` unusable this session — `\"/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''\"` — so `git diff`/`git log` unavailable; verdict rests on checked-out file contents.\n\nSecurity invariants/caps unchanged; frozen literals untouched; read-only throughout.\n\nClean on inspection: kex/confirm cap layering, per-source throttle + eviction bounds, pid constant-time compare ordering, MAC-strike burn ordering, body-size/timeout limits, secret zeroing in `close()` and `handleConfirm` `finally`.\n\n**SHIP**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>52318</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>20146</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
