\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\components\\PairDeviceDialog\\PairDeviceDialog.tsx`\nline: 302-304 (shape at `packages\\host-service\\src\\trpc\\router\\companion\\companion.ts:163-170`)\nsummary: Window identity inferred from `expiresAtMs` + `pairingKind` with a silent-ignore branch, while `pairingRef` exists for exactly this and is missing from `CompanionPairingState`; simpler form is compare `pairingRef`, mismatch → existing \"window is gone\" failure.\nfailure_scenario: Window replaced under the dialog → phase `closing` never resolves; the 363-370 render is a spinner with no footer buttons, so no verdict and no in-panel exit.\n\n3. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts`\nline: 1356\nsummary: Oldest-candidate eviction does an O(n) `createdAtMs` scan with sentinel, dead `oldestKey === null` return, once-only `while` and redundant re-`get`, while `chargePerSource` (1340-1343) evicts by Map insertion order; simpler form is `kexSessions.keys().next()`.\nfailure_scenario: Two eviction idioms for one invariant diverge on any candidate re-insert or timestamp touch; the `(PAIR-JUNK-SURVIVAL)` fairness guarantee becomes false in one table with no test able to observe it.\n\n4. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts`\nline: 2499-2509\nsummary: The burn fact has two owners — `burnMac` (1797-1802) flips `consumed`, the endpoint catch re-derives `failedMacAttempts &gt;= PAIRING_MAX_BAD_MACS` to memo it; simpler form is memoing inside `burnMac`.\nfailure_scenario: A burn reached any other way leaves no memo → `http.ts:833` answers a bare `404` and the user who mistyped three times reads \"no pairing window open\" instead of `pair_code_burned`.\n\n5. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt`\nline: 113 (retry read 185-190)\nsummary: The typed 8-digit code lives in `rememberSaveable`, i.e. system-persisted saved-instance state, for a retry that only needs recomposition/rotation survival; simpler form is `remember` or clearing `digits` in `onStop`, keeping only `submittedAtMs` saveable.\nfailure_scenario: A ~26.6-bit secret bounded to 120 s is written to disk-backed state and restored after process death, where resubmitting a dead code reports `CODE_WRONG` (\"check the code\") for a code that was correct.\n\n6. `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\data\\BridgeCompanionRepository.kt`\nline: 950 (also `RemotePairingHandshake.kt:119-125`, `PairingCode.kt:81`)\nsummary: One code string normalized/validated at four layers with two distinct failure objects; simpler form is normalize once at the UI boundary plus core's `passwordBytes` guard, dropping the repository copy.\nfailure_scenario: The repository branch is unreachable today (Pair enabled only at 8 digits, `takeDigits` already strips non-digits) yet owns a user-visible verdict, so two verdict paths must be hand-synchronised while only one is exercisable.\n\nChecked clean: frozen wire behavior (400 + parsed-body `pair_unknown_candidate`, no 400 status-only fallback, user-triggered retry only); one-window reservation and both `close()` zeroization paths; caps 1024/64/32-32/4-32 each independently reachable; host isolation and `cf-connecting-ip` single-literal rule; SRP ladder, `PAD()` widths, 825-byte transcript cross-runtime agreement; sealed step-4 AAD path binding and counter-0 nonce; `admit()` charge-before-body ordering.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>174668</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>27833</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification