{"parentUuid":"f5650853-61d1-42f3-8afb-ab74da0849be","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cd954ace-8448-487b-8443-01f929f9e1a1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6fd47450b7f4ff77</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_GxXuXDOxYus86X9IZLCdzu79</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a6fd47450b7f4ff77.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify countdown rerenders\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>CONFIRMED (low magnitude).\n\n**Corrected location:** `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\apps\\desktop\\src\\renderer\\components\\PairDeviceDialog\\PairDeviceDialog.tsx:189` (state write), `:195` (`setInterval(tick, 250)`). Candidate's `:253` wrong — that's the pairingState poll error handler.\n\n**Summary:** `setRemainingMs(left)` at 250 ms while sole consumer quantises to whole seconds (`Math.ceil(remainingMs / 1000)`, :359) → ~4x renders for identical visible output.\n\n**Cost scenario:** dialog open full 120 s window → 480 state commits / PairingFlow renders, 120 change pixels; other 360 re-run PairingFlow + QrCode + DialogFooter/Button and reconcile the SVG subtree for zero visual delta. Multiplies per \"Show a new code\" click.\n\n**Evidence**\n- Only two `remainingMs` reads in file: decl :118, `secondsLeft` :359. Other grep hits unrelated (`...\\V2NotificationController\\lib\\resyncAgentStatus.ts`).\n- No subsecond consumption of state: the subsecond value that matters (`left &lt;= 0` → `{kind:\"closing\"}`, :193) is a local from `expiresAtMs - Date.now()`. Interval *frequency* is functionally justified; the *state write* cadence is not.\n- No React bailout — `left` drops ~250 ms/tick → `Object.is(prev,next)` always false → full render + reconcile every tick.\n- `...\\components\\QrCode\\QrCode.tsx:32` not `React.memo` → body re-runs each parent render; `useMemo([value])` with stable `phase.qrUri` spares the ~2800-module encode and returns same `path` reference → no DOM attr writes. Caps cost at React work, not layout/paint → MINOR not MAJOR. Author already noted the pressure at QrCode.tsx:28-30 (\"a visible cost every time the countdown re-renders the dialog\").\n- `aria-live=\"polite\"` (:373-378): identical text → no DOM write → no spurious announcements.\n- Interval lifecycle clean: keyed on `expiresAtMs`, immediate `tick()`, `clearInterval` cleanup (:185-198). No leak, no double-timer.\n\n**Fix (not applied):** keep 250 ms interval for prompt `closing` handoff; quantise the write — `setSecondsLeft(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(left/1000)))` or `setRemainingMs(prev =&gt; Math.ceil(prev/1000) === Math.ceil(left/1000) ? prev : left)`.\n\nChecked clean: interval lifecycle/cleanup, effect keying on `expiresAtMs`, QrCode memoization, poll in-flight guard, absence of other `remainingMs` consumers.\n\nNote: no SendMessage tool in this session — returning verdict here for `code-review` to read.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>29874</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>16574</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"6ce61fb8-ea15-4f68-bec3-ec370153e774","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:29:37.429Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
