{"parentUuid":"ca738d5b-ff69-4ade-8c06-9f918218c81d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f678fde-36f0-4615-843e-b65f6d285252","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>addb9326abc49c7ec</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_zC6micxNfH9xz54jDGrDr9hi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\addb9326abc49c7ec.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify HTTP client leak\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## CONFIRMED\n\n**Location:** `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\PairingClient.kt:223` (line exact; method is `pairWithCode`, not `pairRemote`)\n\n**Summary:** Default arg `handshake: RemotePairingHandshake = RemotePairingHandshake()` re-evaluates per invocation and falls through to `RemotePairingHandshake`'s own `baseClient: OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient()` — remote pairing is the only path in the repo that does not derive from `CompanionCore`'s single process-lifetime `httpClient`.\n\n**Retry/resource scenario:** Mistyped 8-digit code. `BridgeCompanionRepository.pairFromCode` (line 962) calls `core.pairingClient().pairWithCode(...)` with no `handshake` → attempt 1 builds `OkHttpClient()` #1 with its own `ConnectionPool`, runs begin/kex/confirm, fails `CODE_WRONG`. Two more retries inside the desktop's 120 s window (burns at 3 strikes) → clients #2, #3, each with a fresh pool. No retry reuses the prior connection to `REMOTE_PAIRING_ORIGIN`: full TCP+TLS handshake per attempt on a mobile link, inside a flow already racing 120 s; each orphaned pool retains its idle socket until 5-min keepAlive eviction. Any future base-client config (proxy, CT/logging interceptor, socket factory) would silently skip remote pairing.\n\n**Impact correction — candidate overstates two parts:**\n- Not an unbounded leak. No `Cache` configured; no `evictAll`/`shutdown` anywhere (grep: only `PairingScreen.kt:444`, unrelated camera `Executor`). Retention bounded by idle eviction.\n- Not \"separate dispatchers\" in thread-cost terms. `RemotePairingHandshake.post` (line 381) uses synchronous `execute()` → `Dispatcher.executorService` never touched; okhttp 5.4.0 (`gradle/libs.versions.toml:14`) backs pool cleanup with shared `TaskRunner`. Zero per-client threads.\n\nNet: real convention break + real per-retry handshake/connection waste. **MINOR**, not a leak.\n\n**Evidence**\n- `PairingClient.kt:223` — per-call default via Kotlin `$default` bridge; repo-wide `pairWithCode` hits = declaration + one caller, neither supplying it.\n- `RemotePairingHandshake.kt:80` — `baseClient: OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient()`; line 86 `baseClient.newBuilder()` → class is built to inherit a shared pool, handed a fresh one.\n- `CompanionCore.kt:31,49,96,98` — one `httpClient` threaded into `PairingClient`/`SealedTransport`/`EventStreamClient`; `PairingClient.kt:52-63`, `SealedTransport.kt:89,110-111` both derive via `baseClient.newBuilder()` — the convention line 223 breaks.\n- `CompanionContainer.kt:90-106` — core built once in `by lazy` repository → shared client lives for process.\n- `BridgeCompanionRepository.kt:948-1002` — user-invokable retryable entry; failures set `PairingState.Failed` and return, retry left to user.\n- No reuse/cleanup invariant excuses it: `PairingClient` does not retain `baseClient` (only derived `client`), so no existing path lets the handshake inherit the shared pool.\n\n**Fix (not applied):** retain `baseClient` in `PairingClient` and pass `RemotePairingHandshake(baseClient = baseClient)`, or drop the default and have `CompanionCore` build the handshake with `httpClient`.\n\nChecked clean: Kotlin default-arg evaluation semantics, OkHttp 5.4.0 ownership/thread behavior, caller lifetime, close/share paths repo-wide.\n\n**Verdict: FIX-FIRST** (MINOR — mechanism confirmed, impact bounded)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>56235</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>18712</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"3f762939-824e-4548-9228-0ec85fbe2c86","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:32:08.583Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
