{"parentUuid":"3902d38e-49f3-4d42-bd76-4a82fc0533af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4a6c9ae5-250d-450a-a509-0c49bb78d6fb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>add2c8840ff906cd5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_28GTVZizxwm1L0M0Dr86dWd8</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\add2c8840ff906cd5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace pairing cross-file contracts\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Sweep already complete. Final candidates below — unchanged, no re-inspection.\n\n## Tooling caveat\n\nBash tool nonfunctional all session (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''` on every invocation, incl. `echo ok`). No `git diff HEAD` / untracked listing obtainable → candidates derived by reading both working trees directly (Read/Grep/Glob) across the frozen-contract surface. Change-attribution to the diff is inferred, not proven. Finder phase: unverified by design.\n\n## Candidates (6, recall-biased)\n\n**1.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts\n- `line`: 2547\n- `summary`: `chargeRemoteRequest` increments the monotone window total before `chargePerSource` can refuse → per-source-refused requests still spend the global cap.\n- `failure_scenario`: One IP sends 1024 `POST /v1/pair/begin` inside the 120 s window. Requests 1-32 admitted; 33-1024 throw `429 pair_rate_limited` from `chargePerSource` — but each already ran `state.remoteRequests += 1`. `remoteRequests` reaches `REMOTE_PAIR_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW` (32×32=1024). Real phone's first `begin` then hits the ceiling at line 2541 → `429 pair_rate_limited`; PROTOCOL.md §4.9 forbids the phone retrying. Crypto-free junk from a single address rate-limits the legitimate device out of its own window — the invariant config.ts:212-215 and pairing.ts:348-357 both claim holds.\n\n**2.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\SessionViewModel.kt\n- `line`: 360\n- `summary`: `pairFromCode` launches into `viewModelScope` with no in-flight guard; the retained-code \"Try again\" button makes double-fire trivial.\n- `failure_scenario`: Double-tap \"Try again\" (PairingScreen.kt:186, plain `Button`, no enabled-gate; state flips to `Exchanging` only asynchronously). Two concurrent `begin→kex→confirm` runs with two deviceIds. Desktop window is single-use: first `confirm` sets `state.consumed`, second gets `410 pair_window_closed` → `pairingState` (one MutableStateFlow, last writer wins) settles on `Failed(WINDOW_CLOSED)`, overwriting `Paired`, and that branch skips `pushRegistrar.onPairingSucceeded()`. Phone is paired and persisted but shows \"The pairing window closed. Start it again on the desktop.\" with the FCM token never registered → no push ever arrives.\n\n**3.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt\n- `line`: 382\n- `summary`: `response.body.bytes()` buffers every pairing response entirely, uncapped, from an unauthenticated public endpoint.\n- `failure_scenario`: The pairing origin (public Cloudflare host, or anything terminating that hostname) answers `POST /v1/pair/kex` `200` with a multi-hundred-MB body. `bytes()` buffers it all before `Base64Url.decode(kex.bPublic, \"B\")` (line 312, 2-arg — no expected length) and `Srp.decodeGroupElement` can reject → `OutOfMemoryError`, app killed mid-pairing. Asymmetric with the host, which caps at `MAX_PAIR_BODY_BYTES` (4 KiB) in `readBoundedBody` before parsing.\n\n**4.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt\n- `line`: 113\n- `summary`: The typed 8-digit code lives in `rememberSaveable` → written to Android saved-instance-state, so a ~26.6-bit shared secret outlives its 120 s window.\n- `failure_scenario`: User types the code, pairing fails `RESTART_REQUIRED`, app backgrounded. Compose writes `digits` into the Activity `Bundle`; Android persists saved state (recoverable via `onSaveInstanceState` dumps, bugreports, heap capture) with no expiry tied to the desktop window. Post-hoc device access yields a code the desktop deliberately never persists (pairing.ts:490-496 bans logging/persisting it; the desktop zeroes the code bytes at open). Retained-code retry needs the digits in memory only, not in saved state.\n\n**5.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\shell\\CompanionShell.kt\n- `line`: 185\n- `summary`: `onRetry = session::cancelPairing` republishes the existing paired record instead of resetting to entry → an already-paired phone cannot retry a re-pair.\n- `failure_scenario`: Already-paired phone opens PAIRING to re-pair, submits a code, gets a non-resubmittable failure (e.g. `CODE_WRONG`). \"Try again\" (PairingScreen.kt:191-195) clears `digits` and calls `onRetry` → `repository.cancelPairing()` → `publishPairing(pairedRecordOrNull())` → state becomes `PairingState.Paired` with the OLD record. Screen renders \"Paired with &lt;old origin&gt;…\" + Done; the code field never returns. User is told they are paired when the attempt they just made failed, with no in-place route back to entry.\n\n**6.**\n- `file`: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt\n- `line`: 203\n- `summary`: QR entry's `Failed` branch offers only \"Start again\" wired to `onCancel`, which navigates off the pairing route rather than resetting the scanner.\n- `failure_scenario`: QR pairing fails `UNREACHABLE` (wrong Wi-Fi) — the commonest recoverable QR failure. Only control is \"Start again\" → `onCancel` → `session.cancelPairing()` + `route = CompanionRoute.AGENTS` (CompanionShell.kt:181-184). User is ejected from pairing, must re-navigate Diagnostics → Pair, and the camera permission/scanner is torn down and rebuilt. CODE entry got a reset-in-place path; QR did not.\n\n## Checked, consistent across both repos\n\nSRP domain separation and identity/label/transcript-prefix parity (`sc/v3 remote-pair`, `sc/v3-srp*`, salt prefix); fixed-window ladder guards (`srpSecretModPow` exponent width, `table[0] = N+1`, `srpAssertClientPublic`, `u == 0`, `B mod N == 0`); exact-width I2OSP refusal both sides (`srpBigIntToBytes` / `Srp.pad` / `decodeGroupElement`); `base64UrlDecode`/`decodeWireId` canonicality vs `decodeExact` — no outer-accepts/inner-refuses drift against device-store; the frozen wire contract itself (`400` + parsed body literal `pair_unknown_candidate` on both kex and confirm, exactly one double-quoted occurrence confined to `requireRemoteCandidate`, no `pair_restart_required`, no alias, 400 absent from `FAILURE_BY_STATUS` so status alone can never imply it, no automatic re-begin/re-confirm, `retryOnConnectionFailure(false)`); `requireRemoteCandidate` charging neither a confirm attempt nor a MAC strike, reached only after window/version/source/pid; `pair_wrong_peer` narrowed to rewrite/wrong-source/wrong-pid; LAN v1 vocabulary byte-unchanged; `evictOldestKexSessionsIfFull` oldest-first with `zeroKexSession` wipe; monotone `kexComputations` charged only for genuinely new derivations (cached retry and refused rewrite free); sealed step-4 AAD path/protocol-version parity (`/v1/pair/confirm`, protocol 1) and `PROTOCOL_CURRENT` vs `PAIRING_REMOTE_WIRE_VERSION`; host/Access isolation (`routeByHost` matrix, `normaliseHostHeader`, startup assert that pair host ≠ main host); Unicode digit normalisation (`Character.digit` → ASCII, `passwordBytes` guard, `assertAsciiDigitCode`); `GroupedCodeTransformation` offset mapping; window-slot reserve/claim/release plus both `close()` paths (handle identity check, timer clear, code/salt/verifier/keys destruction, burn memo lifecycle); docs (PROTOCOL.md §4.9.3 normative text matches implementation; FEATURES.md marker table consistent with sibling `(PAIR-*)` markers).\n\n**FIX-FIRST**\n\n(No `SendMessage` tool in this session — `code-review` should read these candidates from this output.)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>182606</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>42784</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"49977adb-6169-44c7-aa17-c95504b6b460","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:33:39.775Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
