{"parentUuid":"f3436b14-e8ff-4859-b05d-593d8df52b6b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e6cbd52-68a7-409c-afbe-c41ea2c73c61","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8eaf6c26af20d34c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a8eaf6c26af20d34c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Scan pairing diff linewise\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Sweep already complete. Re-emitting final Angle A candidates unchanged; no further inspection performed.\n\n## Scope caveat\nBash tool dead all session — every invocation (`echo hello`, `git --version`) failed in the shell preamble: `/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''`. No `git diff HEAD` / `git status --short` obtainable. Scope reconstructed by reading the remote-pairing surface directly. Untracked-file enumeration and hunk boundaries unverified — treat coverage as file-level, not diff-level.\n\n## Candidates (6, recall-biased, unverified Phase 1)\n\n**1.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a6c0cf0431904f59f\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts` `line`: 1063\n`summary`: `chargeKexComputation` charged before `A` range validation (which lives inside `srpServerHandshake` → `srp.ts:497`), never refunded on `SrpError`.\n`failure_scenario`: 16 distinct `CF-Connecting-IP` values × 4 `begin`+`kex` pairs (`MAX_KEX_PER_SOURCE`), each `kex` sending a canonical all-zero 384-byte `A` → `decodeClientPublic` passes, charge lands, `srpAssertClientPublic` throws → 64 charges, zero exponentiations, `kexComputations` = `MAX_KEX_COMPUTATIONS_PER_WINDOW`. Real phone's first `kex` → `429 pair_rate_limited`; phone treats 429 as terminal (§4.9) → user-opened window dead. Exactly the outcome the docblock at 1740 says cannot happen.\n\n**2.** same file `line`: 2547\n`summary`: `state.remoteRequests += 1` executes before `chargePerSource`, so over-cap requests still burn the never-refunded window-wide aggregate.\n`failure_scenario`: One IP sends 1024 `POST /v1/pair/begin`. Requests 33-1024 each increment `remoteRequests`, then throw the per-source 429. Aggregate hits `REMOTE_PAIR_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_WINDOW` (32×32) → every source, incl. the real phone, refused at 2541. Contradicts the invariant stated at 352-357 and 2522-2534.\n\n**3.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\ui\\pairing\\PairingScreen.kt` `line`: 113\n`summary`: `var digits by rememberSaveable` puts the typed 8-digit secret into Android saved-instance-state, escaping the process.\n`failure_scenario`: User types `12345678`, then rotates / backgrounds / process death on the `Failed(RESTART_REQUIRED)` screen → `digits` serialised into the Activity `Bundle` held by `system_server` for task restore, outliving both the 120 s window and the app process. ~26.6 bits of authenticator outside the boundary `pairing.ts:488-497` mandates. (`submittedAtMs`, line 119, is legitimately saveable; `digits` is not.)\n\n**4.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\app-phone\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\phone\\data\\BridgeCompanionRepository.kt` `line`: 961\n`summary`: `withTimeout(PAIRING_WINDOW_MS)` can cancel after the desktop persisted the device record; `TimeoutCancellationException` → `WINDOW_CLOSED`, whose text omits the orphan record.\n`failure_scenario`: Confirm reaches desktop → `consumed` set, `onPaired` writes `K_dev` record, sealed 200 delayed by tunnel latency, phone timeout fires. Phone stores nothing, shows \"The pairing window closed. Start it again on the desktop.\" Desktop holds a paired device no phone has a key for; retries mint fresh `deviceId`s → orphan records accumulate. `CONFIRM_UNVERIFIED` (`PairingState.kt:166-169`) gives the correct advice; this path does not.\n\n**5.** `file`: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\superset-companion\\core\\src\\main\\java\\family\\khaira\\supersetcompanion\\core\\pairing\\RemotePairingHandshake.kt` `line`: 382\n`summary`: `response.body.bytes()` reads the pairing-hop response unbounded, on both 200 and error paths.\n`failure_scenario`: Unauthenticated public host, TLS terminated at the edge. A hostile edge / captive portal / misrouted DNS answer returns 400 with a multi-hundred-MB body; `bytes()` buffers it all before `remoteFailureOf` parses → OOM kill. Desktop bounds bodies at `MAX_PAIR_BODY_BYTES` (`http.ts:936-948`); phone has no counterpart despite every field having a known ceiling (`B` 384 B, `pid`/`pairSalt`, sealed envelope).\n\n**6.** `file`: `...\\packages\\host-service\\src\\companion\\pairing.ts` `line`: 2369\n`summary`: `remoteBurnMemo` cleared only by `openRemotePairingReserved`; opening a QR/LAN window leaves a stale memo live.\n`failure_scenario`: Remote window burns on three wrong codes → `rememberRemoteBurn()`. Within 60 s the user opens a QR window (`openPairingWindowReserved`, ~2219, never touches the memo). `currentRemotePairing()` returns `null` (kind `\"lan\"`), so `http.ts:833` consults `remoteWindowWasBurned()` → `true` → every internet caller gets `403 pair_code_burned` instead of the bare 404 that \"no remote window\" must be indistinguishable from, and a phone is told a current code is dead.\n\n## Checked clean\nSRP-6a arithmetic + RFC 5054 padding (refuse-not-truncate, `k = H(PAD(N)||PAD(g))`, `u==0` / degenerate-`A` rejection); fixed 4-bit-window ladder op-count invariance and `table[0] = N+1`; cross-runtime label/salt/identity/transcript agreement (`sc/v3-srp`, `superset-companion/pair/v3-srp`, `\"sc/v3 remote-pair\"`, 825-byte transcript, `PAD(S)` IKM); `base64UrlDecode` canonicality (kills the non-canonical-`deviceId` map-key hazard); frozen wire contract — `pair_unknown_candidate` = 400 + parsed-body-only, no alias, no 400 status fallback, no auto-retry, `resubmitsSameCode` gated on user tap; `assertCandidateSource` pinning on `begin` and `kex`; candidate key wiping on every drop path + `completePairing`'s outermost `finally`; `(PAIR-ONE-WINDOW-ATOMIC)` reserve/claim/release/`claimOrTearDown`; host isolation (`classifyRequestHost`, duplicate-`Host`, root-dot, load-time two-host assertion); `cf-connecting-ip` single-value/IP-literal gate; step-4 request-form AAD + reserved nonce counter 0; `PairingCode` Arabic-Indic/fullwidth→ASCII normalisation and `passwordBytes` guard; QR/LAN `sc/v1` bytes unchanged.\n\n**FIX-FIRST**\n\nReply to `code-review` not sent — no SendMessage tool in this session's toolset. Findings above are the deliverable.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>175084</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>41523</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"e22b1e5c-d84a-4167-b0de-03e0900c4107","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:34:10.172Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
