{"parentUuid":"9381aa71-7fa5-4a3e-bafb-19e0c88e980c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e6b6f12d-0a1c-407d-bce3-41c88806ddb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a099f92dbfd042d82</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-khair-Code-Projects-fork-superset-windows-arm64\\db223e0d-1ca5-4ab0-8b87-291b28fd63ce\\tasks\\a099f92dbfd042d82.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify no-window source shape\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>REFUTED\n\n**Candidate as stated:** `packages/host-service/src/companion/http.ts:820` — does not contain the described code. That line is `export const ROUTES: Record&lt;SealedPath, SealedRoute&gt; = {` (sealed route table).\n\n**Corrected location of nearest real analog:** `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/packages/host-service/src/companion/pairing.ts:1134-1138`\n\n**Summary:** Every load-bearing identifier is absent. `cf-connecting-ip` → one hit repo-wide, unrelated: `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/apps/marketing/src/lib/email-rate-limit.ts:25`. `routeByHost` → zero hits. `pair_unknown_candidate` → zero hits. Bridge caller identity is Cloudflare Access JWT only (`cf-access-jwt-assertion`, `C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64/packages/host-service/src/companion/access-jwt.ts:55`); no client-IP header is read anywhere in host-service. No host-based routing, no remote-window existence branch on this listener. Missing-source state unreachable for every caller → provably impossible.\n\n**Real analog, and why it is not the defect:**\n```ts\n// pairing.ts:1130-1138\nif (path === PAIR_PATH_KEX) {\n    const sourceKey = req.socket.remoteAddress;\n    if (sourceKey === undefined || sourceKey.length === 0) {\n        writeJson(res, 400, { code: \"unknown\" satisfies PairingErrorCode });\n        return;\n    }\n```\n- Separate socket: pairing is its own `createServer` on `PAIRING_BIND_HOST:PAIRING_PORT`, LAN, 120 s (`pairing.ts:1063-1087`). Bodyless 404 catch-all belongs to the loopback Hono app (`http.ts:1188`, `app.all(\"*\", (c) =&gt; c.body(null, 404))`). No tunnel/Access hop → no proxy header.\n- No no-window 404 to differ from: window closed → server closed (`pairing.ts:1016-1061`) → TCP refusal, not a 404 body.\n- Literal is `{\"code\":\"unknown\"}` on `req.socket.remoteAddress`, not `pair_unknown_candidate` on a header → frozen-literal constraint untouched.\n- Unobservable: `remoteAddress` is `undefined` only after socket destruction; handler runs post-`readBody` `'end'` on a live socket. Destroyed case → write lands on dead socket, no caller reads it. All other rejections on this listener (405 / 404 / bad-JSON 400 / `pair_version_unsupported`) share the same JSON envelope → no fingerprint added.\n\n**Failure scenario:** none constructible.\n\n**Evidence:** `http.ts:700-960`, `http.ts:1090-1208`, `pairing.ts:409-545`, `pairing.ts:1000-1292` read directly; repo-wide greps for `cf-connecting-ip`, `pair_unknown_candidate`, `routeByHost|pair_unknown|connecting.ip|cf_connecting`; `handleKex`/`handleConfirm` each have exactly one call site (`pairing.ts:1142`, `pairing.ts:1147`).\n\nChecked clean: pairing kex/confirm ordering + charging, candidate-table eviction bounds, sealed route table coverage, bridge auth boundary and 404 catch-all.\n\n**SHIP**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>45237</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>0</tool_uses><duration_ms>19612</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"2f7d9d89-a297-4457-b367-3d768630bdac","timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:34:40.481Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"exter