{"parentUuid":"5252117a-12b9-4f83-a41d-c1abe0c012ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce8NGoLqWeSVnsVs6Y9Kw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SGR99h8TNU5qhRX2YcpKN7","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Final review verdicts (Opus arbiter + Fable) are in. Apply these confirmed desktop fixes in the worktree, with regression tests, then rerun full suite + all gates. Do not commit yet.\n1) pairing.ts:2547 [MAJOR] — `state.remoteRequests += 1` runs before `chargePerSource`, so one IP sending 1024 begins burns the whole window aggregate and locks out the real phone. Move the aggregate increment to AFTER chargePerSource succeeds. Add a test: single source flooding past its per-source cap does not consume the window aggregate; real phone still admitted.\n2) pairing.ts:1616 [MAJOR-coupled] — `loadAccessToken()` runs after consumed+onPaired persist; a token-file failure becomes 500 \"unknown\" and the phone claims nothing stored while desktop holds an orphan device. Load the Access token BEFORE setting consumed/persisting; if any post-persist failure remains possible, emit a distinct closed-union code instead of \"unknown\". Update docs; test token-load failure leaves no orphan record and no burned honesty.\n3) pairing.ts:1063 [MINOR] — chargeKexComputation charged before A range validation. Move `srpAssertClientPublic` into/before decodeClientPublic's acceptance path so degenerate width-correct A (PAD(1), PAD(N-1)) is refused BEFORE the derivation charge; order = validate → charge → derive. Fix the two docblocks (:1020, :1756) and add a test that degenerate A costs zero kexComputations.\n4) PairDeviceDialog countdown [MINOR] — store quantized integer secondsLeft so identical seconds don't re-render (~4x); keep 250ms tick for prompt closing.\nAlso correct any comments the review flagged as false. Report applied items, test counts, and gate results.","summary":"Apply confirmed desktop revie