{"parentUuid":"cd21b5e0-1f5b-47b8-880d-a581535d2436","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Ce8TEtShpMsUw4fXLQfCE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HrKKUMCHD6CVNbgBA3AdfG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pairing\\commit-msg-fork.txt","content":"feat(companion): secure remote code pairing over public tunnel (SRP-6a)\n\n(REMOTE-CODE-PAIRING) Replaces the blocked X25519+code-in-HKDF prototype\nwith a real PAKE: SRP-6a (RFC 5054 3072-bit group, SHA-256), desktop as\nserver, phone as client. The 8-digit code never leaves the desktop; a\nTLS-terminating edge can no longer validate guesses offline - every\nguess costs one online confirm, charged before verify, burned at 3.\n\n- three-request wire v2 on a dedicated public pairing host\n  (pair-superset.khaira.family): begin -> {pid,pairSalt}, kex {A} ->\n  {B}, confirm {macPhone} -> sealed credentials; no Access token in the\n  APK - strict pre-body host/method/path isolation replaces it; main\n  host keeps Access-JWT on every route and bare-404s all pair paths\n- fixed-window (4-bit, 64 nibbles, table[0]=N+1) BigInt ladder for all\n  secret exponents: uniform operation count, ~3ms/exponentiation vs the\n  ~2.4s/call Electron native-DH constructor it replaces (measured;\n  BoringSSL primality-checks a custom prime on every construction)\n- fresh one-use b per kex candidate; derived keys/transcript stored,\n  b/S dropped in-handler; wipeAllPairingKeys on every drop path\n- monotone per-window bounds an eviction can never refund: 64 SRP\n  derivations, 1024 admitted requests (charged after per-source cap),\n  A range-validated before the derivation charge\n- atomic one-window reservation across the async LAN listener bind;\n  rejected second open no longer orphans the live handle\n- Access token loaded BEFORE persist/consume, so a token-file failure\n  aborts cleanly with the window still usable (PAIR-TOKEN-BEFORE-PERSIST)\n- missing begin candidate at kex/confirm -> 400 pair_unknown_candidate\n  (uncharged, no strike); pair_wrong_peer narrowed to rewrite conflicts\n- cross-runtime golden vectors frozen against the Android BouncyCastle\n  half (independent implementations, byte-identical incl. leading-zero\n  code); RFC 5054 Appendix B anchor; LAN/QR v1 bytes untouched\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 Fable architecture rounds, /simplify x4,\n2-model final verification); 467 companion tests green, 172 markers,\nREFERR clean. Ships in lockstep with superset-companion v0.3.0.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":372454,"output_tokens":1010,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1010,"cache_read_input_tokens":372454,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"20ebc118-f263-41c0-8a0f-c68b0acb7435","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:09:24.157Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
