{"parentUuid":"f4452b6f-cf95-46d9-913d-9fa4dfd8e4b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cFE2yELxcZu7Rccipd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qe64jhCXaKV2eKgqVPJKqY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Kill upstream forced-update gate","model":"opus","name":"update-gate-opus","prompt":"Work in the fork's MAIN checkout: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main, currently 42e3caf4e3). Repository files only; never read user shell/profile files. Bash is broken in this environment — use PowerShell.\n\nPROBLEM (live, blocking the user right now): upstream's server-driven notice API is showing a NON-DISMISSIBLE full-screen \"Update Required\" gate over our fork's build. Screenshot text: \"Update required Superset needs an update to keep syncing your workspaces. This version depends on a background sync service that is being retired… Your version: 1.20.2\", with \"Check for Update\" (does nothing, because our releases are fork-owned and our updater does not track upstream) and \"Download Manually\" (which would install UPSTREAM's build and destroy the fork). The user cannot dismiss it.\n\nMECHANISM (already traced, verify before editing):\n- apps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts fetches `${env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/desktop/version`, and (a) pushes a synthesized non-dismissible `blocking` notice when `lt(appVersion, data.minimumVersion)`, and (b) passes through any server `notices` including `severity: \"blocking\"`.\n- apps/desktop/src/renderer/components/UpdateRequiredPage/UpdateRequiredPage.tsx renders the full-screen blocker. Find its render site(s) and the severity/`dismissible` plumbing in packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts.\n\nREQUIRED FORK BEHAVIOUR — this is a permanent fork-owned override, not a one-off patch:\n1. A remote notice can NEVER block this fork's UI. No code path may render UpdateRequiredPage (or any non-dismissible full-screen update gate) as a result of remote data or a version comparison. Remove/neutralize the synthesized minimum-version notice too.\n2. Do NOT simply delete informational notices: a non-blocking, DISMISSIBLE notice may still show, because upstream announcements can be genuinely useful. Downgrade what would have been blocking into a dismissible informational notice (or drop it entirely if downgrading would render misleading upstream text like \"Download Manually\" / \"Install & restart\" CTAs that would replace our build). Judgement call is yours, but the user must always be able to dismiss and keep working, and no CTA may install an upstream artifact. If you keep a downgraded notice, its CTA must not be `install-update`.\n3. Fail loud in the right direction: if the notice payload cannot be parsed, behave as \"no notices\" (already fails open — keep it).\n4. Make it merge-durable. This must survive upstream merges: implement it so a marker-gated FEATURES.md row protects it, add the marker token to the changed file(s), and add the row + fenced `markers` block entry exactly as the other fork overrides do (read FEATURES.md and scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs first). Suggested marker: `(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)`.\n5. Tests: add real tests proving a remote `blocking` notice and a below-`minimumVersion` payload BOTH result in no blocking gate and a dismissible/absent notice. Put them where the existing desktop-notices tests live (packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.test.ts and/or a renderer-side test) following existing patterns.\n\nGATES (report each): the relevant test suites, `node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` (all markers present), `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` (REFERR gate clean), Biome on touched files only, and a scoped typecheck for the touched packages. Note pre-existing failures separately — the repo carries accepted type debt and CRLF formatter noise; do not normalize unrelated files.\n\nDo NOT commit, push, or bump the app version. Report: files changed, the exact behaviour now, marker name, test names/counts, gate results, and any judgement call you made on point 2.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6312,"cache_read_input_tokens":414631,"output_tokens":3155,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":369},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6312,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3155,"cache_read_input_tokens":414631,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6312},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"64e0a873-d9da-46bf-98d3-6927564d3b67","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:07:51.575Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"64e0a873-d9da-46bf-98d3-6927564d3b67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cFE2yELxcZu7Rccipd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UYc5rY1yBWmhDSphg53T7u","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review update-gate override design","model":"fable","name":"update-gate-fable","prompt":"Read-only architecture review, no edits. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (main). Never read user shell/profile files. Bash is broken; use Read/Grep/Glob.\n\nCONTEXT: This is a vendored Windows ARM64 fork that ships its own releases (see AGENTS.md: \"One version, ever\", \"v2-only, forever\", FEATURES.md marker discipline, merge-durability via markers). Upstream's server-driven desktop-notice API has just pushed a NON-DISMISSIBLE full-screen \"Update Required\" gate that covers the fork's UI and offers only \"Check for Update\" (inert for us) and \"Download Manually\" (which would install upstream's build over the fork). The user is blocked.\n\nRelevant code: apps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts, apps/desktop/src/renderer/components/UpdateRequiredPage/, packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts (+ its test), the render site(s) of UpdateRequiredPage, apps/api/src/app/api/desktop/version/route.ts (upstream server side, for reference only — we do not control it), plans/done/20260720-remote-version-notices.md.\n\nAn Opus agent is concurrently implementing a permanent fork override so remote data can never block the fork's UI, keeping non-blocking notices dismissible, with a FEATURES.md marker for merge durability.\n\nYOUR JOB — answer these precisely, with file:line evidence:\n1. Where is the CORRECT single choke point? Compare suppressing at the hook (useDesktopNotices), at the shared filter (filterApplicableNotices / severity parsing), and at the render site. Which best guarantees NO code path can ever produce a blocking gate, including future upstream code that adds a new render site or a new blocking severity? Name the one you'd pick and why the others leak.\n2. Enumerate EVERY current path that can render UpdateRequiredPage or otherwise present an undismissable update prompt — including any host-service/remote-host min-version gate (see useRemoteHostStatus / v2-workspace layout.tsx, which uses a DIFFERENT minVersion mechanism). State clearly which of those are in scope for \"remote notice cannot block us\" and which are legitimately ours to keep (e.g. a real host-service version mismatch we control).\n3. What upstream-merge failure modes should the marker protect against? Be concrete about what a future upstream refactor would have to do for the override to silently stop working, and what assertion would catch it (mirroring the fork's SCREENREADER-GUARD-DRIFT lesson: never assert incidental upstream names; assert the invariant over the whole surface).\n4. Is there any legitimate reason our fork WOULD want a blocking gate (e.g. a host-service protocol break where continuing genuinely corrupts data)? If so, how should the override distinguish \"our own blocking condition\" from \"upstream's remote blocking notice\"?\n5. Any dismissible-notice CTA that must be neutered because it would install or fetch an upstream artifact over the fork.\n\nReturn a tight, decision-ready answer. Do not edit anything.","subagent_type":"architect-fable"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6312,"cache_read_input_tokens":414631,"output_tokens":3155,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":369},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6312,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3155,"cache_read_input_tokens":414631,"cache_creation_inpu