{"parentUuid":"951e7a11-a413-434b-9512-b53d18bdc7df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cUJ9dWygQ8efzgJoPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's a bigger change than the overlay, and it needs care: your sign-in/session runs through their API, so I need to know exactly what can be cut without bricking the app. Auditing before promising anything."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3555,"cache_read_input_tokens":420943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3555},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"be687c27-8f83-480e-806d-0352258379ba","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:10:31.114Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"be687c27-8f83-480e-806d-0352258379ba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cUJ9dWygQ8efzgJoPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bd1KoVEzCytiQSQKx5St3A","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit all outbound cloud calls","model":"opus","name":"network-audit-opus","prompt":"Read-only exhaustive audit, NO edits. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main). Repository files only — never read user shell/profile files or home-directory credentials. Bash is broken; use Read/Grep/Glob and PowerShell if needed.\n\nGOAL: The fork owner wants to SEVER every connection from the shipped Windows ARM64 desktop app to Superset's cloud/analytics/telemetry, keeping only what is strictly required for the app to function for a self-hosted, local-only user. Before any code changes, produce a complete, evidence-backed inventory.\n\nAUDIT SCOPE — only what actually ships in the packaged desktop app and its host-service/CLI (apps/desktop, packages/host-service, packages/cli, and any shared packages they import). EXCLUDE apps/api, apps/web, apps/marketing, apps/admin, apps/docs, apps/mobile — those are server/other products we do not ship. Say so explicitly if something ambiguous straddles the line.\n\nFor EVERY outbound network destination, report a row with: file:line, the destination (env var and/or literal host), what triggers it (boot / interval / user action / error), what data leaves the machine, and whether it is REQUIRED or SEVERABLE.\n\nSpecifically hunt for and classify:\n1. Analytics / product telemetry SDKs — PostHog, Segment, Amplitude, GA, Mixpanel, or any custom event POST. Include renderer AND main process AND host-service.\n2. Crash/error reporting — Sentry (look for @sentry/*, sentry init, dsn, tracesSampleRate, replay), Electron crashReporter, breakpad/minidump uploads.\n3. Auto-update — electron-updater / update feed URLs / `install-update` actions / `checkForUpdates`. Note which feed our fork's releases actually use vs upstream's.\n4. The desktop notices/version endpoint (`/api/desktop/version`) and anything else polling their API on a timer.\n5. Auth / session / organization — better-auth or equivalent, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` usage, token refresh, `/api/auth/*`. CRITICAL: determine whether the app can boot, sign in, and open a workspace with NO reachable Superset API. Is there any local/offline/self-host mode? Read the `_authenticated` route guards and session restore path and say plainly what happens when the API is unreachable.\n6. Electric / workspace sync (`packages/db`, TanStack DB, electric-sql) — is the sync origin their cloud, our own, or local? What breaks if severed?\n7. AI/model providers reached directly by the app (Anthropic/OpenAI/etc.) and any proxying through their cloud — the user's coding agents legitimately need model access; distinguish \"model API the user pays for directly\" from \"routed through Superset's cloud\".\n8. Any remaining phone-home: license checks, feature flags, remote config, changelog fetch, avatar/CDN fetches, font/CDN loads, marketing links opened at boot.\n9. Env plumbing: how NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and friends are baked at build time (apps/desktop build config, .env handling, electron-builder config) — i.e. what a build-time override could change.\n\nDELIVERABLE — three clearly separated lists:\nA. SAFE TO SEVER with no functional loss for a local-only user (with the mechanism you'd use for each: build-time env, code no-op, dependency drop).\nB. SEVERABLE BUT WITH A COST — name the exact feature lost and how visible it is.\nC. LOAD-BEARING — cutting it breaks boot/auth/workspaces/agents. For each, state precisely what breaks and whether a self-hosted substitute exists in this codebase.\n\nFinish with the honest bottom line: can this app run fully air-gapped from Superset's cloud today, and if not, what is the minimum that must keep talking to them. Cite file:line for every claim. Do not speculate — if you cannot determine something, say so and name the file that would settle it.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3555,"cache_read_input_tokens":420943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3555},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"63f4b765-eb44-4b8c-8a3c-f4f8aa5358ae","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:10:55.257Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
