{"parentUuid":"10035c73-8c56-4f91-b1a0-bbf5af9543eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cbjofwS53fMwtpxDNb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L2TBH9sQuAs1z8vqBqPM42","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"SCOPE UPDATE from the owner: the target state is a FULLY LOCAL app with NO sign-in and NO connection to Superset's cloud/analytics/telemetry at all. So treat auth/session as SEVERABLE-BY-REQUIREMENT, not load-bearing-and-therefore-kept.\n\nRe-frame list C: instead of just declaring auth load-bearing, determine exactly what a no-sign-in local mode would require in THIS codebase. Answer concretely, with file:line:\n- What does the session/org actually gate? Enumerate what reads `activeOrganizationId` / session user id and what would break with a synthesized local identity.\n- Is there any existing offline/local/dev path we could legitimately promote (e.g. the local-dev sign-in, a seeded local org, `setup.local.sh` stack, or any `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` pointing at localhost) rather than inventing a bypass?\n- Does the local SQLite/host-service layer already hold everything the UI needs (workspaces, projects, terminals, kanban, sessions, recycle bin), or is any of it only ever hydrated from their cloud/Electric?\n- Where exactly would a stub identity have to be injected so that the `_authenticated` route guards, tRPC procedures (`protectedProcedure`), and any org-scoped queries all pass without a remote call?\n- What data, if any, currently lives ONLY in their cloud for this user and would be lost/unreachable.\nAlso flag anything that would make a stubbed identity unsafe or corrupting (e.g. IDs that must be globally unique, or writes that assume server-assigned keys).\n\nEverything else in your original brief stands. Still read-only, no edits, cite file:line, and say plainly where you cannot determine something.","summary":"Retarget audit to no-sign-in local mode","to":"network-audit-opus","type":"message","recipient":"network-audit-opus","content":"SCOPE UPDATE from the owner: the target state is …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_read_input_tokens":424498,"output_tokens":1738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":424498,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"3e046316-cd9a-40d2-aaf9-36e67a383c84","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:15.338Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3e046316-cd9a-40d2-aaf9-36e67a383c84","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8959683-9294-45a2-b05a-370465aa3d87","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L2TBH9sQuAs1z8vqBqPM42","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message sent to network-audit-opus's inbox\",\"msg_id\":\"bacb643c-4479-4707-ab6e-9fc9a93e77d1\",\"routing\":{\"sender\":\"team-lead\",\"target\":\"@network-audit-opus\",\"targetColor\":\"yellow\",\"summary\":\"Retarget audit to no-sign-in local mode\",\"content\":\"SCOPE UPDATE from the owner: the target state is …\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"34b124b2-d706-4252-968e-f0bf21ff0672","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:15.643Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message sent to network-audit-opus's inbox","msg_id":"bacb643c-4479-4707-ab6e-9fc9a93e77d1","routing":{"sender":"team-lead","target":"@network-audit-opus","targetColor":"yellow","summary":"Retarget audit to no-sign-in local mode","content":"SCOPE UPDATE from the owner: the target state is …"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3e046316-cd9a-40d2-aaf9-36e67a383c84","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"34b124b2-d706-4252-968e-f0bf21ff0672","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cbjofwS53fMwtpxDNb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014sbefZVz5UZiFTytLVoSsg","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"SCOPE EXPANSION from the owner, in addition to your current 5 questions: the end goal is not just \"remote notices can't block us\" — the owner wants this fork FULLY LOCAL: no sign-in, and no connection to Superset's cloud, analytics or telemetry whatsoever.\n\nKeep your original 5 answers (they're still needed to unblock the user now), then add a second section: the ARCHITECTURE of full severance for this fork. Specifically:\n- What is the right layering: build-time env (baking a dead/localhost API origin), a single fork-owned \"offline mode\" module that every outbound caller must route through, dependency removal, or per-call no-ops? Recommend ONE primary mechanism and say why the alternatives leak or rot across upstream merges.\n- How should a no-sign-in local identity be modelled so it is honest rather than a lie the code can trip over (stable local org/user ids, no server-assigned key assumptions)?\n- How do we make severance MERGE-DURABLE and self-policing, so a future upstream merge that adds a brand-new fetch/telemetry sink FAILS a fork gate rather than silently phoning home? The fork already has precedent for this pattern (scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs, scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs, and the screenreader guard which asserts an invariant over a whole artifact set rather than incidental names). Propose the concrete gate — what it scans, what it asserts, what it allowlists, and how it avoids false positives on legitimate local/model-provider traffic.\n- Explicitly separate what MUST keep working: the user's coding agents reaching model APIs (Anthropic/OpenAI etc.) directly, the local host-service, and our own fork-owned companion bridge/pairing over the user's own Cloudflare tunnel. Severance must not touch those.\nAn Opus agent is auditing every outbound destination in parallel; assume you'll get its inventory, so focus on the DESIGN and the gate rather than enumerating call sites yourself. Read-only, no edits.","summary":"Design full cloud severance architecture","to":"update-gate-fable","type":"message","recipient":"update-gate-fable","content":"SCOPE EXPANSION from the owner, in addition to yo…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_read_input_tokens":424498,"output_tokens":1738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":424498,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fcbce589-ca65-46d2-a42f-e903a76c6754","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:26.859Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"fcbce589-ca65-46d2-a42f-e903a76c6754","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8959683-9294-45a2-b05a-370465aa3d87","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014sbefZVz5UZiFTytLVoSsg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message sent to update-gate-fable's inbox\",\"msg_id\":\"513ec04e-1f51-4f39-89bb-6a90d10eda2d\",\"routing\":{\"sender\":\"team-lead\",\"target\":\"@update-gate-fable\",\"targetColor\":\"green\",\"summary\":\"Design full cloud severance architecture\",\"content\":\"SCOPE EXPANSION from the owner, in addition to yo…\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"f8f85567-ca9b-4cc7-bda2-061a6fdf6516","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:27.211Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message sent to update-gate-fable's inbox","msg_id":"513ec04e-1f51-4f39-89bb-6a90d10eda2d","routing":{"sender":"team-lead","target":"@update-gate-fable","targetColor":"green","summary":"Design full cloud severance architecture","content":"SCOPE EXPANSION from the owner, in addition to yo…"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fcbce589-ca65-46d2-a42f-e903a76c6754","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"f8f85567-ca9b-4cc7-bda2-061a6fdf6516","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14982000 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2c16dde8-00d0-4a2c-b58f-6cf19ddf8a1a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:27.228Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"2c16dde8-00d0-4a2c-b58f-6cf19ddf8a1a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ce2xrHqyDAUKuM7J6X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where things stand and what I'm doing.\n\n**Your immediate blocker:** that overlay is upstream's remote kill-switch. They pushed a server-side notice that renders a full-screen, non-dismissible gate based on your version number. \"Check for Update\" does nothing because your releases are fork-owned and don't track their feed, and \"Download Manually\" would install *their* build over your fork — so neither button can help you. An Opus agent is removing that gate permanently, with a marker so it survives future upstream merges.\n\n**Important:** installing the build already in Downloads won't clear it. That build predates the fix.\n\n**Your bigger ask (sever the cloud entirely, no sign-in):** I won't promise that blind. An audit is running across the desktop app, host-service and CLI to inventory every outbound destination — analytics, Sentry, auto-update, notices polling, auth/session, Electric sync — and to determine what a genuinely local, no-sign-in mode requires. In parallel, a Fable architect is designing the severance so it's one enforced choke point plus a CI gate that *fails* if a future merge adds a new phone-home, rather than something that silently rots.\n\nTwo things stay untouched: your coding agents reaching model APIs directly, and the companion pairing over your own tunnel.\n\nOnce the audit lands I'll tell you plainly what can be cut, what it costs, and whether no-sign-in is achievable in this codebase — then build **one** installer containing the overlay fix plus whatever severance is safe, and put it in Downloads."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":426995,"output_tokens":500,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2106,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":426995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2106},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7d1ab093-f14b-4556-a21f-d94dde019984","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:12:39.935Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
