{"parentUuid":"c3a17ccc-dd6b-4c38-a636-414e5af49314","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8cqTQ66MCsMBirkT2fs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QnCo7rNKpRWSa6zcDkTYL1","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Fable architecture review is in — it CORRECTS the brief I gave you. Implement to this instead:\n\n1) CHOKE POINT = the shared filter, not the hook. Put the invariant in `filterApplicableNotices` (packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts:83). Both remote notices AND the synthesized legacy minimumVersion notice already flow through it (the hook pushes the synthetic one in BEFORE filtering, useDesktopNotices.ts:78-96). In the filter, for every notice that passes: map `severity: \"blocking\"` -> `\"warning\"` AND force `dismissible: true`. Hook-level or render-site-level suppression LEAKS (a future upstream caller of the filter, or a new render site, bypasses it).\n\n2) YOU WOULD HAVE MISSED A SECOND BLOCKING SURFACE: `NoticeDialog` with `dismissible: false` is an undismissable modal in its own right — no close button, Escape and outside-click prevented (NoticeDialog.tsx:48-49, 59-69). So a remote `warning + dismissible:false` bricks the UI even with UpdateRequiredPage unreachable. Forcing dismissible:true in the filter covers it; verify by reading that component.\n\n3) DEFENSE IN DEPTH: also neuter the `severity === \"blocking\"` branch at DesktopNotices.tsx:29 (becomes dead code, but catches a refactor that moves minimumVersion synthesis AFTER filtering).\n\n4) EXPLICITLY DO NOT TOUCH: the host-service min-version gate (useRemoteHostStatus.ts:73-80 vs MIN_HOST_SERVICE_VERSION from @superset/shared/host-version, rendered via WorkspaceHostIncompatibleState) — that threshold is compiled into OUR binary, is workspace-scoped, and has an escape route. Also keep the dev-only blocking preview path (useDesktopNotices.ts:40, DesktopNotices.tsx:20-27). Scope statement for the override: \"no data returned by GET /api/desktop/version may produce a non-dismissible surface.\"\n\n5) NEUTER the `install-update` notice CTA (NoticeDialog.tsx:35-39) and, if UpdateRequiredPage survives at all, its \"Download Manually\" -> COMPANY.CHANGELOG_URL (UpdateRequiredPage.tsx:52-54,119-121) which points at upstream's downloads. Leave `open-url` CTAs alone. Note as a standing risk in your report: the auto-update feed points at superset-sh/superset releases (auto-updater.ts:58-60) and is only held off Windows by `IS_AUTO_UPDATE_PLATFORM` (auto-updater.ts:52) — an upstream merge could extend that to Windows cleanly.\n\n6) TEST = behavioral invariant over the whole output set, NOT incidental names: in packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.test.ts, feed a maximally hostile raw payload through the REAL `desktopVersionResponseSchema.parse` + `filterApplicableNotices` pipeline (include a blocking notice, a warning+dismissible:false notice, and a below-minimumVersion payload) and assert for EVERY output notice: `severity !== \"blocking\" && dismissible === true`. Do NOT assert on UpdateRequiredPage/DesktopNoticesGate names or the severity enum shape — upstream renames those freely.\n\n7) MARKER: token in BOTH packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts and its test, with two tab-rooted lines in the FEATURES.md markers block (format per scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs:104-105; multi-root precedent (WATCHER-BLUE-STOMP) at FEATURES.md:119-120). The FEATURES.md row must state the invariant BEHAVIORALLY (\"remote data can never render a non-dismissible surface; blocking severity is downgraded at the shared filter\") because that text is the input to the (MERGE-SEMANTIC-GATE) review — the only layer that can catch a semantically NEW upstream blocking mechanism. Also state in the row that the synthetic minimum-version notice becomes permanently dismissible via the dismissals store, so a future semantic review doesn't \"fix\" it back.\n\nEverything else from my original brief stands (gates, no commit, no version bump, PowerShell not Bash). Report against THIS spec.","summary":"Correct update-gate fix per Fable review","to":"update-gate-opus","type":"message","recipient":"update-gate-opus","content":"Fable architecture review is in — it CORRECTS the…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_read_input_tokens":429101,"output_tokens":1973,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1973,"cache_read_input_tokens":429101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"6d3bd40b-b5ca-4443-97cb-7015fb222f45","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:15:31.637Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
