res=DropInputEventsWhilePaintHolding,LocalNetworkAccessChecks,NetworkServiceSandbox,ScreenAIOCREnabled,SpareRendererForSitePerProcess,TraceSiteInstanceGetProcessCreation --variations-seed-version --pseudonymization-salt-handle=1836,i,2848902652539657687,9502531183152638407,4 --trace-process-track-uuid=3190708990060038890 --mojo-platform-channel-handle=3336 /prefetch:1\r\n\r\nProcessId : 31932\r\ncmd       : C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\Superset.exe C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources\\app.asar\\dist\\main\\terminal-host.js\r\n\r\nProcessId : 42452\r\ncmd       : C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\Superset.exe C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources\\app.asar\\dist\\main\\pty-daemon.js --socket=\\\\.\\pipe\\superset-ptyd-b3820f0679d3\r\n\r\nProcessId : 2116\r\ncmd       : C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\Superset.exe C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources\\app.asar\\dist\\main\\host-service.js","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"94cec7f1-545d-47c7-a968-6634a7bda9aa","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"6d348e74-ce63-4e91-b585-34c114a7476b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14967217 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"535c72d0-5833-4f7a-9db5-84c487801a6a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:17:14.885Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:17:16.086Z","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","content":"<agent-message from=\"update-gate-fable\">\nPart 2: full-cloud-severance architecture (part 1 — the 5 update-gate answers — already delivered, unchanged).\n\n## Recommended layering: runtime egress fence at process boundaries (primary) + build-time env baking (hygiene), NOT a routing module or dependency surgery\n\nThe app has exactly three egress classes, each with a natural choke point the platform enforces for us:\n\n1. **Renderer/Chromium**: every renderer HTTP/WS goes through Electron sessions. The fork ALREADY has a main-process webRequest chokepoint on the `persist:superset` session — the Windows CORS shim at `apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts:445-462` (which also documents the known sink list: `api.superset.sh`, `*.posthog.com`, `*.sentry.io`, `app.outlit.ai`). Severance = a fork-owned policy module registering `webRequest.onBeforeRequest` DENY-BY-DEFAULT on every session before any window is created: allow `superset-app://`, `superset-icon://`, loopback, the user's tunnel host; cancel everything else with a loud log line.\n2. **Main-process node side**: posthog-node (`apps/desktop/src/main/lib/analytics/index.ts:14-15`), Sentry main (`main/index.ts:497`), auto-updater feed (`main/lib/auto-updater.ts:58-60`) bypass Chromium sessions. Both telemetry keys are already OPTIONAL in the env schemas (`apps/desktop/src/renderer/env.renderer.ts:24-26`; renderer posthog no-ops without a key, `renderer/lib/posthog.ts:9-11`) — so: build without keys AND hard-neuter `initSentry`/`getPostHog`/`setupAutoUpdater` in the severance module so a merge that introduces a default key can't re-arm them.\n3. **Host-service child process**: its cloud egress is entirely config-constructed — `cloudApiUrl` at `packages/host-service/src/serve.ts:64` → api client at `app.ts:102`, and the relay tunnel only starts if `RELAY_URL` is set (`serve.ts:140-143`, optional at `env.ts:22`). Severed mode: never pass RELAY_URL, swap the api-client construction for a local no-op provider, and add a boot assertion that FAILS LOUD if any non-loopback cloud URL reaches config.\n\nWhy the alternatives leak:\n- **Build-time env alone**: the cloud origins are schema DEFAULTS (`env.renderer.ts:18-27`) that regenerate on merges; several endpoints are hardcoded outside env entirely (`renderer/index.html:14` carries `superset-relay2.avi-6ac.workers.dev`; `main/index.ts:446` hardcodes posthog/sentry/outlit); and a dead origin makes callers retry-loop rather than not-call, while a NEW sink silently phones home. Keep env baking as hygiene, not enforcement.\n- **\"Single module every caller routes through\"**: unenforceable — upstream callers will never route through a fork module, and the nightly merge adds callers continuously. It's a convention, not an invariant.\n- **Dependency removal / per-call no-ops**: unbounded merge-conflict surface, violates the fork's merge-the-delta model, rots silently.\n\nThe fence is the SCREENREADER-GUARD-DRIFT pattern applied to networking: assert the invariant over the WHOLE egress surface at platform choke points, never over enumerated upstream call sites.\n\n## Local identity (no sign-in), modelled honestly\n\nToday: better-auth client with cloud baseURL (`renderer/lib/auth-client.ts:116`), AuthProvider hydrates the session, the `_authenticated` route tree + `activeOrganizationId` key the Electric collections, and the embedded host-service takes `ORGANIZATION_ID` from env (`apps/desktop/src/main/host-service/index.ts:36`).\n\nDesign: one fork-owned `localIdentity` provider that mints `{userId, organizationId}` ONCE at first boot as real UUIDs, persists them main-process-side (appState/host.db — DB is source of truth), and implements the auth-client session surface returning an honest session object tagged `provider: \"local\"`. Rules that keep it honest:\n- **Never re-mint** — re-keying the org orphans every org-scoped row.\n- **Same id format upstream uses** (UUID), but never a shared hardcoded constant like `\"local-org\"` — ids leak into backups and companion pairing and must not collide across installs.\n- **No fake credentials**: no token that looks server-verifiable, no stubbed success for genuinely-cloud capabilities (sharing, multi-device orgs, remote hosts via Superset's relay). Those surfaces go visibly absent/disabled, not mocked — a lie the code can't trip over is one that was never told.\n\n## Merge-durable, self-policing gate: `scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs`\n\nFrozen against repair edits like the other gate scripts. Three layers:\n- **Layer A — built-artifact scan (known sinks)**: scan the whole built artifact set (all renderer chunks + main bundle + host-service bundle; no chunk-name assertions) for the cloud-origin hostname list from the Opus inventory (api/app/relay.superset.sh, the two workers.dev proxies, posthog.com, sentry.io, outlit.ai, …). Any hit outside the one allowlisted severance-policy chunk fails. False-positive control: match hostnames only, never words like \"analytics\"; allowlist entries carry a per-line justification.\n- **Layer B — fence-mounted proof (novel sinks)**: a static hostname list cannot catch a brand-new endpoint — the deny-by-default fence catches that at runtime (blocked + logged loudly, i.e. fails loud instead of phoning home). The gate's job is proving the fence exists and runs first: marker tokens in the fence module plus a unit test asserting `onBeforeRequest` is registered on every session before window creation against the single fork-owned allowlist. In practice most new upstream sinks also trip Layer A anyway, since upstream reuses its existing api origin.\n- **Layer C — config assertions**: host-service refuses to boot severed with any non-loopback `cloudApiUrl` or any `RELAY_URL`; the build asserts POSTHOG_KEY/SENTRY_DSN are unset.\n\nWiring: run in the build's verify step + nightly gates; FEATURES.md row states the invariant in behavioral terms (\"no first-party cloud or telemetry egress; deny-by-default; allowlist = loopback + user tunnel + FCM\") so `(MERGE-SEMANTIC-GATE)` reviews new upstream network features against it; markers-block entries for both the fence module and the gate script.\n\n## Explicitly untouched (fence non-goals)\n\n- **Coding agents → model APIs**: claude/codex CLIs are ptys spawned by host-service — separate OS processes that never traverse Electron sessions or host-service's network stack. The fence cannot and must not touch them; no allowlist entry needed. Same for git/gh child processes.\n- **Local host-service**: loopback allowed at every layer.\n- **Companion bridge/pairing**: inbound rides the user's own Cloudflare tunnel; outbound FCM pushes (the companion-alerts feature) need an FCM allowlist entry + the config-derived tunnel hostname, each with justification.\n\n## Consequences to surface to the owner (not silently absorbed)\n\n1. **This is a data-plane migration, not an unplugging.** No sign-in breaks the Electric-backed collections (org-keyed, served through the cloud API — `renderer/routes/_authenticated/providers/CollectionsProvider/collections.ts:270`), the chat runtime service, Linear image proxy, and remote hosts via Superset's relay. The fork already moved the workspace universe to host-served data (`(KANBAN-HOST-SOURCE)`), and upstream ships a local SQLite persistence layer (`createElectronSQLitePersistence`) — the remaining Electric surfaces must move onto those. Phase it: (1) telemetry kill + notices override + fence in log-only mode validated against the Opus inventory; (2) local identity + sign-in removal; (3) data-plane localization, then flip the fence to enforce. Each phase independently verifiable, and log-only-first means the fence's allowlist is proven complete before it can break the user.\n2. **AGENTS.md conflict**: the fork's own non-negotiable says \"v2-only, forever — the v2 CLOUD/host-service stack is pinned on\". Severance redefines that sentence; it must be rewritten in the same commit, or the semantic gate will actively defend the cloud paths against this work.\n3. **Accepted losses to confirm with the owner**: cross-device sync, sharing, and remote hosts through Superset's relay are gone by design. If the owner uses any of them (the companion feature suggests heavy single-machine use, but confirm), that's a scope decision, not a detail.\n</agent-message>"}
