had overwritten the staged snippet. I re-staged the identical 579-char snippet via `Set-Clipboard`, cleared the input (Ctrl+A, Delete), pasted, verified it visually complete (ending `})()`) before pressing Enter. No self-XSS \"allow pasting\" prompt appeared.\n- **DevTools is still open** (detached window, hwnd 6560096, right-hand side). `Ctrl+Shift+I` failed to close it from either the Superset window or DevTools itself. Step 9 was optional so I stopped rather than clicking its close button. The user can close it; the stub is independent of DevTools.\n- **No reload performed** at any point; Superset never closed or restarted. Terminals confirmed alive throughout (console showed 7 live `terminalId`s, and terminal output is rendering).\n- **Stub is session-scoped:** it lives only in the current renderer JS context. Any renderer reload or app restart brings the overlay back until the patched build is installed.\n- Incidental: two `Superset Setup` dialogs (pid 1164) are open on monitor 0 — untouched, outside scope.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>498201</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>29</tool_uses><duration_ms>417270</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
