{"parentUuid":"030da615-79ed-48d1-9db7-5b38109978d3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"65c41137-bd16-44d3-a5f5-ea031f5aa22d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014FLY2Lz3RQ3UEBq64shBGF","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pairing\\commit-msg-gate.txt (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"534bb389-57f4-446b-9f59-a5ad20acc14e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:30:51.556Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pairing\\commit-msg-gate.txt","content":"fix(desktop): upstream can no longer gate this fork behind a forced update\n\n(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) Upstream's notice API pushed a `blocking` notice\nthat replaced the whole window with a non-dismissible forced-update page.\nOn this fork both its buttons are dead ends: \"Check for Update\" can never\nsatisfy an upstream minimum (our releases are fork-owned and our updater\ndoes not track upstream) and \"Download Manually\" installs UPSTREAM's\nbuild over the fork. The user was locked out of a working app with live\nterminal sessions.\n\nRemote data may inform; it may never block, and it may never install\nsomeone else's artifact.\n\n- every notice crosses the parse boundary through `forkSafeNotice`:\n  `blocking` -> `warning`, `dismissible` forced true, and an\n  `install-update` CTA stripped. Done in the zod transform, so there is\n  no path into the app that skips it — a later caller of the filter, or\n  a new render site, inherits the invariant instead of bypassing it\n- `dismissible: true` matters as much as the severity: `NoticeDialog`\n  with `dismissible: false` is itself an undismissable modal (no close\n  button, Escape and outside-click suppressed), so a remote\n  `warning + dismissible:false` was a second gate hiding behind the\n  first\n- `minimumVersion`/`message` are no longer read: upstream synthesized a\n  non-dismissible blocking notice from them whenever the app was older\n  than the server's minimum, which was the other half of the gate\n- `UpdateRequiredPage` is deleted outright rather than left unreferenced,\n  so a merge cannot quietly wire it back up\n- the synthesized minimum-version notice is now permanently dismissible\n  via the dismissals store. That is intended, not a bug to \"fix\" back\n- untouched: the host-service min-version gate, whose threshold is a\n  constant compiled into OUR binary, is workspace-scoped and has an\n  escape route — that one is legitimately ours\n\nTests assert the invariant over the whole output set rather than any\nupstream name: a hostile payload (blocking notice, warning with\ndismissible:false, below-minimum version, install-update CTA) goes\nthrough the real schema parse plus filter, and every surviving notice is\nnon-blocking, dismissible, and free of an update-installing CTA.\n\nStanding risk recorded, not fixed here: the auto-update feed points at\nsuperset-sh/superset releases and is held off Windows only by\nIS_AUTO_UPDATE_PLATFORM.\n\n174 feature markers present; REFERR gate clean; 13 shared tests pass.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"030da615-79ed-48d1-9db7-5b38109978d3","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
