{"parentUuid":"90506568-bfe2-40ed-bd3e-b7d5693903da","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"65c41137-bd16-44d3-a5f5-ea031f5aa22d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Your questions have been answered: \"How far do you want the cloud severance to go? The architecture review says full severance is a data-plane migration, not just unplugging — no sign-in breaks the workspace-sync collections that are currently served through their cloud API, so those have to move onto local storage first.\"=\"Full severance, no sign-in\", \"If we go beyond Phase 1, these features go away by design. Which are you fine losing?\"=\"Cross-device sync, Sharing with others, Remote hosts via their relay\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KmB33ZcKG9mfnjyHN1Ebxg"}]},"uuid":"227ca605-f188-4d1e-bdfa-ed3942005906","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:34:20.238Z","toolUseResult":{"questions":[{"question":"How far do you want the cloud severance to go? The architecture review says full severance is a data-plane migration, not just unplugging — no sign-in breaks the workspace-sync collections that are currently served through their cloud API, so those have to move onto local storage first.","header":"Severance scope","options":[{"label":"Phase 1 only: telemetry + phone-home (Recommended)","description":"Kill analytics/PostHog, Sentry crash reporting, the notices poll and the upstream auto-update feed. Add a deny-by-default network fence in log-only mode first so I can prove nothing legitimate breaks. Keeps sign-in and workspace sync working. Low risk, ships fast."},{"label":"Full severance, no sign-in","description":"Phase 1, plus remove sign-in and mint a permanent local identity, plus move any cloud-backed data onto the local SQLite/host-service layer, then switch the fence to enforcing. Bigger job, and it means giving up cross-device sync, sharing, and remote hosts via their relay."},{"label":"Stop after the update fix","description":"Do nothing further on severance for now; just keep the update-gate fix that's already building."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"If we go beyond Phase 1, these features go away by design. Which are you fine losing?","header":"Accepted losses","options":[{"label":"Cross-device sync","description":"Workspaces/settings syncing between machines via their cloud. Confirm you don't rely on this."},{"label":"Sharing with others","description":"Sharing workspaces or sessions with anyone else through their cloud."},{"label":"Remote hosts via their relay","description":"Connecting to remote hosts routed through Superset's relay service. Your own Cloudflare tunnel and companion pairing are unaffected either way."},{"label":"None of these — ask me first","description":"I might use one of these — stop and check with me before cutting anything in this list."}],"multiSelect":true}],"answers":{"How far do you want the cloud severance to go? The architecture review says full severance is a data-plane migration, not just unplugging — no sign-in breaks the workspace-sync collections that are currently served through their cloud API, so those have to move onto local storage first.":"Full severance, no sign-in","If we go beyond Phase 1, these features go away by design. Which are you fine losing?":"Cross-device sync, Sharing with others, Remote hosts via their relay"},"annotations":{}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"90506568-bfe2-40ed-bd3e-b7d5693903da","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
