{"parentUuid":"e2301efe-a0b3-431a-89a6-ac4cc0e0298a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8eJregyPgYbs2vPhpbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MLv6eugoiiRKWMBmBzDoxN","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"DECISION RECORDED by the owner: FULL severance, NO sign-in. Accepted losses, confirmed explicitly: cross-device sync, sharing with others, and remote hosts via Superset's relay. Your own tunnel/companion pairing and the coding agents' direct model API access are OUT of scope and must keep working.\n\nYour inventory is now the foundation for a 3-phase implementation, so send it NOW even if incomplete. I need, in priority order:\n1. Every telemetry/crash/analytics sink with file:line, and whether POSTHOG_KEY / SENTRY_DSN are optional at build time (so a keyless build no-ops) or have defaults that would re-arm them.\n2. The auto-update feed URL + exactly what holds it off Windows.\n3. What the app reads off the cloud that a no-sign-in local mode must replace: enumerate what consumes activeOrganizationId / session user id, and which Electric/TanStack collections are cloud-served vs already host/SQLite-served.\n4. Where a stub identity must be injected for the _authenticated guards and protectedProcedure to pass with zero remote calls, and any place that assumes server-assigned ids.\n5. Anything that lives ONLY in their cloud for this user and would be unreachable after severance.\nCite file:line. Mark anything you could not determine and name the file that would settle it. Do not edit.","summary":"Full severance approved, send inventory","to":"network-audit-opus","type":"message","recipient":"network-audit-opus","content":"DECISION RECORDED by the owner: FULL severance, N…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1143,"cache_read_input_tokens":474924,"output_tokens":1014,"outp