{"parentUuid":"224faf78-6ed8-4722-9a8f-9fa7635510b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8efn8uuUNhMjLHGsRei","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HNQamfMZaFD5z7UXjZu263","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fable review update-gate commit","model":"fable","name":"gate-review-fable","prompt":"Adversarial code review, read-only. NEVER edit, commit, or push. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main). Repository files only — never read user shell/profile files or home-directory credentials. Bash is broken in this environment; use Read/Grep/Glob and PowerShell for git.\n\nREVIEW TARGET: commit 9b5d2f7c4c \"fix(desktop): upstream can no longer gate this fork behind a forced update\" (10 files, parent 42e3caf4e3). Get the diff with PowerShell, e.g.:\n  git -C \"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\" show 9b5d2f7c4c --stat\n  git -C \"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\" show 9b5d2f7c4c -- <path>\n\nWHY IT EXISTS: upstream's `GET /api/desktop/version` pushed a `blocking` notice that replaced this fork's whole window with a non-dismissible forced-update page. On this fork both its CTAs are dead ends — \"Check for Update\" can never satisfy an upstream minimum (fork-owned releases, updater does not track upstream) and \"Download Manually\" installs UPSTREAM's build over the fork. A user with live terminal sessions was locked out. This build is ALREADY COMPILING for the user to install, so a real defect here matters now.\n\nTHE INVARIANT THE COMMIT CLAIMS: no data returned by that endpoint may (a) block the UI, (b) be undismissable, or (c) offer a CTA that installs an upstream artifact. Implemented as `forkSafeNotice` inside the zod transform at the parse boundary (packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts), `forkVisibleNotices` dropping the `minimumVersion` synthesis, `UpdateRequiredPage` deleted, and a marker-gated FEATURES.md row.\n\nVERIFY, adversarially — try to BREAK the invariant:\n1. Find ANY path from that endpoint's payload to a non-dismissible or app-covering surface that survives this change. Consider: a caller that constructs a DesktopNotice without going through `desktopVersionResponseSchema.parse`; `filterApplicableNotices` called directly; the dev-preview store path; `NoticeDialog`'s dismissible handling (no close button / Escape+outside-click suppression); the command-palette action that was touched; any main-process consumer.\n2. Check the zod transform is actually applied on every parse path — including `.default([])`, nullish/optional wrappers, and any other schema that embeds the notice schema or re-parses raw JSON.\n3. Confirm deleting UpdateRequiredPage left no live import, broken barrel export, or dangling route/lazy import that would crash the renderer at runtime rather than at typecheck.\n4. Read the new/changed tests: do they assert the INVARIANT over the whole output set, or do they merely re-state the implementation? Would they still fail if someone reverted `forkSafeNotice` but kept the rest? Name any hostile payload shape the tests miss (e.g. severity added by a future upstream enum value, cta.action variants, dismissible absent).\n5. Judge merge-durability honestly: what would a plausible upstream refactor do to make this silently stop working, and would the marker + FEATURES.md row + tests actually catch it? Per the fork's SCREENREADER-GUARD-DRIFT lesson, flag any assertion that depends on incidental upstream names.\n6. Flag anything the commit message claims that the code does not actually do.\n\nAlso state whether the host-service min-version gate (useRemoteHostStatus / MIN_HOST_SERVICE_VERSION / WorkspaceHostIncompatibleState) was correctly left intact, since that one is legitimately fork-owned.\n\nReport only findings you have VERIFIED, ranked BLOCKER / MAJOR / MINOR, each with absolute file:line, a one-sentence defect, a concrete payload-or-state -> failure scenario, and the minimal fix. If the invariant genuinely holds, say SHIP and name the strongest attack you tried that failed. Be concise; no code dumps.","subagent_type":"code-reviewer-fable"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":137,"cache_read_input_tokens":477250,"output_tokens":2015,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":137,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2015,"cache_read_input_tokens":477250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":137},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"b00b4c79-ec4b-492a-bb24-cf08bef542d8","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:39:37.516Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
