{"parentUuid":"b58d8fab-2dcc-4725-90ce-fc0095be6ec5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a87295bc-4084-4088-a64c-7a7175a619c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Another Claude session sent a message:\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"gate-review-fable\" color=\"purple\" summary=\"Review 9b5d2f7c4c: FIX-FIRST, 1 MAJOR 1 MINOR\">\nReview of 9b5d2f7c4c (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE). Verdict: FIX-FIRST.\n\nNote on method: Bash is broken here (profile parse error on every invocation) and I have no PowerShell tool, so I could not run git locally. Verified instead that HEAD == 9b5d2f7c4c via .git/HEAD + refs (so the working tree IS the post-commit state), reviewed the actual files, and fetched the parent-commit version of the hook from GitHub to separate introduced vs inherited code.\n\n[MAJOR] apps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts:83\n`lt(appVersion, data.minimumVersion)` passes the remote minimumVersion string to semver.lt unvalidated (schema is z.string(), packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts:32). semver.lt THROWS on any non-strict-semver value (\"1.15\", \"latest\"), inside a render-time useMemo. DesktopNoticesGate is mounted in the root route component (routes/-layout.tsx:20), so the throw hits the root errorComponent and replaces the whole window; reload refetches the same payload and crashes again. That is an app-covering, undismissable surface driven by exactly the endpoint this commit claims can no longer do that. VERIFIED INHERITED: same line exists in parent 42e3caf4e3 (checked raw file on GitHub) — not introduced by this commit, but the commit touched this file and asserts the invariant. Fix: one-line guard — skip synthesis unless semver.valid(semver.coerce(data.minimumVersion)) (or normalize in schema); add a non-semver minimumVersion case to the hostile-payload test. Installing this build is still strictly safer than the gated one; guard can follow immediately.\n\n[MINOR] FEATURES.md:281-282\nMarker block lists only the