{"parentUuid":"d2032292-80d6-450e-95f8-ef8d04ec5450","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8fJWcJGX6qKhNhFBSqX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — Fable is right, and it's worse than it looks: the hook **still** synthesizes the blocking notice from `minimumVersion` (line 83), so the commit message's claim that `minimumVersion` is no longer read is false, and `semver.lt` throws on a malformed value, which would blank your window via the root error boundary. Fixing now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":482822,"output_tokens":3157,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1125},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":482822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"57327365-ef81-45c9-bc46-dd1b6120ea05","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:47:44.862Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"57327365-ef81-45c9-bc46-dd1b6120ea05","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8fJWcJGX6qKhNhFBSqX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FFCFDZEKFBQLMhihzL3JGS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix minimumVersion crash path","model":"opus","name":"gate-fix-opus","prompt":"Urgent, small, surgical fix in C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main, HEAD 9b5d2f7c4c). Repository files only; never read user shell/profile files. Bash is broken — use PowerShell. Do NOT commit or push; I will.\n\nCONTEXT: commit 9b5d2f7c4c added (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) so upstream's notice API can never blank this fork's window. A Fable review found the job half-done, and the user is currently running on a temporary DevTools stub, so this ships immediately.\n\nDEFECT 1 [MAJOR] — apps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts:78-98.\nThe hook STILL synthesizes the blocking minimum-version notice itself, calling `lt(appVersion, data.minimumVersion)` on an unvalidated remote string (schema is plain z.string()). `semver.lt` THROWS on any non-strict-semver value (\"1.15\", \"latest\", \"\"). That throw happens inside a render-time useMemo in DesktopNoticesGate, which is mounted in the root route component — so it hits the root errorComponent and replaces the whole window, and a reload refetches the same payload and crashes again. That is exactly the app-covering, undismissable surface this feature claims to have eliminated, reachable from the very endpoint in question.\nAlso: because the synthesis is still here, the commit message's claim that `minimumVersion`/`message` \"are no longer read\" is currently FALSE, and `forkVisibleNotices` in packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.ts (which exists precisely to drop that synthesis) is unused by this hook.\n\nREQUIRED FIX for defect 1 — delete the code path, do not guard it:\n- Remove the synthesized minimum-version notice from the hook entirely (the notice object, the `lt(...)` call, the now-unused `lt` import and MINIMUM_VERSION_NOTICE_ID constant if they become dead).\n- Have the hook call `forkVisibleNotices(data, ctx)` from @superset/shared/desktop-notices instead of assembling notices + calling `filterApplicableNotices` directly. That is what `forkVisibleNotices` is for, and it makes the invariant structural: no semver comparison against remote data survives, so the throw is impossible rather than merely handled.\n- Verify no other caller in the shipped desktop app reads `minimumVersion` or `message` from that payload. If the schema fields are now unread anywhere, LEAVE the schema fields in place (the server still sends them; dropping them would make parse stricter than the wire) but say so in your report.\n- Update the code comments that currently describe the synthesis-then-downgrade flow so they describe what the code actually does now. Do not leave a comment claiming behaviour that no longer exists.\n\nDEFECT 2 [MINOR] — FEATURES.md marker block (around lines 281-282) lists only the two packages/shared files, but (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) tokens also live in the renderer half (useDesktopNotices.ts, components/DesktopNotices/DesktopNotices.tsx, components/DesktopNotices/components/NoticeDialog/NoticeDialog.tsx, commandPalette/modules/actions/commands.tsx) where no gate checks them. Add marker rows so the renderer half is gate-protected too. Read scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs first for the exact format (tab-rooted lines) and follow the existing multi-root precedent. Only add roots for files that genuinely still carry the token after your fix — if your edit removes the token from a file, do not add a row for it.\n\nTESTS — add to packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.test.ts (and/or a hook-level test if one is warranted):\n- A payload whose `minimumVersion` is NOT valid semver (\"latest\", \"1.15\", \"\") must not throw anywhere and must not produce any notice from that field.\n- A below-minimum payload (valid semver, appVersion older) must produce NO synthesized blocking notice at all now.\n- Keep the existing hostile-payload invariant test passing (every surviving notice non-blocking, dismissible, no install-update CTA).\n\nGATES — run and report each: `bun test src/desktop-notices.test.ts` in packages/shared; the feature-marker gate (IMPORTANT: it needs grep on PATH — run `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"` first, else it falsely reports ~175 missing); `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs`; Biome on the files you touched; and a scoped typecheck. Known-pre-existing and NOT yours to fix: packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.test.ts already fails Biome's formatter on main (CRLF baseline) and apps/desktop carries ~22 pre-existing tsc diagnostics — report them as pre-existing, do not reformat unrelated files.\n\nReport: exact diff summary, whether `lt`/semver is now entirely gone from the hook, marker rows added, test names, gate results, and anything you deliberately left alone.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":482822,"output_tokens":3157,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1125},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":482822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"a1c66a22-8183-4280-a28c-26e42103625e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:48:08.257Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"ex