{"parentUuid":"eeee50f5-9113-4dae-9b39-53255c51c8cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d2bfa194-71e2-411f-b206-6f40acc11236","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mijrdzt5aGgebqbv9NpeQj","type":"tool_result","content":"bun test v1.3.14 (0d9b296a)\r\n\r\n 20 pass\r\n 0 fail\r\n 40 expect() calls\r\nRan 20 tests across 1 file. [160.00ms]\r\n  OK   (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) (apps/desktop/src/renderer/components/DesktopNotices/components/NoticeDialog/NoticeDialog.tsx)\r\n  OK   (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) (apps/desktop/src/renderer/commandPalette/modules/actions/commands.tsx)\r\nAll 178 feature markers present.\r\n=== marker rows ===\r\n\r\n+++ b/FEATURES.md\r\n+| No remote update gate | **no data returned by `GET /api/desktop/version` may render a non-dismissible surface.** Upstream's notice API can brick this \r\nfork two ways, and only one of them is named `blocking`: a `blocking` notice replaced the whole window with `UpdateRequiredPage`, a forced-update screen \r\nwith no way out whose buttons are \"Check for Update\" (a guaranteed no-op — this fork's releases are fork-owned and its updater does not track upstream, so \r\nno check can ever satisfy an upstream minimum) and \"Download Manually\" (which sends the user to upstream's downloads and replaces this build); and ANY \r\nseverity with `dismissible: false` renders as a modal with no close button, no Escape and no outside-click, so a `warning` is just as good a brick. Hit \r\nlive on 2026-08-17 against v1.20.2 with a background-sync retirement notice the user could neither satisfy nor dismiss. The invariant is enforced at ONE \r\nchoke point — `filterApplicableNotices` in packages/shared, which every notice the renderer can show passes through — where each notice is rewritten to at \r\nmost `warning` and always dismissible. It is deliberately NOT enforced at the hook or at a render site: a future upstream caller of the filter, or a \r\nsecond render site, would bypass those. The downgrade runs BEFORE the applicability check, which is what makes a dismissal PERMANENT: the dismissals store \r\nis only consulted for a dismissible notice, so a notice the server authored `blocking`/unclosable is dismissed once and never returns on a later poll — a \r\nsemantic review must not \"restore\" the pre-check ordering or such a notice reappears every 30 minutes forever. The legacy `minimumVersion`/`message` pair \r\nis parsed (the server still sends it) but read by NOTHING: upstream synthesized an unclosable notice from it whenever the app was below the server's \r\nminimum, which this fork can never satisfy, and compared the raw remote string with `semver.lt`, which THROWS on a non-strict-semver value (\"1.15\", \r\n\"latest\", \"\") inside a render-time `useMemo` under the root route — one such value replaced the whole window and every reload after it. The renderer \r\ntherefore reaches notices only through `forkVisibleNotices`, which takes the payload and returns `filterApplicableNotices(data.notices, ctx)`, so no \r\nversion comparison against remote data survives anywhere and the throw is impossible rather than merely handled — a merge must not reintroduce the \r\nsynthesis. Two layers sit behind it: `UpdateRequiredPage` is DELETED and no severity has a full-screen branch left, and the notice dialog honours only \r\n`open-url` CTAs — an `install-update` CTA renders no button, because it drives the auto-updater whose feed is upstream's releases. Dev command-palette \r\npreviews are NOT remote data and pass through as authored (the dev Escape handler is their way out). An unparseable payload still fails open as no \r\nnotices. Out of scope on purpose: the host-service minimum-version gate, whose threshold is compiled into our own binary, is workspace-scoped and has an \r\nescape route | `(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)` |\r\n+(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)\tapps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts\r\n+(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)\tapps/desktop/src/renderer/components/DesktopNotices/DesktopNotices.tsx\r\n+(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)\tapps/desktop/src/renderer/components/DesktopNotices/components/NoticeDialog/NoticeDialog.tsx\r\n+(NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE)\tapps/desktop/src/renderer/commandPalette/modules/actions/commands.tsx","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c25a47c8-1a53-49c4-896a-5798a5158c8c","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:01:41.526Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"bun test v1.3.14 (0d9b296a)\r\n\r\n 20 pass\r\n 0 fail\r\n 40 expect() calls\r\nRan 20 tests across 1 file. [160.00ms]\r\n  OK   (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) (apps/desktop/src/renderer/components/DesktopNotices/components/NoticeDialog/NoticeDialog.tsx)\r\n  OK   (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) (apps/desktop/src/renderer/commandPalette/modules/actions/commands.tsx)\r\nAll 178 feature markers present.\r\n=== marker rows ===\r\n\r\n+++ b/FEATURES.md\r\n+| No remote update gate | **no data returned by `GET /api/desktop/version` may render a non-dismissible surface.** Upstream's notice API can brick this \r\nfork two ways, and only one of them is named `blocking`: a `blocking` notice replaced the whole window with `UpdateRequiredPage`, a forced-update screen \r\nwith no way out whose buttons are \"Check for Update\" (a guaranteed no-op — this fork's releases are fork-owned and its updater does not track upstream, so \r\nno check can ever satisfy an upstream minimum) and \"Download Manually\" (which sends the user to upstream's downloads and replaces this build); and ANY \r\nseverity with `dismissible: false` renders as a modal with no close button, no Escape and no outside-click, so a `warning` is just as good a brick. Hit \r\nlive on 2026-08-17 against v1.20.2 with a background-sync retirement notice the user could neither satisfy nor dismiss. The invariant is enforced at ONE \r\nchoke point — `filterApplicableNotices` in packages/shared, which every notice the renderer can show passes through — where each notice is rewritten to at \r\nmost `warning` and always dismissible. It is