{"parentUuid":"e21c72df-3bf5-41f9-b8c3-f85c1f7adac4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8gvQZ3MupN5fnnWVHJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The broad audit is taking a while, so I'm parallelising it with a tightly-scoped one that only needs to answer Phase 1."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":495987,"output_tokens":1828,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":366},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1828,"cache_read_input_tokens":495987,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"4235d03b-3631-4c3e-8fe6-32430a49beec","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:08:47.817Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"4235d03b-3631-4c3e-8fe6-32430a49beec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8gvQZ3MupN5fnnWVHJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YNzqudWBnFSJjAuApuB2tk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit telemetry and phone-home sinks","model":"opus","name":"phase1-audit-opus","prompt":"Narrow, fast, read-only audit. NO edits. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main). Repository files only — never read user shell/profile files or home-directory credentials. Bash is broken; use Read/Grep/Glob (+ PowerShell if needed).\n\nThe owner wants this Windows ARM64 fork to stop talking to Superset's cloud entirely. This audit covers PHASE 1 ONLY: telemetry, crash reporting, and phone-home that can be cut with ZERO functional loss. Do NOT audit auth/session/Electric data-plane — a separate agent has that.\n\nSCOPE: only code that ships in the packaged desktop app and its child processes — apps/desktop (main + renderer + preload), packages/host-service, packages/cli, and shared packages they import. EXCLUDE apps/api, apps/web, apps/marketing, apps/admin, apps/docs, apps/mobile. Flag anything ambiguous.\n\nANSWER EXACTLY THESE, each with absolute file:line:\n\n1. PRODUCT ANALYTICS. Every PostHog/Segment/Amplitude/GA/Mixpanel/custom-event sink, in BOTH the renderer and the main process (and host-service if present). For each: the init site, the key/DSN source, and — critically — whether the key is OPTIONAL (absent key = no-op, cut for free at build time) or has a hardcoded/default value that would still fire. Quote the env schema lines that decide it.\n\n2. CRASH / ERROR REPORTING. Sentry (any @sentry/* package, init call, dsn, tracesSampleRate, replay/session-replay), Electron `crashReporter`, breakpad/minidump upload URLs. Same optional-vs-default analysis. Note whether session replay or PII-bearing context is enabled.\n\n3. AUTO-UPDATE. The feed URL, the publish/provider config (electron-builder), every call path that hits it, and EXACTLY what prevents it running on Windows today — quote the constant/condition and say how load-bearing it is (i.e. could an upstream merge flip it on for Windows in a one-line change?).\n\n4. TIMER-DRIVEN CALLS to their API. Anything polling on an interval or on window focus/reconnect (the desktop-notices poll is one — find the rest). Give the interval and endpoint.\n\n5. HARDCODED REMOTE HOSTS anywhere in shipped code or shipped HTML/templates — including any *.workers.dev, relay, CDN, font, image-proxy, or marketing URL. Grep for hostnames, not for words like \"analytics\". Include apps/desktop/src/renderer/index.html and any CSP/allowlist declarations (there is a Windows CORS shim in apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts that documents a sink list — read it and verify whether that list is complete or stale).\n\n6. THE FENCE POINT. Confirm whether every renderer-originated request goes through an Electron session we control (name the session, e.g. `persist:superset`, and the file where it is created), and list what does NOT go through it (main-process node fetch, host-service child process, spawned CLIs). This determines where a deny-by-default egress fence can actually be enforced.\n\n7. For each item in 1–5, state the CHEAPEST honest kill: build-time env absence, code no-op, config change, or dependency removal. Prefer \"absent key\" where the code genuinely no-ops.\n\nDELIVERABLE: a compact table-like list, then a short \"cut list\" ordered by risk (safest first), then explicitly: anything in scope you could NOT determine, naming the file that would settle it. No speculation — cite or say unknown. Under 60 lines if you can.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":495987,"output_tokens":1828,"output_tokens_detai