{"parentUuid":"7c99c062-9a44-4ed4-8d9f-191b7ab6cc03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8hsMJrdYYxCjBP6mPCs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No root `.env`, so PostHog and Sentry are already inert in your builds — the work there is *enforcing* that, not switching it off. Putting the Phase 1 plan to Fable for audit."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":504805,"output_tokens":3070,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3070,"cache_read_input_tokens":504805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"20f81a73-3929-49d3-9ee2-2907c7012ea3","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:21:08.858Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"20f81a73-3929-49d3-9ee2-2907c7012ea3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8hsMJrdYYxCjBP6mPCs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FGT8y5LAmdMqw3vurPNhBV","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit severance Phase 1 plan","model":"fable","name":"phase1-plan-fable","prompt":"Read-only PLAN AUDIT. No edits. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main, HEAD 46da2b8b9f). Repository files only — never read user shell/profile files or home-directory credentials. Bash is broken; use Read/Grep/Glob.\n\nOWNER DECISION (fixed, not up for debate): this Windows ARM64 fork must stop talking to Superset's cloud entirely, with NO sign-in, eventually. Accepted losses, explicitly confirmed: cross-device sync, sharing with others, remote hosts via Superset's relay. OUT OF SCOPE and must keep working: the user's coding agents reaching model APIs directly (claude/codex CLIs are ptys), the local host-service, and the fork's own companion bridge/pairing over the user's own Cloudflare tunnel (incl. FCM pushes).\n\nThis audit covers PHASE 1 ONLY — telemetry/phone-home that can go with no functional loss. Phases 2 (local identity, no sign-in) and 3 (data-plane localization, fence to enforcing) come later.\n\nAUDITED FACTS ESTABLISHED (verify any you doubt, don't re-derive wholesale):\n- Repo-root `.env` does NOT exist, and CI injects no keys, so PostHog and Sentry are already inert in shipped builds. BUT apps/desktop/electron.vite.config.ts:22 loads `../../.env` with override:true, so a future local key would bake in silently.\n- PostHog: renderer lib/posthog.ts:8-32 (guard :9, capture_exceptions:true), main lib/analytics/index.ts:9-22 (guard :10, flushAt:1). Keys optional in env.main.ts:24 / env.renderer.ts:24. ALSO serves feature flags at ~7 call sites (HiringBanner, usePaneRegistry chat-v3, useCommandWatcher DISABLE_REMOTE_AGENT, useNewWorkspaceScreenVariant, V1AutoMigration, settings cloud pages CLOUD_ACCESS) — all already resolve false/undefined in fork builds.\n- Telemetry opt-out is a STUB: settings router always returns true; DEFAULT_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=true. Absent key is the only real switch.\n- Sentry: main lib/sentry.ts:11 + renderer lib/sentry.ts:9 (both gated on DSN + production), host-service src/sentry.ts:5-31 gated on HOST_SERVICE_SENTRY_DSN passed only when packaged. No crashReporter, no session replay. tracesSampleRate 0, sendDefaultPii false. Capture middleware on EVERY publicProcedure (apps/desktop/src/lib/trpc/index.ts:48-78).\n- LIVE, NOT key-gated: bundled CLI posts an event on every command — packages/cli/src/lib/analytics.ts:9 via packages/cli/src/commands/middleware.ts:2, to SUPERSET_API_URL default https://api.superset.sh (packages/cli/src/lib/env.ts:9).\n- Auto-update: feed https://github.com/superset-sh/superset/releases/latest/download (main/lib/auto-updater.ts:58-60), 4h interval + boot check, held off Windows ONLY by `IS_AUTO_UPDATE_PLATFORM = PLATFORM.IS_MAC || PLATFORM.IS_LINUX` (auto-updater.ts:52). NO FEATURES.md marker covers this file.\n- Notices poll: 30min + focus + reconnect to /api/desktop/version (useDesktopNotices.ts:14,62). Already capped by the just-shipped (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE).\n- CSP renderer/index.html:21 allows https://*.posthog.com (script-src AND connect-src), https://*.sentry.io, sentry-ipc:, relay hosts; img-src/frame-src are `https: http:`.\n- Windows CORS shim main/index.ts:446 lists api.superset.sh, *.posthog.com, *.sentry.io, app.outlit.ai — STALE (outlit unreferenced elsewhere) and INCOMPLETE (omits Electric/relay/streams).\n- Fence point: ONE renderer session `persist:superset` (main/windows/main.ts:136). BYPASSES a session fence: main-process posthog-node, electron-updater, @sentry/electron main transport (renderer Sentry too, IPCMode.Classic), the host-service child process, the bundled CLI, spawned agent CLIs, pty-daemon.\n\nPROPOSED PHASE 1 (audit this, don't just approve it):\n1. Build-time enforcement: fail the build if NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY / SENTRY_DSN_DESKTOP / SENTRY_DSN_HOST_SERVICE / SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN are present, closing the electron.vite.config.ts:22 hole.\n2. No-op the CLI analytics call (the one genuinely live sink).\n3. Stop the notices poll entirely — no request to their API at all.\n4. Hard-disable auto-update on this fork (not just Windows) and put it under a FEATURES.md marker so an upstream one-line platform flip cannot re-point users at upstream releases.\n5. Tighten CSP (drop posthog/sentry origins) and delete the stale outlit entry from the CORS shim.\n6. Add a deny-by-default egress fence on persist:superset in LOG-ONLY mode first, so the allowlist is proven complete before it can break the user.\n7. Add scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs: scan the whole built artifact set for cloud hostnames (allowlisted with per-line justification), assert telemetry keys unset, assert the fence is registered before any window is created. Frozen against repair edits like the other gate scripts.\n\nANSWER PRECISELY:\na. Is the ORDER right, and is anything in Phase 1 actually a Phase 2/3 dependency in disguise? Flag anything that will visibly change behaviour for the user today (feature flags going from undefined to explicitly-false, notices disappearing, the Check-for-Updates menu item, telemetry settings UI).\nb. Item 4: hard-disable vs marker-pin — which, and where exactly should the kill live so a merge cannot reintroduce it? Should the electron-builder publish config (electron-builder.ts:38-41, owner superset-sh) also change, given our releases go to khairm/superset-windows-arm64?\nc. Item 6: what EXACTLY should the log-only fence log so the allowlist can be proven complete without leaking secrets into logs (URLs can carry tokens)? Where must it be registered, and how do we prove it runs before the first request rather than merely before window creation?\nd. Item 7: is a built-artifact hostname scan sound given the audit found hostnames living in env DEFAULTS and in index.html placeholders? Name the false-negative it cannot catch and what covers that instead. How should the allowlist be expressed so legitimate traffic (loopback, the user's tunnel, FCM, model APIs) is not flagged?\ne. Item 1: is failing the build the right move, or should the build instead force the keys empty? Consider that a maintainer might legitimately want a local .env for other vars.\nf. What in Phase 1 risks breaking the fork's OWN features — companion pairing/FCM, the pty/terminal stack, kanban/host-served data, the nightly merge machinery?\ng. The fork's AGENTS.md non-negotiable says \"v2-only, forever — the v2 cloud/host-service stack is pinned on; never v1\". Does Phase 1 already conflict with that sentence, or only Phase 2/3? Give the exact rewrite you'd apply and when.\nh. Anything MISSING from Phase 1 that is a live phone-home the audit or I overlooked.\n\nBe decision-ready and concise. Rank your corrections by whether they block starting implementation.","subagent_type":"architect-fable"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":504805,"output_tokens":3070,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3070,"cache_read_input_tokens":504805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"a64425f3-7945-42a0-bf81-a9a24503af2b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:21:46.944Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli