SKTOP, SENTRY_DSN_HOST_SERVICE, SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN. Exactly those four — a local .env for other vars (ports etc.) must keep working. Do NOT silently force-empty them; silent masking is the opposite of this repo's fail-loud rule. Note SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN also drives the build-time sourcemap-upload plugin blocks (~:38, ~:51), which is itself a phone-home — banning the token covers it.\n\n=== ITEM 2 — no-op the bundled CLI's per-command ping (the one genuinely live sink) ===\npackages/cli/src/lib/analytics.ts — gut the BODY of trackCommandInvoked so it performs no network call (currently posts api.analytics.captureEvent.mutate to SUPERSET_API_URL, default https://api.superset.sh, on EVERY command via packages/cli/src/commands/middleware.ts). Leave middleware.ts and the auth/resolveAuth chain INTACT — the bundled superset-cli preset and startup shim depend on it. Keep the function signature and call sites so nothing else changes.\n\n=== ITEM 3 — stop the notices poll, but DO NOT delete the pipeline ===\nCRITICAL (Fable B1): six (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) marker rows pin exact file paths (FEATURES.md ~281-286). Deleting the pipeline fails the marker gate and breaks the nightly. So: change ONLY the fetch inside apps/desktop/src/renderer/hooks/useDesktopNotices/useDesktopNotices.ts (~:61-72) so the query performs NO network request and yields an empty payload (`{ notices: [] }` shaped to satisfy the schema/type), and drop the refetchInterval/refetch-on-focus/reconnect churn that now has nothing to fetch. KEEP the whole downgrade/filter/render pipeline, NoticeDialog, and the dev command-palette preview path alive and functional. Extend the existing (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) FEATURES.md prose to record that the poll itself is now off.\n\n=== ITEM 4 — hard-disable auto-update on this fork, layered ===\n(a) In apps/desktop/src/main/lib/auto-updater.ts add ONE fork constant (e.g. FORK_AUTO_UPDATE_DISABLED) carrying a marker token, and early-return from setupAutoUpdater (~:334), checkForUpdates (~:202) and checkForUpdatesInteractive (~:222). Keep the kill INSIDE this module — do not rely on removing call sites in main/index.ts, which churns upstream. Today it is held off Windows only by `IS_AUTO_UPDATE_PLATFORM` (~:52), a one-line upstream flip away from pointing our users at superset-sh/superset releases.\n(b) apps/desktop/electron-builder.ts (~:38-42) publishes to owner superset-sh — this bakes an app-update.yml into the package naming upstream. Set `publish: null` (our releases go out via gh in CI) or point it at khairm/superset-windows-arm64. Explain which you chose.\n(c) The \"Check for Updates...\" entries in apps/desktop/src/main/lib/menu.ts (~:206) and apps/desktop/src/main/lib/tray/index.ts (~:228) become permanent no-ops. Do NOT leave a dead dialog: either remove them or relabel to open the FORK's releases page (github.com/khairm/superset-windows-arm64/releases). Pick one and say why.\n\n=== ITEM 5 — tighten CSP + CORS shim, surgically ===\napps/desktop/src/renderer/index.html (~:21): remove ONLY `https://*.posthog.com` (from BOTH script-src and connect-src), `https://*.sentry.io`, and `sentry-ipc:`. DO NOT touch `ws:`/`wss:`/`http://127.0.0.1:*` (terminals + host-service — removing these kills every terminal), `blob:`/`data:` (file previews), or the relay/api/electric entries (Phase 2/3).\napps/desktop/src/main/index.ts (~:446) CORS shim: delete the `app.outlit.ai`, `*.posthog.com` and `*.sentry.io` patterns. KEEP `api.superset.sh` — sign-in still needs it on Windows until Phase 2.\n\n=== ITEM 6 — egress fence, LOG-ONLY mode ===\nNew fork-owned module in the main process. Register `session.fromPartition(\"persist:superset\").webRequest.onBeforeRequest` in the boot path BEFORE the main window is created.\n- LOG ONLY. Cancel nothing. This phase proves the allowlist is complete.\n- CRITICAL (Fable B2): `persist:superset` is ALSO the browser-pane webview partition (see usePersistentWebview.ts ~:209 setting partition=\"persist:superset\"). Arbitrary user browsing MUST NOT be logged as app egress or the log is noise now and a broken feature later. Resolve `details.webContentsId` -> `webContents.fromId(...)` and treat `getType() === \"webview\"` as exempt (skip, or log to a clearly separate channel). Handle the id being absent/stale without throwing.\n- LOG ORIGIN ONLY: `scheme://host:port` + method + resourceType + initiator class (app-renderer | webview | unknown) + first-seen timestamp + count. NEVER log full URLs, paths or query strings — the pairing secret travels in a URL FRAGMENT and other URLs carry tokens. Dedupe in memory keyed on origin+resourceType, bounded, flush periodically.\n- Prove it runs before the first request with a RUNTIME assertion, not a comment: fence install sets a module flag and main-window creation throws loudly if it is unset.\n- Document honestly in-file: this sees session webRequests only. Main-process node fetch, electron-updater, @sentry/electron's main transport (renderer Sentry too, IPCMode.Classic), the host-service child, the bundled CLI, spawned agent CLIs and pty-daemon all BYPASS it.\n\n=== ITEM 7 — new gate: scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs ===\nPhase-scoped (Fable B3): in Phase 1, api.superset.sh / electric / streams / relay / superset.sh are LEGITIMATELY baked, so a blanket cloud-hostname scan can never go green. Include an explicit `phase` field so widening later is a one-line diff.\nPhase 1 assertions:\n- Built artifact set (all renderer chunks + main bundle + host-service bundle; assert over the WHOLE set, never named chunks — see the SCREENREADER-GUARD-DRIFT footgun) contains no `posthog.com`, `sentry.io`, `outlit.ai`.\n- The exact string `superset-sh/superset/releases` is absent from the built main bundle (this catches an upstream platform flip even if the constant in item 4 gets mangled).\n- No packaged `app-update.yml` names `superset-sh`.\n- Telemetry key shapes absent from artifacts (e.g. `phc_` prefix, Sentry DSN pattern) AND the four env vars unset at build time.\n- Allowlist expressed as `<literal hostname>\\t<justification>` lines, frozen alongside the gate. Entries: loopback (127.0.0.1, localhost, 0.0.0.0) and fcm/oauth2 googleapis hosts (companion push). Do NOT allowlist the user's tunnel host — it is runtime config, never baked, so a hit there is a real bug.\n- Match hostnames/literals, never words like \"analytics\" (false positives).\nWire it into the build's verify step. Add it to whatever mechanism freezes gate scripts against repair edits (AGENTS.md says gate scripts are frozen — find that enumeration and add this script explicitly).\n\n=== ITEM 8 — markers + docs (Fable B4: this is what stops the nightly reverting all of the above) ===\nEVERY upstream-owned file Phase 1 touches needs marker protection, not just the auto-updater. Add a FEATURES.md row (or rows) for cloud severance phase 1 with marker tokens in: electron.vite.config.ts (key ban), packages/cli/src/lib/analytics.ts (CLI no-op), apps/desktop/src/renderer/index.html (CSP), apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts (CORS shim), auto-updater.ts + electron-builder.ts (updater), the new fence module, and the new gate script. Extend the existing (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) row for the poll-off per item 3. Read FEATURES.md and scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs FIRST for the exact tab-rooted format and follow existing multi-root precedent.\nAGENTS.md: add ONE sentence to the non-negotiables recording that upstream telemetry/update/notice channels are severed as of Phase 1, so the nightly's semantic reviewer stops treating dead telemetry as breakage. Do NOT rewrite the \"v2-only, forever\" bullet yet — that lands at Phase 2 when sign-in goes.\n\n=== GATES (run and report each) ===\n- Feature-marker gate — IMPORTANT: needs grep on PATH or it falsely reports ~175 missing. Run `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"` first. Expect the count to rise from 178.\n- `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` (REFERR).\n- Your new `scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs` — run it. If it needs a build to check artifacts, say exactly what it does when artifacts are absent (it must fail loud or clearly skip, not silently pass).\n- Relevant unit tests, plus new tests where behaviour is testable (the key ban, the fence's webview exemption and origin-only logging, the CLI no-op).\n- Biome on touched files only. Scoped typecheck.\nKNOWN PRE-EXISTING, not yours: packages/shared/src/desktop-notices.test.ts fails Biome's formatter on main (CRLF baseline); apps/desktop carries ~22 tsc diagnostics. Report as pre-existing; do NOT reformat unrelated files.\n\nREPORT: what you changed per item, the choices you made in 4b/4c, marker tokens added and the new marker count, gate results, new tests, what you deliberately left for Phase 2/3, and anything you could not do. Flag loudly if any item turned out to be unsafe as specified.","teammate_id":"phase1-impl-opus@session-c2694464","agent_id":"phase1-impl-opus@session-c2694464","agent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","name":"phase1-impl-opus","color":"red","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-c2694464","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c06d82a6-2d0d-403b-9844-790a309c9439","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
