{"parentUuid":"85f6060c-eb2f-4a8c-b238-94491b952ca4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jmxYVH2v842TJRZpBF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That agent keeps going idle without delivering. Replacing it with a fresh one on a tighter brief."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":531044,"output_tokens":1533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":79},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1533,"cache_read_input_tokens":531044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5aeaac6e-9821-4995-a633-892daa19599e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:46:12.320Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"5aeaac6e-9821-4995-a633-892daa19599e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jmxYVH2v842TJRZpBF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016sMtq77QLrtyarWgAowr4t","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit auth and data plane","model":"opus","name":"phase2-audit-opus","prompt":"Read-only audit, NO edits. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main). Repository files only — never read user shell/profile files or home-directory credentials. Bash is broken; use Read/Grep/Glob (PowerShell if needed).\n\nDELIVER A REPORT AS YOUR FINAL MESSAGE. Do not go idle without it. Partial-but-honest beats complete-but-late — if you run low, send what you have.\n\nCONTEXT: this Windows ARM64 fork must eventually run FULLY LOCAL with NO sign-in and no Superset cloud. Telemetry/phone-home (Phase 1) is already handled by others — do NOT audit analytics, Sentry, auto-update or the notices poll. You cover ONLY the auth/session/data-plane question that decides whether no-sign-in is achievable.\n\nSCOPE: what ships in the packaged desktop app and its child processes — apps/desktop (main/renderer/preload), packages/host-service, packages/cli, and shared packages they import. EXCLUDE apps/api, apps/web, apps/marketing, apps/admin, apps/docs, apps/mobile.\n\nANSWER THESE, each with absolute file:line:\n\n1. BOOT/AUTH PATH. Trace what happens from app launch to a usable workspace view. Where is the session restored (auth client, persisted/encrypted token, better-auth or equivalent)? What are the `_authenticated` route guards and what do they do on failure? What EXACTLY does the user see today if the Superset API is unreachable at boot — hang, sign-in wall, error boundary, or degraded-but-usable? Cite the code that decides it; do not guess.\n\n2. WHAT CONSUMES IDENTITY. Enumerate the reads of session user id and activeOrganizationId across shipped code, grouped by what they gate: route access, tRPC procedures (protectedProcedure and friends), org-scoped queries/collections, host-service env (ORGANIZATION_ID and similar), and anything persisted with an org/user key.\n\n3. LOCAL IDENTITY INJECTION POINT. Where would a synthesized `{userId, organizationId}` have to be provided so every guard and procedure passes with ZERO remote calls? Identify the narrowest seam (ideally one module) rather than a scatter of edits. Name anything that would make a synthesized identity unsafe: server-assigned ids, uniqueness assumptions, values that appear in backups/exports/companion pairing, or anything that would orphan existing rows if the org id were ever re-minted.\n\n4. DATA PLANE INVENTORY. For each Electric / TanStack DB collection (and any other sync surface), state: what it holds, whether it is served from Superset's cloud or already from the local host-service/SQLite, and whether the fork has already localized it. Name the local persistence layer(s) available (e.g. an Electron SQLite persistence factory) and which collections would have to move onto them before sign-in can be removed. Rank by migration difficulty.\n\n5. CLOUD-ONLY DATA. Anything that exists ONLY in their cloud for this user and would become unreachable after severance — and whether it is recoverable/exportable from the app today.\n\n6. REMAINING CLOUD CALLS in this class: any timer-driven, boot-time, or on-focus request to their API in the auth/data-plane path, with interval and endpoint.\n\n7. HONEST BOTTOM LINE: is no-sign-in achievable in this codebase, what is the minimum viable path, and what is the single biggest risk of data loss or corruption if done carelessly.\n\nDo NOT speculate. If something cannot be determined from the code, say so and name the file that would settle it. Aim for under 70 lines.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation