{"parentUuid":"50fcc297-5e78-4a01-96db-d38dd9cb34b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8m41pVpFKWTZR26fysp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked your actual data rather than assuming, and the result is reassuring:\n\n**Severance costs you almost nothing.** The things the audit flagged as hard to migrate — tasks, chat history, automations, agent commands, integration connections — are **all empty** in your account. You have none of them.\n\nEverything you actually use is already local, and in places your local copy is *ahead* of theirs:\n\n| Data | Local (`host.db`) | Their cloud mirror |\n|---|---|---|\n| Workspaces | 249 | 128 |\n| Projects | 23 | 22 |\n| Terminal sessions | 935 | — |\n| Agent bindings | 115 | — |\n| Sidebar layout | 253 rows | — |\n| Companion devices | 3 | — |\n\nThe only cloud data with more rows than local is GitHub pull requests (484 vs 177) and repositories (32) — and both are re-derivable from GitHub itself, not original content.\n\n**The one real hazard** is the organization ID. It's the folder name your `host.db` lives in and the key suffix for your kanban and sidebar state, and there's no migration code anywhere. If severance minted a *new* ID, every workspace, terminal session, kanban card and paired companion device would silently vanish. So Phase 2 will adopt your existing ID (`30e16b5a…`) and treat it as immutable — never generate a fresh one.\n\nI also spotted a stray empty org folder (`00000000-0000-4000-8000-…`) from some earlier mock run; I'll make sure local mode doesn't land on that by accident."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":550475,"output_tokens":1009,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_