uded, and cut the size cap well below 1 GB. Still deletes the existing sensitive files."},{"label":"Leave it as is","description":"Change nothing. Full URLs, headers and cookies keep being written to disk on every launch."}],"multiSelect":false}],"answers":{"Your app records ALL of its own network traffic to disk on every launch, in 'includeSensitive' mode — full URLs, headers and cookies. One existing file is 1,014 MB and it keeps 3 sessions. That means bearer tokens, your Cloudflare Access cookie, and potentially the companion pairing code have been written to C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Roaming\\Superset\\network-logs in plain JSON. This is local-only (not sent anywhere), but it's exactly the data the new egress fence deliberately refuses to log. What do you want done?":"Disable it and delete the logs (Recommended)"},"annotations":{}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60f33dc7-088a-40fc-b335-bc1ee1e53ca9","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
