{"parentUuid":"0d36e225-4776-4dc8-bcd1-b518fb0147bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8oLqMQc16jkiGuXArxs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UfXrsP7wdKDsTvuhqBZngU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Disable network logger","model":"opus","name":"netlog-off-opus","prompt":"Small, surgical change in C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main). The working tree already contains UNCOMMITTED cloud-severance Phase 1 work — do NOT disturb, revert or reformat any of it; add your change alongside. Repository files only; never read user shell/profile files. Bash is broken — use PowerShell. Do NOT commit or push.\n\nPROBLEM (owner-approved fix): apps/desktop/src/main/network-logger/index.ts calls `netLog.startLogging` with `captureMode: \"includeSensitive\"` and a 1 GB cap, retaining 3 sessions, and `startNetworkLogger()` is called unconditionally at boot (apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts ~:516). It records the app's FULL network traffic — URLs with query strings and fragments, request/response headers, cookies — to plain JSON under `%APPDATA%/Superset/network-logs`. On this machine one session file reached 1,014 MB. That means bearer tokens, the Cloudflare Access cookie, and potentially the companion pairing code (which travels in a URL fragment) are sitting on disk in cleartext. This directly contradicts the egress fence added in the same tree, which deliberately logs ORIGIN ONLY for exactly this reason.\n\nOWNER DECISION: disable it entirely, and make re-enabling a deliberate act.\n\nIMPLEMENT:\n1. Make network logging OFF by default. Do not delete the module — keep it working behind an explicit opt-in so it stays available for debugging. Use an environment-variable opt-in (pick a clear fork-owned name, e.g. SUPERSET_NETWORK_LOG=1) checked at the single call site or at the top of startNetworkLogger(); when not set, do nothing, log one clear line saying network logging is off and how to enable it, and leave `started` false so stopNetworkLogger() stays a safe no-op.\n2. When it IS explicitly enabled, reduce the blast radius: use captureMode \"default\" (excludes cookies/auth headers/bodies) rather than \"includeSensitive\", and cut MAX_FILE_BYTES well below 1 GB (e.g. 64 MB). If you believe \"includeSensitive\" should still be reachable, gate it behind a SECOND, separate env var and say so in your report — do not make it the default under any circumstance.\n3. On startup, proactively delete any pre-existing files in the network-logs directory (both `current.json` and `session-*.json`), because they were written in the sensitive mode. Be careful and fail-soft: only touch files inside that directory matching those known names, wrap in try/catch, never throw at boot, and never delete the directory itself if that would break the module's own mkdir assumptions. Log how many files were removed.\n4. Add the fork's marker discipline: give this a marker token (fold into the existing (CLOUD-SEVERANCE-P1) row already in FEATURES.md if that reads honestly, or add a small dedicated row — read FEATURES.md and scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs first for the exact tab-rooted format). This is an upstream-owned file, so without a marker the nightly merge can silently restore sensitive logging.\n5. Tests where sensible, following existing patterns near that module (there is a quit-sequence.test.ts using dependency injection as precedent). At minimum assert: default = disabled, opt-in = enabled, and the mode used when enabled is not \"includeSensitive\".\n\nALSO DO THIS (separate, one-off, on the user's machine — they approved deleting the logs):\nDelete the existing sensitive log files now via PowerShell: `%APPDATA%\\Superset\\network-logs\\current.json` and every `session-*.json` in that directory. Report how many files and how many MB you reclaimed. Only that directory, only those file patterns. Note the app is RUNNING, so a file may be locked — if a delete fails, report it rather than forcing, and say which file remains.\n\nGATES (report each): feature-marker gate — IMPORTANT, it needs grep on PATH: run `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"` first, else it falsely reports ~175 missing (expect the count to rise from 193). Then `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` (REFERR), any tests you add plus the existing desktop main suite (baseline is 684 pass / 27 pre-existing failures — do not introduce new ones), and Biome on the files you touched. IMPORTANT: `npx biome` on this machine resolves to an unrelated package; use `bunx @biomejs/biome@2.4.2`. Known pre-existing and NOT yours: a CRLF formatter baseline on some files and ~19-22 tsc diagnostics in apps/desktop.\n\nREPORT: what you changed, the env var name(s) you chose, how many log files/MB you deleted (and any that were locked), marker token + new count, gate results, and anything you judged unsafe.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":788,"cache_read_input_tokens":566683,"output_tokens":1833,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":788,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1833,"cache_read_input_tokens":566683,"cache_creation_input_tokens":788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":788},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"449e6f5d-f341-4c0d-b850-3b3c2f93f751","timestamp":"2026-08-17T18:33:23.883Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
