{"parentUuid":"697766a4-49fe-4d07-b890-3c724efb7849","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8rC9hKmdwp8geAru5Zj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fable's right, and it found the elegant fix: this fork's **workflow YAML is frozen once a run starts**, so putting the enforcement there is untouchable by a mid-run repair. Dispatching."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_read_input_tokens":590656,"output_tokens":2197,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2197,"cache_read_input_tokens":590656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"736e6be4-ccd4-4bd5-aada-65f777318919","timestamp":"2026-08-17T19:10:24.391Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"736e6be4-ccd4-4bd5-aada-65f777318919","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8rC9hKmdwp8geAru5Zj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R3JFRZFyDGhMtMn9VBgnPt","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Final Fable review: FIX-FIRST — 1 MAJOR + 2 MINOR. The MAJOR is the exact hole this round claimed to close, so it needs the stronger fix. Fix all three; do not commit.\n\n[MAJOR] ci-repair.sh:289 — your assertion is presence-only text matching. It proves the string exists on a non-comment line without `--no-artifacts`; it does NOT prove the gate runs and enforces. All of these pass your greps and still neuter it: `run: node scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs || true`; `continue-on-error: true` on the step; `if: ${{ false }}` on the step; `run: echo \"node scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs\"`; or duplicating the step with one weakened copy. Your three tested variants (deleted / flag-appended / commented-out) are the friendly ones.\nFIX (preferred, uses a property the fork already has): make enforcement live in `.github/workflows/build-arm64.yml`, which per AGENTS.md is FROZEN once a run starts and therefore cannot be edited by a mid-run repair at all. Have check-cloud-severance.mjs write a stamp file on success (include at least the commit sha it validated and the number of assertions that actually executed), and have the WORKFLOW require that stamp — verify it exists, that its sha matches the sha actually built, and that the assertion count is at or above the expected minimum, else fail loud. A repair that deletes/neuters the composite-action step then simply produces no valid stamp and the workflow fails. Belt-and-braces: keep your existing ci-repair.sh assertion, and additionally reject `||`, `;`, `&`, backticks and quote characters on the matched line, plus `continue-on-error` and `if:` in that step's YAML block. Verify adversarially against ALL the bypass shapes listed above, not just the friendly three.\nNote: changing a workflow file needs the WORKFLOW_PUSH_TOKEN path and only takes effect the NEXT run — call that out in your report so I sequence the commit correctly.\n\n[MINOR] egress-fence.ts:52 — app-renderer classification trusts `getType() !== \"webview\"`, but browser panes carry `allowpopups` and the deny `setWindowOpenHandler` is installed asynchronously (renderer dom-ready -> tRPC browser.register -> browser-manager.ts:73). A site whose inline script calls window.open during first parse gets a REAL window (type \"window\") on persist:superset before the handler exists; its requests are classified app-renderer and its ORIGINS get logged — user-browsing leakage in exactly the direction the allowlist narrowing exists to prevent.\nFIX: install a deny setWindowOpenHandler immediately on `app.on(\"web-contents-created\")` for any webContents of type \"webview\" (the pane-scoped handler then only adds the new-window emit), and/or have the fence treat a type \"window\" webContents it did not itself create as unattributed. Prefer whichever is provable by a test.\n\n[MINOR] FEATURES.md:102 and :104 — two honesty defects, which is this batch's own standard. (a) The row claims the gate \"proves all of it against the BUILT artifact set\", but the bundled-CLI channel is provable by no artifact assertion: the CLI ships as a compiled bun binary (scripts/build-bundled-cli.ts -> dist/resources/bin/superset.exe) and the gate scans only dist/main|renderer|preload filtered to .js/.html/.css, so it never sees it. Either soften the sentence to name the CLI channel as SOURCE-enforced only, or add a strings-scan of the packaged CLI binary for the analytics route name. (b) :104 says \"a test asserts the string is absent from the module\", but policy.test.ts:43 actually asserts no `captureMode:` value equals includeSensitive — align the description with the assertion.\n\nRe-run all gates afterwards (marker gate with grep on PATH, REFERR, check-cloud-severance.mjs on a real build, desktop main suite — note the reviewer confirmed ~2 of the pre-existing failures are flaky so treat 25-27 as a band, Biome via bunx @biomejs/biome@2.4.2). Report the workflow-file sequencing point explicitly. Push back if you disagree with any of it rather than implementing it badly.","summary":"Fix CI stamp hole and 2 minors","to":"phase1-impl-opus","type":"message","recipient":"phase1-impl-opus","content":"Final Fable review: FIX-FIRST — 1 MAJOR + 2 MINOR…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_read_input_tokens":590656,"output_tokens":2197,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2197,"cache_read_input_tokens":590656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"9b21f964-5617-476b-a914-6cc5bae41532","timestamp":"2026-08-17T19:10:43.982Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
