{"parentUuid":"280c450b-5e59-452c-aefd-2aa4ddd0c87e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8tku97zC8VuwNLkAreg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MRavsFqajzRAHNEt7o47no","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Yes — repeat the full sweep before I commit. A real release build follows immediately, so I want the whole batch re-verified in its final state rather than trusting that a gate/workflow/doc-only change could not disturb anything: REFERR, the desktop main suite (expect the 25-27 flaky band, no NEW failures), a fresh compile, check-cloud-severance.mjs on a genuinely packaged build (expect exactly 11/full and a stamp with the right sha), the marker gate with grep on PATH (expect 201), and Biome via bunx @biomejs/biome@2.4.2 on everything you touched across all rounds.\n\nAlso tighten the step-block extraction now rather than leaving it as a known soft spot: key it on the INVOCATION LINE (`node scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs`) rather than the step NAME, so a pure rename cannot make the extractor return empty. You reason that empty currently fails closed — confirm that by actually testing a pure rename, and if it does fail closed keep the name check as a secondary signal, but the primary anchor should be the thing that cannot be cosmetically renamed. Re-run your nine-shape adversarial harness afterwards, plus the rename case, and report the matrix.\n\nNothing else. Report when the sweep and the matrix are done.","summary":"Request full sweep and rename hardening","to":"phase1-impl-opus","type":"message","recipient":"phase1-impl-opus","content":"Yes — repeat the full sweep before I commit. A re…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2129,"cache_read_input_tokens":610072,"output_tokens":828,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":288},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_reque