{"parentUuid":"28b888b2-7c2b-4f1e-a10d-d0dfcfc7c368","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8uJLPmf8patfjhLMSe2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good findings, but I need to be proportionate about which of these gate your install.\n\nMost of them harden CI against a *hostile, prompt-injected repair agent* — a risk your fork's own AGENTS.md already documents as accepted. They matter for unattended nightly builds, not for the build I'm about to dispatch and watch myself. Two of them, though, are plain correctness bugs. Fixing those now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3397,"cache_read_input_tokens":614440,"output_tokens":3006,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1700},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":614440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"e5b1415c-18d7-44a8-aae9-d9bf137dbd2b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T19:51:26.144Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"e5b1415c-18d7-44a8-aae9-d9bf137dbd2b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8uJLPmf8patfjhLMSe2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012g8mbjwd8LLyG2VG9jZydQ","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Fable's CI review is in. I am splitting it deliberately — do EXACTLY these now, and NOT the rest:\n\nDO NOW (real correctness bugs + cheap hardening):\n1. [MAJOR, genuine gate bug] check-cloud-severance.mjs:359-363 — with release/ PRESENT but ZERO app-update.yml found, it still calls ok() (\"0 manifest(s) found\") and counts toward 11. That is a vacuous pass and contradicts the file's own no-vacuous-scan rule; an upstream electron-builder layout change that relocates the manifest would leave the gate green with the updater manifest never verified. FIX: fail loud when releaseRoot exists and manifests.length === 0. Re-verify the packaged count is still exactly 11.\n2. [cheap, strictly safer] build-arm64.yml frozen enforce step (all three attempt jobs) — it resolves `node` from PATH and honors NODE_OPTIONS, so an earlier repairable step could poison $GITHUB_PATH/$GITHUB_ENV and have the frozen step execute attacker code. Add `unset NODE_OPTIONS NODE_PATH` and pin an absolute node path inside the frozen step.\n3. [MINOR] main.ts:154-156 — capture `const id = window.webContents.id` at registration and use it in the destroyed handler, instead of re-reading the getter chain during teardown where it can throw \"Object has been destroyed\" and escape an event handler.\n4. [MINOR] egress-fence.ts:44-57 duplicated JSDoc block — remove the duplicate.\n5. [MINOR] composite action: the now-dead `publish` input and the stale \"publish\" wording in action.yml:2-13, plus the step names at build-arm64.yml:101,242,380 that still say publish. Clean up so the names describe what the steps actually do.\n\nDO NOT DO NOW — I am deferring these deliberately, do not start them:\n- The BLOCKER (ci-repair.sh validating itself from the agent-edited tree) and MAJOR (4) (YAML-aware extraction from a trusted base blob). Both are real, both only matter for an UNATTENDED repair with a hostile/injected agent. The build I am about to dispatch is attended — I watch it and can intervene. I will land these before the next nightly at 02:13 UTC, as their own change with their own review.\n- MAJOR (a) (the composite receiving a contents:write token, so a hostile repair could publish before enforcement ever runs). That needs a new read-scoped credential, which is the owner's decision, not something to slip in silently. I will raise it with them.\nRecord all three in your report as KNOWN DEFERRED so they are not lost.\n\nThen finish the full sweep I already asked for (REFERR, desktop suite vs the 25-27 flaky band, fresh compile, gate on a genuinely packaged build expecting exactly 11/full with correct sha, marker gate with grep on PATH, Biome via bunx @biomejs/biome@2.4.2 across all rounds) plus the nine-shape adversarial matrix INCLUDING the pure rename, and report. I commit straight after.","summary":"Fix gate bug, defer hostile-agent hardening","to":"phase1-impl-opus","type":"message","recipient":"phase1-impl-opus","content":"Fable's CI review is in. I am splitting it delibe…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3397,"cache_read_input_tokens":614440,"output_tokens":3006,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1700},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":614440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"as