{"parentUuid":"ec410412-4f2a-490e-bbcb-45ca309ded55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a112c5d0-0b3d-4deb-a983-c9d717fd0614","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ew835HKGJPjhBz4s4z9xGZ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pairing\\commit-msg-severance.txt (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"cf5b4aad-9e44-4c9f-826f-a359c11c12a0","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:13:04.602Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\pairing\\commit-msg-severance.txt","content":"feat(fork): cloud severance phase 1 — no telemetry, no phone-home, no updater\n\n(CLOUD-SEVERANCE-P1) The owner runs this fork entirely on their own\nmachine and wants no traffic to Superset's cloud. Phase 1 removes the\nchannels that cost nothing to lose. Sign-in, Electric and the\napi.superset.sh data plane are deliberately UNTOUCHED — they are phase\n2/3, and severing them is a data-plane migration, not an unplugging.\n\nAudited first: PostHog and Sentry were already inert here (no keys are\ninjected by CI and no repo-root .env exists), so most of this is making\nthat state ENFORCED rather than incidental. The genuinely live channels\nwere the bundled CLI's per-command ping and the notices poll.\n\n- build FAILS if NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY, SENTRY_DSN_DESKTOP,\n  SENTRY_DSN_HOST_SERVICE or SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN is set. electron.vite\n  loads repo-root .env with override:true, so without this a key placed\n  there would bake in silently. Throws by name rather than force-emptying:\n  quietly discarding a maintainer's key is the opposite of fail-loud.\n  Both Sentry sourcemap-upload plugins die with the token.\n- posthog-js IS still initialised every boot (PostHogProvider); its\n  inertness rests on the key gate + the vite define bake + this ban, and\n  the comments now say so. A later phase must not delete those gates\n  believing init is unreachable — the previous comment claimed exactly\n  that and was wrong.\n- the bundled CLI posted an event to api.superset.sh on EVERY command,\n  key-gated by nothing. Body gutted; the auth/resolveAuth chain the\n  superset-cli preset depends on is untouched.\n- the desktop-notices poll no longer performs a request at all. The\n  (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) downgrade pipeline stays intact around it — the\n  gate that stops a remote notice blanking the app is not deleted just\n  because nothing is fetched today.\n- auto-update is hard-disabled inside auto-updater.ts, not by removing\n  call sites: it was held off Windows only by IS_AUTO_UPDATE_PLATFORM,\n  one upstream line away from pointing our users at superset-sh's x64\n  build. electron-builder publish:null so no app-update.yml is baked at\n  all, and RELEASES_URL — previously upstream's URL with ZERO consumers,\n  a landmine a merge would have armed — is repointed to the fork and is\n  now the single constant behind menu, tray and command palette. Those\n  three now say \"Download Latest Release\" and open the fork's releases,\n  instead of silently invoking a no-op.\n- CSP drops *.posthog.com, *.sentry.io and sentry-ipc:; the Windows CORS\n  shim drops those plus a stale app.outlit.ai. ws/wss/127.0.0.1 (every\n  terminal), blob:/data:, and the relay/api/electric origins are kept —\n  removing them would kill terminals and sign-in.\n\n(EGRESS-FENCE) A log-only deny-nothing fence on the persist:superset\nsession records which ORIGINS the renderer dials, so phase 2/3 can prove\nthe allowlist before anything is enforced. It logs origin only — never\npath, query or fragment — because the companion pairing secret travels\nin a fragment and other URLs carry bearer tokens. An origin is recorded\nonly for POSITIVELY app-owned webContents: browser panes share this\nsession, so webview traffic and anything unattributable (service workers,\ndestroyed contents, a popup that beat the deny handler) are counted as\nbare integers. \"Not provably a webview\" is not \"provably the app\" — the\nfirst cut got that wrong and would have written the user's browsing\nhistory to disk. Accepted cost, stated rather than buried: unattributable\nAPP traffic is invisible to the fence too, and the counter is the honest\nmeasure of what it could not see. Install is asserted at window creation,\nso the fence cannot be silently skipped.\n\n(NETLOG-OFF) Unrelated to egress, found while auditing it: upstream\nstarts netLog with captureMode \"includeSensitive\" and a 1 GB cap on\nevery boot, writing full URLs, headers and cookies to disk. One session\nfile on this machine had reached 1,014 MB, holding bearer tokens, a\nCloudflare Access cookie and potentially the pairing code in cleartext —\nprecisely what the fence refuses to log. Now off unless SUPERSET_NETWORK_LOG\nis set, \"default\" capture mode when on, 64 MB cap, and pre-existing logs\npurged at boot. includeSensitive is deliberately unreachable by any\nenvironment variable: re-enabling it must be a code change someone\nreviews.\n\nGate (scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs, phase-scoped): asserts over the\nWHOLE built artifact set — no telemetry hostnames, no baked key shapes,\nno upstream releases URL, no /api/desktop/version string (the poll-off is\notherwise protected only by comments), no app-update.yml naming upstream\nanywhere including dist/, and the packaged CLI binary free of its\nanalytics symbols. Fails loud rather than passing vacuously: absent\nartifacts, an empty release dir or an empty artifact set are all errors.\n\nPublishing MOVED out of the repairable composite action into the frozen\nworkflow, behind the gate: enforcement that runs after the release is\npublic is not enforcement. A build-repair can still neuter the composite\naction's copy of the gate — the frozen step then fails and PUBLISH NEVER\nRUNS. The frozen step deletes any stamp, re-runs the gate itself, and\nrequires mode=full with the exact assertion count and a stamp sha\nmatching the sha built; it unsets NODE_OPTIONS/NODE_PATH and resolves an\nabsolute node so an earlier repairable step cannot poison the interpreter.\nci-repair.sh additionally requires the gate's step block to be\nbyte-identical to its pre-repair form — verified against 16 tamper\nshapes including || true, continue-on-error, if:false, echo-wrapping,\nduplication and a pure rename.\n\nKnown deferred, unattended-hostile-repair scenarios only, none affecting\nan attended build: ci-repair.sh still validates itself from the\nagent-edited tree; the step-block extraction is line-based rather than\nYAML-aware; and the composite action still holds a contents:write token,\nso ordering alone cannot stop a repair that publishes itself.\n\n201 feature markers present. REFERR clean. Desktop suite 704 pass, 27\npre-existing failures (~2 flaky), no new failures. Reviewed adversarially\nby Fable across four rounds; every finding fixed or explicitly deferred.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ec410412-4f2a-490e-bbcb-45ca309ded55","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
