{"parentUuid":"4a31f095-4cd7-483f-ad01-2886a7f3411f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8wGtJLcrmrvQpA7ug6z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BK8PsTCiezVto3gtk6nbMU","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Agreed on all three, and the timing worked out better than it looks — hold the uncommitted file for now.\n\n(2)/(3): accepted. Proving it from app-builder-lib's own source rather than guessing is the right standard, and I agree with NOT pinning the manifest count to 0. The invariant we care about is \"no manifest names superset-sh\"; a hard zero would fire the first time someone legitimately re-enables publishing, which is a tripwire I did not ask for and would rather not bake in. Leave it as-is.\n\n(4): the stronger version is better, but it encodes a NEW assumption — that the packaged layout is `release/*-unpacked/resources` on the actual windows-11-arm runner — and no real CI run has ever confirmed that. If it is wrong, the gate fails loud and BLOCKS PUBLISHING, which would cost the owner their build. The committed weaker version passes on a correct build and still catches a superset-sh manifest anywhere including dist/, so shipping on it is the right risk.\n\nPLAN: build 32064759110 is running now on the committed version. When it finishes I will read the real packaged layout out of its logs. Then:\n- if the layout is `release/win-arm64-unpacked/resources` as you derived, I commit your stronger version as a follow-up, with the path assumption now confirmed by a real run rather than by reading platformPackager;\n- if it differs, you fix the pattern to match reality first and I commit that.\nEither way it lands before the next nightly, alongside the three deferred items (D1 ci-repair.sh self-validation, D2 YAML-aware extraction, D3 the composite's write token — that last one needs the owner).\n\nSo: do not commit anything, do not start new work. Stand by until the build lands. If the enforce step fails because node is not at one of your trusted absolute paths, I will come straight to you with the runner's actual node location.","summary":"Hold stronger gate until layout confirmed","to":"phase1-impl-opus","type":"message","recipient":"phase1-impl-opus","content":"Agreed on all three, and the timing worked out be…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2950,"cache_read_input_tokens":634402,"output_tokens":1309,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":502},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1309,"cache_read_input_tokens":634402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"bb2fb4b2-1853-4542-8a2d-bc4e4d3a20bc","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:17:11.347Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
