{"parentUuid":"0125711b-ebf4-416b-9ef8-364965a4442d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAE1tssktocfy6eRQkse","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WuuShMeucZpFQivJrATcnK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Verify installed app health","model":"opus","name":"postinstall-verify-opus","prompt":"Verify the freshly installed Superset desktop build on this machine. READ-ONLY on the app; use PowerShell (the Bash tool is broken in this environment — every invocation dies in the shell wrapper). Repository files and app-data files only; never read user shell/profile files or print secret values.\n\nCONTEXT: The user just installed C:\\Users\\khair\\Downloads\\Superset-1.20.2-arm64.exe (SHA-256 0A1FB9FA7C38AF7EF287468F19428D5D5431049D5508C47B5B3EBD100874726D, built from fork commit 7a818cebc5). It bundles: (NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE) removal of upstream's forced-update overlay, a fix so remote minimumVersion cannot crash the renderer, (CLOUD-SEVERANCE-P1) telemetry/updater/notices-poll severance, (EGRESS-FENCE) log-only origin fence, (NETLOG-OFF) network logging off by default with boot purge of old logs.\n\nVERIFY, in order, and report each with evidence:\n1. INSTALLED BINARY: C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\Superset.exe exists and is running (several processes expected: main, renderer, host-service.js, pty-daemon.js, terminal-host.js). Report PIDs and the ProductVersion.\n2. BUILD IDENTITY: grep the asar (C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources\\app.asar) as BINARY text (grep -a via \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\grep.exe\", or Select-String) for these markers and report counts: CLOUD-SEVERANCE-P1 (expect >0), EGRESS-FENCE (>0), NETLOG-OFF (>0), NO-REMOTE-UPDATE-GATE (>0), UpdateRequiredPage (expect 0 or comment-only — the component was deleted; if the string appears, check whether it is only in a comment/marker context), superset-sh/superset/releases (expect 0), app.outlit.ai (expect 0).\n3. NETWORK LOGGING OFF: C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Roaming\\Superset\\network-logs should contain NO new session-*.json since install (~13:27 today) and current.json should be absent or 0 bytes and NOT growing. List the dir with sizes and timestamps. Also confirm no app-update.yml exists under C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\resources.\n4. EGRESS FENCE ACTIVE: find the fence's log output. Check the app's log files under C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Roaming\\Superset (e.g. logs\\*.log or main.log) for lines mentioning egress fence install/flush and collect the ORIGINS it has recorded so far. Report the distinct origins seen — this is the phase-2 evidence the owner asked for. Do not print anything beyond scheme://host:port entries and counters.\n5. BRIDGE/HOST-SERVICE HEALTH: 127.0.0.1:47610 listening and owned by the new Superset host-service process (netstat -ano + process lookup). Companion data intact: C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\host\\30e16b5a-e2af-4874-b126-acc7b3f17aa9\\host.db exists with a recent mtime and nonzero size.\n6. LOCAL DATA INTACT: C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\tanstack-db.sqlite and local.db still present with sizes similar to before (mirror was ~19 MB, local.db ~0.3 MB).\n\nDo NOT interact with the app UI, do not kill or restart anything, do not modify any file. Report a concise checklist with PASS/FAIL per item and raw evidence lines, then an overall verdict. If a check cannot be completed, say exactly why rather than guessing.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":619782,"output_tokens":1490,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610,"ephem