{"parentUuid":"7cdf23f5-0487-415e-bf62-09c90ab0b2c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAEFxPMdpxSG5rv6XrNJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUWHpmxgyrak1kxgF6UPB2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fable review CI trust batch","model":"fable","name":"ci-trust-review-fable","prompt":"Adversarial review, READ-ONLY. Never edit/commit/push. Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (branch main, HEAD 7a818cebc5, THREE UNCOMMITTED files). Repository files only; never read user shell/profile files. The Bash tool is broken in this environment — use Read/Grep/Glob and PowerShell for git (`git -C \"<repo>\" diff`, `git -C \"<repo>\" diff --stat`).\n\nTARGET: the deferred CI-integrity batch, uncommitted:\n  M .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml   (+52)\n  M scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs   (+50/-19)\n  M scripts/ci-repair.sh                (+141/-65)\n\nCONTEXT: This fork's build has a bounded AI self-repair loop ((BUILD-REPAIR)); a previous review found the severance gate's protections could be defeated by a hostile/prompt-injected repair agent. This batch closes three holes:\n1. STRONGER GATE ASSERTION: check-cloud-severance.mjs now requires locating the packaged resources dir (release/*-unpacked/resources — CONFIRMED against a real CI run logging appOutDir=release\\win-arm64-unpacked) before accepting \"no app-update.yml found\"; distinguishes \"path moved\" (fail loud) from \"correctly none\" (pass); also scans dist/ for relocated manifests; release/ empty = fail; --allow-unpackaged stamps mode=partial which CI rejects.\n2. D1 TRUSTED VALIDATOR: the frozen workflow now records the pre-repair sha as a STEP OUTPUT before the AI step; the validate+push step extracts scripts/ci-repair.sh AND scripts/ai-run.sh from that sha into $RUNNER_TEMP/ci-repair-trusted-<round>/ and runs the EXTRACTED copy, passing TRUSTED_BASE_SHA; push mode prefers TRUSTED_BASE_SHA over $STATE_DIR/base-sha and fails loud if they disagree. Rationale: validating from a trusted blob is useless if the executing validator itself was rewritten; the executing bytes must be trusted.\n3. D2 YAML-AWARE EXTRACTION: the severance step-block comparison now uses python3+PyYAML, emitting canonical JSON for every parsed STEP whose content mentions scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs, comparing base (from `git show BASE_SHA:file`) vs head; a byte-identical look-alike embedded in another step's `run: |` scalar is now rejected (the implementer demonstrated the old awk reader was fooled by exactly that); import failure of PyYAML fails loud rather than falling back to the weaker text reader; the exactly-one-invocation count is now interpreter-agnostic.\n\nThe implementer ran an 18-shape tamper matrix (all fail-loud, both baselines pass). Known accepted residuals, NOT findings unless you show them worse than stated: D3 (composite action holds contents:write token — owner decision pending); $RUNNER_TEMP writable by the agent for anything OTHER than the step-output sha; trusted extraction assumes the agent does not commit (sha-disagreement tripwire detects, does not prevent).\n\nATTACK:\na. The TRUSTED-VALIDATOR chain end to end: is the recorded step output genuinely pre-agent (ordering in BOTH repair jobs)? Can the agent influence it (e.g. by the checkout step's ref, a detached HEAD, or rewriting git history so rev-parse HEAD differs)? Does the extraction quote/escape paths safely? Is ai-run.sh really the only sourced sibling (verify BASH_SOURCE-relative sourcing in ci-repair.sh)? Does the extracted copy behave identically when invoked from $RUNNER_TEMP (relative paths, cwd assumptions, GITHUB_* env)?\nb. The YAML extractor: correctness on the REAL files (does it find exactly the intended steps in both action.yml and build-arm64.yml?); robustness to YAML aliases/anchors, flow-style steps, unicode/CRLF; can a hostile edit make base and head both parse to the SAME canonical JSON while behaviour differs (e.g. moving enforcement behind an anchor, changing a sibling key the serializer drops, duplicate keys)? Does `git show BASE_SHA:file` handle the path correctly on Windows-style separators (CI runs it on ubuntu — but ci-repair.sh may also run locally)?\nc. The gate change: on a real packaged tree, is the resources-dir requirement satisfied exactly once; can a crafted directory (release/evil-unpacked/resources, empty) satisfy the location requirement while the REAL output went elsewhere; does the dist/ manifest scan false-positive on anything legitimate?\nd. RE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"refusal","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":{"type":"refusal","category":"cyber","explanation":"This request triggered restrictions on violative cyber content and was blocked under Anthropic's Usage Policy. To learn more, see https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback.","fallback_has_prefill_claim":true},"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":622386,"output_tokens":2610,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":757},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2610,"cache_read_input_tokens":622386,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"857ed177-4449-4a08-9290-153f757c3482","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:40:49.440Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
