{"parentUuid":"1a6dc83c-9b42-4286-b399-3b379f97fc49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAEdCWVrPJvPrg6kLpih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"output_tokens":3653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3653,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"c3a36968-1fe4-4101-9a07-b132c983485a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:45:10.295Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"c3a36968-1fe4-4101-9a07-b132c983485a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAEdCWVrPJvPrg6kLpih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two threads resuming: terminal-persistence exploration (Opus), plus pending Fable review of uncommitted CI-integrity files (must land before 02:13 UTC nightly).\n\nKnown baseline: Ctrl+R (renderer reload) already preserves terminals — PTYs live outside renderer. Question is whether they can survive full app quit + installer run. Spawning both agents now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"output_tokens":3653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3653,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"85c94bf5-4de0-414c-86b1-f2da47ff89a5","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:45:12.361Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"85c94bf5-4de0-414c-86b1-f2da47ff89a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAEdCWVrPJvPrg6kLpih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139EM5a6ZuEkTYcMjJHptx9","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore terminal persistence architecture","name":"term-persist-explore-opus","subagent_type":"architect-opus","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (vendored fork of superset-sh/superset, Windows ARM64 desktop app). READ REPOSITORY FILES ONLY — never read user home-directory files, shell profiles, or credentials; that is out of scope.\n\nGOAL: The owner wants to install a new version of the desktop app WITHOUT losing running terminal sessions. Today, quitting the app kills every terminal (user tested this). Renderer reload (Ctrl+R) preserves terminals, so PTYs survive renderer death — they live in main process or the host-service. We need a design where terminals detach (survive app quit) and the new app version reattaches to them.\n\nINVESTIGATE (cite file:line for everything):\n1. Process tree: where exactly are node-pty PTYs spawned? Main process? host-service? A coordinator child? Trace from renderer terminal component → IPC → pty spawn. Key dirs: apps/desktop/src/main, packages/* (look for host-service, terminal, pty packages).\n2. What is the host-service lifecycle? Is it a child process of Electron main? What kills it on app quit (explicit kill, process group, stdio inheritance, job object)? Note: fork keeps WS_NO_BUFFER_UTIL=1/WS_NO_UTF_8_VALIDATE=1 in the coordinator child env — find that spawn site.\n3. Existing reconnect machinery: how does the renderer re-hydrate terminals after Ctrl+R? Is there a session/terminal registry, scrollback buffer server-side, WebSocket reconnect protocol? If the transport already tolerates renderer death, the delta to tolerating APP death may be small.\n4. Windows specifics: ConPTY handles — can a detached process holding ConPTY survive parent exit? Does the app use Windows job objects (e.g. JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE) that would kill children on quit? Search for job object usage, `detached: true`, `windowsHide`, process-kill logic on quit (before-quit/will-quit handlers).\n5. The installer angle: NSIS one-click installer — does it force-kill the running app / its children? Check electron-builder NSIS config (apps/desktop/electron-builder* or package.json build section) for `allowToChangeInstallationDirectory`, runAfterFinish, and whether per-user install kills processes.\n6. Candidate designs, ranked, with concrete deltas:\n   a. Detach host-service: host-service becomes a daemon that outlives the app; app (re)connects on boot. What breaks (stdio pipes, env, auth, ports, version skew between old host-service and new app)?\n   b. \"Update mode\" handoff: on explicit \"install update\" action, main re-parents/detaches the pty-owning process, quits, installer runs, new app adopts the orphan by a well-known port/pipe + auth token file.\n   c. External multiplexer (tmux-style) — probably wrong for Windows ARM64, but assess honestly.\n   Include version-skew handling (old pty host + new renderer protocol) and failure modes (orphan leak, auth, two apps fighting over one daemon).\n\nDELIVER: architecture blueprint — files to modify, protocol changes, risks, recommended option with rationale. Be concrete; this feeds a Fable plan audit next. Final message = full report (it is the only thing returned to the orchestrator)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"output_tokens":3653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3653,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ac1dc53e-8310-470f-98c5-c0c36013cf20","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:45:31.658Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"ac1dc53e-8310-470f-98c5-c0c36013cf20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAEdCWVrPJvPrg6kLpih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XN1VfbkYqg6z3bXxK4x18r","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fable review of CI-integrity diffs","name":"ci-trust-review-fable","subagent_type":"code-reviewer-fable","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64. REPOSITORY FILES ONLY — never read user home-directory files, shell profiles, or credentials; out of scope.\n\nBash tool may be broken in this environment (`unexpected EOF` errors). If so, use PowerShell-style via Bash anyway first; if Bash truly fails, note it and review via Read/Grep tools directly on files plus `git diff` attempted through Bash. Get the diff with: git -C \"C:/Users/khair/Code Projects/fork-superset-windows-arm64\" diff -- .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs scripts/ci-repair.sh\n\nCONTEXT: This fork's CI has a bounded AI self-repair loop ((BUILD-REPAIR)): on build failure an agent edits the checked-out tree and pushes; next attempt builds that sha. Threat model: a hostile/prompt-injected repair agent must not be able to publish a Release that violates the cloud-severance gate. Prior committed state (HEAD) already: moved publish into the frozen workflow behind an enforcement step; the enforcement step deletes any stamp, re-runs scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs itself, requires mode=full + exact assertion count (11) + stamp sha == built sha; unsets NODE_OPTIONS/NODE_PATH and uses absolute node.\n\nTHE THREE UNCOMMITTED CHANGES UNDER REVIEW (working-tree diffs vs HEAD):\n1. scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs — stronger gate assertion set; writes .fork/cloud-severance-stamp.json only on success with sha from `git rev-parse HEAD`, mode, assertion count.\n2. scripts/ci-repair.sh — D1: trusted-validator extraction (validator copied from a trusted ref, not the agent-edited tree) + D2: YAML-aware step-block comparison (replaces line-based awk extraction; a prior attack embedded a byte-identical look-alike step inside another step's `run: |` scalar and fooled the line-based reader).\n3. .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml — corresponding wiring.\n\nImplementer reports an 18-shape tamper matrix all failing loud. Verify skeptically:\n- Does the trusted-validator extraction actually source the validator from a ref the repair agent cannot have modified in this run (e.g. the workflow's pinned sha / pre-repair tip), or does it still read from the agent-edited tree at any point (TOCTOU)?\n- Is the YAML-aware extraction genuinely YAML-parsing (yq? node/js-yaml? python?) or a smarter regex that a nested block scalar / anchors / flow-style step could still fool? Try to construct a bypass: YAML anchors/aliases, merge keys, flow mappings, duplicate keys, CRLF tricks, unicode homoglyphs in step names/ids.\n- Stamp integrity: can a repair pre-place a stamp, or race the delete-then-recheck? Is the sha comparison against the sha actually built?\n- Workflow file frozen at run start — so build-arm64.yml changes only take effect NEXT run. Does anything in the diff wrongly assume same-run effect?\n- Shell quoting/injection in ci-repair.sh (paths with spaces — repo path has one), `set -euo pipefail` discipline, error paths that silently pass.\n- Any way the exact-count assertion (11) is satisfiable by a degenerate run (empty artifact set, skipped packaging).\nRank findings BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and a concrete attack/failure scenario each. Verify each finding against the real code before reporting. If clean, say so plainly. Final message = full review."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"output_tokens":3653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3653,"cache_read_input_tokens":34817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29075},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ad278673-88d9-4da6-9d4d-770d6eb082e4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T12:45:49.829Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
