W (working-tree diffs vs HEAD):\n1. scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs — stronger gate assertion set; writes .fork/cloud-severance-stamp.json only on success with sha from `git rev-parse HEAD`, mode, assertion count.\n2. scripts/ci-repair.sh — D1: trusted-validator extraction (validator copied from a trusted ref, not the agent-edited tree) + D2: YAML-aware step-block comparison (replaces line-based awk extraction; a prior attack embedded a byte-identical look-alike step inside another step's `run: |` scalar and fooled the line-based reader).\n3. .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml — corresponding wiring.\n\nImplementer reports an 18-shape tamper matrix all failing loud. Verify skeptically:\n- Does the trusted-validator extraction actually source the validator from a ref the repair agent cannot have modified in this run (e.g. the workflow's pinned sha / pre-repair tip), or does it still read from the agent-edited tree at any point (TOCTOU)?\n- Is the YAML-aware extraction genuinely YAML-parsing (yq? node/js-yaml? python?) or a smarter regex that a nested block scalar / anchors / flow-style step could still fool? Try to construct a bypass: YAML anchors/aliases, merge keys, flow mappings, duplicate keys, CRLF tricks, unicode homoglyphs in step names/ids.\n- Stamp integrity: can a repair pre-place a stamp, or race the delete-then-recheck? Is the sha comparison against the sha actually built?\n- Workflow file frozen at run start — so build-arm64.yml changes only take effect NEXT run. Does anything in the diff wrongly assume same-run effect?\n- Shell quoting/injection in ci-repair.sh (paths with spaces — repo path has one), `set -euo pipefail` discipline, error paths that silently pass.\n- Any way the exact-count assertion (11) is satisfiable by a degenerate run (empty artifact set, skipped packaging).\nRank findings BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR with file:line and a concrete attack/failure scenario each. Verify each finding against the real code before reporting. If clean, say so plainly. Final message = full review.","teammate_id":"ci-trust-review-fable-2@session-92794baa","agent_id":"ci-trust-review-fable-2@session-92794baa","agent_type":"code-reviewer-fable","model":"fable","name":"ci-trust-review-fable-2","color":"purple","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-92794baa","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad278673-88d9-4da6-9d4d-770d6eb082e4","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
