 race between the delete and the re-check? Is the sha compared against the sha actually built?\n- Workflow YAML is frozen at run start, so build-arm64.yml edits only take effect on the NEXT run. Does anything in the diff wrongly assume same-run effect?\n- Shell correctness in ci-repair.sh: quoting (the repo path contains a space), `set -euo pipefail` discipline, error paths that silently succeed, exit-code propagation through pipes.\n- Can the exact-count assertion (11) be satisfied by a degenerate run — empty artifact set, skipped packaging, missing release dir?\n\nRank findings BLOCKER / MAJOR / MINOR, each with file:line and a concrete failure scenario. Verify every finding against the real code before reporting it — no speculative findings. If the batch is clean, say so plainly; do not manufacture issues. Your final message is the entire report returned to the orchestrator.","teammate_id":"ci-trust-review-opus@session-92794baa","agent_id":"ci-trust-review-opus@session-92794baa","agent_type":"code-reviewer-opus","model":"opus","name":"ci-trust-review-opus","color":"orange","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-92794baa","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"65d32d8b-21ee-4633-b37a-74702a592fe1","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
