{"parentUuid":"1f7b3259-7067-461a-95f5-06b21a8add9d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d99e7a2b-26b3-4e1d-861a-a81ce3f955e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Krquqy1weNDgi63srB49Pk","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the ID below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagent_id: ci-cheap-fixes-opus@session-92794baa\nname: ci-cheap-fixes-opus\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"64d96498-1abc-4eb8-adf1-da02d0c0e366","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:00:56.273Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (owner's own private fork). REPOSITORY FILES ONLY — never read user home-directory files, shell profiles, or credentials; out of scope per owner.\n\nENV: the Bash tool is BROKEN in this session (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: unexpected EOF`). Use the PowerShell tool for everything. Gate scripts need Git-for-Windows coreutils: `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"`.\n\nThere are already uncommitted working-tree changes to `.github/workflows/build-arm64.yml`, `scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs`, `scripts/ci-repair.sh`. DO NOT revert or restructure them. You are adding three targeted fixes on top, found by an adversarial review.\n\nA separate, larger structural refactor (splitting enforcement/publish and validate/push into fresh-runner jobs) is being designed in parallel by someone else and will touch build-arm64.yml heavily. To avoid conflicts: keep your edits MINIMAL and confined to the specific lines below. Prefer `scripts/ci-repair.sh` edits; touch `build-arm64.yml` only for fix 3, which is a one-line comparison operator or comment.\n\nFIX 1 (MAJOR) — scripts/ci-repair.sh around lines 108, 219, 273-277.\nThe \"one version, ever\" freeze compares post-agent package versions against `$STATE_DIR/base-versions`, a file under $RUNNER_TEMP written before the agent runs. The workflow's own comment (build-arm64.yml:214-217) concedes the agent can rewrite files under RUNNER_TEMP. Only base-sha is anchored to a step output; base-versions is not. A hostile repair can bump versions and rewrite base-versions to match, defeating the freeze — which matters because the publish script does `gh release delete \"$TAG\" --yes`, so a version bump enables clobbering an existing Release.\nFix: recompute the base side from trusted git objects instead of the runner-temp file — `git show \"$TRUSTED_BASE_SHA:<pkg>/package.json\"` for each versioned package. TRUSTED_BASE_SHA already exists in this script's flow (it comes from a pre-agent step output). Keep the existing failure messages loud. If base-versions is still used elsewhere for non-security bookkeeping, leave that alone but make the SECURITY comparison use git objects.\n\nFIX 2 (MINOR) — scripts/ci-repair.sh around line 336, the python3 `yaml.safe_load` used by the YAML-aware step-block comparison.\nPyYAML resolves duplicate mapping keys last-wins with no error. A step rewritten as `{run: EVIL, ..., run: <original>}` therefore compares EQUAL to base. Today the Actions runner rejects duplicate keys so the practical worst case is a next-run parse failure rather than a bypass — but that safety rests on the runner's parser, not on this gate.\nFix: reject duplicate mapping keys explicitly so the comparison itself fails loud. Either subclass yaml.SafeLoader and override construct_mapping to raise on a repeated key, or use ruamel with allow_duplicate_keys=False. Keep the existing fail-loud exit-code convention (the script already exits 3 when PyYAML is missing — follow that pattern).\n\nFIX 3 (MINOR) — .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml around lines 163-169.\nThe comment and design intent say the assertion count must be EXACT, but the code enforces `>= 11`. Harmless today (the stamp only exists when every assertion passed, and a full packaged run yields exactly 11) but the semantics diverge from the documented intent. Make them agree — prefer tightening the code to an equality check, since \"exactly the expected assertion set ran\" is the stronger and intended property. Keep the message loud and self-explaining on mismatch.\n\nAFTER EDITING, verify:\n- `node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` → must end \"All 201 feature markers present.\"\n- `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` → must end \"(REFERR-GATE) clean\".\n- Syntax-check the shell script: `bash -n scripts/ci-repair.sh` via `& \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe\" -n scripts/ci-repair.sh`\n- Exercise your duplicate-key rejection with a small throwaway YAML fixture under `tmp/` proving it now fails loud, and a normal step block proving it still passes. Delete the fixtures after, or leave them under tmp/ only.\n- Do NOT commit. Do NOT push. Leave changes in the working tree and report exactly what you changed with file:line.\n\nYour final message is the entire report returned to the orchestrator: what you changed, verification output, anything you chose not to do and why.","teammate_id":"ci-cheap-fixes-opus@session-92794baa","agent_id":"ci-cheap-fixes-opus@session-92794baa","agent_type":"claude","model":"opus","name":"ci-cheap-fixes-opus","color":"pink","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-92794baa","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1f7b3259-7067-461a-95f5-06b21a8add9d","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
