{"parentUuid":"8686c6f7-773e-4685-8e54-2d18bd52d0e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAGe7HVG7QfueMqsA4NF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured facts that change the ranking. Sending to the auditor."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4260,"cache_read_input_tokens":114703,"output_tokens":2233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":714},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2233,"cache_read_input_tokens":114703,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4260},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fff6e08e-2d49-4562-82a7-82bca144addc","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:11:34.144Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"fff6e08e-2d49-4562-82a7-82bca144addc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAGe7HVG7QfueMqsA4NF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011iQJwfWurNMDp5KhJf1ezz","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"RUNTIME MEASUREMENTS — I ran these myself on the installed app just now. They resolve one of the architect's unverified items and materially change the sidecar cost. Fold them into your audit.\n\n(a) RENAMED ELECTRON UNDER ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE — **VERIFIED WORKING**. I copied Superset.exe to `superset-ptyd.exe` in a scratch dir along with the top-level runtime files + locales, then ran it:\n    ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 superset-ptyd.exe -e \"console.log(process.version, process.argv0)\"\n    → `NODE_OK v24.18.0 ...\\tmp\\ptyruntime-probe\\superset-ptyd.exe`\nSo the rename is fine, and note it ran with **NO `resources/` directory present at all** (no app.asar). The architect's \"single assumption that could invalidate Rank 1\" is dead — the rename works.\n\n(b) SIZE — the architect's ~300 MB estimate is WRONG BY 7x. Actual installed tree:\n    TOTAL install dir            2,372,511,804 B  = 2.21 GB  (1671 files)\n    resources\\app.asar           1,215.1 MB\n    resources\\app.asar.unpacked    594.5 MB  (1437 files)\n    Electron runtime only (top-level files + locales, NO resources\\)  =  361,157,844 B = 0.34 GB\nSo \"copy the packaged app directory\" per version means **2.21 GB per retained version**, not 300 MB. That is a serious cost at boot (copy time, disk, Defender scan) and makes GC correctness far more important than the architect implied.\n\n(c) THE INTERESTING CONSEQUENCE. Since the renamed exe runs as Node with no resources/ at all, a MINIMAL sidecar may need only:\n    - Electron runtime files + locales  ~344 MB\n    - the pty-daemon script itself\n    - @lydell/node-pty-win32-arm64 — `conpty.node` 290 KB + `conpty_console_list.node` 118.5 KB (that is the whole native surface; there is no pty.node, the architect's name for it was wrong)\ni.e. potentially ~345 MB instead of 2.21 GB — a 6.5x reduction.\n\nPLEASE DETERMINE, since this decides the design:\n1. What exactly does `scriptPath` in DaemonSupervisor.spawn() resolve to, and is the pty-daemon a SELF-CONTAINED bundle or does it `require` broadly across the asar at runtime? If self-contained, the minimal sidecar above is viable and Rank 1 gets 6.5x cheaper. If it pulls in the asar graph, say so and price it honestly.\n2. Can the daemon load `conpty.node` from a relocated path, or does anything hardcode a path relative to the install dir / `app.getAppPath()` / `process.resourcesPath`? `process.resourcesPath` in particular will point somewhere different (or nowhere) in a sidecar tree — check whether the daemon or node-pty reads it.\n3. Given (b), is copying at BOOT even acceptable, or should the sidecar be materialised at INSTALL time / lazily on first daemon spawn / only when the version actually changes? Note the app already has a documented footgun: no synchronous/blocking fs on the main thread at startup or the renderer starves and the window stays blank for minutes.\n4. Does a cheaper design now beat the sidecar entirely — e.g. shipping the daemon as a small separate binary, or having the INSTALLER place the runtime outside $INSTDIR, or the daemon copying ITSELF out on first run?\n\nMy scratch probe dir is at `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\ptyruntime-probe` (361 MB, renamed exe + runtime files, no resources). You may reuse it read-only for further probing — e.g. dropping in a daemon bundle and seeing whether it actually starts. Do NOT touch the installed app, and do not quit/kill/restart anything.","summary":"Send runtime measurements to plan auditor","to":"term-plan-audit-fable","type":"message","recipient":"term-plan-audit-fable","content":"RUNTIME MEASUREMENTS — I ran these myself on the …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4260,"cache_read_input_tokens":114703,"output_tokens":2233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":714},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2233,"cache_read_input_tokens":114703,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4260},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"39a219ed-9367-453e-b747-46e552894b9a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:11:53.483Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
