{"parentUuid":"f9618329-b73e-40d7-9d93-8dd19f141140","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAGpM2G8Y1mDmobsHqbt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two independent reviews converged on the same two BLOCKERs — environment inheritance (`BASH_ENV`/`PATH` via `$GITHUB_ENV`/`$GITHUB_PATH`) into the supposedly-frozen shells. Opus found two more the first review missed. Collecting the two outstanding reports."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13883,"cache_read_input_tokens":121377,"output_tokens":1821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":757},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13883,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1821,"cache_read_input_tokens":121377,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13883},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"31b65b2c-81f3-472b-b605-8134309d5210","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:13:53.983Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"31b65b2c-81f3-472b-b605-8134309d5210","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAGpM2G8Y1mDmobsHqbt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HKRBbTomSqHQhF5yinzt76","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"You went idle without sending me your report. Send your full job-split design audit now as a single message: verdict (SOUND / SOUND-WITH-CHANGES / REDESIGN), the corrected implementable design, and what stays unsolved. If you did not finish, say exactly what you did and did not establish rather than guessing.\n\nTwo independent reviews have since converged on findings you should account for in your corrected design:\n- BLOCKER: the frozen enforcement step unsets NODE_OPTIONS/NODE_PATH but NOT BASH_ENV. Bash sources $BASH_ENV for every non-interactive shell including the runner's. A repairable step writes BASH_ENV=<evil> to $GITHUB_ENV; the next attempt's enforcement step sources it and exits 0 before the gate runs. (Note NODE_OPTIONS is already in the runner's _setEnvBlockList, so the one variable explicitly handled is the one that could not be set anyway.)\n- BLOCKER: same class in the validate+push step — poisoned PATH/BASH_ENV means bash, git, python3, node, grep, diff are all attacker-resolved, inside the shell that holds the push PAT.\n- MAJOR: ci-repair.sh collect() flattens steps from all jobs into one list and discards job/index, and the three enforcement steps are byte-identical. Deleting the one in build-attempt-3 and adding a duplicate elsewhere leaves base_steps == head_steps.\n- MAJOR: the gate scans apps/desktop/dist rather than the packaged artifact that actually ships. A repairable step inserted AFTER packaging can scrub telemetry strings from dist/ so the gate validates content that is not what was published.\n\nAddress specifically whether your job-split design closes each of these by construction, or whether each still needs its own targeted fix on top. Be explicit about which are structurally solved and which are not.","summary":"Request job-split audit plus converged findings","to":"jobsplit-audit-fable","type":"message","recipient":"jobsplit-audit-fable","content":"You went idle without sending me your report. Sen…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13883,"cache_read_input_tokens":121377,"output_tokens":1821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":757},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13883,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1821,"cache_read_input_tokens":121377,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13883},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"0e479456-b8a1-4f68-8031-531a5ebbda99","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:14:03.153Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
