{"parentUuid":"bbe6966c-e313-4a5f-a856-0b89ce9e0f9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAHDyNS7AoBmAwvsx3Ra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fable's audit landed with three corrections that change the in-flight implementation. Relaying immediately."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6460,"cache_read_input_tokens":147236,"output_tokens":3011,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1339},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3011,"cache_read_input_tokens":147236,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"aa80ed86-bec0-49ee-b418-06fbeba3d5a8","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:19:20.961Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"aa80ed86-bec0-49ee-b418-06fbeba3d5a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAHDyNS7AoBmAwvsx3Ra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MFwP43k7y2UFxMKgbvovF4","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"TWO REFINEMENTS to your task, from a design audit that just landed. Both change what you are building. Read before continuing.\n\n--- REFINEMENT 1: my M2 instruction was incomplete. The asar scan is necessary but not sufficient. ---\nWhat actually gets published is ONLY the NSIS installer .exe (scripts/publish-arm64-release.sh:14-16,37). Chain: dist/ → electron-builder → release/*-unpacked/resources/app.asar → NSIS .exe.\nSo there are three scrub windows, not one:\n  (a) scrub dist AFTER packaging → unpacked asar AND exe both stay dirty → an asar scan CATCHES this (this is the attack I described to you; your asar scan handles it).\n  (b) scrub the unpacked asar AFTER the exe is built → asar clean, exe dirty → an asar scan MISSES this.\nTherefore the load-bearing assertion must be over the EXTRACTED INSTALLER, with the asar and dist scans kept as cheaper corroboration.\nCritical mechanical detail: a raw byte-scan of the .exe is USELESS because NSIS payloads are LZMA-compressed. You must extract: NSIS .exe → `$PLUGINSDIR/app-64.7z` → `resources/app.asar`. Use 7z. The asar itself is an uncompressed concatenation, so a plain byte-regex over the extracted asar works — no asar parser needed.\nImplement: extract the published .exe and run the SAME telemetry patterns against the extracted payload (phc_ key shape, Sentry DSN regex, outlit.ai, /api/desktop/version, superset-sh releases URL), plus the app-update.yml check. Fail loud — not vacuously — if extraction yields nothing, if 7z is unavailable, or if the extracted asar is missing/empty. Keep the dist/ assertions as fast feedback.\nRemember the assertion-count lockstep: EXPECTED appears in THREE places in build-arm64.yml (~:171, ~:360, ~:546). Every added assertion must update all three, and the mismatch message must explain the lockstep requirement.\n\n--- REFINEMENT 2: NEW, high value, cheap — close the workflow-edit induction break ---\nscripts/ci-repair.sh:412-418 currently PERMITS a repair to edit .github/workflows when WORKFLOW_PUSH_TOKEN is set, and only ONE step is pinned. The nightly advance then pushes those commits to main with the PAT (nightly-merge.yml:690-693, 717). Net effect: a hostile workflow edit survives the night and GOVERNS THE NEXT RUN — which defeats every protection you are adding, one night later.\nFix: pin by identity rather than set membership. Compare the ENTIRE enforcement-related job mapping base-vs-head as one block keyed by JOB NAME, and additionally pin the workflow-level and per-job `permissions:` blocks. Do not extend the existing \"collect steps matching an anchor across all containers\" approach (ci-repair.sh:341-355) — that pattern is exactly what M1 exploits. If whole-job pinning proves awkward, the acceptable simpler alternative is to forbid repair edits to .github/workflows/build-arm64.yml outright and fail loud; choose that if it is materially more robust, and say which you chose and why.\n\n--- ALSO NOTE (do NOT act on these, they belong to a later structural change) ---\nAn audit recommends eventually moving enforcement+publish and validate+push to separate fresh-runner jobs, which would solve B1/B2 by construction rather than by sanitization. I have deliberately deferred that refactor. Your targeted B1/B2 sanitization fixes are still exactly what I want now — do not attempt the job split.\nTwo bugs that audit found in the FUTURE design, recorded so you do not accidentally introduce them: a \"stamp sha == BUILT_SHA\" comparison always fails (the gate derives the stamp sha from `git rev-parse HEAD` in its own repoRoot), and publish-arm64-release.sh reads the version from the working tree and tags HEAD (:11, :35), which under a split would delete the previous good release and mis-tag. Leave publish-arm64-release.sh alone unless one of your fixes genuinely requires touching it.\n\nEverything else in your brief stands, including the full tamper matrix and the no-commit rule. Report the extraction-scan results explicitly — I want to see it catch a dirty exe with a clean dist.","summary":"Send audit refinements to CI implementer","to":"ci-blockers-impl-opus","type":"message","recipient":"ci-blockers-impl-opus","content":"TWO REFINEMENTS to your task, from a design audit…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6460,"cache_read_input_tokens":147236,"output_tokens":3011,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1339},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3011,"cache_read_input_tokens":147236,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"29f0600d-18a1-489e-9675-49b656a9969a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:19:42.786Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
