{"parentUuid":"ddbfa398-b7b9-4a00-b817-cfec43261d42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAHH6HExQTkXhDoJJeTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cache_read_input_tokens":153696,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":270},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3187,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":153696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3187},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"40c200ac-2047-44d1-a7cd-74766b8a4b71","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:19:49.688Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"40c200ac-2047-44d1-a7cd-74766b8a4b71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAHH6HExQTkXhDoJJeTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job-split audit came back **SOUND-WITH-CHANGES** — and usefully, it caught two bugs in *my* proposed design before anything was built:\n\n- My \"stamp sha must equal the built sha\" check **would have failed every single run**. The gate derives that sha from `git rev-parse HEAD` in its own checkout, which is the trusted sha, never the built one.\n- The publish script reads the version from the working tree and tags `HEAD`. Under my split that means it would have **deleted the previous good Release** and tagged the wrong commit. That's the kind of thing that's much cheaper to catch in an audit than in production.\n\nIt also confirmed the split would remove the write-scoped token from the agent's runner entirely, which closes the item I'd deferred and owed you.\n\n**The more important correction is to the \"gate validates the wrong thing\" finding — it's worse than I described.** There are three scrub windows, not one. Scrubbing `dist` after packaging leaves both the unpacked archive and the installer dirty, so an archive scan catches it. But scrubbing the *unpacked archive* after the installer is built leaves the installer dirty and the archive clean — an archive scan misses that entirely. Only extracting the actual installer is faithful. And a raw byte scan of the installer is useless because NSIS payloads are LZMA-compressed; it has to be properly extracted first. I've sent that correction to the implementer.\n\nAlso added a cheap high-value fix: a repair can currently edit the workflow file, and the nightly pushes that to main — so **a hostile edit survives the night and governs the next run**, defeating everything else one night later.\n\n**Judgement call, stated plainly**: I'm deferring the full job-split refactor. It's the structurally correct end state, but it rewrites a workflow that runs unattended nightly and adds 5–15 minutes of artifact transport per run. The targeted fixes close the actual attack chains now; the split gets done deliberately, with a test dispatch, not rushed. Fable gave a seven-step build order for it when we do.\n\nTerminal-persistence audit still running."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cache_read_input_tokens":153696,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":270},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3187,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":153696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3187},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"88df41c4-71d3-4f58-932e-20d5737c7652","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:19:58.635Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
