{"parentUuid":"301b4f9b-e180-42df-921c-193902476469","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAHiMXiMfxCUczG1HcFg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CWtD9Ae7om24E7ufJkxQHA","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"DECISIVE MEASUREMENTS — I resolved your question 1 myself. The daemon IS a self-contained bundle, and I now have exact sizes.\n\nEVIDENCE:\n- `apps/desktop/src/main/pty-daemon/index.ts` header comment states plainly: \"We need a desktop-side entry so electron-vite emits `apps/desktop/dist/main/pty-daemon.js` alongside `host-service.js` — the supervisor's `sideBySide` script-path resolution looks for the daemon binary right next to its own bundle.\" So `scriptPath` resolves to `dist/main/pty-daemon.js`, sitting beside `host-service.js`.\n- I parsed the SHIPPED app.asar header directly. Actual sizes in `dist/main/`:\n      pty-daemon.js          41.3 KB      <-- the entire daemon\n      pty-daemon.js.map     105.5 KB\n      host-service.js      3,529.2 KB\n      index.js             3,430.4 KB\n      terminal-host.js       321.3 KB\n  There is also a `chunks` directory under dist/main — CHECK whether pty-daemon.js requires anything from it, since that decides whether 41.3 KB is really the whole story.\n\nSO THE MINIMAL SIDECAR IS, WITH REAL NUMBERS:\n    Electron runtime files + locales      ~344 MB   (measured: 361,157,844 B)\n    dist/main/pty-daemon.js                 41.3 KB\n    node-pty native (conpty.node 290 KB + conpty_console_list.node 118.5 KB) + the node-pty JS wrapper\n    ------------------------------------------------\n    ~345 MB total, versus 2.21 GB to copy the whole install directory — a 6.4x reduction.\nThe 1.2 GB app.asar and the 594 MB app.asar.unpacked are NOT needed, except for extracting those few files out of them.\n\nWHAT I STILL NEED FROM YOU, since these decide implementability:\n1. Does pty-daemon.js pull anything from `dist/main/chunks/` at runtime, or is the 41.3 KB genuinely self-contained? If it needs chunks, price that.\n2. How does the bundle load node-pty — bundled, or an external `require` resolved relative to the script? Does anything read `process.resourcesPath` or `app.getAppPath()`, which will point somewhere different (or nowhere) in a sidecar tree?\n3. `DaemonSupervisor`'s `sideBySide` script-path resolution: if we relocate the daemon, does that resolution still work when host-service.js is NOT beside it (host-service stays in the install dir, daemon moves to the sidecar)? This is the crux of the whole design — the supervisor expects them adjacent. Say exactly how the remap must work, or whether host-service must ALSO be copied to the sidecar.\n4. Note `apps/desktop/scripts/check-pty-daemon-bundle.ts` exists — a post-build marker check on the daemon bundle asserting fd-handoff markers survive bundling. Whatever we do must not break it, and it may be a useful place to assert sidecar invariants too.\n\nAlso fold in the earlier facts I sent: renamed Electron under ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE is VERIFIED WORKING (Node v24.18.0) and ran with no resources/ directory present at all.\n\nGive me your verdict and corrected design. If you have already finished, send it now — I have received nothing from you yet.","summary":"Send daemon bundle sizing to auditor","to":"term-plan-audit-fable","type":"message","recipient":"term-plan-audit-fable","content":"DECISIVE MEASUREMENTS — I resolved your question …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":162406,"output_tokens":1727,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":417},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1727,"cache