{"parentUuid":"169b2bea-3d9d-4164-a1f5-4bd973c6a479","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAJ8tRkV6wsaZ4BTQurL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Root cause confirmed, and it's a real bug — not a design gap. Dispatching the fix."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":195545,"output_tokens":4232,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4232,"cache_read_input_tokens":195545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"5039fb2e-a4ab-4949-bb5d-89fdc0e9802a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:31:21.561Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"5039fb2e-a4ab-4949-bb5d-89fdc0e9802a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAJ8tRkV6wsaZ4BTQurL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019vvdvzotHYFxQPJ4iqbyzS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix Windows daemon kill crash","model":"opus","name":"pty-kill-fix-opus","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64 (owner's own private Windows ARM64 fork of the Superset desktop app). REPOSITORY FILES ONLY — never read user home-directory shell profiles or credentials; out of scope per owner. Reading the app's own state dir (`~\\.superset\\host\\...`) and the installed app under `C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\@supersetdesktop\\` IS in scope and useful.\n\nENV: the Bash tool is BROKEN (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: unexpected EOF`). Use the PowerShell tool for everything. Coreutils: `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"`. `node_modules` is NOT installed in this checkout, so you cannot run the test suite; rely on reading + targeted reasoning, and say so plainly rather than claiming you ran tests.\n\nDO NOT quit, kill, or restart the running Superset app or any of its processes — the owner has live terminals in it, and this session runs inside it.\n\n=== FINDING 1 (CONFIRMED BY ME — root cause, fix this) ===\nThe Windows pty-daemon crashes and takes EVERY session with it, because node-pty's Windows kill throws.\n\nInstalled node-pty (`...\\app.asar.unpacked\\node_modules\\node-pty\\windowsTerminal.js`):\n    WindowsTerminal.prototype.kill = function (signal) {\n        var _this = this;\n        this._deferNoArgs(function () {\n            if (signal) { throw new Error('Signals not supported on windows.'); }\n            _this._close();\n            ...\n    };\nand:\n    WindowsTerminal.prototype._deferNoArgs = function (deferredFn) {\n        if (this._isReady) { deferredFn.call(this); return; }   // SYNCHRONOUS\n        this._deferreds.push({ run: function () { return deferredFn.call(_this); } });  // DEFERRED\n    };\n\nSo passing ANY signal throws. Two regimes:\n  - terminal READY  → throws SYNCHRONOUSLY into the caller (catchable).\n  - terminal NOT READY → queued, then thrown later from the conpty agent's socket event → UNCAUGHT EXCEPTION → the daemon process DIES, killing all other sessions with it.\n\nThe daemon passes a signal on EVERY kill path. In `packages/pty-daemon/src/Pty/Pty.ts`:\n    :261  this.term.kill(sig)\n    :326  this.killer.kill(signal ?? \"SIGHUP\")     <-- default is truthy, so ALWAYS a signal\n    :435  adapter.kill(\"SIGKILL\")\n    :442  term.kill(\"SIGKILL\")\n    :600  this.killer.kill(signal ?? \"SIGHUP\")     <-- same\nNote `registerPendingKill` (:37-46) attaches a promise `.catch`, which CANNOT catch a throw raised from an unrelated socket event loop callback.\n\nPROOF FROM THE OWNER'S LIVE LOG (`~\\.superset\\host\\30e16b5a-e2af-4874-b126-acc7b3f17aa9\\pty-daemon.log`, 432 lines): two full uncaught-exception crash dumps ending in a `Node.js v24.18.0` footer — the process-death format — with this stack shape:\n    Error: Signals not supported on windows.\n        at WindowsTerminal.<anonymous> (...\\node-pty\\windowsTerminal.js)\n        at Array.forEach (<anonymous>)\n        at Object.run (...\\windowsTerminal.js)\n        at Socket.<anonymous> (...\\windowsTerminal.js)\n        at Socket.emit / readableAddChunkPushByteMode / Pipe.onStreamRead\ni.e. exactly the deferred-queue-drained-from-socket-event path.\n\nREQUIRED FIX: on Windows, never pass a signal to node-pty's kill. Call `kill()` with no argument so it takes the `_close()` path. Do this at every call site listed above, in a single well-named helper rather than five scattered `process.platform` checks. Preserve POSIX behaviour EXACTLY — signals are load-bearing there (SIGHUP-then-SIGKILL escalation). Add a fork marker comment token and a `FEATURES.md` entry (suggest `(WIN-PTY-KILL-NOSIGNAL)`), because this file is upstream-owned and a nightly merge will otherwise silently drop it.\nAlso add a defensive top-level `process.on(\"uncaughtException\")` handler in the daemon entry (`packages/pty-daemon/src/main.ts`, and mirror in `apps/desktop/src/main/pty-daemon/index.ts` if it has its own entry logic) that LOGS the full stack to the daemon log and then decides deliberately whether to exit — one bad session must never silently destroy every other session. Fail loud in the log, and justify in a comment whichever choice you make.\n\n=== FINDING 2 (CONFIRMED BY ME — fix this too) ===\n`packages/pty-daemon/src/process-tree.ts` is POSIX-only: it shells out to `ps -axo pid=,ppid=,pgid=,tty=,stat=` (:130) and uses process-group kills. On Windows this cannot work, and the owner's log contains **287** occurrences of:\n    [pty-daemon] kill escalation for pid N: final ps failed, survivor state unknown   (Pty.ts:171)\nConsequence: on Windows, killing a session signals only the root pid and ORPHANS the entire shell subtree — every child process leaks, permanently, and the daemon cannot even tell.\nFIX: add a Windows branch that enumerates and terminates the real process tree. `taskkill /PID <pid> /T /F` is the straightforward option; a CIM/WMI `Win32_Process` ParentProcessId walk is the more precise one and avoids taskkill's own quirks. Choose one, justify it, and make the \"survivor state unknown\" path report accurately on Windows instead of always claiming failure. Beware pid reuse — verify a candidate's parent chain before killing it. Mark with a token and a FEATURES.md entry (suggest `(WIN-PROCESS-TREE)`).\n\n=== SCOPE BOUNDARIES ===\n- Do NOT build the \"sidecar runtime\" (relocating the daemon out of the install directory). That is a separate, larger piece of work being designed. These two fixes are independent of it and valuable regardless.\n- Do NOT change the detach/spawn behaviour, the pipe naming, the manifest format, or the adoption logic.\n- Do NOT commit and do NOT push. Leave everything in the working tree.\n\n=== VERIFICATION ===\n- `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"; node scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs` → must end \"All N feature markers present\" (N will rise by 2 once you add the entries; make sure FEATURES.md and the in-code tokens agree).\n- `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` → must end \"(REFERR-GATE) clean\".\n- Since you cannot run the test suite, instead write down for EACH call site you changed: the exact before/after, which platform takes which branch, and why POSIX behaviour is provably unchanged.\n- State explicitly whether your Windows tree-kill has been exercised at all, and if not, say so — do not imply verification you did not perform.\n\nYour final message is the entire report: what you changed with file:line, your reasoning on the uncaughtException decision, the Windows tree-kill approach and its pid-reuse handling, verification output, and anything you could not establish.","subagent_type":"claude"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":195545,"output_tokens":4232,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4232,"cache_read_input_tokens":195545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"58c0b84d-92c8-416f-83fe-0910dd3fe20e","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:31:57.491Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
