{"parentUuid":"8eaabb30-f204-4084-99ce-f858cac959a5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"51b620fc-5d74-4e89-a4b6-b504e385424e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EwV1i9ZJU9jXr9iZFP6jMX","type":"tool_result","content":"=== killTerm implementation ===\r\n392:\tprivate killTerm(signal: NodeJS.Signals): void {\n393-\t\tif (!IS_WINDOWS) {\n394-\t\t\tthis.term.kill(signal);\n395-\t\t\treturn;\n396-\t\t}\n397-\t\tthis.killConptyOnce();\n398-\t}\n399-\n400-\t/**\n401-\t * The Windows kill is a CLOSE, not a repeatable signal: a second\n402-\t * `_agent.kill()` disposes the conout worker twice and calls the native\n403-\t * kill on a freed pty handle from inside a promise — an unhandled\n404-\t * rejection, i.e. another dead daemon. Fire it at most once.\n405-\t */\n406-\tprivate killConptyOnce(): void {\n407-\t\tif (this.conptyKilled) return;\n408-\t\tthis.conptyKilled = true;\n409-\t\tthis.term.kill();\n410-\t}\n411-\n412-\tdispose(_options?: DisposeOptions): void {\n413-\t\tif (this.disposed) return;\n414-\t\tthis.disposed = true;\n415-\t\t// Keep TreeKiller's escalation chain intact. A root shell can exit while\n416-\t\t// a detached descendant that ignored SIGHUP is still alive; the kill\n417-\t\t// chain's later snapshots are what find and reap those survivors.\n418-\t\ttry {\n419-\t\t\tif (IS_WINDOWS) {\n420-\t\t\t\t// WindowsTerminal.destroy() IS kill() (deferred, no argument),\n421-\t\t\t\t// so it goes through the same one-shot guard.\n422-\t\t\t\tthis.killConptyOnce();","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8beec844-b8d6-426f-8c38-6f7363ce6ea4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:55:44.517Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== killTerm implementation ===\r\n392:\tprivate killTerm(signal: NodeJS.Signals): void {\n393-\t\tif (!IS_WINDOWS) {\n394-\t\t\tthis.term.kill(signal);\n395-\t\t\treturn;\n396-\t\t}\n397-\t\tthis.killConptyOnce();\n398-\t}\n399-\n400-\t/**\n401-\t * The Windows kill is a CLOSE, not a repeatable signal: a second\n402-\t * `_agent.kill()` disposes the conout worker twice and calls the native\n403-\t * kill on a freed pty handle from inside a promise — an unhandled\n404-\t * rejection, i.e. another dead daemon. Fire it at most once.\n405-\t */\n406-\tprivate killConptyOnce(): void {\n407-\t\tif (this.conptyKilled) return;\n408-\t\tthis.conptyKilled = true;\n409-\t\tthis.term.kill();\n410-\t}\n411-\n412-\tdispose(_options?: DisposeOptions): void {\n413-\t\tif (this.disposed) return;\n414-\t\tthis.disposed = true;\n415-\t\t// Keep TreeKiller's escalation chain intact. A root shell can exit while\n416-\t\t// a detached descendant that ignored SIGHUP is still alive; the kill\n417-\t\t// chain's later snapshots are what find and reap those survivors.\n418-\t\ttry {\n419-\t\t\tif (IS_WINDOWS) {\n420-\t\t\t\t// WindowsTerminal.destroy() IS kill() (deferred, no argument),\n421-\t\t\t\t// so it goes through the same one-shot guard.\n422-\t\t\t\tthis.killConptyOnce();","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8eaabb30-f204-4084-99ce-f858cac959a5","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
