{"parentUuid":"254f60ce-9e90-4637-9658-19a23965ee87","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14841207 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7eedb5e5-2a03-45eb-a03f-0076c9bfcf42","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:59:29.126Z","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"7eedb5e5-2a03-45eb-a03f-0076c9bfcf42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeALK31hHZpe7rJePtLQu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The terminal fix report is in, and it's stronger than I expected in a few places.\n\n**What was actually tested** (correcting my earlier statement — `node_modules` *is* installed here, so real verification was possible): the pty-daemon suite runs **81 pass, 1 fail**, and the failure is pre-existing and unrelated — a test asserting a POSIX path shape against a Windows temp path in code that wasn't touched. Type errors are all pre-existing and were *proven* so by reproducing them from a two-line file, not just asserted.\n\n**The Windows process-tree walk was exercised against live processes**: a real three-deep process tree was spawned and correctly identified among 497 enumerated processes, and — the important test — pointing it at a deliberately wrong anchor returned nothing, demonstrating the pid-reuse guard works. It selected targets without killing anything, deliberately, because your sessions are running.\n\nTwo design decisions worth your awareness:\n\n- **The crash guard logs and keeps running rather than exiting**, escalating to exit only on a burst. That cuts against the usual fail-fast rule, and the reasoning is sound: this daemon owns your PTY handles, a restart can't recover them, and realistic faults are per-session — so surviving costs one broken terminal while exiting costs all of them. It also covers unhandled rejections, which matters because the double-close hazard produces exactly that shape.\n- **Windows tree enumeration costs ~590 ms per round**, worst case about 9 seconds for a full escalation chain. That's a real cost, chosen over the faster `taskkill /T /F` because taskkill does no creation-time check and would happily kill a recycled process ID that merely *looks* like your shell.\n\n**The honest gap**: target selection is verified, but **actual termination has never been run** — that needs a packaged build. So this fixes a confirmed crash, but the end-to-end kill path is unproven until you're running a build with it.\n\nOne adjacent issue found and deliberately left alone: the legacy terminal path has the same throw, but it lives in its own process, so it kills one session rather than all of them.\n\nFable's review is still running; I'll hold the commit until it lands."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_read_input_tokens":231296,"output_tokens":712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":978,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":231296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":978},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8e31dada-4bef-48b7-b3e4-a20b202e6ad7","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:59:42.629Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
