{"parentUuid":"336d73b9-77d4-4c0b-b067-46c57837eb69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAM2EZsJweDPxjtXiS5C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011WV2n1HfmDDPtxGzVS2gPZ","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"You went idle without sending me your report. Send it now as a single message: BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR findings with file:line and a concrete failure scenario each, or a plain statement that the batch is clean.\n\nI specifically need your verdict on these five, since they are the ones I would hold the commit for:\n1. Is POSIX behaviour provably unchanged at every touched call site?\n2. The one-shot `killConptyOnce` guard — if the first close fails to terminate the shell, does the guard permanently block later escalation attempts and leak the process, or does the Windows tree-kill independently reap it?\n3. Can the new Windows tree-kill ever target a process outside the session's own subtree? Is the start-time pid-reuse check actually enforced rather than merely carried?\n4. Is the crash guard's log-and-continue decision (exit only on >5 events/60s) sound, and does it cover unhandledRejection?\n5. Where does the fix depend on node-pty PRIVATE internals (`_isReady`, `_deferreds`, `_agent`), and how would it fail on a node-pty upgrade?\n\nIf you did not finish, say precisely what you did and did not check rather than guessing.","summary":"Request pty fix review findings","to":"pty-fix-review-fable","type":"message","recipient":"pty-fix-review-fable","content":"You went idle without sending me your report. Sen…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":266,"cache_read_input_tokens":232986,"output_tokens":497,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input