{"parentUuid":"564ac5ec-5354-4a77-9aaa-a84cb6ec086d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAMEHVZnojt3Zk6Xzt2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fable found a genuine regression — the fix introduced one. Dispatching the correction and chasing the CI report."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3583,"cache_read_input_tokens":237689,"output_tokens":2695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":528},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3583,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2695,"cache_read_input_tokens":237689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3583},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"df2f77dc-a487-4da6-84bb-af6e0e1d0f93","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:11:42.353Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"df2f77dc-a487-4da6-84bb-af6e0e1d0f93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAMEHVZnojt3Zk6Xzt2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P9rw1dAJwXPM8AkNpChgfb","name":"SendMessage","input":{"message":"Adversarial review found a BLOCKER: your change introduced a Windows REGRESSION. Fix this plus the MINORs below. Do not restructure anything else; the rest of your work reviewed clean and POSIX was confirmed provably unchanged.\n\n--- BLOCKER: synchronous tree-signal now signals NOTHING on Windows ---\npackages/pty-daemon/src/process-tree.ts:87 (the IS_WINDOWS routing in the sync path).\nMechanism: the Windows branch builds its table from `readProcessTable()`, which you deliberately made return `[]` on Windows (:334-350). `collectWindowsSignalTargets` then finds no root row and returns `[]` (:293-294), so ZERO `process.kill` calls happen.\nAt HEAD, that same empty table fell through to the POSIX logic, which still emitted `{pid: rootPid}` (includeRoot defaults true) → `process.kill(rootPid, sig)` → TerminateProcess, which DOES work on Windows. So you replaced \"kills at least the root\" with \"kills nothing\".\nCallers this breaks (outside your diff, broken BY your diff):\n  - packages/host-service/src/daemon/DaemonSupervisor.ts:1528/1530 `terminateProcessTreeAndGroups`, reached from `stop()` (:577), `killAdoptedDaemon` (:265), spawn-failure cleanup (:1241), dev stale-daemon kill (:872). Note `runUpdate` refuses on Windows and says \"use restart instead\", so restart IS the Windows path. Consequence: the supervisor cannot terminate ANY daemon on Windows — both the SIGTERM and SIGKILL passes no-op, both `waitForPidExit` timeouts burn, the manifest is removed anyway, and the old daemon keeps holding `\\\\.\\pipe\\superset-ptyd-*` while a fresh daemon binds a second pipe instance → nondeterministic client cross-talk between two live daemons.\n  - packages/host-service/src/terminal/clean-shell-env.ts:165 — the timeout path now leaks the probe shell (this file does run on Windows; COMSPEC branch at :127).\nFIX: in the IS_WINDOWS branch, when the synchronous table is empty, fall back to a root-pid-only target so the old degenerate semantics are preserved — never regress to signalling nothing. Additionally consider moving `terminateProcessTreeAndGroups` (already async) and clean-shell-env onto `readProcessTableAsync` + `collectWindowsSignalTargets` so Windows gets the real tree walk there; do that only if it stays a small, contained change.\nAlso fix the warning text at :345 — it says \"reaped no descendants\" when in fact it reaps nothing at all, root included. Say what is true.\n\n--- MINOR 1: chain reports CLEAN while descendants survive ---\nPty.ts:207-222 + process-tree.ts:293. Once the root row disappears from the snapshot the walk returns `[]`, so the escalation chain reports a clean kill even though detached or new-console descendants (which are outside the conpty console process list) are still alive and now unreported. POSIX covers this case via knownPgids/tty; Windows has no counterpart.\nFIX: latch descendant pid + startedAt pairs from each successful volley and re-target those on later rounds, so losing the root does not blind the chain.\n\n--- MINOR 2: root killed with no identity proof when the anchor is null ---\nprocess-tree.ts:296-299. If `rootStartedAt` is null (both captures failed, or a kill races the ~0.5s capture) the root is targeted anyway with `includeRoot: true` — a direct TerminateProcess on whatever currently holds that pid. POSIX never direct-kills the root from the tree path.\nFIX: skip the root target when the anchor is null. Losing a kill is far better than killing a stranger's process.\n\n--- MINOR 3: no unit tests for the new Windows logic ---\n`collectWindowsSignalTargets` (both pid-reuse rules), `parseWindowsProcessTable`, and the crash-guard burst threshold have zero tests, and all three are trivially unit-testable on any platform by feeding synthetic tables. Add them. Note node_modules IS installed, so run them: `bun run test` in packages/pty-daemon. Baseline is 81 pass / 1 fail, where the single failure is a pre-existing macOS `probeTrustdHealthy` cert test unrelated to this work — I confirmed that myself. Do not \"fix\" that test.\n\nVERIFY, and report exact output: marker gate ends \"All 205 feature markers present\"; `node scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs` ends \"(REFERR-GATE) clean\"; `bun run test` in packages/pty-daemon shows your new tests passing with no NEW failures; `biome check` clean.\nDo NOT commit, do NOT push. Do not quit/kill/restart the running Superset app — the owner has live terminals and this session runs inside it. Note: a detached watcher process (pid 38312, parent WmiPrvSE.exe) is logging Superset process state to tmp/daemon-death-watch.log — leave it alone.\n\nYour final message is the entire report: the regression fix with file:line, how you preserved the old degenerate semantics, the descendant-latching approach, and full verification output.","summary":"Send blocker regression fix to implementer","to":"pty-kill-fix-opus","type":"message","recipient":"pty-kill-fix-opus","content":"Adversarial review found a BLOCKER: your change i…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3583,"cache_read_input_tokens":237689,"output_tokens":2695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":528},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3583,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2695,"cache_read_input_tokens":237689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3583},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"ass