TE_DIR/base-sha says $STATE_BASE_SHA. Refusing to validate against an uncertain base.\"\n309:    BASE_SHA=\"$TRUSTED_BASE_SHA\"\n311:    # $TRUSTED_BASE_SHA whenever the workflow supplies it — the disagreement\n\r\n=== FROZEN_GATE_PATHS contents ===\r\n104:FROZEN_GATE_PATHS=(\r\n105-  .github/workflows\r\n106-  scripts/check-dangerous-diagnostics.mjs\r\n107-  scripts/check-feature-markers.mjs\r\n108-  scripts/check-cloud-severance.mjs\r\n109-  scripts/cloud-severance-allowlist.tsv\r\n110-  scripts/verify-renderer-guards.sh\r\n111-  scripts/verify-packaged-natives.sh\r\n112-  scripts/materialize-native-closure.sh\r\n113-  scripts/ci-repair.sh\r\n114-  scripts/ai-run.sh\r\n115-  scripts/ai-streak.sh\r\n116-  packages/host-service/src/companion*\r\n117-  .claude\r\n118-  .mcp.json\r\n119-)\r\n120-# One release version across the repo (bun run check:versions invariant).\r\n121-VERSIONED_PKGS=(apps/desktop packages/host-service packages/cli)\r\n122-\r\n--\r\n244:    FROZEN_LIST=$(printf '%s, ' \"${FROZEN_GATE_PATHS[@]}\" FEATURES.md)\r\n245-    FROZEN_LIST=\"${FROZEN_LIST%, }\"\r\n246-\r\n247-    REPAIR_PROMPT=\"IMPORTANT: Do NOT enter plan mode. You are the CI build-repair agent for the superset-windows-arm64 vendored fork (a Windows ARM64 fork of superset-sh/superset; see AGENTS.md for architecture). Build attempt $ROUND of the Windows ARM64 installer FAILED. The failed job's log is at: $LOG_FILE — read it, find the root cause, and fix it in this working tree (branch $REPAIR_BRANCH, currently checked out).\r\n248-\r\n249-Rules:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"19116e30-c954-4a0f-ab6f-c6a252f9c21b","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:15:23.454Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== m1: .claude handling ===\r\n77:# .claude and .mcp.json are frozen because they are EXECUTION config, not\n78:# documentation: .claude/settings.json can declare PreToolUse hooks and\n83:# CLI itself writes under .claude/ are swept before `git add -A` instead, so a\n117:  .claude\n268:    echo \"$AI_UNAVAILABLE_E