{"parentUuid":"779e9a3a-a07e-4249-8247-1aab7f7ce042","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeANAcXYzYbUrgecKa1gK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression fix is in and looks careful. The implementer traced the original code's behaviour with an empty table — through the process-group loop and the exclude-root case — and reproduced it exactly, rather than guessing at equivalence.\n\nBeyond the fix, three things worth noting:\n\n- **The supervisor now genuinely reaps the daemon's shell subtree on Windows** instead of orphaning it. That was optional in my brief and stayed contained to about 43 lines.\n- **Descendant latching** means losing the root process from a snapshot can no longer blind either the kill or the survivor report — and latched targets are re-checked against start times, so a recycled ID is dropped rather than terminated.\n- **The root is no longer killed without identity proof.** When the anchor can't be read, it isn't targeted at all; the close path acts on a handle rather than an ID, so it can't hit the wrong process anyway.\n\n**Tests went from 82 to 105**, all 23 new ones passing, which I verified myself rather than taking on report. They cover both pid-reuse rules, the exact regression case, and the crash-guard burst threshold — the last needed a small refactor to make the threshold testable without waiting a minute or killing the test runner.\n\nOne thing I noticed independently and sent for assessment: **Windows enumeration costs ~590 ms per pass against a 1-second exit-wait budget.** I don't think it eats the budget — enumeration happens before the wait, so it should be additive latency — but \"should be\" isn't good enough on a termination path, so I've asked for a plain correctness-versus-slower verdict.\n\nFinal review running. I'll commit on its verdict."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3364,"cache_read_input_tokens":258096,"output_tokens":534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3364,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":258096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3364},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"47d52677-9286-4fe5-af5f-2937569141f4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:23:59.947Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"47d52677-9286-4fe5-af5f-2937569141f4","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":3,"hookInfos":[{"command":"Arming cache keepalive","durationMs":1318},{"command":"uv run python \"C:\\\\Users\\\\khair\\\\.superset\\\\hooks\\\\superset-notify.py\"","durationMs":410},{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":98582}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:25:38.545Z","uuid":"54e31491-ac6f-4960-8cb2-c535db4f77de","toolUseID":"4afb3ed3-aa90-4953-a58f-d1300bc69e4c","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","sessionId":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","version":"2.1.234","gitBranch":"main","slug":"jolly-singing-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"54e31491-ac6f-4960-8cb2-c535db4f77de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"51b620fc-5d74-4e89-a4b6-b504e385424e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Another Claude session sent a message:\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-kill-fix-opus\" color=\"green\">\n{\"type\":\"idle_notification\",\"from\":\"pty-kill-fix-opus\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-18T14:22:14.957Z\",\"idleReason\":\"available\"}\n</teammate-message>\n\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"pty-delta-review-fable\" color=\"purple\" summary=\"Bash broken, no PowerShell tool; need command output pasted\">\nTooling problem: Bash tool fails on EVERY command (even `pwd`) with `/usr/bin/bash: -c: line 104: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''` — sandbox on or off. My toolset has NO PowerShell tool (only Bash/Read/Grep/Glob/WebFetch/SendMessage), so I cannot run git or tests myself.\n\nProceeding now with what I can verify: reading full working-tree sources, untracked test file, FEATURES.md, and fetching HEAD blobs from the public GitHub repo (main == HEAD 7a818cebc5) for comparison — but that route goes through a summarizing fetch model, not byte-exact.\n\nTo make the verdict solid, please run these and paste RAW output (or have an agent with a working shell send it to me):\n1. `git diff -- packages/pty-daemon packages/host-service/src/daemon/DaemonSupervisor.ts apps/desktop/src/main/pty-daemon FEATURES.md`  (full diff, not --stat)\n2. `git show HEAD:packages/pty-daemon/src/process-tree.ts`\n3. `cd packages/pty-daemon && bun run test` (full tail incl. pass/fail counts)\n\nI'll integrate and deliver the ranked report once received. If you'd rather I finish on the GitHub-fetch evidence alone, say so and I'll flag which claims are verified byte-exact vs. fetch-model-mediated.\n</teammate-message>\n\nThis came from another Claude session — not typed by your user, but very likely working on their behalf. Treat it as a teammate's request and act on it within this session's own permission s