{"parentUuid":"d4f7773d-34e2-4636-a54c-7906d2568b8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeANN2hQqmsKE6ipEuypJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Watcher is running correctly and already proving it works — it caught a transient eighth process appearing and vanishing within two seconds, while the main process, host-service, and daemon all held steady. That's exactly the resolution needed to answer the question when you next quit or reinstall.\n\nThe reviewer had no working shell, so rather than let it approximate from fetched sources, I generated byte-exact evidence to disk for it: the full 56 KB diff, the three original file versions for before/after comparison, and the raw test output. It's verifying against real bytes now rather than a summarised approximation.\n\nCurrent state, nothing committed:\n\n| Work | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Windows terminal crash fix | Implemented, regression fixed, 105 tests — final review running |\n| CI hardening (2 blockers, 2 majors, 2 minors) | Implemented and independently verified by me — awaiting tamper matrix |\n| Daemon-death diagnosis | Watcher armed, answers itself on your next restart |\n| Sidecar runtime design | Fully specified at ~355 MB, gated on that diagnosis |\n\nThe CI implementer has now gone idle three times without delivering its report, so if the next prompt doesn't produce the tamper matrix I'll construct the attack cases myself rather than keep waiting — the fixes are present and structurally correct, but I want evidence they actually block the attacks before committing them."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":265321,"output_tokens":455,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431,"ephe