{"parentUuid":"c8b6686f-415e-4a2d-b402-c230fc2072c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAPSV9NCXUaCZKahK7Q4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PxGSd3WZb7YRMirMGNgKwT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Reuse review of pty diff","model":"opus","name":"simplify-reuse","prompt":"Repo: C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64. REPOSITORY FILES ONLY — never read user home-directory shell profiles or credentials.\n\nENV: Bash tool is BROKEN (`/usr/bin/bash: -c: unexpected EOF`). Use PowerShell. node_modules IS installed. Coreutils: `$env:PATH = \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin;$env:PATH\"`. Do NOT quit/kill/restart the running Superset app; leave watcher pid 38312 alone. Do NOT edit any file — you are review-only, report findings.\n\nDIFF UNDER REVIEW: `C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64\\tmp\\review\\simplify-scope.diff`\nTwo files are NEW and therefore not in the diff — read them directly:\n  packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\crash-guard.ts\n  packages\\pty-daemon\\src\\crash-guard.test.ts\n\nWHAT THE CHANGE DOES: fixes a Windows crash where node-pty's `kill(signal)` throws asynchronously and kills the whole pty-daemon; adds a Windows process-tree walk (Win32_Process via Get-CimInstance, ppid walk, start-time pid-reuse guards) to replace POSIX-only `ps -axo`/pgid logic; adds an uncaughtException/unhandledRejection crash guard.\n\nYOUR ANGLE: **REUSE**. Flag new code that re-implements something the codebase ALREADY has. Grep shared/utility modules and files adjacent to the change and NAME the existing helper that should be called instead.\n\nSpecifically worth checking:\n- Is there already a Windows process enumeration / CIM or WMI helper anywhere in the repo (apps/desktop/src/main, packages/host-service, packages/pty-daemon, scripts)? The v1 terminal-host stack and `tree-kill.ts` (apps/desktop/src/main/lib/tree-kill.ts) do Windows process killing — does the new code duplicate them?\n- Is there an existing start-time / process-identity helper, or an existing `isProcessAlive`-style utility (packages/host-service/src/daemon/manifest.ts has one) that the new pid-reuse guard duplicates?\n- Is there an existing platform predicate? Note the diff replaced/reused `SUPPORTS_FD_HANDOFF`'s `process.platform !== \"win32\"` test with `IS_WINDOWS` — check for OTHER existing platform constants in these packages that should have been reused instead of a new one, and whether DaemonSupervisor's own `IS_WINDOWS` (around :98) and the pty-daemon one are now redundant duplicates that should be shared.\n- Does the crash guard duplicate any existing error-logging/reporting utility in the daemon or host-service?\n- Do the new tests duplicate existing test helpers/fixtures rather than reusing them?\n\nReport each finding with: file, line, one-line summary, the concrete cost (what is duplicated and what maintaining both costs), and the NAME of the existing thing to call instead. If there is genuinely nothing to reuse, say so plainly — do not manufacture findings. Your final message is the entire report.","subagent_type":"claude"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1111,"cache_read_input_tokens":289281,"output_tokens":5823,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1111,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5823,"cache_read_input_tokens":289281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1111},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"attributionSkill":"simplify","type":"assistant","uuid":"87e9d6bf-073a-4b60-846f-2a1af3f9778a","timestamp":"2026-