{"parentUuid":"9191ef28-596e-4c95-88da-6e775c414f51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAPvgEe9dar6hyb4E4PU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verified the implementer's reasoning there was sound rather than lazy: the obvious millisecond format (`20260818144649023`) is **2.0 × 10¹⁶**, which exceeds JavaScript's safe integer limit of 9.0 × 10¹⁵ — so it would silently lose precision, which is worse than second resolution. Their comment said exactly that, and it checks out.\n\nThere is a clean alternative (epoch milliseconds, ~1.8 × 10¹², comfortably safe and simpler), but changing the format means touching the parser and about ten test literals in code that's now passed two reviews. Given the reviewer graded the race \"probabilistically negligible\" and explicitly said no fix required, I'm not churning it on the way to a commit. If a cleanup agent independently flags it, I'll reconsider.\n\nWaiting on the four `/simplify` agents and the tamper matrix."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":299604,"output_tokens":1012,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":717},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1012,"cache_read_input_tokens":299604,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8bee9e62-0011-4167-9cf4-be4d0aedefe5","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:47:10.714Z","effort":"high","session_id":"41b65f55-7b51-4cfd-82d1-d1d1eec49d91","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64","